E["item:andron-s-ledger"] = {t="item",n="Andron's Ledger",z="undercity",s="Andron's Ledger is an intelligence document obtained from Andron Gant in the Undercity. It details clandestine activities that uncover the unexpected involvement of the Syndicate in regional affairs, drawing the direct attention of Varimathras.",h="Andron's Ledger is an intelligence document obtained from Andron Gant in the Undercity.",sec={{t="Uncovering the Syndicate",b="Retrieved from Andron Gant's bookshelf within the Undercity, this ledger contains far more intelligence than the Deathstalkers initially anticipated. Its contents reveal that the Syndicate—the remnants of the fallen human nobility of Alterac—is actively maneuvering in the region. Upon reviewing the entries, Deathstalker Mennet Carkad immediately realizes the strategic value of the document, recognizing that the ruined lords of Alterac are scheming once again. The ledger provides the Forsaken leadership with concrete proof of Syndicate operations, turning a routine errand into a major intelligence coup.",sp=1},{t="A Matter for the Dreadlord",b="Because the revelation concerns regional threats to the Forsaken realm, Mennet Carkad dispatches the bearer to carry the ledger directly to Varimathras in the Royal Quarter. As Sylvanas Windrunner's dreadlord majordomo, Varimathras oversees internal security and espionage through the Deathstalkers. The ledger earns Varimathras's commendation, proving both the competence of the Deathstalker network and the reliability of the operative who brought it to light.",sp=2}},faq={{q="What is Andron's Ledger?",a="It is a record book retrieved from Andron Gant's bookshelf in the Undercity, containing secret intelligence regarding the Syndicate's movements and operations in Lordaeron.",al={"androns ledger","what is this book","andron ledger"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Andron Gant?",a="Andron Gant is an informant or contact based in the Undercity who maintains business arrangements with the Deathstalkers, providing them with critical regional intelligence.",al={"who is andron","andron gant"},it="people"},{q="Why is the Syndicate mentioned in the ledger important?",a="The ledger reveals that the Syndicate—composed of the disgraced nobility of the former Kingdom of Alterac—is actively involved in local plots, giving the Forsaken early warning of their maneuvers.",al={"why syndicate matters","what does the ledger reveal"},it="ties"},{q="Who receives the ledger?",a="It is first brought to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter, who evaluates its contents and then instructs that it be delivered directly to Lord Varimathras in the Hall of the Dark Lady.",al={"who gets androns ledger","who do i bring the ledger to"},it="target"},{q="What does delivering the ledger achieve for a rogue?",a="Delivering the ledger and uncovering the Syndicate's involvement completes the operative's initiation into the Deathstalkers, earning formal induction into the Forsaken's secretive assassin guild.",al={"deathstalker induction","joining deathstalkers"},it="for_you"},{q="Where did Andron's Ledger come from?",a="The ledger belongs to Andron Gant, an informant residing in the Undercity who keeps detailed records of his covert dealings. It rests on a bookshelf in his quarters until retrieved by an operative on behalf of the Deathstalkers.",al={"who made androns ledger","androns ledger origin","where did the ledger come from"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why do the Deathstalkers want Andron's Ledger?",a="Mennet Carkad and the Deathstalkers seek the ledger for vital intelligence gathered on regional threats. The documents unexpectedly expose the operations of the Syndicate—the fallen human nobles of Alterac—providing crucial insight that warrants reporting directly to Lord Varimathras.",al={"why is androns ledger wanted","who wants androns ledger","why does mennet carkad want the ledger"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Retrieving and deciphering Andron's Ledger serves as your proving ground, marking your formal induction into the Deathstalkers by Mennet Carkad and earning the personal acknowledgment of Varimathras.",["race:Undead"]="The ledger exposes the meddling of the Syndicate, showing that the living human nobles of Alterac still attempt to threaten the sovereignty of the Forsaken."},kw={"alterac","andron gant","andron's ledger","deathstalkers","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","syndicate","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1886","quest:1885","npc:varimathras","subzone:rogues-quarter","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom","zone:undercity","topic:rogue"},src={"Andron's Ledger","The Deathstalkers (3)","The Deathstalkers (4)"}}
E["item:astor-s-letter-of-introduction"] = {t="item",n="Astor's Letter of Introduction",z="undercity",s="Astor's Letter of Introduction is a document carried by Astor Hadren, a courier traveling between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity. Taken by aspiring Deathstalkers, the letter serves as cover to infiltrate a suspected conspiracy involving the shopkeeper Andron Gant.",h="Astor's Letter of Introduction is a document carried by Astor Hadren, a courier traveling between Silverpine...",sec={{t="A Courier's Credentials",b="Astor Hadren served as a discreet courier moving between Silverpine Forest and the capital. His personal letter of introduction establishes the bearer's bona fides to illicit contacts in the city. When Deathstalker handler Mennet Carkad needed to investigate suspicious leaks within the Undercity, Astor's travels made him an immediate target. By eliminating or robbing Hadren of his papers, an operative can assume his identity and intercept covert communications meant for Astor's eyes alone.",sp=0},{t="The Sting at the Apothecarium",b="Mennet Carkad uses the recovered letter to dupe Andron Gant, a book dealer and shopkeeper located near the Apothecarium. Gant is suspected by Lord Varimathras of leaking Forsaken intelligence to an unknown third party. Armed with Astor's letter, an undercover operative presents themselves as the expected contact, taking advantage of Gant's unwitting trust to uncover the identity of his conspirators and secure proof of his treason.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Astor's Letter of Introduction used for?",a="It serves as proof of identity to fool the merchant Andron Gant. By presenting the letter, an operative pretends to be the courier Astor Hadren to uncover Gant's secret dealings.",al={"purpose of the letter","what does the letter do","astors letter use"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who was Astor Hadren?",a="Astor Hadren was an emissary and messenger who traveled the roads between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity, carrying correspondence for private parties before being intercepted by Deathstalker agents.",al={"who is astor","astor hadren lore","who had the letter"},it="people"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want this letter?",a="Mennet Carkad needs the letter to test recruits wishing to join the Deathstalkers and to run a sting operation against Andron Gant, whom Lord Varimathras suspects of treason.",al={"why does mennet need it","carkad's plan"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does Andron Gant suspect the letter is stolen?",a="No. Mennet notes that Gant lacks the wit to suspect foul play, and Gant readily accepts the letter's bearer as the regular messenger sent by his conspirators.",al={"does gant notice","does andron get tricked"},sp=1},{q="What is Astor's Letter of Introduction?",a="It is a credential carried by Astor Hadren, a traveling courier journeying between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity. The document identifies its bearer as an expected go-between to Andron Gant, an Undercity merchant suspected of collaborating with an unknown external faction.",al={"what is astor's letter","astor letter of introduction","what is this letter"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Procuring and utilizing Astor's letter is a foundational field exercise for Forsaken rogues seeking entry into the Deathstalkers, testing tradecraft in assassination, theft, and impersonation.",["race:Undead"]="The scheme surrounding the letter highlights the internal paranoia within the Undercity, where Lord Varimathras uses the Deathstalkers to root out subversion among the Forsaken populace."},kw={"andron gant","apothecarium","astor hadren","deathstalkers","mennet carkad","silverpine forest","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1886","npc:andron-gant","npc:varimathras","subzone:rogues-quarter","subzone:apothecarium","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity"},src={"Astor's Letter of Introduction","The Deathstalkers","The Deathstalkers (2)"}}
E["item:balnir-snapdragons"] = {t="item",n="Balnir Snapdragons",z="undercity",s="Balnir Snapdragons are vibrant flowers cultivated at the Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades. Naturally receptive to magical currents, they serve the Forsaken as delicate indicators for detecting the creep of Scourge corruption from the bordering Plaguelands.",h="Balnir Snapdragons are vibrant flowers cultivated at the Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Bloom in Ruin",b="Originally tended by Vara Balnir before the fall of Lordaeron, these colorful blooms miraculously endured the death of the Balnir family and the rise of the Scourge. Even when Prince Arthas returned to the desecrated homestead to raise his steed Invincible, the snapdragons remained in full flower, untainted by the rot claiming the surrounding kingdom. Their enduring vitality against dark magic makes them a striking landmark amid the decay of Tirisfal Glades.",sp=0},{t="Magical Barometers",b="Because snapdragons are unusually sensitive to atmospheric magic, they act as living barometers for magical blights. Anastasia Hartwell and the Forsaken mages in the Undercity seek fresh specimens from the farmstead's window boxes. By turning the plants over to the Royal Apothecary Society, the Undercity hopes to analyze the flora and measure how deeply the Lich King's plague has seeped across the border into Tirisfal's soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Balnir Snapdragons be found?",a="They grow in flower boxes and garden beds around the ruined Balnir Farmstead, located in the eastern reaches of Tirisfal Glades near the border of the Western Plaguelands.",al={"balnir snapdragons location","where are the flowers","balnir flower location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell want these snapdragons?",a="Snapdragons readily absorb latent magical energies. Anastasia Hartwell wants fresh specimens delivered to Undercity apothecaries to measure whether the magical taint of the Plaguelands is actively spreading into Tirisfal Glades.",al={"why collect snapdragons","balnir farmstead quest goal","anastasia hartwell snapdragons"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who originally grew these flowers?",a="They were the pride and joy of Vara Balnir, who cultivated them at her family's farm before the third war wiped out Lordaeron's rural settlements.",al={"who planted balnir snapdragons","vara balnir flowers","balnir family snapdragons"},it="origin"},{q="Did the Scourge destroy the Balnir flowers?",a="No. Remarkably, the snapdragons stayed in full bloom even after the Balnirs were slain. Arthas noted their survival when he returned to the homestead to raise his horse Invincible, though he avoided touching them lest his deathly presence wither the petals.",al={"did plague kill snapdragons","arthas balnir flowers"},it="history"},{q="What are Balnir Snapdragons?",a="Balnir Snapdragons are a distinctive breed of flower grown in the garden boxes of the Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades. Naturally sensitive and exceptionally receptive to magical energies, they absorb latent magical currents from their surroundings, making them prime indicators for detecting nearby environmental corruption.",al={"what is balnir snapdragons","balnir snapdragon flower","balnir snapdragons lore"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Forsaken mages study Balnir Snapdragons as raw magical conduits, utilizing their natural sensitivity to quantify how magical blights distort ambient leylines.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the flowers provide practical surveillance on their eastern border, warning Undercity researchers if the Lich King's corruption is overtaking Tirisfal's soil."},kw={"anastasia hartwell","balnir farmstead","balnir snapdragons","invincible","mage quarter","plaguelands","tirisfal glades","vara balnir"},rel={"subzone:balnir-farmstead","quest:1882","npc:anastasia-hartwell","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity","subzone:mage-quarter","topic:forsaken","topic:lich-king"},src={"Balnir Snapdragons","The Balnir Farmstead"}}
E["item:berard-s-journal"] = {t="item",n="Berard's Journal",z="undercity",s="Berard's Journal is a collection of research notes penned by Apothecary Berard before he fell victim to Archmage Arugal's curse. Left behind in Pyrewood Village, the book documents Berard's study of an ancient plague that once wiped out the aquatic life of Lake Lordamere, making it highly valuable to the Royal Apothecary Society.",h="Berard's Journal is a collection of research notes penned by Apothecary Berard before he fell victim to...",sec={{t="Lost Research of Lake Lordamere",b="Before Archmage Arugal unleashed his shadow magic across Silverpine Forest, Apothecary Berard was considered one of the Royal Apothecary Society's most promising minds. Stationed in Pyrewood Village, he focused his work on an ancient, virulent blight that had eradicated all aquatic life within Lake Lordamere centuries prior. When Arugal's curse gripped the settlement, Berard's mind was shattered, turning him into another mindless thrall. His detailed field notes remained behind on a bookshelf in his quarters at the Pyrewood Village Inn.",sp=0},{t="Fuel for the New Plague",b="Though Berard himself was lost to the Society, his research survived intact. Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher recognizes the journal's strategic value and directs Forsaken agents into the hostile village to recover it. The gathered notes on the ancient lake toxin provide critical groundwork for Master Apothecary Faranell and the Society in the Apothecarium, serving as a vital foundation for concocting the Forsaken's own new plague.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Apothecary Berard?",a="Apothecary Berard was a gifted member of the Royal Apothecary Society living in Pyrewood Village. He was conducting vital research into historical toxins when Archmage Arugal cast his curse over the region, breaking Berard's mind and enslaving him.",al={"who is berard","berard lore","apothecary berard"},it="people"},{q="Where is Berard's Journal found?",a="The journal rests on a bookshelf in Berard's old study, located on the upper floor of the inn within Pyrewood Village, deep in southern Silverpine Forest.",al={"find berards journal","journal location","where is the book"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What research is recorded in the journal?",a="The journal details Berard's findings on a primordial contagion that completely wiped out all aquatic creatures in Lake Lordamere in ancient times. The Royal Apothecary Society hopes to adapt these toxic properties into their own chemical weapons.",al={"what is in the journal","berards research","journal contents"},it="power"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want the journal?",a="Renferrel seeks to reclaim any useful scientific assets before they are destroyed or lost forever. Berard's unique insights into the Lake Lordamere contagion provide crucial components needed by Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity to develop the Forsaken's new plague.",al={"why does renferrel want it","renferrel journal quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Berard's Journal?",a="Berard's Journal is a scientific research notebook compiled by Apothecary Berard, a former member of the Royal Apothecary Society. It contains his detailed findings regarding an ancient contagion that wiped out all aquatic life in Lake Lordamere long ago, which the Forsaken hope to study for their own alchemy.",al={"berard journal","what is berards journal","berards journal"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Berard's Journal come from, and who made it?",a="The journal was authored by Apothecary Berard prior to losing his mind to Archmage Arugal's shadow magic. He kept his study in the inn within Pyrewood Village, where the tome was left behind on a bookshelf after he became a mindless thrall.",al={"where is berards journal from","who wrote berard journal","berards journal origin"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every scrap of venomous lore helps the Royal Apothecary Society secure a weapon capable of defending the Forsaken against both the Scourge and living enemies.",["faction:Horde"]="Venturing into Pyrewood Village to reclaim lost research aids the Forsaken in establishing a firm defensive stronghold across Silverpine Forest."},kw={"apothecary berard","apothecary renferrel","berard's journal","lake lordamere","master apothecary faranell","pyrewood village","royal apothecary society","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:447","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:pyrewood-village","topic:royal-apothecary-society","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher"},src={"Berard's Journal","A Recipe For Death (2)"}}
E["item:cantation-of-manifestation"] = {t="item",n="Cantation of Manifestation",z="undercity",s="The Cantation of Manifestation is a specialized arcane incantation written on a parchment scroll, used by mages to reveal unseen magical anomalies. In the Undercity, Anastasia Hartwell provides it to apprentices investigating invisible magical entities haunting Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium.",h="The Cantation of Manifestation is a specialized arcane incantation written on a parchment scroll, used by...",sec={{t="Unveiling the Invisible",b="The Cantation of Manifestation holds a focused spell designed to pierce magical veils and force incorporeal, invisible beings into the visible spectrum. Kept in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity near Anastasia Hartwell, the scroll is entrusted to capable mages tasked with containing rogue magical anomalies. When read aloud in an area suffering from arcane instability—such as Algernon's alchemical workshop in the Apothecarium—the words force stray rift spawns to materialize, allowing the caster to subdue and trap them within containment coffers for further study.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Cantation of Manifestation do?",a="It is a magical scroll that casts a spell revealing invisible arcane anomalies. When recited in areas experiencing magical tears or disturbances, it forces unseen creatures—such as rift spawns—into plain sight so they can be fought and captured.",al={"what is cantation of manifestation","cantation purpose","how does cantation work"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Where can I find the Cantation in Undercity?",a="It rests on the floor directly behind the mage trainer Anastasia Hartwell, located in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"cantation location undercity","where is cantation of manifestation","find cantation undercity"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell need this scroll used?",a="A strange magical disturbance broke out in Algernon's alchemical shop down in the Apothecarium. Unseen entities made entirely of magic began wandering the premises, and Hartwell needs the scroll read on site to reveal and capture the creatures before the rift worsens.",al={"why use cantation","hartwell quest motive","anastasia disturbance"},it="motive"},{q="Do I get to keep the scroll after using it?",a="No. Once you have manifested the rift spawns and captured them in containment coffers, you must return the Cantation of Manifestation along with the coffers back to Anastasia Hartwell.",al={"keep cantation","do i lose cantation","return cantation"},gp=true},{q="What is the Cantation of Manifestation?",a="The Cantation of Manifestation is a specialized arcane scroll utilized by mages. When invoked, its incantation pierces magical concealment, forcing invisible entities woven purely of arcane energy to reveal themselves to the naked eye.",al={"what is cantation of manifestation","cantation of manifestation scroll","what does cantation do"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell want the Cantation of Manifestation?",a="Invisible magical creatures have appeared around Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium, signaling a rift in the flow of magic. Mage trainers need the cantation read so an apprentice can reveal and capture the entities for study, allowing Undercity's magi to determine whether this disturbance is an accident or an active magical attack.",al={"why want cantation","why need cantation of manifestation","why does anastasia want cantation"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The Cantation of Manifestation is an essential tool in your early training, teaching you how to detect hidden arcane currents and contain volatile rift entities.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken spellcasters in the Magic Quarter keep tight control over arcane fluctuations, ensuring magical rifts don't compromise the stability of the Undercity."},kw={"algernon","anastasia hartwell","apothecarium","cantation of manifestation","containment coffer","magic quarter","rift spawn","undercity"},rel={"npc:anastasia-hartwell","quest:1960","subzone:magic-quarter","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","topic:mage","item:chest-of-containment-coffers","item:filled-containment-coffer"},src={"Cantation of Manifestation","Investigate the Alchemist Shop"}}
E["item:chest-of-containment-coffers"] = {t="item",n="Chest of Containment Coffers",z="undercity",s="The Chest of Containment Coffers contains enchanted receptacles used by mages to capture unstable magical phenomena. It serves as essential equipment for practitioners sent to investigate and safely trap unseen mana anomalies.",h="The Chest of Containment Coffers contains enchanted receptacles used by mages to capture unstable magical...",sec={{t="Vessels for the Unseen",b="Magical experimentation and sudden planar rifts frequently spawn volatile, invisible anomalies made entirely of arcane force. Standard physical cages cannot hold entities composed purely of magic. The Chest of Containment Coffers provides mages with specialized, enchanted coffers engineered to entrap and bind these subdued creatures alive. Kept near senior instructors such as Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity and Jennea Cannon in Stormwind, the chest provides the necessary gear for initiates tasked with surveying anomalies before they can destabilize their surroundings.",sp=0},{t="Arcane Containment Protocols",b="When invisible disturbances manifested within Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium, Forsaken instructors dispatched mages equipped with these coffers to contain the incident. Capturing a rift entity requires revealing it with a specialized scroll, weakening its form through spellcasting, and trapping it within one of the coffers taken from this chest. The filled receptacles allow the Magus Senate and Forsaken researchers to safely dissect, study, and determine whether such disturbances are random tears in the Ley or deliberate arcane assaults.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Chest of Containment Coffers?",a="The chest holds specialized, empty containment coffers. Mages draw these vessels to secure and trap subdued, magical creatures such as rift spawns during hazardous field investigations.",al={"what does the chest give","containment coffers contents","chest contents"},it="item"},{q="Where can this chest be found?",a="In the Undercity, it sits directly behind Mage Trainer Anastasia Hartwell in the Magic Quarter. A matching chest can also be found in Stormwind City behind Jennea Cannon in the Wizard's Sanctum.",al={"chest of containment coffers location","where is containment coffers chest","coffer chest location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do mages need these coffers instead of normal cages?",a="The creatures being investigated are rift spawns made purely of intangible arcane energy. Normal materials cannot hold them; only magically enchanted containment coffers can physically trap and stabilize an arcane anomaly.",al={"why use coffers","what are coffers for","how do coffers work"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens to the coffers once they are filled?",a="Filled coffers are handed over to senior instructors for study. The captured creatures are analyzed to discover whether an arcane disturbance was an accidental natural rift or an intentional attack by outside forces.",al={"what happens to captured rift spawns","filled containment coffer use","why capture creatures"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Chest of Containment Coffers?",a="It is a heavy supply chest kept by mage instructors to outfit practitioners investigating magical anomalies. Inside rests a set of enchanted containment coffers specially constructed to bind and hold erratic, non-physical beings composed purely of arcane energy.",al={"what is chest of containment coffers","chest of containment coffers","chest of coffers"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell want you to take the Chest of Containment Coffers?",a="Anastasia Hartwell has detected invisible magical entities wandering Algernon's alchemist shop in the Apothecarium. Ordinary restraints cannot touch creatures woven entirely of raw magic, so she provides you with this chest of specially prepared coffers to capture the anomalies alive for study.",al={"why take the chest of containment coffers","why do i need containment coffers","why anastasia chest of coffers"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The chest provides essential field tools for mages learning to manage volatile arcane manifestations and preserve living specimens for study.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken mages use these coffers to secure magical anomalies appearing near the Apothecarium without letting unvetted arcane forces corrupt their work."},kw={"anastasia hartwell","apothecarium","arcane anomaly","containment coffer","magic quarter","rift spawn"},rel={"quest:1960","npc:anastasia-hartwell","item:filled-containment-coffer","item:cantation-of-manifestation","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","npc:jennea-cannon","topic:mage"},src={"Chest of Containment Coffers","Investigate the Alchemist Shop"}}
E["item:comar-s-heart"] = {t="item",n="Comar's Heart",z="undercity",s="Comar's Heart is a macabre ritual component carved from Comar Villard, a faithful human wanderer searching the marshes of the Wetlands for his lost wife. Forsaken warlocks in the Undercity seek out this relic of pure devotion to feed the summoning rites of a succubus.",h="Comar's Heart is a macabre ritual component carved from Comar Villard, a faithful human wanderer searching...",sec={{t="A Beacon of Purity",b="To bind a creature as capricious and predatory as a succubus, warlocks must bait the demon with true purity and devotion. Carendin Halgar's disciples in the Undercity identify Comar Villard as one of the few men possessing such unblemished fidelity. While his wife was lost amidst the turmoil sweeping the Eastern Kingdoms, Comar stubbornly wanders the sodden roads of the Wetlands, refusing to abandon his search. It is precisely this unwavering love that marks him for slaughter, turning his still-beating heart into the ideal lure for a demonic servant.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Seduction",b="Procuring the heart requires Forsaken apprentices to venture far south through contested territories, past the Thandol Span and deep into Alliance-dominated marshes. Carried back to the Temple of the Damned alongside Dalin's Heart, the organ looks utterly mundane despite the profound goodness that once drove it. Yet to the senses of the Nether, the residual virtue radiating from Comar's flesh is intoxicating bait, strong enough to draw a succubus across the dimensional veil into the warlock's thrall.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Comar Villard?",a="Comar Villard was a devoted human searching the dangerous Wetlands for any trace of his missing wife. His unending love and steadfast refusal to give up hope made him renowned as a truly pure-hearted man.",al={"who is comar","comar villard lore","why kill comar"},it="identity"},{q="Why do warlocks need Comar's Heart?",a="Warlocks of the Undercity require the heart of a completely pure and honorable mortal to lure and bind a succubus. The demon is naturally drawn to corrupt and feast upon genuine virtue, making Comar's unwavering devotion irresistible bait.",al={"why need comar heart","what is comars heart for","succubus heart lore"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Comar Villard found?",a="He wanders along the main road in the northern Wetlands, just south of the Thandol Span that bridges Arathi Highlands and Khaz Modan.",al={"comar villard location","where is comar","how to find comar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sends warlocks to collect the heart?",a="The task is assigned by the warlock trainers in the Undercity, directed by Carendin Halgar within the Temple of the Damned, as part of an apprentice's ritual training to summon a succubus.",al={"who wants comar heart","who gives hearts of the pure","carendin halgar heart"},it="motive"},{q="What is Comar's Heart?",a="Comar's Heart is the literal heart carved from Comar Villard, a faithful human wanderer in the Wetlands. Warlocks prize it as a rare specimen of untainted virtue, steeped in fidelity and enduring love.",al={"what is comars heart","comar heart item","comar's heart lore"},it="item",add=true},{q="Where does Comar's Heart come from?",a="It is taken directly from the chest of Comar Villard, a man searching the treacherous marshes of the Wetlands for any trace of his lost wife. It is not an artifact forged by sorcery, but a mortal organ whose pure devotion makes it a potent ritual reagent.",al={"where does comars heart come from","who made comars heart","origin of comars heart"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Taking Comar's Heart demonstrates the cold, pragmatic cruelty of demonology: unblemished mortal virtue is merely bait used to lure a succubus into your servitude.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, harvesting the heart of a loyal human lover highlights the total emotional severance between the living and the undead in Lordaeron."},kw={"carendin halgar","comar villard","comar's heart","hearts of the pure","succubus","temple of the damned","undercity","wetlands"},rel={"quest:1476","item:dalin-s-heart","npc:carendin-halgar","zone:wetlands","subzone:thandol-span","zone:arathi"},src={"Comar's Heart","Hearts of the Pure"}}
E["item:daggerspine-scale"] = {t="item",n="Daggerspine Scale",z="undercity",s="A Daggerspine Scale is a tough reptilian scale harvested from the Daggerspine naga prowling the southern shores of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Sought after by the Royal Apothecary Society, these scales serve as a crucial catalyst to activate virulent brews in the Forsaken's ongoing plague experiments.",h="A Daggerspine Scale is a tough reptilian scale harvested from the Daggerspine naga prowling the southern...",sec={{t="Apothecary Research",b="The Royal Apothecary Society constantly seeks biological reagents to enhance their toxins, plagues, and concoctions. When refining the experimental brew known as the Elixir of Agony, the apothecaries discovered that scales taken from the local Daggerspine naga possessed unique reactive properties. When combined with troll regenerative elixirs and murloc organs, the scales help chemically activate dormant contaminating agents suspended in raw mixtures. Procuring them requires hunting along the rocky coastline east of Southshore, braving both the vicious naga tribe and nearby Alliance forces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Daggerspine Scales used for?",a="They are gathered for Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill as part of the research into the Elixir of Agony. When combined with other reagents, the scales activate the contaminating properties of an alchemical mudsnout mixture.",al={"daggerspine scale use","why get daggerspine scales","what do daggerspine scales do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do these scales come from?",a="They are stripped from Daggerspine naga—including shorestalkers, shorehunters, screamers, sirens, and their leader Lady Zephris—who inhabit the coastline of Hillsbrad Foothills directly east of the human settlement of Southshore.",al={"where to find daggerspine scales","who drops daggerspine scales","daggerspine scale location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want naga scales?",a="The Society's apothecaries determined that the resilient scales of the Daggerspine tribe carry the exact chemical properties needed to trigger specific infectious agents within their experimental blight and disease concoctions.",al={"why naga scales","apothecary naga scales"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Daggerspine Scale?",a="A Daggerspine Scale is a tough, aquatic scale harvested from the Daggerspine naga prowling the coast of Hillsbrad Foothills. These serpent-like creatures possess unique biological properties that make their shed and harvested scales prized reagents for the sinister concoctions of the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"what are daggerspine scales","daggerspine scale item","about daggerspine scale"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Procuring these scales directly advances the Royal Apothecary Society's research to develop devastating new plagues against the enemies of the Forsaken.",["faction:Horde"]="Gathering scales along the southern shore requires careful navigation, as the Daggerspine encampments sit dangerously close to the Alliance port of Southshore."},kw={"daggerspine","daggerspine scale","elixir of agony","hillsbrad","lydon","naga","royal apothecary society","undercity"},rel={"quest:509","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:naga","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","item:mudsnout-mixture","item:torn-fin-eye","npc:umpi"},src={"Daggerspine Scale","Elixir of Agony (3)"}}
E["item:dalaran-mana-gem"] = {t="item",n="Dalaran Mana Gem",z="undercity",s="Dalaran Mana Gems are crystallized arcane reserves carried by Kirin Tor personnel operating in Silverpine Forest. Forsaken spellcasters covet these gems as potent raw components for crafting enchanted vestments like spellfire robes.",h="Dalaran Mana Gems are crystallized arcane reserves carried by Kirin Tor personnel operating in Silverpine...",sec={{t="Stolen Arcana",b="The mages, conjurors, and guards of the Kirin Tor stationed around Ambermill in Silverpine Forest carry specialized mana gems to focus and replenish their arcane energies. For the Forsaken practitioners in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, these crystalline conduits represent an accessible source of concentrated magical essence. Although some undead mages acknowledge a shared academic heritage with Dalaran, pragmatic necessity and a philosophy of survival dictate that unyielding rivals are fair game to be stripped of their magical resources.",sp=0},{t="Weaving the Spellfire",b="When harvested from fallen Kirin Tor operatives, these gems are brought to tailors like Josef Gregorian in the Undercity alongside bundles of simple linen. While ordinary craftsmen cannot directly channel arcane power, skilled tailors can bind the mana gems into the weave of the cloth. This infusion transforms common thread into enchanted garments capable of bolstering a fledgling spellcaster's connection to the arcane.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Dalaran Mana Gems come from?",a="They are carried by Kirin Tor forces stationed in Silverpine Forest, particularly around the Dalaran encampments and outposts near Ambermill, southeast of the Sepulcher.",al={"where to farm mana gems","dalaran gem drop","who drops mana gems"},it="origin"},{q="What are these gems used for?",a="Forsaken mages use them as essential enchanting components. Brought alongside linen to Josef Gregorian in the Undercity, they provide the magical charge required to weave spellfire robes.",al={"mana gem purpose","why do i need dalaran mana gems"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the Kirin Tor in Silverpine carrying these gems?",a="Members of the Kirin Tor use mana gems as personal reservoirs of arcane power to sustain their spellcasting, defense wards, and conjurations in hostile territories like Silverpine Forest.",al={"why do dalaran wizards have gems","kirin tor mana gems lore"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken target Dalaran mages for these gems?",a="While the Forsaken share academic roots with Dalaran's magical tradition, they view their living counterparts as rivals. Undercity mentors consider any mage who cannot defend their arcane wealth too weak to survive, justifying the harvest of their components.",al={"forsaken vs dalaran mages","why kill dalaran for robes"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Dalaran Mana Gem?",a="A Dalaran Mana Gem is a magically charged stone carried by the Kirin Tor operatives stationed in Silverpine Forest. Imbued with arcane energy, these crystals are essential components for crafting enchanted garments, such as the spellfire robes sewn by Forsaken tailors in the Undercity.",al={"what is dalaran mana gem","dalaran mana gem","mana gem silverpine"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Apprentice Forsaken mages are dispatched to harvest these gems as a rite of passage, proving both their martial competence and their mastery over harvested arcane sources.",["race:Undead"]="The harvest highlights the cold pragmatism of the Forsaken, who discard sentimentality toward former human colleagues in Dalaran to fuel their own faction's survival."},kw={"ambermill","dalaran mana gem","josef gregorian","kirin tor","linen","mana gem","silverpine forest","spellfire robes"},rel={"quest:1961","quest:1962","npc:josef-gregorian","subzone:ambermill","subzone:magic-quarter","subzone:dalaran","zone:silverpine","topic:mage"},src={"Dalaran Mana Gem","Gathering Materials (Horde)"}}
E["item:dalaran-status-report"] = {t="item",n="Dalaran Status Report",z="undercity",s="The Dalaran Status Report is a cache of sensitive intelligence compiled by the Kirin Tor wizards stationed at Ambermill in Silverpine Forest. It details the secretive ongoing reconstruction behind Dalaran's glowing protective dome, making it a prized prize for the Forsaken and the Deathstalkers of Undercity.",h="The Dalaran Status Report is a cache of sensitive intelligence compiled by the Kirin Tor wizards stationed at...",sec={{t="Eyes Behind the Violet Shield",b="Ever since the Scourge sacked Dalaran and Archimonde brought down its towering spires, the ruined city-state has remained sealed off behind an impenetrable purple energy shield. Outside that barrier, the surviving magi of the Kirin Tor have established forward enclaves, most notably Ambermill in southeastern Silverpine Forest. From this fortified settlement, the mages coordinate logistics, guard surrounding roads, and communicate with those laboring within the dome. The Dalaran Status Report represents their localized assessments, troop distributions, and records on the reconstruction efforts underway behind the violet ward.",sp=0},{t="A Deathstalker's Test",b="Control of Lordaeron requires absolute vigilance, and Lord Varimathras keeps a keen eye on any remnants of the Alliance and Kirin Tor. After Forsaken interrogators squeezed admissions from a Kirin Tor captive, the dreadlord ordered the Deathstalkers to acquire the status report. Hidden away within a locked strongbox deep inside Ambermill, the document became both an operational necessity and a rite of passage for newly initiated rogues mastering the craft of lockpicking under Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Dalaran Status Report?",a="It is a set of confidential Kirin Tor documents outlining the current conditions, recovery operations, and status of Dalaran, compiled by the mages maintaining the outpost of Ambermill.",al={"what is this report","dalaran report","ambermill documents"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the report kept?",a="The mages of Ambermill locked the report inside a strongbox within their settlement in southeastern Silverpine Forest, keeping it protected from intruders and curious eyes.",al={"where is the report","ambermill strongbox location","how to find the status report"},it="place"},{q="Why does the Undercity want this report?",a="Lord Varimathras and the Forsaken consider the surviving Kirin Tor an active threat on their doorstep. Recovering the report allows the Deathstalkers to assess Dalaran's military strength and secret reconstruction projects.",al={"why do forsaken want this","varimathras dalaran report","deathstalkers objective"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How did the Deathstalkers learn about the document?",a="The Deathstalkers extracted the document's existence and location directly from a captured Kirin Tor prisoner held and questioned in the Undercity.",al={"how did undercity find out","prisoner confession"},it="history"},{q="Where does the Dalaran Status Report come from, and who made it?",a="The report was drafted by the Kirin Tor wizards stationed at Ambermill in southern Silverpine Forest. Following the devastation of Dalaran during the Third War, the surviving mages maintain outposts throughout the surrounding regions to monitor their fallen city, document ongoing affairs, and coordinate their remaining forces.",al={"who wrote dalaran status report","dalaran status report origin","who made dalaran status report"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Mennet Carkad uses the retrieval of this report as a field test for training Deathstalkers in the delicate craft of lockpicking and infiltration against vigilant mages.",["race:Undead"]="The Kirin Tor remnants at Ambermill are a thorn in the side of the Forsaken in Silverpine, making any intelligence on their operations vital to Undercity's security."},kw={"ambermill","ambermill strongbox","dalaran status report","deathstalkers","kirin tor","mennet carkad","tools of the trade","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1999","subzone:ambermill","quest:1886","subzone:dalaran","npc:varimathras","zone:silverpine","subzone:rogues-quarter","topic:rogue"},src={"Dalaran Status Report","Tools of the Trade (Classic)"}}
E["item:dalin-s-heart"] = {t="item",n="Dalin's Heart",z="undercity",s="Dalin's Heart is a macabre ritual component carved from Dalin Forgewright, an honorable man patrolling near the Greymane Wall in Silverpine Forest. Undercity warlocks seek it out as an offering of unblemished purity, intended to lure and bind a succubus to their service.",h="Dalin's Heart is a macabre ritual component carved from Dalin Forgewright, an honorable man patrolling near...",sec={{t="A Pure Heart for Dark Arts",b="To summon and subjugate a succubus, Undercity warlocks require rare bait: the physical hearts of truly virtuous mortals. Dalin Forgewright earned his dark fate through selfless devotion, spending his days defending desperate Lordaeron refugees barred from safety at the sealed Greymane Wall. His unstinting altruism marks him as an emblem of goodness in a fallen land, making his heart an irresistible prize for demonic seduction rites conducted within the Temple of the Damned.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Dalin Forgewright?",a="Dalin Forgewright was an honorable human who dedicated his life to protecting Lordaeron refugees stranded outside the closed gates of the Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine Forest.",al={"dalin forgewright","who is dalin","dalin lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why do warlocks need Dalin's Heart?",a="Warlock summoners in the Undercity require the heart of a genuinely pure and honorable man as a ritual lure to attract and dominate a succubus.",al={"why dalin heart","purpose of dalins heart","why do warlocks want dalin's heart"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who accepts Dalin's Heart?",a="The heart is brought to Carendin Halgar, a warlock trainer located in the Temple of the Damned within the Undercity.",al={"who takes the heart","dalin heart turn in","where to bring dalins heart"},it="target"},{q="What other component is needed alongside this heart?",a="Carendin Halgar requires both Dalin's Heart and Comar's Heart, belonging to Comar Villard, a faithful widower wandering the Wetlands.",al={"hearts of the pure other heart","other heart needed","second heart"}},{q="What is Dalin's Heart?",a="It is the literal, physical heart cut from Dalin Forgewright, an honorable man tending to Lordaeron refugees near the Greymane Wall in Silverpine Forest. Though physically indistinguishable from any other human heart, it possesses the distinct spiritual purity of a selfless and virtuous soul.",al={"what is dalins heart","dalins heart description","dalin heart item"},it="item",add=true},{q="Where does Dalin's Heart come from?",a="The heart comes from Dalin Forgewright, a virtuous man found mounted on horseback patrolling the southern road of Silverpine Forest near the closed Greymane Wall. A warlock must track him down and slay him to claim the organ directly from his corpse.",al={"where do you get dalins heart","dalins heart origin","who drops dalins heart"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Procuring this heart is an essential rite of passage for Forsaken warlocks learning to ensnare a succubus, proving their willingness to harvest untainted virtue for demonic mastery.",["race:Undead"]="The hunt for Dalin's heart highlights the bitter reality of post-Scourge Lordaeron, where remaining living human altruists outside the Greymane Wall become prey for the Forsaken."},kw={"carendin halgar","dalin forgewright","dalin's heart","greymane wall","hearts of the pure","silverpine forest","succubus","undercity"},rel={"quest:1476","item:comar-s-heart","npc:carendin-halgar","subzone:greymane-wall","zone:silverpine","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Dalin's Heart","Hearts of the Pure"}}
E["item:darthalia-s-sealed-commendation"] = {t="item",n="Darthalia's Sealed Commendation",z="undercity",s="Darthalia's Sealed Commendation is an official dispatch penned by the Forsaken battle commander in Tarren Mill. It praises a soldier's relentless campaign against the humans of Hillsbrad and delivers word of those victories directly to Undercity's high command.",h="Darthalia's Sealed Commendation is an official dispatch penned by the Forsaken battle commander in Tarren...",sec={{t="Report to High Command",b="Following the brutal clashes across the Hillsbrad Foothills, High Executor Darthalia drafted this sealed dispatch to officially record the fall of Southshore's leadership and the devastation wrought upon human positions. Sealed to preserve the commander's appraisal from prying eyes, the document is addressed to Varimathras, dreadlord advisor to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. For the Forsaken leadership in the Royal Quarter, such missives offer tangible proof that Alliance enclaves south of Lordaeron can be broken, freeing northern garrisons to focus on the relentless threat of the Scourge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Darthalia's Sealed Commendation?",a="It is an official war commendation written by High Executor Darthalia of Tarren Mill. The document formally commends a fighter's combat performance against the Alliance during the Battle of Hillsbrad and is meant for the high command in the Undercity.",al={"sealed commendation","darthalia letter","hillsbrad report"},it="identity"},{q="Who receives this commendation?",a="The commendation must be brought directly to the dreadlord Varimathras, who oversees military operations beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"who do i bring this to","commendation turn in","who gets darthalia's commendation"},it="target"},{q="Why does Varimathras care about the fighting in Hillsbrad?",a="Although the Forsaken consider the Lich King and his Scourge to be their foremost existential threat from the north, human presence in Hillsbrad constantly interrupts their supply lines and southern border security. Varimathras values battlefield victories that remove the human obstacle, allowing Undercity's forces to focus on the greater war.",al={"why varimathras cares","hillsbrad dreadlord","forsaken strategy hillsbrad"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Darthalia's Sealed Commendation come from, and who made it?",a="This letter is written and sealed by Darthalia, a Forsaken commander coordinating Horde forces in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Recognizing your valor and relentless perseverance during the bitter campaign against Southshore and its Alliance defenders, she penned this official dispatch to personally praise your battlefield accomplishments to the high command.",al={"who wrote darthalia commendation","where did darthalia commendation come from","who gave sealed commendation"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Varimathras want Darthalia's Sealed Commendation?",a="Darthalia sends the document directly to Varimathras in the Undercity so the Forsaken leadership takes note of your deadly effectiveness. While the dreadlord views the Scourge to the north as the primary threat, Alliance humans in Hillsbrad disrupt their broader strategic plans. This commendation formally proves that decisive strikes against human settlements can succeed under capable field champions like you.",al={"why deliver sealed commendation","why does varimathras want commendation","purpose of darthalias commendation"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The commendation marks a crucial strategic victory in Lordaeron, demonstrating to Undercity's leadership that the Alliance's fortified toeholds in the southern foothills can be systematically dismantled.",["race:Undead"]="Earning high praise from Darthalia and presenting it directly to the throne room elevates a soldier's standing within the Dark Lady's burgeoning military hierarchy."},kw={"commendation","darthalia","hillsbrad","southshore","tarren mill","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:527","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","npc:varimathras","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:human","topic:lich-king"},src={"Darthalia's Sealed Commendation","Battle of Hillsbrad (7) (Classic)"}}
E["item:egalin-s-grimoire"] = {t="item",n="Egalin's Grimoire",z="undercity",s="Egalin's Grimoire is a prized arcane tome detailing the foundational rites required to summon and command a voidwalker. Penned by a master warlock, it serves as an essential teaching text within the Undercity's Temple of the Damned.",h="Egalin's Grimoire is a prized arcane tome detailing the foundational rites required to summon and command a...",sec={{t="A Master's Work",b="Written by the master summoner Egalin, this grimoire details the delicate and dangerous process of pulling a being of chaos from the Nether. Egalin was renowned among practitioners for his effortless command over summoned voidwalkers, an ability passed down to his students, including Carendin Halgar. Without the specific formulas and channeling methods recorded in the text, an unprepared summoner risks being torn apart by the very entity they call forth.",sp=0},{t="The Scarlet Theft",b="The grimoire was stolen from the Forsaken warlocks by an operative of the Scarlet Crusade named Perrine, who stashed it in a chest within a tower along western Tirisfal Glades. Despite the zealots' hatred of dark magic, the thief seemed largely ignorant of the book's true significance, treating it as little more than seized heretical salvage until retrieved by Forsaken initiates seeking to master the void.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Egalin?",a="Egalin was an exceptionally talented warlock and the mentor of Carendin Halgar. He is remembered for being the first among them to summon a voidwalker and for commanding chaotic entities with absolute ease.",al={"who is egalin","egalin lore","who wrote the grimoire"},it="people"},{q="Why is Egalin's Grimoire so dangerous?",a="The book contains the incantations and channeling methods needed to summon a voidwalker. If a warlock attempts the ritual without properly mastering these instructions, the summoned void entity will tear them apart.",al={"what does the grimoire do","voidwalker tome danger","why dangerous"},it="danger"},{q="How did the Scarlet Crusade get the book?",a="A Scarlet Crusade agent named Perrine managed to steal the tome from the Forsaken warlocks. He locked it away inside a chest at a Crusade watchtower in western Tirisfal Glades, seemingly unaware of its true magical worth.",al={"who stole the book","perrine grimoire","why do crusaders have it"},it="history"},{q="Who needs this grimoire returned?",a="Carendin Halgar, the warlock trainer residing in the Temple of the Damned beneath the Undercity, requires the grimoire to teach new initiates how to summon and bind voidwalkers.",al={"who wants the grimoire","who turns in egalin grimoire","carendin halgar book"},it="target"},{q="What is Egalin's Grimoire?",a="Egalin's Grimoire is a musty, specialized spellbook containing the secrets of calling upon beings from the chaos beyond. Specifically, it details the intricate process and spell structure required to summon and bind a voidwalker—a creature capable of tearing an unprepared summoner apart.",al={"what is egalins grimoire","egalin book","what is the grimoire"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Egalin's Grimoire come from, and who made it?",a="The tome was penned by Egalin, a master warlock celebrated among practitioners in the Undercity as the first to summon a voidwalker. Egalin taught other prominent warlocks, including Carendin Halgar, who revered his mentor's effortless command over summoned horrors.",al={"who wrote egalins grimoire","egalin book origin","who made egalins grimoire"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why is Egalin's Grimoire wanted?",a="The warlocks in the Temple of the Damned require the grimoire to instruct aspiring practitioners in summoning voidwalkers. After a Scarlet Crusade operative named Perrine stole it and hid it in a nearby tower, recovering the text became critical to keep its dangerous rituals out of enemy hands and return vital knowledge to the Forsaken.",al={"why do they want egalins grimoire","who wants the grimoire","why recover egalin book"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Egalin's Grimoire contains the precise techniques needed to pull a voidwalker from the Nether and bind it to your will, a crucial rite of passage for any practitioner.",["race:Undead"]="Recovering the book denies the fanatic Scarlet Crusade possession of a powerful magical artifact stolen directly from the Undercity's practitioners."},kw={"carendin halgar","creature of the void","egalin","egalin's grimoire","perrine","temple of the damned","voidwalker"},rel={"quest:1473","npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1471","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:undercity","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Egalin's Grimoire","Creature of the Void (Undercity)"}}
E["item:fenwick-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Fenwick's Head",z="undercity",s="Fenwick's Head is the grisly proof of execution taken from Fenwick Thatros on the shores of Lordamere Lake. It is claimed by Forsaken rogues operating on direct orders passed down through Lord Varimathras.",h="Fenwick's Head is the grisly proof of execution taken from Fenwick Thatros on the shores of Lordamere Lake.",sec={{t="A Contract from the Shadows",b="Within the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity, Mennet Carkad acts on urgent intelligence routed directly from dreadlord Varimathras. A hostile undead leader named Fenwick Thatros has established a foothold near the decaying docks along Lordamere Lake in Silverpine Forest. To prevent this threat from rallying hostile undead against the Forsaken, Carkad dispatches promising Deathstalkers to locate Thatros, eliminate him, and sever his head as undeniable proof of the kill.",sp=0},{t="A Rite of Passage",b="Returning Fenwick's Head to Carkad is more than a simple bounty collection; it serves as a crucial trial for Deathstalker operatives. Presenting the severed trophy validates the rogue's competence in infiltration and assassination, opening the door to deeper, more specialized instruction in the shadow arts from the Forsaken masters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Fenwick Thatros?",a="Fenwick Thatros was identified by Lord Varimathras as an undead leader entrenched in Silverpine Forest. His presence near the decrepit docks of Lordamere Lake marked him as an immediate danger to Forsaken interests in the region.",al={"who is fenwick","fenwick thatros lore","who was thatros"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Fenwick's Head?",a="The head is demanded by Mennet Carkad, a Deathstalker trainer residing in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity, fulfilling an urgent order passed down by Lord Varimathras.",al={"who wants the head","who turned in to","mennet carkad"},it="target"},{q="Where is Fenwick Thatros located?",a="According to intelligence gathered by Deathstalker scouts, Fenwick Thatros lurks by the decrepit docks along the shore of Lordamere Lake in Silverpine Forest.",al={"fenwick thatros location","where is fenwick","find fenwick"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why must his head be severed?",a="Mennet Carkad requires undeniable physical proof that the threat has been thoroughly eliminated before he will advance an operative to advanced shadow training.",al={"why take his head","why decapitate him"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does Fenwick's Head come from?",a="This severed head is taken from Fenwick Thatros, an undead leader encountered near the decaying docks along the shores of Lordamere Lake in Silverpine Forest. It is not an crafted object, but the grim remains of an enemy commander claimed in the field.",al={"fenwicks head origin","where do you get fenwicks head","who had fenwicks head"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Claiming Fenwick's Head is a definitive milestone for rising Forsaken rogues, establishing their reliability as Deathstalkers and earning them access to advanced training.",["race:Undead"]="The hunt demonstrates the Forsaken's ruthless suppression of rival undead factions contesting control over Silverpine Forest and the shores of Lordamere Lake."},kw={"deathstalkers","fenwick","lordamere","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","silverpine","thatros","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1998","quest:1999","npc:varimathras","quest:1886","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity","topic:rogue"},src={"Fenwick's Head","Fenwick Thatros (quest)"}}
E["item:filled-containment-coffer"] = {t="item",n="Filled Containment Coffer",z="undercity",s="A Filled Containment Coffer is an enchanted receptacle used by Forsaken spellcasters to trap erratic magical entities. By deploying a Cantation of Manifestation to reveal and weaken rift spawn in the Apothecarium, mages can trap the anomalies inside these reinforced boxes for safe examination.",h="A Filled Containment Coffer is an enchanted receptacle used by Forsaken spellcasters to trap erratic magical...",sec={{t="Trapping the Unseen",b="When unexplained magical disturbances manifested within Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium, the Forsaken mage Anastasia Hartwell commissioned practitioners of the arcane to capture the entities responsible. Because the rift creatures exist purely as living magical energy and wander unseen, ordinary cages are useless. Instead, spellcasters reveal the entities with a Cantation of Manifestation, defeat them in combat, and snap these specially prepared containment coffers shut around them. The sealed boxes shield the carrier from volatile magical backlashes while keeping the specimens intact for magical dissection.",sp=0},{t="Arcane Forensics",b="The presence of living mana creatures in the Undercity poses a serious threat. Once sealed into containment coffers, the captive beasts are transported back to Anastasia Hartwell and the city's scholars. The primary concern among the Forsaken mages is determining whether these intrusions are natural rifts in Azeroth's magical fabric or the preliminary probes of a calculated magical assault aimed at the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside a Filled Containment Coffer?",a="Each coffer holds a captured rift spawn, an invisible creature made purely of raw magical energy that manifested inside Algernon's alchemy shop in the Apothecarium.",al={"what is in the coffer","coffer contents","filled coffer monster"},it="item"},{q="How is a containment coffer filled?",a="A mage must read the Cantation of Manifestation to make the hidden creatures visible, defeat them in combat, and deploy an empty coffer to trap the remaining energy before it dissipates.",al={"how to fill coffer","how do i capture the rift spawn","filling coffer"},gp=true},{q="Who wants these filled coffers in Undercity?",a="Anastasia Hartwell, a prominent mage trainer in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, asks for these sealed coffers to investigate the disturbance threatening the city.",al={"who takes the coffers","coffer quest giver","anastasia hartwell coffer"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the Forsaken studying these creatures?",a="Undercity's scholars need to discover whether the anomaly was a random tears in the local flow of magic or a deliberate, coordinated attack by a rival hostile magical force.",al={"why study rift spawn","undercity rift reason"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Filled Containment Coffer?",a="A Filled Containment Coffer is an enchanted container used by mages to trap and hold volatile beings made purely of magical energy, such as rift spawns. Once the creature is forced into visibility and subdued, the coffer secures it safely for transportation and study without letting its magical essence disperse.",al={"what is filled containment coffer","filled containment coffer","containment coffer item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does a Filled Containment Coffer come from, and who made it?",a="The empty coffers are specialized arcane devices provided by mage instructors such as Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity. They become filled when an adept mage tracks down invisible magical entities—such as those lurking around Algernon's shop in the Apothecarium—forces them to manifest, weakens them, and seals them inside.",al={"who made containment coffer","origin of containment coffer","where do containment coffers come from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Forsaken apprentices handle these containment coffers as a practical lesson in abjuration, learning how to reveal hidden magical entities and bind unstable arcane energy into physical wards.",["race:Undead"]="The safety of the Apothecarium is paramount to the Forsaken, making the investigation and containment of any mysterious magical breach an urgent domestic priority."},kw={"algernon","anastasia hartwell","apothecarium","arcane disturbance","cantation of manifestation","containment coffer","filled containment coffer","rift spawn"},rel={"quest:1960","npc:anastasia-hartwell","item:cantation-of-manifestation","item:chest-of-containment-coffers","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","topic:mage"},src={"Filled Containment Coffer","Investigate the Alchemist Shop"}}
E["item:gordon-s-crate"] = {t="item",n="Gordon's Crate",z="undercity",s="Gordon's Crate is a heavy shipment of weapons packed in the Undercity for the Forsaken forces stationed in Silverpine Forest. It serves as an essential supply consignment meant to be ferried directly to the remote garrison at the Sepulcher.",h="Gordon's Crate is a heavy shipment of weapons packed in the Undercity for the Forsaken forces stationed in...",sec={{t="Supplies for Silverpine",b="Maintaining the Forsaken grip on Silverpine Forest requires a steady logistical flow from the Undercity. Gordon's Crate holds armaments intended to bolster Deathguard Podrig's defenders at the Sepulcher, ensuring outpost sentries are not caught off guard by the worgen, wild beasts, or human remnants lurking in the woods.",sp=0},{t="The Bat Handler's Route",b="Because overland roads out of the capital are dangerous and slow, valuable shipments rely on the Undercity's bat handlers. The crate is handed to Michael Garrett, the bat master perched above the city's trade quarter, who secures passage atop a trained flying bat back to Karos Razok's roost in the Sepulcher.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Gordon's Crate?",a="The crate contains weapons and vital combat supplies requisitioned from the Undercity to reinforce Deathguard sentries stationed in Silverpine Forest.",al={"contents of gordons crate","what does crate contain"},it="item"},{q="Who is supposed to receive Gordon's Crate?",a="Deathguard Podrig at the Sepulcher receives the crate. Transporting it requires coordinating with Undercity bat handler Michael Garrett to arrange a direct flight.",al={"who gets gordons crate","where does crate go"},it="target"},{q="Why is the crate transported by bat instead of a courier on foot?",a="Silverpine Forest remains contested and hazardous. Using trained bats overseen by handlers like Michael Garrett and Karos Razok ensures fast, aerial transit that avoids hostile threats along the ground routes.",al={"why fly the crate","bat travel crate"}},{q="Why does Michael Garrett require you to visit the Sepulcher first?",a="Forsaken bats instinctively return to the capital, but to reach outlying bases like the Sepulcher safely, travelers must establish a prior connection with the local handler, Karos Razok, before bats can make the journey.",al={"why need flight path","bat flight requirement"}},{q="What is Gordon's Crate?",a="Gordon's Crate is a shipment of vital weapons and military supplies packed in the Undercity. It is prepared specifically to be flown via bat handler to the remote Forsaken outpost at the Sepulcher.",al={"gordon's crate","what is this crate","gordons crate"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Gordon's Crate come from, and who made it?",a="The crate originates in the Undercity, where Gordon packed the garrison supplies into it before arranging for its delivery to the bat handlers.",al={"where did gordons crate come from","who packed gordons crate","who made gordons crate"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want Gordon's Crate?",a="Deathguard Podrig and the soldiers stationed at the Sepulcher desperately need the shipment. The crate contains weapons necessary to ensure the local Deathguards defending Silverpine Forest are well-armed and not caught unprepared against their enemies.",al={"why is gordons crate needed","why bring gordons crate to the sepulcher","who needs gordons crate"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every shipment of blades and gear from the capital solidifies Lady Sylvanas's tenuous frontier borders in Silverpine Forest.",["faction:Horde"]="The delivery demonstrates the growing integration of the Forsaken's flight routes, moving supplies and couriers swiftly across contested Lordaeron."},kw={"bat handler","deathguard podrig","gordon's crate","gordons crate","karos razok","michael garrett","silverpine supplies","the sepulcher","undercity"},rel={"quest:6322","quest:6324","zone:undercity","subzone:sepulcher","npc:karos-razok"},src={"Gordon's Crate","Michael Garrett (Classic)","Return to Podrig"}}
E["item:grizzled-bear-heart"] = {t="item",n="Grizzled Bear Heart",z="undercity",s="A Grizzled Bear Heart is a biological reagent harvested from the sturdy bears roaming Silverpine Forest. It serves as a vital component in the Royal Apothecary Society's grim research into the New Plague.",h="A Grizzled Bear Heart is a biological reagent harvested from the sturdy bears roaming Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Reagent for the New Plague",b="The Royal Apothecary Society works ceaselessly to develop an engineered blight capable of exterminating both the Scourge and living humanity. In the woodlands of Silverpine Forest, Apothecary Renferrel discovered that a unique toxin derived from the heart of a grizzled bear, when combined with arachnid ichor, yields a remarkably lethal concoction. Couriers and Forsaken loyalists hunt down ferocious grizzled bears, giant grizzled bears, and the infamous beast Old Vicejaw to carve out these organs and deliver them directly to Master Apothecary Faranell deep within the Apothecarium of the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Grizzled Bear Heart used for?",a="Grizzled Bear Hearts are harvested as experimental reagents for the Royal Apothecary Society. Apothecary Renferrel discovered that toxins derived from these hearts can be distilled into a lethal elixir as part of the Forsaken effort to brew the New Plague.",al={"what does bear heart do","bear heart quest","recipe for death reagents"},it="purpose"},{q="Who wants these bear hearts?",a="Apothecary Renferrel in Silverpine Forest directs travelers to gather the hearts alongside Skittering Blood and deliver them directly to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity's Apothecarium.",al={"who needs bear heart","faranell bear heart","who do i give bear heart to"},it="item"},{q="Where do Grizzled Bear Hearts come from?",a="They are carved from the various grizzled bears roaming Silverpine Forest, including ferocious grizzled bears, giant grizzled bears, and the formidable roaming beast Old Vicejaw.",al={"where do i find bear hearts","which bears drop heart","bear heart location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society need natural animal toxins?",a="The society seeks potent biological agents that can contaminate and destroy living flesh as well as undead physiology. The unique chemical properties found within the heart tissues of Silverpine's hearty bears provide an ideal reactive base when blended with virulent spider blood.",al={"why do apothecaries use bear venom","why animal hearts for plague"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Grizzled Bear Heart?",a="It is the fresh organ harvested from the ferocious grizzled bears that prowl Silverpine Forest. While a mundane organ at first glance, the heart contains a natural, resilient biological toxin that makes it an alluring reagent for alchemical experiments.",al={"what is grizzled bear heart","bear heart info","grizzled bear heart lore"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, harvesting these organs directly aids Master Apothecary Faranell in engineering the ultimate weapon against both Arthas's Scourge and the living mortals threatening Lordaeron.",["class:Hunter"]="Silverpine's massive bears are dangerous prey, and tracking beasts like Old Vicejaw for biological samples tests a huntsman's patience and field-dressing skill."},kw={"a recipe for death","apothecary renferrel","grizzled bear heart","master apothecary faranell","new plague","old vicejaw","royal apothecary society","silverpine forest","skittering blood"},rel={"quest:447","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","item:skittering-blood","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity"},src={"Grizzled Bear Heart","A Recipe For Death"}}
E["item:hardened-tumor"] = {t="item",n="Hardened Tumor",z="undercity",s="A Hardened Tumor is a rare biological anomaly harvested from the Vile Fin murlocs dwelling around Lake Lordamere. Noted originally in the research of the fallen Apothecary Berard, this calcified growth serves as an unusual reagent in the Royal Apothecary Society's efforts to brew the New Plague.",h="A Hardened Tumor is a rare biological anomaly harvested from the Vile Fin murlocs dwelling around Lake...",sec={{t="A Rare Biological Anomaly",b="While studying the indigenous wildlife along the eastern borders of Silverpine Forest, Apothecary Berard cataloged an abnormal, calcified growth developing within the Vile Fin murlocs of Lake Lordamere. Such growths are exceedingly rare, appearing only in mature specimens along the shoreline and the Dawning Isles. What causes the Vile Fin murlocs to produce these hardened masses remains uncertain, but their dense, morbid tissue caught the immediate attention of the Royal Apothecary Society.",sp=0},{t="Fuel for the New Plague",b="Following Berard's untimely demise, his field notes were recovered by Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher. Recognizing the potential within Berard's work, Renferrel tasked Forsaken agents with retrieving a Hardened Tumor alongside native aquatic mosses. Master Apothecary Faranell oversees the Apothecarium in the Undercity, seeking reagents that can resist decay or alter biological matter. He incorporated this peculiar growth directly into the Society's ongoing compounding of the New Plague.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Hardened Tumor?",a="It is an abnormal, calcified mass that rarely forms inside Vile Fin murlocs living around Lake Lordamere. Discovered by the Forsaken researcher Apothecary Berard, it resists normal physical degradation and possesses unique biological properties.",al={"what is this tumor","tumor lore","hardened tumor drop"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want it?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell and the Royal Apothecary Society are gathering unusual toxic and biological specimens to synthesize the New Plague. The tumor's abnormal resilience and cellular composition make it a prime candidate for their blight experiments.",al={"why apothecary want tumor","recipe for death tumor use","faranell tumor"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these tumors found?",a="They are retrieved from Vile Fin murlocs in Silverpine Forest, specifically those inhabiting the Dawning Isles in eastern Lake Lordamere and the village shores northeast of Ambermill.",al={"where to find hardened tumor","which murlocs drop tumor","tumor location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who was Apothecary Berard?",a="Berard was an apothecary of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Silverpine Forest. Before his death, he compiled detailed research on local flora, fauna, and murloc mutations, uncovering the utility of the Dawning Isles' mosses and hardened tumors.",al={"who is berard","berard lore","berard journal"}},{q="Where does a Hardened Tumor come from?",a="Hardened tumors are abnormal biological growths found on the Vile Fin murlocs dwelling around Lake Lordamere in Silverpine Forest. They are not crafted by mortal hands, but rather harvested from the flesh of these tainted amphibious creatures. Apothecary Berard first documented their existence in his field research, noting that finding a murloc bearing such an unusually dense, calcified growth is remarkably rare.",al={"hardened tumor origin","where do hardened tumors come from","who made hardened tumor"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Procuring the tumor advances Master Apothecary Faranell's vital research into the New Plague, serving Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken's struggle against their living and undead adversaries."},kw={"apothecary faranell","apothecary renferrel","berard","dawning isles","hardened tumor","lake lordamere","murloc","new plague","vile fin"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","item:berard-s-journal","quest:447","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:murloc","subzone:dawning-isles","zone:silverpine"},src={"Hardened Tumor","A Recipe For Death (3)"}}
E["item:lake-creeper-moss"] = {t="item",n="Lake Creeper Moss",z="undercity",s="Lake Creeper Moss is an organic compound harvested from the aquatic creepers dwelling among the Dawning Isles in Lake Lordamere. It serves as a vital reagent sought by the Royal Apothecary Society for their efforts to engineer a lethal new plague.",h="Lake Creeper Moss is an organic compound harvested from the aquatic creepers dwelling among the Dawning Isles...",sec={{t="Alchemical Harvest",b="Grown along the hides of the vicious freshwater beasts that prowl the southern Dawning Isles of Lake Lordamere, Lake Creeper Moss carries unique properties shaped by Lordaeron's blighted waters. The late herbalist Berard documented its potential in his journals, noting that the growth could serve as a reactive base for necrotic alchemical concoctions. When recovered by Forsaken agents, samples are dispatched directly to the Apothecarium in the Undercity to fuel Master Apothecary Faranell's dark research.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the New Plague",b="The moss is not merely a curious aquatic growth; it forms a critical stage in the development of the Forsaken's signature weapon. Alongside the related moss gathered from Lake Skulkers and diseased tumors taken from local Vile Fin murlocs, the creeper moss provides the organic foundation needed to refine a strain capable of exterminating living tissue and Scourge alike. Despite the loss of the apothecary who discovered its utility, the Royal Apothecary Society continues to brew his recipe in service of the Dark Lady.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Lake Creeper Moss used for?",a="It is an alchemical reagent used by Master Apothecary Faranell and the Royal Apothecary Society to brew and refine their New Plague in the Undercity.",al={"creeper moss purpose","why collect lake creeper moss","lake creeper moss use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does this moss come from?",a="It is gathered from Lake Creepers and Elder Lake Creepers that inhabit the waters around the southern Dawning Isles in eastern Lake Lordamere.",al={"where to get creeper moss","creeper moss location","lake creeper location"},it="origin"},{q="Who discovered the moss's alchemical value?",a="Apothecary Berard documented the moss's unique properties in his field journal before his demise in Silverpine Forest. His notes were later recovered by Apothecary Renferrel.",al={"who found the moss","berard moss","who wrote about creeper moss"}},{q="Who receives the harvested moss?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell accepts the moss in the Apothecarium of the Undercity, combining it with Lake Skulker Moss and a hardened tumor to advance his research.",al={"who wants creeper moss","turn in creeper moss","faranell moss"}},{q="What is Lake Creeper Moss?",a="Lake Creeper Moss is an organic growth harvested directly from the bodies of the aquatic creepers inhabiting Lake Lordamere. While outwardly ordinary swamp flora, the Royal Apothecary Society values it as a vital reagent in their dark experiments.",al={"what is creeper moss","lake creeper moss lore","creeper moss explained"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every sample of lake moss brought to the Apothecarium moves the Forsaken closer to perfecting the New Plague, securing vengeance against both the Scourge and the living.",["profession:Herbalism"]="While native to water beasts rather than standard soil, the moss represents the darker, experimental fringe of Lordaeron's flora harvested for apothecary research."},kw={"berard","dawning isles","elder lake creeper","faranell","lake creeper","lake creeper moss","lake lordamere","new plague","royal apothecary society"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","item:lake-skulker-moss","item:hardened-tumor","item:berard-s-journal","quest:447","subzone:dawning-isles","topic:royal-apothecary-society"},src={"Lake Creeper Moss","A Recipe For Death (3)"}}
E["item:lake-skulker-moss"] = {t="item",n="Lake Skulker Moss",z="undercity",s="Lake Skulker Moss is a biological reagent gathered from the amphibious threshadon beasts inhabiting the northern reaches of Lake Lordamere. It was identified by the deceased Apothecary Berard as a key organic component for the Royal Apothecary Society's research into brewing a New Plague.",h="Lake Skulker Moss is a biological reagent gathered from the amphibious threshadon beasts inhabiting the...",sec={{t="A Plague Reagent",b="Harvested from the hides and shells of Lake Skulkers and Elder Lake Skulkers on the Dawning Isles, this damp aquatic moss possesses properties prized by Forsaken alchemists. Prior to his demise, Apothecary Berard meticulously cataloged the flora and fauna of eastern Silverpine Forest, concluding in his journal that both Lake Skulker and Lake Creeper mosses could serve as stabilizing or reactive agents. Following Berard's death, Apothecary Renferrel recovered these field notes and instructed Forsaken champions to gather moss samples alongside a rare tumor from local Vile Fin murlocs, delivering them directly to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Lake Skulker Moss used for?",a="It is utilized by the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity as an organic base ingredient for concocting the New Plague, serving the goals of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken.",al={"moss use","why collect skulker moss","what does skulker moss do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this moss come from?",a="The moss is scraped from the bodies of Lake Skulkers and Elder Lake Skulkers, aquatic beasts that inhabit the waters around the Dawning Isles in northeastern Lake Lordamere, off the coast of Silverpine Forest.",al={"where to get skulker moss","skulker moss location","who drops lake skulker moss"},it="origin"},{q="Who discovered the moss's usefulness?",a="Apothecary Berard first identified its potential during his field research in Silverpine Forest. Although Berard was killed, his surviving journal guided Apothecary Renferrel and Master Apothecary Faranell to continue his experiments.",al={"who found the moss","berard moss","apothecary berard research"},it="history"},{q="Who requires this reagent?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell, the leader of the Royal Apothecary Society residing in the Apothecarium of the Undercity, requires the moss to advance his biological warfare projects.",al={"who wants skulker moss","faranell skulker moss"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Lake Skulker Moss?",a="Lake Skulker Moss is a natural growth harvested from the backs of lake skulkers, amphibious beasts lurking around the Dawning Isles of Lake Lordamere. While unremarkable to fishermen and travelers, this organic matter possesses specific properties that drew the attention of Forsaken alchemists studying local flora and fauna.",al={"what is lake skulker moss","lake skulker moss info","skulker moss explained"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every batch of harvested moss brings the Royal Apothecary Society one step closer to perfecting the New Plague, the Forsaken's greatest weapon against both the Scourge and the living."},kw={"berard","dawning isles","faranell","lake lordamere","lake skulker","lake skulker moss","new plague","renferrel"},rel={"quest:447","item:lake-creeper-moss","item:berard-s-journal","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:dawning-isles","item:hardened-tumor"},src={"Lake Skulker Moss","A Recipe For Death (3)"}}
E["item:letter-from-lor-themar-theron"] = {t="item",n="Letter from Lor'themar Theron",z="undercity",s="This diplomatic dispatch, penned by Regent Lord Lor'themar Theron of Silvermoon, confirms the execution of the Scourge-aligned traitor Dar'Khan Drathir. Entrusted to an envoy traveling south to the Undercity, the missive serves as vital proof that Quel'Thalas possesses the strength to handle its internal threats and join the Horde as an equal power.",h="This diplomatic dispatch, penned by Regent Lord Lor'themar Theron of Silvermoon, confirms the execution of...",sec={{t="A Plea Turned Bargaining Chip",b="Following the devastation of Quel'Thalas, Regent Lord Lor'themar Theron sought allies to safeguard his recovering kingdom against the lingering Scourge. Whispers among the Horde questioned whether the blood elves had the grit to reclaim their lands or if they would become a liability. The death of the traitor Dar'Khan Drathir at the hands of elven champions changed that calculus entirely. By committing news of this victory to parchment, Lor'themar crafted an opening for formal entry into Thrall's Horde, relying on his envoy to prove that the Sin'dorei could pull their own weight.",sp=0},{t="To the Banshee Queen",b="Addressed specifically to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the letter is more than an ordinary diplomatic courtesy. As the former Ranger-General of Silvermoon, Sylvanas retains a profound interest in the fate of Quel'Thalas and has championed the Sin'dorei cause within the Horde's high councils. Hearing of Dar'Khan's demise brings personal vindication to the Banshee Queen, who utilizes Lor'themar's missive to arrange further diplomatic introductions in Orgrimmar, smoothing over friction with the Darkspear trolls and Warchief Thrall.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this letter?",a="The letter reports the death of the traitor Dar'Khan Drathir and affirms that Quel'Thalas is securing its borders. Regent Lord Lor'themar Theron sends it as tangible proof of elven capability to petition for entry into the Horde on equal terms.",al={"what is lorthemars letter","letter purpose","envoy letter"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the letter brought to Sylvanas first instead of Thrall?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner is the former Ranger-General of Silvermoon and the blood elves' strongest advocate among the Horde's leaders. Undercity serves as the natural staging ground before the elven envoy travels onward to Orgrimmar.",al={"why sylvanas","why deliver to undercity","why not go to thrall"},it="motive"},{q="Who was Dar'Khan Drathir and why is his death important?",a="Dar'Khan was the high elf magistrate who betrayed Quel'Thalas to Arthas and the Scourge during the Third War. Eliminating him removes the foremost threat to the Ghostlands and demonstrates to potential allies that the Sin'dorei are resilient enough to handle their own crises.",al={"who is darkhan","why kill darkhan","darkhan death"}},{q="How does the letter help relations with the Darkspear trolls?",a="Centuries of bitter war in the northern forests left immense distrust between elves and trolls. Demonstrating martial strength and eliminating a major Scourge commander reassures the Darkspear and Warchief Thrall that accepting Quel'Thalas will strengthen the Horde rather than burden it.",al={"troll relations","why do trolls care","lorthemar trolls"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Letter from Lor'themar Theron?",a="It is an official missive penned by Regent Lord Lor'themar Theron of Silvermoon. Sent to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity, the letter formally announces the death of the traitor Dar'Khan Drathir and details additional developments intended to demonstrate the blood elves' worthiness to stand alongside the Horde as equals.",al={"what is lorthemar theron letter","what is this letter","letter from lorthemar theron lore"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Letter from Lor'themar Theron come from, and who made it?",a="The letter was drafted in Quel'Thalas by Lor'themar Theron, the Regent Lord overseeing the surviving blood elves of Silvermoon. It was prepared following the defeat of the traitor Dar'Khan Drathir and entrusted to an envoy to carry across the sea directly to the Forsaken capital.",al={"who wrote the letter from lorthemar theron","where did lorthemar letter come from","who made letter from lorthemar theron"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The missive marks a pivotal turning point for the Horde, providing proof that the blood elves are formidable enough to defend the northern front of the Eastern Kingdoms alongside the Forsaken.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Lor'themar's correspondence validates Sylvanas Windrunner's sponsorship of her former kin and secures an enduring northern alliance for the Undercity."},kw={"dar'khan","envoy","letter","lor'themar","sin'dorei","sylvanas","theron","undercity"},rel={"npc:lor-themar-theron","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","zone:undercity","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","zone:orgrimmar","topic:troll"},src={"Letter from Lor'themar Theron","Envoy to the Horde (blood elf)"}}
E["item:letter-sealed-by-sylvanas"] = {t="item",n="Letter Sealed by Sylvanas",z="undercity",s="This diplomatic document bears the personal mark of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, Dark Lady of the Forsaken. Entrusted to an envoy traveling to Orgrimmar, it serves as her formal push to integrate the struggling blood elves into the Horde.",h="This diplomatic document bears the personal mark of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, Dark Lady of the Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Plea for Silvermoon",b="Though she now commands the undead Forsaken from the subterranean halls of the Undercity, Sylvanas Windrunner has not forgotten the kingdom of Quel'Thalas. The Dark Lady has repeatedly championed the cause of the sin'dorei, advocating that Silvermoon deserves an equal seat beside Orgrimmar and the Undercity at the negotiating table. This missive carries her direct endorsement, aiming to silence the lingering skepticism among the orcish leadership regarding her former people's worth to the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Diplomatic Friction",b="Forging an alliance with Silvermoon is not universally embraced across the sea in Durotar. When carried before the Horde leadership in Orgrimmar, the missive is met with cautious reserve rather than immediate jubilation. Even with Sylvanas's personal seal stamping the parchment and a decorated champion of the sin'dorei presenting it, the Warchief and his generals remain keenly aware of the persistent, calculating nature of the Banshee Queen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this letter?",a="The letter contains Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's formal diplomatic endorsement of the blood elves. It asks the Horde leadership in Orgrimmar to formally accept Silvermoon as an allied power alongside the Forsaken and the orcs.",al={"what does the letter say","why send letter","letter purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Sylvanas helping the blood elves?",a="In life, Sylvanas was the Ranger-General of Silvermoon who died defending Quel'Thalas. Although she now leads the Forsaken, she maintains a fierce loyalty to her homeland and seeks to secure strong allies for both Quel'Thalas and the Undercity.",al={"why does sylvanas care about blood elves","sylvanas silvermoon connection"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does this letter need to be delivered?",a="The letter is addressed to the orcish leadership in the valley of Orgrimmar, the capital city of Durotar, requiring travel across the Great Sea via zeppelin.",al={"who gets the letter","where do i take sylvanas letter"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="How is the letter received in Orgrimmar?",a="The leadership in Orgrimmar acknowledges Sylvanas's relentless persistence in advocating for Silvermoon, though they remain measured and cautious about how quickly they can embrace the sin'dorei into the faction.",al={"orc reaction to letter","thrall reaction"}},{q="What is the Letter Sealed by Sylvanas?",a="It is a diplomatic document bearing Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's personal seal, written to petition the leaders of the Horde on behalf of Silvermoon. By personally endorsing the sin'dorei, the Banshee Queen aims to overcome skepticism in Orgrimmar and secure the blood elves a formal place within the Horde.",al={"what is sylvanas letter","letter sealed by sylvanas identity","letter from sylvanas"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Letter Sealed by Sylvanas come from, and who made it?",a="The letter was authored and sealed by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner herself in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity. Bound by her lingering devotion to her elven homeland, she drafted the endorsement to personally sponsor the blood elves' bid to enter the Horde coalition.",al={"who wrote the letter","where does sylvanas letter come from","letter sealed by sylvanas origin"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This document represents the ongoing efforts to bind the northern kingdoms of Lordaeron and Quel'Thalas to the shamanic core of the Horde in Kalimdor.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, bringing Silvermoon into the fold secures a neighboring ally in the Eastern Kingdoms and reinforces Sylvanas's political standing within the Horde."},kw={"blood elf","letter sealed by sylvanas","meeting the orcs","orgrimmar","silvermoon","sin'dorei","sylvanas windrunner","undercity"},rel={"npc:sylvanas-windrunner","zone:undercity","zone:orgrimmar","npc:thrall","zone:durotar"},src={"Letter Sealed by Sylvanas","Meeting the Orcs (blood elf)"}}
E["item:mudsnout-composite"] = {t="item",n="Mudsnout Composite",z="undercity",s="Mudsnout Composite is an alchemical paste prepared by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill from harvested Mudsnout Blossoms. It serves as an essential base ingredient carried to the Undercity for the Royal Apothecary Society's research into a new plague.",h="Mudsnout Composite is an alchemical paste prepared by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill from harvested Mudsnout...",sec={{t="A Base for Decay",b="Crafted in the field by Apothecary Lydon, this fine composite is derived directly from Mudsnout Blossoms gathered in the Hillsbrad Foothills. While noxious on its own, the mash requires a specialized colloid of decay—concocted by Master Apothecary Faranell himself—to activate its more lethal qualities. Once bound, the mixture forms a key chemical component in the development of the Dark Lady's Elixir of Agony.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Correspondence",b="Transporting the composite from Tarren Mill to the Undercity's Apothecarium reflects the decentralized, iterative nature of Forsaken alchemy. Field researchers constantly gather regional reagents and dispatch samples back to the capital's masters for refinement. Despite high demands from Lady Sylvanas to rush results against both living humans and the Scourge, Faranell commends the composite as ingenious groundwork toward their overarching goal.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Mudsnout Composite used for?",a="It is an intermediary paste created from Mudsnout Blossoms. It is meant to be treated with a colloid of decay by Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity, helping formulate the Elixir of Agony.",al={"mudsnout composite purpose","what does mudsnout composite do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who created the composite?",a="Apothecary Lydon, a Forsaken researcher stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, crushed fresh blossoms to mix the paste before sending it north.",al={"who made mudsnout composite","mudsnout composite creator"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Master Apothecary Faranell need it?",a="Faranell oversees the Royal Apothecary Society's grand work on creating a new plague. Lydon's composite provides the specific herbal base needed to advance their research into lethal toxins.",al={"why bring it to faranell","faranell mudsnout"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Mudsnout Composite?",a="Mudsnout Composite is a refined mixture concocted by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. Crafted by grinding down rare Mudsnout Blossoms found in the Hillsbrad Foothills, this potent substance serves as an essential alchemical base in the Royal Apothecary Society's research to engineer a devastating new plague for the Forsaken.",al={"mudsnout composite","what is mudsnout composite","mudsnout mixture"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every shipment like this composite contributes directly to the Dark Lady's mandate: securing the future of the Forsaken by developing a plague to destroy both the living and the Scourge.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Mudsnout Blossoms prove that even humble native flora can be crushed and weaponized under the practiced eye of an apothecary."},kw={"apothecarium","apothecary lydon","elixir of agony","master apothecary faranell","mudsnout blossom","mudsnout composite","royal apothecary society"},rel={"quest:509","item:mudsnout-blossom","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","subzone:apothecarium","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","quest:367"},src={"Mudsnout Composite","Elixir of Agony (2)"}}
E["item:mudsnout-mixture"] = {t="item",n="Mudsnout Mixture",z="undercity",s="Mudsnout Mixture is a toxic alchemical base concocted by Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity. Created by blending a mudsnout composite with an alchemical colloid of decay, it serves as the foundation for the Royal Apothecary Society's deadly Elixir of Agony.",h="Mudsnout Mixture is a toxic alchemical base concocted by Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Colloid of Decay",b="When Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill seeks to craft a virulent new biological weapon, he sends the base composite from Hillsbrad's native Mudsnout gnolls north to the Undercity. Impressed by the composite's potential, Master Apothecary Faranell introduces his own colloid of decay into the blend, producing the volatile Mudsnout Mixture. The solution stabilizes the gnoll compound while readying its virulent properties for further catalytic refinement back in the foothills.",sp=0},{t="Catalyzing the Agony",b="Though potent on its own, the Mudsnout Mixture is inert without key catalysts to trigger its contaminating agents. Faranell tasks couriers with returning the vial to Tarren Mill alongside a Strong Troll's Blood Elixir, venomous Daggerspine naga scales, and Torn Fin murloc eyes. Once catalyzed by Lydon, this mixture forms the lethal Elixir of Agony—a signature poison intended to spread ruin among the living enemies of the Forsaken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Mudsnout Mixture used for?",a="It serves as the intermediary chemical base for the Elixir of Agony, an experimental poison being perfected by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill to slaughter the enemies of the Forsaken.",al={"mudsnout mixture purpose","what does mudsnout mixture do","mudsnout mixture use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who creates the Mudsnout Mixture?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell, the leader of the Royal Apothecary Society residing in the Apothecarium of the Undercity, creates it by infusing a raw mudsnout composite with his own colloid of decay.",al={"who makes mudsnout mixture","mudsnout mixture creator"},it="origin"},{q="Why does it require gnoll components?",a="The Mudsnout gnolls of Hillsbrad Foothills yield organic compounds that the Royal Apothecary Society discovered make an exceptional base for carrying virulent blights and toxic concoctions.",al={"why mudsnout","gnoll poison lore"}},{q="How is the mixture activated?",a="To awaken the dormant contaminating agents within the mixture, Apothecary Lydon requires a Strong Troll's Blood Elixir, along with Daggerspine naga scales and Torn Fin murloc eyes harvested along the Hillsbrad coast.",al={"activate mudsnout mixture","elixir of agony reagents"}},{q="What is Mudsnout Mixture?",a="It is an experimental alchemical concoction formulated by the Royal Apothecary Society. Built around a composite of Mudsnout gnoll components, the mixture incorporates Master Apothecary Faranell's own colloid of decay to serve as a volatile base for the apothecaries' plague research.",al={"what is mudsnout mixture","mudsnout mixture","mudsnout composite"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want Mudsnout Mixture?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill requires it to synthesize the Elixir of Agony, an experimental concoction aimed at spreading disease and death to the enemies of the Forsaken. By activating its contaminating agents with troll's blood and coastal reagents, he intends to advance the Royal Apothecary Society's plague research.",al={"why is mudsnout mixture needed","why does lydon want mudsnout mixture","what is mudsnout mixture for"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The concoction demonstrates the ruthless ingenuity of the Royal Apothecary Society, refining base wilderness ingredients into chemical weapons designed to eliminate the living.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers working in Tarren Mill act as couriers and field agents, carrying toxic concoctions across Lordaeron to secure the Forsaken foothold in Hillsbrad."},kw={"apothecary","colloid of decay","elixir of agony","faranell","hillsbrad","lydon","mudsnout mixture","undercity"},rel={"quest:509","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","topic:royal-apothecary-society","item:mudsnout-composite","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:undercity","item:daggerspine-scale","item:torn-fin-eye"},src={"Mudsnout Mixture","Elixir of Agony (3)"}}
E["item:nether-gem"] = {t="item",n="Nether Gem",z="undercity",s="The Nether Gem is an enchanted arcane stone entrusted by the reclusive necromancer Gunther Arcanus. Imbued with magical power, it acts as a long-distance conduit allowing Gunther to manifest an arcane projection and communicate directly with his old associate, Bethor Iceshard, in the Undercity.",h="The Nether Gem is an enchanted arcane stone entrusted by the reclusive necromancer Gunther Arcanus.",sec={{t="A Conduit of Arcane Communion",b="Forged or enchanted by Gunther Arcanus on his solitary island in Brightwater Lake, the Nether Gem serves as a mystical link across Tirisfal Glades. Gunther, having broken free from the Lich King's control through his own sheer willpower, long avoided the fledgling Forsaken nation out of suspicion. After receiving his lost spellbook, he entrusts the gem to an emissary as a gesture of goodwill. Once brought to Bethor Iceshard atop the Magic Quarter in the Undercity, the stone channels Gunther's magical visage directly before the Mage Guild leader, opening the path for the solitary mage to align with Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Nether Gem do?",a="The Nether Gem allows Gunther Arcanus to communicate across long distances with Bethor Iceshard. When Bethor channels magic into the stone in the Undercity, it projects an ethereal visage of Gunther, enabling the two powerful mages to speak directly.",al={"nether gem purpose","what is nether gem","what does nether gem do"},it="power"},{q="Who crafted the Nether Gem?",a="The gem is provided by Gunther Arcanus, a formidable necromancer dwelling on an island in Brightwater Lake. He gives it to an adventurer to deliver to his old comrade Bethor after his lost spellbook is returned to him.",al={"who made nether gem","where does nether gem come from","gunther gem"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the Nether Gem significant to the Forsaken?",a="It serves as the instrument that successfully brings Gunther Arcanus into the fold of the Forsaken. Gunther originally mistrusted other undead, fearing they were still thralls of the Scourge; the gem allows him to reconnect with Bethor Iceshard and pledge his allegiance to Lady Sylvanas.",al={"why is nether gem important","gunther forsaken","forsaken nether gem"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Nether Gem?",a="The Nether Gem is a magical focus entrusted to you by Gunther Arcanus, a powerful undead mage residing on an island in Brightwater Lake. Charged with mystical arcane energies, it acts as a magical conduit that allows Gunther to communicate across great distances and project his visage directly to his old ally Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.",al={"what is nether gem","nether gem lore","nether gem item"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, the Nether Gem demonstrates how master mages bridge vast distances via magical scrying and projected visages rather than risking travel.",["race:Undead"]="The delivery of the stone marks a major diplomatic triumph for the Forsaken, securing the powerful Gunther Arcanus as an ally against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brightwater lake","gunther arcanus","nether gem","prodigal lich","undercity"},rel={"quest:411","quest:405","npc:bethor-iceshard","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"Nether Gem","The Prodigal Lich Returns"}}
E["item:pure-hearts"] = {t="item",n="Pure Hearts",z="undercity",s="Pure Hearts are ritual reagents provided to Forsaken warlocks by Carendin Halgar in the Undercity. They are used to lure and manifest a succubus across the Twisting Nether so the practitioner can defeat and bind the demon.",h="Pure Hearts are ritual reagents provided to Forsaken warlocks by Carendin Halgar in the Undercity.",sec={{t="Bait for the Nether",b="Demonology relies on exploiting base desires and spiritual vulnerabilities. To summon a succubus into the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, Carendin Halgar provides warlocks with Pure Hearts. When placed upon the summoning circle, these untainted spiritual essences act as potent bait, drawing the seductive demon across the Twisting Nether into the mortal realm. Once the demon manifests, the warlock must resist her enthralling mind-charms and strike her down in combat. Overcoming the succubus asserts mystical dominance, banishing her back to the Twisting Nether until the warlock invokes her true name to bind her into permanent servitude.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Pure Hearts used for?",a="They serve as the mystical catalyst used at the summoning circle in Undercity's Magic Quarter to lure and manifest a succubus across the void, allowing a warlock to battle and bind her.",al={"pure hearts use","why pure hearts","what do pure hearts do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Pure Hearts?",a="Carendin Halgar, the Forsaken warlock trainer located in the Magic Quarter beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, gives them to aspiring practitioners ready to master the summoning of a succubus.",al={"who gives pure hearts","pure hearts quest giver"},it="origin"},{q="Why does a succubus respond to Pure Hearts?",a="Succubi thrive on corruption, seduction, and corrupting innocence. The radiance of unblemished, pure hearts is an irresistible lure across the Twisting Nether, drawing them straight into the warlock's prepared summoning circle.",al={"why succubus wants pure hearts","lore behind pure hearts"},it="power"},{q="Do you get to keep the Pure Hearts after the ritual?",a="No. Once the succubus is summoned and subdued, the remnants of the Pure Hearts are returned to Carendin Halgar as proof of completing the binding trial.",al={"do i keep pure hearts","what happens to pure hearts"},gp=true},{q="What are the Pure Hearts?",a="The Pure Hearts are potent ritual components used by Forsaken warlocks in the Undercity. When cast upon a summoning circle, their untainted essence acts as a lure across the Twisting Nether, opening a rift specifically designed to entice and summon a dangerous succubus into your presence.",al={"what are pure hearts","pure hearts item","pure hearts warlock"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why would anyone want the Pure Hearts?",a="An aspiring warlock requires the Pure Hearts to complete the dangerous binding ritual for a succubus. Without offering such untainted bait to bridge the void, you cannot draw the demon through into the mortal realm to subdue her and master the art of summoning her to your command.",al={"why want pure hearts","pure hearts purpose","why are pure hearts sought"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="For Forsaken warlocks, obtaining and using these hearts represents a pivotal milestone in demonology: proving one's mental fortitude against the seductive lures of the Twisting Nether.",["race:Undead"]="Amidst the rot and blight of the Undercity, using purely untainted hearts to manipulate demonic appetites exemplifies the cold, pragmatic sorcery practiced by the Forsaken."},kw={"carendin halgar","magic quarter","pure hearts","succubus","summoning","the binding","undercity"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1471","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity"},src={"Pure Hearts","The Binding (Succubus, Undercity)"}}
E["item:runes-of-summoning"] = {t="item",n="Runes of Summoning",z="undercity",s="The Runes of Summoning are a ritual item provided by the warlock trainer Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. They are used to call forth an unbound voidwalker into a summoning circle so that an aspiring warlock may bend it to their will.",h="The Runes of Summoning are a ritual item provided by the warlock trainer Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter...",sec={{t="Subjugation in the Magic Quarter",b="Within the dark recesses of the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Forsaken practitioners of the dark arts study the manipulation of the Nether. Carendin Halgar entrusts the Runes of Summoning only to warlocks who have prepared themselves to take command of a voidwalker. By casting the runes within the active summoning circle below Halgar's station, the practitioner tears through the fabric of the Void, drawing forth a creature that must be overpowered and bound into servitude.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Runes of Summoning used for?",a="They are used within the summoning circle in the Undercity's Magic Quarter to draw an unbound voidwalker from the Nether into the physical world, allowing a warlock to defeat and subjugate it.",al={"runes of summoning purpose","what do runes of summoning do","how to use runes of summoning"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Runes of Summoning?",a="Carendin Halgar, the Forsaken warlock trainer located in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, provides them during the final stage of training to bind a voidwalker.",al={"who gives runes of summoning","runes of summoning trainer","carendin halgar runes"},it="origin"},{q="Where must the runes be activated?",a="They must be brought to the purple summoning circle situated directly below Carendin Halgar's platform in the Magic Quarter.",al={"where do i use runes of summoning","runes of summoning location","summoning circle undercity"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after the entity is summoned?",a="The voidwalker attacks immediately. The warlock must subdue it by force of magic and arms. Once defeated, the entity is indentured, and Carendin Halgar imparts the permanent spell to summon it.",al={"what happens after using runes","voidwalker subdued","after summoning voidwalker"},it="next_step"},{q="What are the Runes of Summoning?",a="The Runes of Summoning are a specialized ritual catalyst given to aspiring Forsaken warlocks in the Undercity. When brought to the circle of summoning in the Magic Quarter, the runes focus magical energies to tear open a passage and draw forth an unbound voidwalker from the Nether.",al={"what are runes of summoning","runes of summoning","runes of summoning item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar want the Runes of Summoning returned?",a="Carendin Halgar provides the runes specifically as a trial of mastery. Once you activate them and subdue the summoned voidwalker in combat, returning the runes proves to him that you have dominated the creature, allowing him to properly teach you the permanent spell to summon and command voidwalkers.",al={"why return runes of summoning","why does carendin want the runes","return runes of summoning"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Forsaken warlocks use the runes to prove their dominion over the Void, transforming a chaotic shadow into an enduring, loyal minion.",["race:Undead"]="In the subterranean depths of the Undercity, Forsaken practitioners bypass ancient taboos to bind void entities directly beneath the ruins of Lordaeron."},kw={"carendin halgar","magic quarter","runes of summoning","the binding","undercity","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"quest:1471","npc:carendin-halgar","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:1473","quest:1478","topic:warlock"},src={"Runes of Summoning","The Binding (Voidwalker, Undercity)"}}
E["item:sample-ichor"] = {t="item",n="Sample Ichor",z="undercity",s="This vial contains a refined extract of the foul fluid that sustains the rot hide gnolls of Silverpine Forest. Distilled down to its base components by Apothecary Renferrel, the substance carries lingering traces of both necromancy and warlock sorcery.",h="This vial contains a refined extract of the foul fluid that sustains the rot hide gnolls of Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="Unraveling the Rot Hides",b="The Rot Hide gnolls that prowl Silverpine Forest are no ordinary beasts. After recovering samples from the creatures and their lingering remnants, Apothecary Renferrel of the Royal Apothecary Society reduced the vile liquid into its constituent elements. His chemical breakdown revealed that the ichor was artificially manufactured through a convergence of dark schools: necromantic rites woven together with warlock magics. Because the craft behind it borders on arcane disciplines outside simple alchemy, Renferrel packaged this sample and dispatched it to the Undercity for Bethor Iceshard to examine with divination.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sample Ichor?",a="It is a refined extract prepared by Apothecary Renferrel from the bodily fluids of the rot hide gnolls. Renferrel separated it into its base components to analyze the magical methods used to create the walking dead beasts.",al={"sample ichor","what is this ichor","what is sample ichor"},it="identity"},{q="Who needs to see this sample?",a="The sample must be delivered to Bethor Iceshard, an undead mage stationed within the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Bethor's expertise in divination and magical traditions allows him to identify traces of magic that standard alchemy cannot discern.",al={"who do i bring the ichor to","sample ichor turn in","bethor iceshard ichor"},it="purpose"},{q="What kind of magic is inside the ichor?",a="Renferrel detected a combination of warlock and necromantic magic bound into the fluid. Upon examining the vial, Bethor Iceshard notes that it is laced with powerful, ancient enchantments that demand a deeper spell of divination to fully uncover.",al={"what magic is in the ichor","ichor magic type","rot hide magic"},it="power"},{q="Why didn't the apothecaries finish analyzing it themselves?",a="While the Royal Apothecary Society excels in alchemy, toxins, and bodily blights, deciphering complex arcane weaves requires a dedicated sorcerer. Bethor Iceshard is skilled in identifying magical schools and unraveling esoteric spells beyond an apothecary's standard apparatus.",al={"why apothecary sent to bethor","why not renounce rot hide ichor"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this Sample Ichor come from, and who made it?",a="Apothecary Renferrel prepared this vial by breaking down crude ichor gathered from the rot hide gnolls in Silverpine Forest. His initial analysis revealed that whoever created the original substance infused it with both necromancy and warlock magic, though the true mastermind behind its creation remains to be unraveled.",al={"sample ichor origin","where did sample ichor come from","who made sample ichor"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want the Sample Ichor?",a="Apothecary Renferrel hit the limits of alchemical science trying to determine what created the rot hides. He sent this refined sample to Bethor Iceshard in Undercity's Magic Quarter because Bethor possesses deep knowledge of arcane and dark arts, allowing him to use divination magic to identify the obscure spells woven into the fluid.",al={"why does bethor want sample ichor","why is sample ichor wanted","sample ichor purpose bethor"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Apothecary Renferrel specifically detects warlock arts interwoven with necromancy inside the ichor, hinting that fel practices helped bind these undead beasts.",["class:Mage"]="Bethor Iceshard relies on specialized divination spells to read the residue in the sample, demonstrating the value of classical arcane analysis when confronting dark sorcery."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","bethor iceshard","magic quarter","rot hide","rot hide origins","sample ichor","silverpine","undercity"},rel={"quest:444","npc:apothecary-renferrel","npc:bethor-iceshard","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","topic:warlock"},src={"Sample Ichor","Rot Hide Origins"}}
E["item:sealed-sin-dorei-orders"] = {t="item",n="Sealed Sin'dorei Orders",z="undercity",s="Sealed Sin'dorei Orders are an official diplomatic dispatch drafted by Ambassador Sunsorrow in the Undercity. Bound for Advisor Sorrelon at the Sepulcher, the sealed letter serves to coordinate blood elf efforts and observations among their new Forsaken allies in Silverpine Forest.",h="Sealed Sin'dorei Orders are an official diplomatic dispatch drafted by Ambassador Sunsorrow in the Undercity.",sec={{t="Diplomatic Correspondence",b="The orders are drafted by Ambassador Sunsorrow, who resides within the Royal Quarter of the Undercity serving as the diplomatic face of Quel'Thalas. Addressed to Advisor Sorrelon stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, the missive provides official guidance on operating alongside the Forsaken. Beyond formal instructions, the dispatch notes high regard for the courier who carried Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's recovered necklace, while urging careful conduct so as not to damage the fledgling ties binding the sin'dorei to the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Sealed Sin'dorei Orders?",a="They are a confidential official dispatch written by Ambassador Sunsorrow in the Undercity. They contain instructions for Advisor Sorrelon, the sin'dorei representative stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"sealed sindorei orders","sindorei orders","what are these orders"},it="identity"},{q="Who wrote these orders and why?",a="Ambassador Sunsorrow penned them after the return of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's long-lost necklace. He dispatched the courier to Silverpine Forest with instructions to help maintain stable, respectful relations with their new undead allies.",al={"who wrote sealed sindorei orders","ambassador sunsorrow orders"},it="origin"},{q="What is inside the orders?",a="While delivered sealed, Advisor Sorrelon reveals upon opening that Sunsorrow commended the courier's service to Quel'Thalas. The missive also addresses navigating relations with the Forsaken and urges travelers to remain on their best behavior to protect their bond with the Horde.",al={"contents of sindorei orders","what does the letter say"},it="item"},{q="Where must the orders be delivered?",a="The orders are addressed to Advisor Sorrelon at the Sepulcher, a weathered crypt and settlement in northern Silverpine Forest, situated along the road south from the Tirisfal Glades border.",al={"where do i take the orders","sepulcher delivery"},it="target"},{q="Why does Advisor Sorrelon want the Sealed Sin'dorei Orders?",a="Advisor Sorrelon represents the sin'dorei at the Sepulcher, serving as an emissary to the Forsaken in Silverpine Forest. These confidential orders from Ambassador Sunsorrow keep Sorrelon informed of events in the Undercity—including your handling of Lady Sylvanas's lost locket—and apprise him of your service so he can guide you in strengthening the nascent ties between Silvermoon and the Horde.",al={"why want sealed sindorei orders","why give orders to advisor sorrelon","purpose of sindorei orders"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The document highlights the fragile, nascent relationship between the sin'dorei and the Horde, urging elf emissaries to avoid causing friction among the Forsaken.",["race:Undead"]="Though written by high-born elven diplomats who find the undead and their decrepit crypts rather jarring, the orders mandate respectful cooperation with Forsaken leadership."},kw={"sealed sin'dorei orders","sepulcher","silverpine","sindorei orders","sorrelon","sunsorrow","undercity"},rel={"npc:ambassador-sunsorrow","subzone:sepulcher","zone:undercity","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Sealed Sin'dorei Orders","Delivery to the Sepulcher"}}
E["item:sevren-s-orders"] = {t="item",n="Sevren's Orders",z="undercity",s="Sevren's Orders are written dispatches penned by Magistrate Sevren of Brill. They direct a proven Forsaken agent to report to Bethor Iceshard, a formidable mage stationed in the Undercity's Magic Quarter.",h="Sevren's Orders are written dispatches penned by Magistrate Sevren of Brill.",sec={{t="Summons to the Capital",b="As the Forsaken solidify their grip on the ruins of Lordaeron, skilled agents who have proven their worth against the Scourge in Tirisfal Glades are summoned south to the capital. Issued by Magistrate Sevren, these written orders serve as official introduction and credentials to Bethor Iceshard, one of the Dark Lady's foremost practitioners of the arcane in the Magic Quarter. While Sevren knows little beyond the fact that the assignment involves reaching out to an errant lich, the summons carries the absolute authority of the Undercity's high mages.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wrote these orders?",a="Magistrate Sevren, the Forsaken overseer administering affairs in the town of Brill within Tirisfal Glades, drafted the orders.",al={"author of sevren's orders","who is sevren","who gives sevrens orders"},it="origin"},{q="Who is intended to receive these orders?",a="They are addressed to Bethor Iceshard, a high-ranking Forsaken mage located in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"who gets the orders","where do i bring sevren's orders","who is bethor iceshard"},it="target"},{q="What is the mission mentioned in the orders?",a="The mission involves recruiting a wayward lich to aid the Forsaken, a perilous task requiring an agent who has already proven capable against the Scourge.",al={"what is the lich mission","what does bethor want","prodigal lich mission"},it="purpose"},{q="Why was I chosen to deliver them?",a="Bethor requested an operative of proven capability against the Scourge. Magistrate Sevren deemed your efforts in Tirisfal Glades sufficient to handle Bethor's dangerous task.",al={"why me","why did sevren pick me"},it="why_me"},{q="What is Sevren's Orders?",a="Sevren's Orders is an official dispatch written by Magistrate Sevren of Brill. It acts as formal credentials, identifying you as an agent of proven worth who has fought effectively against the Scourge and is ready to undertake a sensitive assignment.",al={"what are sevrens orders","sevren orders item","what is this document"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want Sevren's Orders?",a="Bethor Iceshard, a prominent mage in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, demanded that Sevren provide an agent capable of handling a perilous task involving a rogue lich. Presenting these orders proves that you are Sevren's chosen operative and that your interruption of the powerful wizard is warranted.",al={"why deliver sevren orders","why does bethor want orders","who needs sevren's orders"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Carrying Sevren's seal marks an operative's transition from local service in Tirisfal to directly aiding the Undercity's arcane elite.",["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, delivering these orders provides an audience with Bethor Iceshard, one of the foremost spellcasters in the Forsaken kingdom."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brill","magic quarter","magistrate sevren","prodigal lich","sevren's orders","undercity"},rel={"quest:405","npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:bethor-iceshard","zone:undercity","subzone:magic-quarter","topic:scourge","topic:mage"},src={"Sevren's Orders","The Prodigal Lich"}}
E["item:skittering-blood"] = {t="item",n="Skittering Blood",z="undercity",s="Skittering Blood is an alchemical reagent harvested from the arachnids dwelling within the Skittering Dark of Silverpine Forest. It serves as a vital toxic ingredient for the Royal Apothecary Society's research into a New Plague designed to eradicate both Scourge and humanity.",h="Skittering Blood is an alchemical reagent harvested from the arachnids dwelling within the Skittering Dark of...",sec={{t="A Toxic Distillate",b="Harvested from Skitterweb lurkers, strikers, and their broodmother Krethis the Shadowspinner, this venomous hemolymph possesses virulent properties prized by Forsaken alchemists. Apothecary Renferrel discovered that when refined alongside toxins extracted from grizzled bear hearts, the blood forms the base of an exceptionally lethal elixir. The compounds within the fluid demonstrate severe contaminating agents, making it an ideal biological catalyst for the Apothecarium's chemical experiments.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the New Plague",b="Under the direction of Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity, the Royal Apothecary Society gathers reagents like Skittering Blood to engineer a devastating New Plague. Faced with overwhelming Scourge hordes and hostile human remnants, the Forsaken pursue biological warfare as an equalizer. Faranell analyzes the blood's toxic potency to devise a contagion potent enough to snuff out unlife and living flesh alike.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Skittering Blood used for?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society utilizes Skittering Blood to develop the Forsaken's New Plague. When blended with toxins derived from bear hearts, it produces a volatile mixture that Master Apothecary Faranell studies to eradicate both Scourge undead and living humans.",al={"skittering blood use","why gather spider blood","what does faranell do with skittering blood"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Skittering Blood found?",a="It is gathered from the bodies of Skitterweb spiders—including lurkers, strikers, and Krethis the Shadowspinner—lurking in and around the Skittering Dark, a gloomy web-choked wood located in northwestern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where to get skittering blood","skittering blood location","who drops skittering blood"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who requests these samples?",a="Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest commissions the collection of the blood, directing adventurers to deliver the harvested fluid straight to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Apothecarium of the Undercity.",al={"who wants skittering blood","quest giver for skittering blood"},it="people"},{q="Why do the Forsaken need venom from local beasts?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society constantly isolates natural toxins from Lordaeron's corrupted fauna. The inherent venom of the giant arachnids of Silverpine provides raw biological pathogens that can be concentrated and weaponized into synthetic plagues.",al={"why spider venom","apothecary beast research"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Skittering Blood?",a="Skittering Blood is the virulent ichor harvested from the massive spiders dwelling in the Skittering Dark of Silverpine Forest. It possesses natural venomous and contaminable properties that make it an invaluable biological reagent for alchemical experiments.",al={"what is skittering blood","skittering blood item","about skittering blood"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Skittering Blood come from, and who made it?",a="It is not manufactured, but naturally drawn from the predatory arachnids inhabiting northwestern Silverpine Forest, including Skitterweb Lurkers, Skitterweb Strikers, and the broodmother Krethis the Shadowspinner. The blood is extracted directly from their carcasses by hunters gathering materials for the Forsaken.",al={"where does skittering blood come from","who made skittering blood","skittering blood origin"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Contributing Skittering Blood directly aids Queen Sylvanas and the Royal Apothecary Society in engineering the ultimate biological weapon against Arthas and living humanity.",["faction:Horde"]="While Forsaken apothecaries welcome the raw materials to secure Lordaeron, other Horde members often view the virulent concoctions brewed from this blood with moral unease."},kw={"faranell","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","silverpine forest","skittering blood","skittering dark","skitterweb"},rel={"quest:447","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","item:grizzled-bear-heart","subzone:skittering-dark","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity"},src={"Skittering Blood","A Recipe For Death"}}
E["item:sturdy-dragonmaw-shinbone"] = {t="item",n="Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbone",z="undercity",s="Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbones are durable skeletal trophies gathered from the renegade Dragonmaw orcs in the Wetlands. Required by armor crafter Velora Nitely in the Undercity, they serve as reinforcement struts for bespoke warrior armor.",h="Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbones are durable skeletal trophies gathered from the renegade Dragonmaw orcs in the...",sec={{t="Bones for the Frame",b="When forging brutal leg guards for frontline warriors, smiths require raw components that can endure severe punishment. In the Undercity, Velora Nitely prizes the skeletal density of the renegade Dragonmaw orcs entrenched at the Angerfang Encampment in the northern Wetlands. Dragonmaw orcs are known for their thick, sturdy frames, making their shins well suited to serve as structural bracers. However, not every collected bone can withstand the strain; warriors must test each piece with their bare hands, discarding those that snap under pressure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes these shinbones sturdy compared to normal ones?",a="Dragonmaw orcs possess naturally thick skeletal frames, but minor fractures or brittle bone make many samples useless for forging armor. To confirm one is sturdy, a warrior bends the raw bone with their bare hands; only those that resist breaking are considered strong enough to frame protective leg guards.",al={"why sturdy shinbones","dragonmaw bone strength","testing shinbones"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbones?",a="Velora Nitely, an armorer located in the Undercity, seeks them out. She uses them as core framing struts when crafting brutal leg guards for promising Horde warriors.",al={"who needs shinbones","velora nitely bones","turn in dragonmaw shinbones"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these bones gathered?",a="They are taken from the renegade Dragonmaw orcs occupying the Wetlands south of the Arathi Highlands, most notably at the Angerfang Encampment nestled in the hills southwest of the Thandol Span.",al={"where to find dragonmaw shinbones","dragonmaw shinbone location","angerfang bones"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Velora Nitely use orc bones for armor?",a="Forsaken craftsmanship frequently integrates bone, sinew, and metal into morbid yet highly durable wargear. The Dragonmaw clan remains hostile to Thrall's Horde, making their remains fair game for Forsaken smiths looking for resilient, heavy-duty crafting material.",al={"why orc bones","forsaken bone armor","velora bone crafting"},it="motive"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Procuring and testing these dense orc bones with bare hands proves a warrior's physical might while gathering the framing pieces for custom armor.",["race:Undead"]="Velora Nitely represents typical Forsaken pragmatism, repurposing the bones of their enemies into functional equipment for the Dark Lady's champions."},kw={"angerfang encampment","dragonmaw shinbone","leg guards","sturdy dragonmaw shinbone","undercity","velora nitely","wetlands"},rel={"quest:1846","npc:velora-nitely","subzone:angerfang-encampment","zone:wetlands","subzone:thandol-span","zone:undercity"},src={"Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbone","Dragonmaw Shinbones"}}
E["item:the-lich-s-spellbook"] = {t="item",n="The Lich's Spellbook",z="undercity",s="The Lich's Spellbook is a volume of necromantic lore kept within a chest on the island in Brightwater Lake. Recovered for Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity, the tome reveals the true identity and immense magical power of a reclusive undead lich dwelling just north of the Forsaken capital.",h="The Lich's Spellbook is a volume of necromantic lore kept within a chest on the island in Brightwater Lake.",sec={{t="A Reclusive Master's Tomes",b="On an isolated island in Brightwater Lake stands an enigmatic lich surrounded by skeletal guardians. Though free-willed, this sorcerer distrusts the outside world, mistaking all other undead for thralls of the Scourge and ordering his minions to destroy any who approach. Bethor Iceshard, seeking gifted necromancers to bolster the Forsaken ranks beneath Queen Sylvanas Windrunner, tasked an emissary with infiltrating the island camp to retrieve the lich's spellbook. Through its study, Bethor hoped to discern the master's magical aptitude and uncover who he was before death took Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Unmasking Gunther Arcanus",b="Upon opening the glowing pages of the recovered spellbook, Bethor Iceshard made an astonishing discovery: the recluse was his old friend and comrade-in-arms from before the Third War, Gunther Arcanus. Already a prodigy in necromancy in life, Gunther's writings revealed that his arts had grown even more formidable in undeath. Bethor recognized that securing Gunther's allegiance would grant the Forsaken an invaluable master of the dark arts, provided someone could convince the suspicious lich that the Forsaken are truly free from the Lich King's grip.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Lich's Spellbook found?",a="The spellbook rests inside a container named Gunther's Books, situated in the encampment on the central island of Brightwater Lake in northern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is the book","spellbook location","gunther's books"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who owns this spellbook?",a="The book belongs to Gunther Arcanus, a former human necromancer from Dalaran who broke free of the Scourge's control through his own sheer willpower and now dwells in seclusion as a lich.",al={"whose book is this","lich identity","who wrote the spellbook"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want the book?",a="Bethor Iceshard sought the book to deduce the mysterious lich's identity and evaluate his mastery of necromancy, hoping to recruit the recluse into the service of Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken.",al={"why get the book","bethor quest reason","why does undercity want this"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does the lich attack visitors to his island?",a="The lich believes all other undead in the region remain mind-controlled slaves of the Scourge. Paralyzed by suspicion, he commands his minions to attack anyone venturing near his sanctum.",al={"why is gunther hostile","why do minions attack","brightwater lake hostile"},it="hostile"},{q="What relation does Bethor Iceshard have to the author?",a="Bethor and Gunther were close friends and comrades-in-arms before the plague ravaged Lordaeron, though Bethor did not realize the lake's lich was Gunther until deciphering the spellbook's pages.",al={"did bethor know gunther","gunther and bethor","bethor friend"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Where does The Lich's Spellbook come from, and who made it?",a="The spellbook belongs to Gunther Arcanus, a powerful necromancer who was a comrade of Bethor Iceshard before the Third War and the fall of Lordaeron. Gunther penned and maintained the tome himself, filling its glowing pages with his esoteric necromantic arts both in life and throughout his transformation into a free-willed lich on Brightwater Lake.",al={"who made the lich spellbook","origin of the lich's spellbook","where did the lich spellbook come from"},sp=1,it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The tome proves that not all who broke free from the Lich King joined the Forsaken immediately, highlighting the lingering distrust among rogue undead survivors scattered across Tirisfal.",["class:Mage"]="The spellbook represents an extraordinary bridge between classic Dalaran wizardry and dark necromancy, showing how mortal spellcasters dramatically expanded their craft after succumbing to undeath."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brightwater lake","gunther arcanus","lich","necromancy","spellbook","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"quest:357","npc:gunther-arcanus","npc:bethor-iceshard","subzone:brightwater-lake","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"The Lich's Spellbook","The Lich's Identity"}}
E["item:torn-fin-eye"] = {t="item",n="Torn Fin Eye",z="undercity",s="Torn Fin Eyes are ocular organs harvested from the Torn Fin murlocs prowling the shores of Hillsbrad Foothills. They serve as a crucial reactive ingredient for the Royal Apothecary Society's grim alchemical research into new plagues.",h="Torn Fin Eyes are ocular organs harvested from the Torn Fin murlocs prowling the shores of Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Reagent for Ruin",b="The Royal Apothecary Society rarely lets any vile biological component go to waste in their quest to develop the Forsaken's New Plague. Torn Fin Eyes, harvested from the salt-crusted murlocs prowling the Western Strand of Hillsbrad Foothills, possess specialized organic properties needed to activate volatile alchemical compounds. When combined with Daggerspine naga scales, restorative troll elixirs, and gnoll-derived sludge, the optic tissues help stabilize and trigger toxic mixtures formulated to sow death across enemy territories.",sp=0},{t="Brewing Agony",b="In the Apothecarium of the Undercity, master alchemists discovered that adding decaying colloids to Mudsnout composites required catalysts found only along Hillsbrad's coastline. Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill relies on these harvested eyes to catalyze his infamous Elixir of Agony. The concoction represents one of the Forsaken's relentless experiments to manufacture devastating bio-weapons right beneath the nose of neighboring human settlements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Torn Fin Eye used for?",a="Torn Fin Eyes are an alchemical catalyst sought by the Royal Apothecary Society. Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill uses them alongside Daggerspine Scales and a Strong Troll's Blood Elixir to activate the contaminating agents in a volatile Mudsnout Mixture, progressing his research into new deadly plagues.",al={"torn fin eye use","why get torn fin eyes","torn fin eye purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do you find Torn Fin Eyes?",a="They are harvested from Torn Fin murlocs inhabiting the Western Strand of Hillsbrad Foothills, located directly along the coastline west of the human town of Southshore.",al={"where to get torn fin eyes","torn fin eye location","who drops torn fin eye"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who orders the gathering of these eyes?",a="Forsaken researchers in the Undercity and Apothecary Lydon stationed in Tarren Mill require them to finalize the concoction known as the Elixir of Agony.",al={"who needs torn fin eyes","torn fin eye quest giver"},it="motive"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society need murloc parts?",a="The society's researchers experiment constantly with bizarre local fauna to uncover compounds that activate or intensify toxic contaminants. The physiology of the Torn Fin murlocs yields ocular humors capable of catalyzing volatile plague prototypes.",al={"why murloc eyes","apothecary murlocs"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Torn Fin Eye?",a="A Torn Fin Eye is an alchemical reagent harvested from the coastal murlocs prowling the shores of Hillsbrad Foothills. Viscous and saturated with amphibious humors, these eyes are utilized by Forsaken apothecaries who require biological catalysts to awaken volatile contaminating agents in their experimental concoctions.",al={"what is torn fin eye","torn fin eye info","about torn fin eyes"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do Torn Fin Eyes come from?",a="These organic reagents are carved from the Torn Fin tribe of murlocs, who inhabit the Western Strand along the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills, just west of the human settlement of Southshore. They are natural biological parts harvested directly from slain murlocs rather than crafted items.",al={"torn fin eye source","where to get torn fin eyes","who drops torn fin eye"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Procuring organic catalysts like Torn Fin Eyes directly advances the Royal Apothecary Society's ultimate ambition: perfecting a plague to wipe out both the Scourge and the living.",["faction:Horde"]="Gathering these coastal reagents aids the Horde war effort in Hillsbrad Foothills, strengthening the Forsaken foothold against hostile Alliance encroachments from Southshore."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of agony","hillsbrad foothills","murloc","royal apothecary society","torn fin","torn fin eye","undercity"},rel={"quest:509","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","subzone:tarren-mill","item:daggerspine-scale","item:mudsnout-mixture","topic:murloc"},src={"Torn Fin Eye","Elixir of Agony (3)"}}
E["item:valdred-s-hands"] = {t="item",n="Valdred's Hands",z="undercity",s="Valdred's Hands are the severed limbs of Valdred Moray, claimed after his death in southern Silverpine Forest. They are sought by Raleigh Andrean in the Undercity as a morbid trophy and proof of vengeance for the murder of his wife.",h="Valdred's Hands are the severed limbs of Valdred Moray, claimed after his death in southern Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Trophy of Betrayal",b="Before the plague consumed Lordaeron, Valdred Moray and Raleigh Andrean were close friends. That bond was shattered when Valdred murdered Raleigh's wife, Deliah. Though Raleigh succumbed to death and arose as one of the Forsaken—professing an inability to genuinely grieve—the lingering hunger for retribution never left him. When Valdred attempted to flee southward past the Greymane Wall into Gilneas, Raleigh dispatched an emissary to end his former friend's flight, demanding his severed hands as definitive proof that the deed was done.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Remembrance",b="Upon receiving the severed hands, Raleigh relinquishes his late wife's engraved ring, dismissing it as a meaningless bauble. Because Deliah has been dead to him for so long, he finds no comfort in sentimental keepsakes of the past. Instead, he preserves Valdred's hands as an enduring, cold reminder of betrayal and finalized vengeance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Valdred Moray?",a="Valdred Moray was once a close friend of Raleigh Andrean during life. He betrayed that friendship by murdering Raleigh's wife, Deliah, before eventually trying to flee south toward Gilneas.",al={"who is valdred","valdred moray lore","valdred story"},it="people"},{q="Why does Raleigh Andrean want Valdred's hands specifically?",a="Raleigh wants the hands because they were the instruments that strangled or struck down his wife. In Forsaken fashion, he keeps them as a physical trophy of his friend's betrayal and the revenge he extracted.",al={"why hands","why valdreds hands","raleigh hands trophy"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Valdred Moray found?",a="Valdred is located in southern Silverpine Forest, lingering near the towering gate of the Greymane Wall in an attempt to escape into the isolationist kingdom of Gilneas.",al={"where is valdred","valdred location","valdred moray spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens to the hands after bringing them to Undercity?",a="Raleigh keeps the hands in the Undercity as a permanent memento of his completed revenge, simultaneously discarding his murdered wife's ring as a useless trinket.",al={"what does raleigh do with hands","turn in valdreds hands"},sp=1},{q="What are Valdred's Hands?",a="These are the severed hands of Valdred Moray, taken as proof of his death and as a macabre trophy of vengeance. Valdred was once a trusted friend to Raleigh Andrean before betraying him and murdering Raleigh's wife, Deliah. Now, the severed appendages serve as the physical culmination of Raleigh's bitter quest for retribution.",al={"valdreds hands item","what are valdreds hands","valdred hands"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do Valdred's Hands come from?",a="They are severed directly from the body of Valdred Moray. Desperate to flee the Forsaken and escape retribution for his crimes, Valdred retreated south through Silverpine Forest toward the Greymane Wall, hoping to slip into the walled kingdom of Gilneas before his hunter could claim him.",al={"origin of valdreds hands","who has valdreds hands","where do valdreds hands come from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The demand for Valdred's hands exemplifies the cold, vengeful nature of the Forsaken, who often channel their inability to feel conventional sorrow into lingering, obsessive grudges."},kw={"a husband's revenge","deliah","greymane wall","raleigh andrean","silverpine forest","valdred","valdred moray","valdred's hands"},rel={"npc:raleigh-andrean","quest:530","quest:440","quest:441","subzone:greymane-wall","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity"},src={"Valdred's Hands","A Husband's Revenge"}}
E["item:wolf-heart-samples"] = {t="item",n="Wolf Heart Samples",z="undercity",s="Wolf Heart Samples are peculiar organic specimens gathered from corrupted wolves in Silverpine Forest. Despite their lethal toxicity, the hearts beat within the living creatures without killing them, drawing the intense scientific interest of the Royal Apothecary Society.",h="Wolf Heart Samples are peculiar organic specimens gathered from corrupted wolves in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Toxic Paradox",b="While examining carcasses in Silverpine Forest, Apothecary Renferrel discovered that certain wolf hearts harbor a deadly compound. Strangely, the level of poison present within the tissue should easily be fatal to the wolves themselves. Recognizing the unique value of a physiology that thrives while saturated in lethal toxicity, Renferrel set aside tissue samples to be dispatched directly to Undercity. For the Forsaken, studying naturally resilient or toxic organisms is a critical step in mastering biological warfare and compounding new reagents.",sp=0},{t="Consignment to Undercity",b="Entrusted to couriers heading deep beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, the samples are delivered to Apothecary Zinge within the Royal Apothecary Society's headquarters in the Apothecarium. Zinge and her colleagues prize novel toxins above almost all else. By dissecting and experimenting on these tainted tissues, the Society seeks to isolate the virulent compounds and unravel how the beasts survived them, hoping to apply the principles to their own alchemical projects.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are these wolf hearts significant to the Forsaken?",a="The samples contain an intense, unexplained toxicity that normally would have killed the host wolves. The Royal Apothecary Society is fascinated by both the virulent poison itself and the biological mechanism allowing the creatures to survive it.",al={"why are wolf hearts important","what makes the hearts special","why do apothecaries want wolf hearts"}},{q="Who requests these samples?",a="Apothecary Renferrel collected the samples after studying wolves in Silverpine Forest. He instructed a courier to deliver them directly to his colleague, Apothecary Zinge, at the Society's headquarters in Undercity.",al={"who wants the wolf hearts","who sent the samples","who receives the samples"}},{q="What will Apothecary Zinge do with them?",a="Apothecary Zinge conducts alchemical experiments and dissections on the samples. The Royal Apothecary Society constantly catalogs and weaponizes novel toxins to develop new plagues and concoctions for Queen Sylvanas.",al={"what does zinge do with the hearts","zinge experiments","apothecary zinge research"}},{q="Where did the wolves originate?",a="The wolves were hunted in the tainted wilds of Silverpine Forest, an area heavily afflicted by dark magic, decay, and strange corruption that alters the local fauna.",al={"where are the wolves from","silverpine wolves","wolf location"}},{q="What are the Wolf Heart Samples?",a="These are harvested tissue specimens preserved from corrupted wolves. Unlike ordinary beast remains, these hearts exhibit an extraordinary internal toxicity—a venomous quality so severe that, by rights, it should have proved fatal to the beasts while they still lived.",al={"what are wolf heart samples","wolf heart samples item","wolf heart samples"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do the Wolf Heart Samples come from?",a="They were prepared and portioned out by Apothecary Renferrel from the tainted wolf hearts you gathered for his research. Recognizing their unusual properties, Renferrel set aside these specific cuts to be carried directly to his peers in the Undercity.",al={"where did wolf heart samples come from","who made wolf heart samples","wolf heart samples source"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want the Wolf Heart Samples?",a="Apothecary Zinge and the Royal Apothecary Society seek them to investigate novel forms of poison. The unnatural venom coursing through the specimens offers fresh insight into virulent agents, which the apothecaries are eager to isolate, test, and adapt for their own lethal concoctions.",al={"why want wolf heart samples","who wants wolf heart samples","why does zinge want wolf heart samples"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Royal Apothecary Society's endless pursuit of lethal reagents fuels the survival and defense of the Forsaken against living and undead enemies alike."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","apothecary zinge","royal apothecary society","silverpine forest","toxin","undercity","wolf heart samples"},rel={"quest:1359","npc:apothecary-zinge","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:undercity","item:wolf-heart-sample"},src={"Wolf Heart Samples","Zinge's Delivery"}}
E["item:woven-wand"] = {t="item",n="Woven Wand",z="undercity",s="The Woven Wand is a unique enchanted relic crafted long ago by three Dalaran apprentice magi as a pledge of brotherhood. Following the fall of Lordaeron and bitter betrayals among its creators, the wand was hidden away in Fenris Keep before resurfacing in the hands of the Forsaken.",h="The Woven Wand is a unique enchanted relic crafted long ago by three Dalaran apprentice magi as a pledge of...",sec={{t="A Sundered Bond",b="In the days when Dalaran still trained the young magi of the north, three aspiring wizards—Bethor Iceshard, Gunther Arcanus, and Thule Ravenclaw—intertwined their individual apprentice wands into a single talisman. This Woven Wand served as both a conduit of combined magical power and a symbol of their enduring friendship. That fellowship shattered irrevocably when the Scourge swept through Lordaeron. Thule Ravenclaw chose to swear fealty to the Lich King, turning to foul necromancy. Meanwhile, the Plague of Undeath claimed both Bethor and Gunther, eventually cutting their ties to Dalaran entirely.",sp=0},{t="The Hidden Alcove",b="Though Thule came to detest the sentimentality of the wand after turning to darkness, he could never bring himself to destroy it or surrender it to his former peers. Instead, he carried the artifact into Silverpine Forest and concealed it deep within an alcove in Fenris Keep. Decades later, with Thule's lair breached and his servant Alaric directing Horde agents to the hiding place, the relic was retrieved intact. Never having had its dormant enchantments invoked by the necromancer, the wand was finally delivered to Bethor Iceshard within the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who created the Woven Wand?",a="The wand was crafted jointly by three Dalaran apprentice mages: Bethor Iceshard, Gunther Arcanus, and Thule Ravenclaw. They combined their three separate apprentice wands into one shared artifact to represent their friendship.",al={"who made woven wand","creators of woven wand","wand creators"},it="origin"},{q="Why was the wand hidden in Fenris Keep?",a="After Thule betrayed his colleagues to serve the Lich King, he grew to despise the artifact and the bond it represented. However, he was unable to part with it or destroy it, so he hid it away within a secret niche in his lair at Fenris Keep.",al={"why did thule hide the wand","where was woven wand found","why fenris keep"},it="history"},{q="Why did Bethor Iceshard think the wand was lost?",a="Bethor assumed the wand had been permanently lost when their friendship collapsed and the plague ravaged the land. He also noted that Thule never dared to invoke its magical energies; had Thule used it, Bethor would have sensed the surge through their lingering magical link.",al={"what does bethor say about the wand","bethor reaction to wand"}},{q="How was the wand recovered?",a="Horde adventurers assaulted Fenris Keep to defeat Thule Ravenclaw. Guided by the severed, still-talking head of Ravenclaw's former servant Alaric, they located the hidden niche containing the wand and brought it out of the ruins.",al={"who found the wand","how to get woven wand"},sp=1},{q="What is the Woven Wand?",a="The Woven Wand is a enchanted relic woven together from the apprentice wands of three Dalaran magi: Thule Ravenclaw, Bethor Iceshard, and Gunther Arcanus. Created as a token of their early camaraderie, it binds their magical crafts into a single instrument. That bond shattered when Thule pledged himself to the Scourge and his companions were claimed by the plague.",al={"what is woven wand","woven wand lore","woven wand"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want the Woven Wand?",a="Bethor Iceshard believed the wand was lost forever when their fellowship fell apart and Thule Ravenclaw defected to the Lich King. Beyond its sentimental value from their mortal days studying in Dalaran, the wand holds dormant magical power that Thule never invoked—power Bethor feared falling into Scourge hands and is eager to keep secure.",al={"why does bethor want woven wand","why wand to bethor","who wants the woven wand"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The Woven Wand illustrates the old traditions of Dalaran's apprentices, who often experimented with melding personal conduits to focus their collective arcane potential.",["race:Undead"]="The artifact serves as a bittersweet reminder of mortal lives lost to the Scourge, uniting the memories of two Forsaken survivors against the madness of their fallen former peer."},kw={"alaric","bethor iceshard","dalaran","fenris keep","gunther arcanus","magic quarter","thule ravenclaw","woven wand"},rel={"npc:bethor-iceshard","quest:491","quest:461","quest:446","subzone:fenris-keep","npc:gunther-arcanus","subzone:dalaran","subzone:magic-quarter"},src={"Woven Wand","Wand to Bethor"}}
E["npc:advisor-duskingdawn"] = {t="npc",n="Advisor Duskingdawn",z="undercity",s="Advisor Duskingdawn is a blood elf advisor stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. She serves as a point of contact for travelers arriving in the settlement on official Horde business.",h="Advisor Duskingdawn is a blood elf advisor stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Diplomatic Presence",b="Standing watch in Tarren Mill, Advisor Duskingdawn is among the few blood elves operating within Lordaeron alongside the Horde. The hamlet serves as a fortified forward base against the Alliance in Southshore and the Syndicate lingering in the hills, making regional coordination essential. Duskingdawn receives dispatch reports and ensures new arrivals assist with local operations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Advisor Duskingdawn?",a="Advisor Duskingdawn is a blood elf advisor stationed in Tarren Mill within the Hillsbrad Foothills, acting as an administrative presence for Horde affairs in the region.",al={"who is duskingdawn","duskingdawn lore","advisor duskingdawn identity"},it="identity"},{q="Where can she be found?",a="She is located inside the settlement of Tarren Mill in northern Hillsbrad Foothills, coordinating regional tasks alongside Forsaken and orcish authorities.",al={"duskingdawn location","where is advisor duskingdawn","duskingdawn map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is a blood elf in Tarren Mill?",a="Duskingdawn represents diplomatic and advisory interests within Lordaeron, helping direct resources and personnel who arrive to stabilize Tarren Mill against local threats.",al={"why is blood elf in hillsbrad","duskingdawn purpose"},it="why_here"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde couriers and fighters, reporting to Advisor Duskingdawn is an early step in coordinating the defense of Tarren Mill against regional hostilities."},kw={"advisor duskingdawn","blood elf","duskingdawn","hillsbrad foothills","horde advisor","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:horde"},src={"Advisor Duskingdawn"}}
E["npc:ambassador-sunsorrow"] = {t="npc",n="Ambassador Sunsorrow",z="undercity",s="Ambassador Sunsorrow serves as the blood elf diplomatic envoy stationed beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity. Surrounded by the restless dead, he represents the interests of Quel'Thalas and helps coordinate communication and supplies between the Forsaken and his people.",h="Ambassador Sunsorrow serves as the blood elf diplomatic envoy stationed beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in...",sec={{t="Diplomat in the Shadow of the Throne",b="Standing beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in the shadowed depths of the Royal Quarter, Ambassador Sunsorrow acts as an official diplomatic link between the blood elves and the Forsaken. Even in the gloom of the Undercity, Sunsorrow maintains courtly composure, keeping a watchful eye over visitors and directing messengers southward to Forsaken bastions like the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest and Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He shares an unspoken understanding of tragic loss with the Banshee Queen, whose former life as Ranger-General of Silvermoon remains a deeply resonant memory to the people of Quel'Thalas.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ambassador Sunsorrow?",a="He is an envoy from the blood elves of Quel'Thalas, stationed directly in the Undercity's Royal Quarter beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner to oversee diplomatic ties and logistics between their peoples.",al={"sunsorrow who","who is sunsorrow","blood elf in undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a blood elf standing beside Sylvanas Windrunner?",a="Before her death and rebirth as the Banshee Queen, Lady Sylvanas was the Ranger-General of Silvermoon and died defending Quel'Thalas. The surviving blood elves maintain active diplomatic ties with her Forsaken kingdom, with Sunsorrow representing their interests.",al={"why elf in undercity","blood elf sylvanas court","sunsorrow purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="What tasks does Ambassador Sunsorrow give to travelers?",a="He assists in coordinating field communications and vital supplies, dispatching adventurers with orders and deliveries to key Forsaken strongholds such as the Sepulcher in Silverpine and Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad.",al={"sunsorrow quests","what does sunsorrow do","delivery to the sepulcher"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="How does he react to visitors in the Royal Quarter?",a="Sunsorrow maintains strict courtly etiquette. He expects proper decorum before the Banshee Queen and keeps a close eye on anyone granted an audience in the royal chamber.",al={"sunsorrow dialogue","speaking to sunsorrow"}},{q="Whose side is Ambassador Sunsorrow on?",a="Ambassador Sunsorrow represents the blood elves of Quel'Thalas. Stationed right beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in the Royal Quarter, he serves as an official diplomatic envoy fostering relations between his beleaguered people and the Forsaken.",al={"ambassador sunsorrow faction","who does sunsorrow serve","is sunsorrow horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Ambassador Sunsorrow want?",a="Sunsorrow seeks to maintain strong diplomatic ties between Quel'Thalas and the Forsaken. To that end, he coordinates communication across Lordaeron, dispatching couriers and couriering vital messages to Forsaken bastions like the Sepulcher and Tarren Mill.",al={"sunsorrow motives","what is sunsorrow doing in undercity","sunsorrow goals"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Ambassador Sunsorrow tied to?",a="Sunsorrow answers directly to the leadership of Quel'Thalas as their formal emissary. In the Undercity, he works alongside his fellow blood elf Cyssa Dawnrose under the watchful gaze of the Banshee Queen, Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"sunsorrow allies","who does sunsorrow work with","sunsorrow connections"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Sunsorrow is a visible reminder of their Queen's noble heritage and a rare living ally welcome at the foot of her throne.",["faction:Horde"]="Sunsorrow provides vital logistical dispatches for Horde travelers, routing hands and supplies through the Forsaken holdings of Silverpine Forest and Hillsbrad."},kw={"ambassador sunsorrow","blood elf","diplomat","envoy","royal quarter","sunsorrow","sylvanas windrunner","undercity"},rel={"npc:sylvanas-windrunner","subzone:royal-quarter","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:tarren-mill"},src={"Ambassador Sunsorrow"}}
E["npc:anastasia-hartwell"] = {t="npc",n="Anastasia Hartwell",z="undercity",s="Anastasia Hartwell is a prominent Forsaken mage trainer residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. She guides fledgling and developing spellcasters in mastering the arcane arts and oversees vital magical research and field missions across Lordaeron and beyond.",h="Anastasia Hartwell is a prominent Forsaken mage trainer residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",sec={{t="Arcane Mastery in the Ruins",b="Standing within the dark, echoing chambers of the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Anastasia Hartwell instructs Forsaken and Horde mages in channeling arcane energies. Though the kingdom of Lordaeron fell to ruin, former human practitioners like Anastasia have preserved their scholarly traditions in undeath. She maintains that magic demands strict discipline, warning any traveler she meets that careless incantations will quickly consume the untrained.",sp=0},{t="Field Research and Relics",b="Beyond fundamental spell instruction, Anastasia directs promising students toward vital field investigations. She dispatches mages into Tirisfal Glades, including the blighted grounds of the Balnir Farmstead and ruined alchemist workshops, to recover lost reagents and salvage remnants of forgotten arcane lore. Through her tasks, practitioners learn that securing magical dominance requires braving the hazardous ruins of their former homeland.",sp=0},{t="Allies of the Craft",b="Anastasia's connections reach well beyond the borders of Tirisfal. As Horde spellcasters grow in proficiency, she coordinates with fellow trainers in distant lands, such as Deino in Orgrimmar, and directs advanced students toward solitary masters like Tabetha in the swamplands of Dustwallow Marsh. Her guidance ensures that Forsaken mages remain woven into the wider tapestry of the Horde's magical pursuits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Anastasia Hartwell?",a="Anastasia Hartwell is a Forsaken mage trainer located in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. She teaches spells to developing mages and provides specialized assignments to retrieve arcane artifacts and reagents across Lordaeron.",al={"anastasia hartwell","who is anastasia","hartwell undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Anastasia Hartwell?",a="She is located in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, gathered among other arcane practitioners and trainers under the city's vaulted subterranean ceilings.",al={"anastasia hartwell location","where is anastasia hartwell","undercity mage trainer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Anastasia say to non-mages?",a="She offers cautious advice to non-mage visitors, warning them to be wary of magic as they journey across the world, noting that it readily burns the untrained.",al={"anastasia gossip","anastasia dialogue","hartwell advice"}},{q="What quests does Anastasia Hartwell offer?",a="Anastasia offers various training assignments for mages, including investigating the Balnir Farmstead, exploring ruined alchemist shops for supplies, and liaising with distant teachers such as Deino in Orgrimmar and Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"anastasia quests","hartwell tasks","undercity mage quests"},gp=true},{q="Is Anastasia Hartwell related to other Hartwells in Tirisfal?",a="She shares a surname with other Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades, such as Andrew Hartwell and Geoffrey Hartwell, pointing to common familial roots in pre-plague Lordaeron.",al={"hartwell family","andrew hartwell","geoffrey hartwell"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Anastasia send mages to the Balnir Farmstead?",a="She directs mages to the Balnir Farmstead in Tirisfal Glades to recover specific items and conduct research into arcane remnants preserved in the blighted countryside.",al={"balnir farmstead quest","why balnir farmstead","hartwell balnir"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Anastasia Hartwell on?",a="Anastasia Hartwell stands firmly with the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed deep within the Undercity's Magic Quarter, she serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner by preparing newly risen mages to harness the arcane in defense of their fledgling kingdom.",al={"anastasia hartwell faction","who does anastasia hartwell serve","anastasia hartwell loyalty"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Anastasia Hartwell here?",a="She resides in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity to train aspiring Forsaken and Horde practitioners in the arcane arts. She offers guidance to fledgling spellcasters, warning the uninitiated of magic's perils while directing capable mages on critical missions across Lordaeron and beyond.",al={"why is anastasia hartwell in undercity","what is anastasia hartwell doing here","anastasia hartwell role"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Anastasia Hartwell want?",a="She seeks to ensure that arcane practitioners are disciplined, capable, and cautious, frequently reminding outsiders that wild power burns the untrained. Through rigorous tasks and magical investigations, she works to strengthen the arcane capabilities of the Forsaken.",al={"anastasia hartwell goals","what are anastasia hartwell's motives"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Anastasia Hartwell is an essential mentor for Horde mages passing through the Undercity, training higher spell ranks and commissioning vital class quests.",["race:Undead"]="She represents the continuation of Dalaran and Lordaeron's esteemed arcane traditions among the Forsaken, preserved even through the tragedy of undeath.",["faction:Horde"]="Through partnerships with trainers like Deino in Orgrimmar, Anastasia bridges Lordaeron's arcane heritage with the broader magical endeavors of the Horde."},kw={"anastasia","balnir","deino","forsaken","hartwell","lordaeron","mage","magic quarter","tabetha","trainer","undercity"},rel={"subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","quest:1882","quest:1960","quest:1943","npc:deino","npc:tabetha"},src={"Anastasia Hartwell"}}
E["npc:andron-gant"] = {t="npc",n="Andron Gant",z="undercity",s="Andron Gant is a reclusive, frequently intoxicated Forsaken residing in the murky depths of the Apothecarium in the Undercity, handling occasional research commissions and relic recoveries for local scholars.",h="Andron Gant is a reclusive, frequently intoxicated Forsaken residing in the murky depths of the Apothecarium...",sec={{t="A Slurring Informant",b="Lounging amidst the noxious fumes of the Apothecarium, Andron Gant rarely ventures beyond the safety of the Undercity's stone walls. To the casual observer, he appears to be little more than a drunken scholar, occasionally hiring adventurous couriers to retrieve obscure relics like the Tablet of Beth'Amara or the Tablet of Markri from distant shores on behalf of local mages. However, beneath his liquor-soaked demeanor lies a clandestine operative. Gant secretly serves as an informant for the Syndicate, funneling sensitive intelligence out of the Forsaken capital in exchange for coin and illicit favors.",sp=0},{t="Unmasked by the Deathstalkers",b="Gant's treacherous dealings did not escape the notice of Undercity's intelligence network. When the Syndicate dispatched a courier named Astor Hadren to collect a ledger of compromised data, aspiring operatives within the Deathstalkers intercepted the runner. Disguised as Hadren, an agent was able to trick the drunken Gant into parting with his incriminating ledger without raising an eyebrow, handing Lord Varimathras definitive proof of Gant's treason against the Forsaken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Andron Gant?",a="Andron Gant is located inside the Undercity, lingering in the lower levels of the Apothecarium district.",al={"andron gant location","where is andron gant","gant undercity location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Andron Gant interested in Azshara tablets?",a="Gant acts as an intermediary for certain Undercity mages, arranging payments to scavengers and contacts like Jediga to recover ancient relics from the ruins of Azshara.",al={"andron gant azshara","tablet of markri andron gant","why does gant want tablets"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Andron Gant's connection to the Syndicate?",a="Despite living within the heart of the Forsaken capital, Gant secretly acts as an informant for the Syndicate, collecting intelligence into ledgers to smuggle to human outlaws.",al={"gant syndicate","is andron gant a traitor","who does andron gant work for"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Who exposed Andron Gant's treachery?",a="The Deathstalkers, the assassin and espionage order answering to Lord Varimathras, intercepted Gant's Syndicate courier and tricked him into handing over his spy ledger.",al={"who caught andron gant","deathstalkers andron gant","varimathras andron gant"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Who is Andron Gant?",a="Andron Gant is a Forsaken resident who frequents the Apothecarium in the Undercity. To outward appearances, he is little more than a habitual drunkard who rarely ventures outside the capital, acting as a broker for odd scholarly tasks like procuring ancient tablets for local mages.",al={"who is andron gant","andron gant lore","who is gant"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Andron Gant on?",a="While he lives among the Forsaken in the Undercity, Gant secretly works as an informant for the Syndicate. He gathers intelligence from within the capital and passes sensitive ledgers to Syndicate messengers, making him a covert traitor to the Dark Lady's realm.",al={"is andron gant loyal","who does andron gant serve","andron gant loyalty"},sp=1,it="side",add=true},{q="What does Andron Gant want?",a="Publicly, Gant spends his time drinking and brokering curiosities, such as paying adventurers to retrieve relics like the Tablet of Markri from Azshara for the Undercity's mages. In secret, his main endeavor is compiling sensitive ledgers and intelligence to sell to the Syndicate.",al={"what does andron want","andron gant motives","andron gant goals"},sp=1,it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Andron Gant in the Undercity?",a="Gant stays sequestered in the Apothecarium under the pretense of being a harmless, drunken scholar and broker. The Undercity provides him the ideal cover to quietly gather intelligence and maintain a covert channel of communication with outside conspirators.",al={"why is andron gant here","why is andron in undercity","andron gant apothecarium"},sp=1,it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Forsaken rogues climbing the ranks of the Deathstalkers learn firsthand through Gant how drunkenness and complacency can unravel even the tightest espionage operations.",["race:Undead"]="Gant serves as a stark reminder that loyalty among the Forsaken is never guaranteed, and human criminal factions like the Syndicate have eyes even within Lordaeron's catacombs."},kw={"andron gant","apothecarium","astor hadren","deathstalkers","jediga","tablet of markri","varimathras"},rel={"npc:varimathras","subzone:apothecarium","topic:syndicate","topic:forsaken","zone:undercity","zone:azshara"},src={"Andron Gant"}}
E["npc:austil-de-mon"] = {t="npc",n="Austil de Mon",z="undercity",s="Austil de Mon is a Forsaken warrior trainer stationed in Brill within Tirisfal Glades. Based out of the Gallows' End Tavern, he instructs newly risen warriors looking to hone their martial prowess in service of the Dark Lady.",h="Austil de Mon is a Forsaken warrior trainer stationed in Brill within Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Veteran in Gallows' End",b="Found inside the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, Austil de Mon serves as one of the earliest instructors for Forsaken warriors venturing out of Deathknell. While the living once populated the inn to drink and rest, Austil now uses the gloomy refuge to teach newly liberated undead how to channel raw martial discipline and ruthless combat techniques against the kingdom's surrounding foes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Austil de Mon?",a="Austil de Mon is an undead warrior trainer located on the grounds of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, offering training to Forsaken fighters.",al={"austil de mon","austil","who is austil"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Austil de Mon?",a="You can find him stationed in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, Tirisfal Glades, just north of the Undercity.",al={"austil de mon location","where is austil","austil de mon map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does he play in Brill?",a="He instructs novice warriors in fighting techniques, stances, and martial abilities to help strengthen the Forsaken military against local threats.",al={"what does austil do","austil trainer","austil role"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Austil de Mon on?",a="Austil de Mon is loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. As part of the nascent undead kingdom carved from Lordaeron's ruins, he serves alongside his brethren in the Horde, offering his martial experience to hone the strength of incoming Forsaken warriors fighting to defend Tirisfal Glades from the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade.",al={"austil de mon faction","austil de mon loyalty","who does austil serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Austil de Mon want?",a="Austil de Mon seeks to strengthen the Forsaken military line against Lordaeron's many enemies. By training freshly awakened warriors at Gallows' End Tavern, he works to ensure that those who take up arms under the Dark Lady possess the discipline and technique required to survive against both the relentless Scourge and the fanatical zealots of the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"austil de mon goal","what does austil want","austil de mon purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Austil de Mon in Brill?",a="Austil is stationed at Gallows' End Tavern in Brill to greet and drill fighters emerging from Deathknell. Because Brill serves as the primary outpost and logistical center for northern Tirisfal Glades, warrior trainers like Austil are essential to turn newly risen undead into capable front-line combatants before they march deeper into contested territory.",al={"why is austil in brill","why is austil de mon here","austil de mon location why"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="For Forsaken warriors leaving Deathknell, Austil de Mon is one of the primary mentors providing guidance and formal ability training in Tirisfal Glades.",["race:Undead"]="Austil helps steel newly risen undead into formidable frontline combatants prepared to defend Lordaeron against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade."},kw={"austil de mon","brill","forsaken warrior","gallows' end tavern","tirisfal glades","warrior trainer"},rel={"subzone:brill","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:1818"},src={"Austil de Mon"}}
E["npc:bethor-iceshard"] = {t="npc",n="Bethor Iceshard",z="undercity",s="Bethor Iceshard is a powerful Forsaken mage based in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Presiding over the arcane and shadow practitioners within the Temple of the Damned, he commands considerable authority in Sylvanas's realm. Beneath his chilly demeanor lies a past entwined with old friends torn apart by the Scourge.",h="Bethor Iceshard is a powerful Forsaken mage based in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",sec={{t="Master of the Magic Quarter",b="Standing within the Temple of the Damned, Bethor Iceshard oversees the practitioners of the arcane arts and shadow magic in the Undercity. Respected and feared for his intellect and icy resolve, Bethor wields sufficient political and magical weight to give direct instructions to provincial magistrates across Lordaeron. He directs agents of the Forsaken to secure valuable grimoires, investigate arcane anomalies, and stamp out rival powers that threaten the Undercity's dominion.",sp=0},{t="Bonds of Apprenticehood",b="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, Bethor was a mortal apprentice studying magic alongside two close companions: Gunther Arcanus and Thule Ravenclaw. As a testament to their fellowship, the three students wove their practice wands together. The Scourge shattered that bond entirely. When death and dark magic swept across the kingdom, Thule Ravenclaw willfully surrendered his soul to the Lich King, Gunther perished and rose on an isolated island in Brightwater Lake, and Bethor succumbed only to later break free as Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="Old Friends and Bittersweet Reunions",b="Bethor has not forgotten his former companions. Tracking down powerful undead spellcasters throughout Tirisfal and Silverpine, he dispatches agents to discern whether rogue practitioners serve the Lich King or might be turned toward the Forsaken cause. When Bethor identifies Gunther Arcanus raising the dead on Brightwater Lake, he works patiently to bring his old friend into Lady Sylvanas's fold, while offering no mercy to Thule Ravenclaw, whose willing betrayal doomed their past brotherhood.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Bethor Iceshard?",a="Bethor Iceshard is a high-ranking Forsaken mage who presides over the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. He coordinates magical research, rogue intelligence, and covert arcane operations on behalf of the Dark Lady.",al={"bethor iceshard","who is bethor","bethor lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Bethor Iceshard be found?",a="Bethor resides inside the Temple of the Damned, the central structure situated in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"where is bethor","bethor location","find bethor iceshard"},it="why_here",gp=true},{q="What is Bethor's history with Gunther Arcanus?",a="Bethor and Gunther were close friends during their days as apprentice mages in Lordaeron. After dying during the Scourge invasion, both eventually broke free from the Lich King's control, and Bethor orchestrated Gunther's recruitment into the Forsaken.",al={"gunther and bethor","gunther arcanus friendship","how does bethor know gunther"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Who was Thule Ravenclaw to Bethor?",a="Thule Ravenclaw was the third member of Bethor and Gunther's apprentice circle. Unlike the other two, Thule willingly pledged his soul to the Lich King during the Scourge invasion, becoming a hated necromancer residing at Fenris Isle.",al={"thule ravenclaw connection","thule and bethor","bethor ravenclaw"},it="ties"},{q="What is the story behind Bethor's wand?",a="In their youth, Bethor, Gunther, and Thule wove their practice wands together as a symbol of their eternal friendship. That braided keepsake remains a poignant artifact tying the three fractured spellcasters to their mortal past.",al={"woven wand","wand to bethor","bethor apprentice wand"},it="item"},{q="What role does Bethor play in Forsaken society?",a="Bethor serves as one of the leading arcane authorities in the Undercity. He guides newly risen magi and warlocks, directs military intelligence regarding rogue necromancers, and holds authority over regional Forsaken civil officials such as magistrate Sevren.",al={"bethor role","what does bethor do","bethor authority"},it="fame"},{q="Whose side is Bethor Iceshard on?",a="Bethor is fully devoted to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. From his sanctum in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, he commands significant authority within the Forsaken hierarchy, directing arcane practitioners and marshaling resources against the Scourge and other threats to their people.",al={"bethor iceshard faction","bethor iceshard allegiance","who does bethor serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Bethor Iceshard want?",a="Bethor seeks to strengthen the Forsaken's arcane power and safeguard their fledgling kingdom. This includes recruiting gifted practitioners like his former friend Gunther Arcanus to the Forsaken cause, while ruthlessly confronting the Scourge and holding traitors like Thule Ravenclaw accountable for selling their souls to the Lich King.",al={"bethor iceshard goals","what does bethor want","bethor iceshard motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity?",a="Bethor presides over the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, serving as a leader for the Forsaken's mages and warlocks. He remains here to orchestrate arcane affairs, guide promising spellcasters, and coordinate strategic efforts across Lordaeron from the heart of the capital.",al={"why is bethor in undercity","bethor iceshard location lore","why is bethor here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For Forsaken mages, Bethor represents the pinnacle of perseverance, demonstrating that the arcane arts can thrive even within the cold grasp of undeath.",["race:Undead"]="Bethor's personal tragedy mirrors that of many Forsaken: severed from cherished friendships and homes by the Scourge, only to face former allies as bitter enemies.",["faction:Horde"]="Bethor coordinates crucial offensive magic and counter-necromancy operations that protect the Horde's foothold across Lordaeron."},kw={"bethor iceshard","forsaken","gunther arcanus","magic quarter","prodigal lich","temple of the damned","thule ravenclaw","undercity"},rel={"npc:gunther-arcanus","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:405","quest:411","quest:446","quest:491","topic:forsaken"},src={"Bethor Iceshard"}}
E["npc:cain-firesong"] = {t="npc",n="Cain Firesong",z="undercity",s="Cain Firesong is a Forsaken mage trainer located in the settlement of Brill within Tirisfal Glades. He assists fledgling practitioners of the arcane as they grow in power, guiding them before directing them onward to deeper studies in the Undercity. When not instructing initiates, he pursues his own unsavory experiments in Brill's laboratory.",h="Cain Firesong is a Forsaken mage trainer located in the settlement of Brill within Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Practitioner in Brill",b="While many Forsaken spellcasters delve into shadow or necromancy, Cain Firesong maintains mastery over traditional arcane disciplines. Stationed in Brill, he serves as an early mentor to Forsaken mages venturing forth from Deathknell. According to local Deathguards, Cain arrived too late to secure lodgings at the Gallows' End Tavern and instead took up residence around Brill's laboratory. There, amidst brewing concoctions and alchemical apparatuses, he quietly pursues esoteric research between lessons.",sp=0},{t="Guiding New Talent",b="As novice mages under his tutelage advance beyond their preliminary studies in Tirisfal Glades, Cain ensures they do not stagnate. Recognizing the limits of what a roadside laboratory can offer, he directs his most capable students to seek out Anastasia Hartwell, a master sorceress residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Cain Firesong?",a="Cain Firesong is a Forsaken mage trainer stationed in Brill in Tirisfal Glades. He teaches arcane spells to fledgling Horde spellcasters and directs advanced students toward the Undercity.",al={"who is cain firesong","cain firesong lore","cain firesong brill"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Cain Firesong stay in Brill?",a="According to the local Deathguards, Cain arrived too late to claim a room at the Gallows' End Tavern. Instead, he made a home around Brill's laboratory, where he works on arcane and unsavory projects.",al={"where is cain firesong","cain firesong location","cain tavern room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does Cain send mages after their initial training?",a="Once a mage has advanced sufficiently under his guidance, Cain directs them to travel down into the Undercity's Magic Quarter to continue their instruction under Anastasia Hartwell.",al={"cain firesong quest","who does cain send mages to","speak with anastasia"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Cain Firesong on?",a="Cain Firesong stands firmly with the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed in Brill, he serves the Dark Lady by schooling newly risen undead in the arcane arts, ensuring that Forsaken spellcasters have the magical prowess needed to defend Tirisfal Glades and advance the realm of the Undercity.",al={"cain firesong faction","cain firesong loyalty","who does cain firesong serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Cain Firesong want?",a="Cain aims to hone the arcane discipline of fledging Forsaken mages before sending them onward to master trainers in the Undercity. Outside of his teaching duties, he keeps to Brill's laboratory, quietly pursuing his own unsavory magical experiments away from the crowded common rooms of the tavern.",al={"cain firesong goal","what is cain firesong doing","cain firesong purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Cain Firesong here?",a="Cain is stationed in Brill to act as the primary arcane instructor for young mages emerging from Deathknell. After arriving too late to secure lodgings at the Gallows' End Tavern, he set up his quarters and workspace in the town laboratory, where he can both instruct initiates and conduct his arcane studies undisturbed.",al={"why is cain firesong in brill","cain firesong location reason","why is cain firesong here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For young Forsaken mages stepping out from Deathknell, Cain Firesong is your primary mentor in Tirisfal Glades before you are summoned to the Undercity.",["race:Undead"]="Cain proves that even in undeath, the arcane traditions of former human magi remain a potent weapon for the Forsaken."},kw={"anastasia hartwell","arcane","brill","cain firesong","gallows' end tavern","mage trainer","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","quest:1881","quest:1959","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","topic:forsaken"},src={"Cain Firesong"}}
E["npc:carendin-halgar"] = {t="npc",n="Carendin Halgar",z="undercity",s="Carendin Halgar is a prominent Forsaken warlock trainer residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Sharp-tongued and notoriously short on patience, he oversees the training of fledgling practitioners of the dark arts. He instructs aspiring warlocks on how to subjugate powerful demonic entities from the Twisting Nether, notably teaching the rituals to bind Voidwalkers and Succubi.",h="Carendin Halgar is a prominent Forsaken warlock trainer residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",sec={{t="Master of the Dark Arts",b="Within the noxious gloom of the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Carendin Halgar instructs those who delve into the Twisting Nether. He demands focus and obedience, holding little tolerance for failure, hesitation, or weakness. Under his watchful gaze, warlocks are pushed beyond basic incantations into the dangerous mastery of summonings and soul manipulation, cementing the Forsaken's ruthless approach to demonic servitude.",sp=0},{t="Subjugating the Nether",b="Carendin's core tutelage revolves around binding ever more dangerous demons to the summoner's will. He sends his students across Lordaeron and beyond to retrieve ancient runes, runic stones, and the distilled pure essence of mortals to complete treacherous summoning circles. Whether commanding a shadowy creature of the void or luring a temptress succubus into subjugation, Carendin ensures the warlock dominates the demon before it can devour its master.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Carendin Halgar be found?",a="Carendin Halgar is located in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, gathered among the other practitioners of fel and shadow magic.",al={"carendin halgar location","undercity warlock trainer location","where is halgar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Carendin Halgar play for warlocks?",a="He serves as a mentor and questgiver for Horde warlocks, instructing them in the rituals required to summon and permanently bind major demons, such as the Voidwalker and the Succubus.",al={"what does carendin do","halgar purpose","carendin quests"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Carendin Halgar's personality like?",a="He is notoriously blunt, demanding, and utterly devoid of patience. He expects prompt results from his pupils and despises wasting time or dealing with excuses.",al={"halgar temperament","is carendin nice","carendin halgar lore"}},{q="Why does Carendin require pure hearts for summoning rituals?",a="In his lessons on summoning a succubus, Halgar tasks acolytes with procuring the untainted hearts of the pure, using their innocence and essence as bait to entice and ensnare the fiendish demon in a binding circle.",al={"hearts of the pure purpose","succubus summoning carendin","why hearts of the pure"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does Carendin Halgar interact with warlocks outside the Undercity?",a="Yes, Carendin maintains contact with other senior warlocks across the Horde, including Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar, coordinating efforts to advance the dark arts across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"carendin connections","halgar orgrimmar","gan'rul bloodeye carendin"}},{q="Who does Carendin send advanced warlocks to see?",a="Once an acolyte demonstrates sufficient mastery over basic demons, Carendin directs them outward to seek further esoteric instruction, such as sending them to find the eccentric summoner Strahad Farsan in the Barrens.",al={"seeking strahad","who does carendin send you to","halgar next mentor"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar is a prominent Forsaken warlock trainer residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Known for his stern and impatient demeanor, he instructs aspiring practitioners in the dark arts of summoning and binding demonic entities to their will.",al={"who is carendin halgar","carendin halgar lore","who is halgar"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Carendin Halgar on?",a="Carendin is loyal to the Forsaken and the Horde. He operates openly from the Undercity, dedicating his dark expertise to strengthening the magical might of Lady Sylvanas's followers against their shared enemies across Lordaeron.",al={"carendin halgar faction","who does carendin serve","is carendin loyal to sylvanas"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Carendin Halgar want?",a="Carendin seeks to shape disciplined, capable warlocks who command demons without hesitation or weakness. He demands rigorous adherence to binding rituals and tests his students thoroughly to ensure they control their summoned servitors rather than falling victim to them.",al={"what does carendin want","carendin halgar motives","carendin halgar goals"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Carendin Halgar here?",a="He is stationed in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity to mentor emerging Forsaken warlocks. Beneath the ruins of Capital City, he oversees the hazardous summonings necessary to bind greater minions of the Twisting Nether into service.",al={"why is carendin in undercity","why is carendin halgar here","carendin halgar location reason"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar tied to?",a="Carendin coordinates with fellow practitioners across the Horde, including mentors like Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar and Talionia. When his students outgrow his instruction, he directs them onward to more specialized masters such as Strahad Farsan in the Barrens.",al={"carendin halgar allies","carendin halgar connections","who does carendin work with"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Carendin Halgar is a crucial mentor in Lordaeron, guiding warlocks through the grueling trials required to dominate and bind both Voidwalkers and Succubi.",["race:Undead"]="Reflecting the uncompromising spirit of the Forsaken, Carendin shows no pity or hesitation, viewing demonic entities strictly as tools to be broken and exploited.",["faction:Horde"]="Carendin serves as the primary eastern conduit for Horde warlocks, coordinating training with fellow dark practitioners across the sea in Kalimdor."},kw={"carendin halgar","creature of the void","forsaken","halgar","magic quarter","succubus","the binding","trainer","undercity","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:1473","quest:1471","quest:1476","quest:1472","quest:1798","npc:gan-rul-bloodeye"},src={"Carendin Halgar"}}
E["npc:elder-darkcore"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Darkcore",z="undercity",s="Elder Darkcore is an ancient spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival within the throne room of the Ruins of Lordaeron above the Undercity. Representing the honored ancestors of the world, he offers his blessing and festive tokens to travelers who seek him out. His presence marks a peaceful, reflective moment amidst the ruins of a fallen human kingdom.",h="Elder Darkcore is an ancient spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival within the throne room of the Ruins...",sec={{t="A Spirit in the Throne Room",b="During the annual Lunar Festival, the spirits of ancient elders manifest across Azeroth to share their wisdom with adventurers. Elder Darkcore takes his vigil in one of the world's most somber locations: the royal throne room in the Ruins of Lordaeron, directly above the entrance to the Undercity. Surrounded by the blood-stained floor where King Terenas Menethil II fell, this spectral ancestor offers a Coin of Ancestry and his blessing to those brave enough to enter the heart of Forsaken territory to pay their respects.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Darkcore?",a="Elder Darkcore is one of the honored spectral ancestors who manifests during the seasonal Lunar Festival. He appears in the throne room above the Undercity to bestow blessings and Coins of Ancestry on visitors.",al={"elder darkcore","darkcore","who is darkcore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Elder Darkcore?",a="He is located in the ruined throne room of Capital City, in the Ruins of Lordaeron right above the entrance descent leading down into the Undercity.",al={"where is darkcore","darkcore location","undercity elder"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Elder Darkcore hostile to the Alliance?",a="Elder Darkcore himself is neutral and welcomes all travelers who come to honor him. However, because he stands within the Forsaken stronghold of the Ruins of Lordaeron, Alliance adventurers must carefully evade the hostile guards patrolling nearby.",al={"can alliance talk to darkcore","is darkcore horde","undercity lunar festival alliance"},it="hostile",gp=true},{q="What does honoring Elder Darkcore give you?",a="Paying respects to him completes the festival quest to honor his memory, rewarding a Coin of Ancestry and a lucky red packet containing festive treats.",al={"darkcore reward","darkcore quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Elder Darkcore on?",a="Elder Darkcore does not align with the modern conflicts of the Horde or Alliance. As an honored ancestral spirit participating in the Lunar Festival, he stands peacefully above mortal squabbles, welcoming any traveler who approaches him with respect, regardless of which banner they march under.",al={"elder darkcore faction","is elder darkcore horde or alliance","darkcore allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Elder Darkcore want?",a="Elder Darkcore seeks to share the ancient wisdom and blessings of the ancestors during the Lunar Festival. He waits for travelers to pay their respects to the past, offering his blessing and tokens of elder heritage to those who honor his long-enduring memory.",al={"what does elder darkcore want","elder darkcore purpose","why visit elder darkcore"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Elder Darkcore in the Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="Elder Darkcore appears in the ruined throne room above the Undercity as part of the worldwide observance of the Lunar Festival. The spirits of the ancients manifest in places steeped in profound history and sorrow across Azeroth, allowing mortals to commune with ancestral memories even amid fallen kingdoms.",al={"why is elder darkcore in undercity","why ruins of lordaeron darkcore","elder darkcore location lore"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Visiting Elder Darkcore requires slipping past high-level Forsaken sentries and royal guards stationed around Capital City's ruins, making him one of the festival's most perilous stops for the Alliance.",["race:Undead"]="Elder Darkcore lingers mere steps from the surface elevators of the Undercity, standing upon the very stones where the kingdom of Lordaeron was torn down."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","darkcore","elder darkcore","lunar festival","ruins of lordaeron","throne room","undercity"},rel={"quest:8648","zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Elder Darkcore"}}
E["npc:godrick-farsan"] = {t="npc",n="Godrick Farsan",z="undercity",s="Godrick Farsan is an undead warlock assistant located in the Undercity, serving alongside Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter. Despite being entirely blind, he possesses mystical senses that allow him to perceive the dark energies and souls around him.",h="Godrick Farsan is an undead warlock assistant located in the Undercity, serving alongside Carendin Halgar in...",sec={{t="Eyes in the Dark",b="Situated amidst the summoning circles of the Magic Quarter, Godrick Farsan aids Master Carendin Halgar in guiding aspiring Forsaken warlocks. Though he lacks physical sight, Godrick claims to see through unconventional, demonic means, perceiving the world through shadows and residual soul energies. He tests practitioners seeking to bind greater demonic entities, dispatching them to gather pure hearts and essences needed for intricate summoning rituals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Godrick Farsan?",a="Godrick Farsan is a Forsaken warlock stationed in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. He serves as an assistant to Master Carendin Halgar, aiding in the instruction and rituals of fledgling warlocks.",al={"godrick farsan","who is godrick"},it="identity"},{q="How can Godrick see if he is blind?",a="While Godrick has lost his mortal eyesight, he perceives his surroundings through magical senses. He taps into the flow of fel power and the spiritual resonance of souls to navigate and observe the world around him.",al={"is godrick blind","how does godrick see"}},{q="Is Godrick related to Strahad Farsan?",a="Sharing the same surname and affinity for demonology, Godrick is believed to be kin to Strahad Farsan, the warlock master residing above Ratchet in the Barrens.",al={"strahad farsan relation","strahad farsan brother","are godrick and strahad related"},it="ties"},{q="What role does he play in warlock training?",a="Godrick helps oversee the binding rites for warlocks, specifically guiding them through tasks such as acquiring pure hearts to lure and bind a succubus.",al={"godrick warlock quests","hearts of the pure quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Godrick Farsan on?",a="Godrick is loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, dwelling deep within the Undercity. He serves alongside Carendin Halgar, aiding practitioners of the dark arts and guiding Horde warlocks who seek to master demonic powers.",al={"godrick farsan allegiance","who does godrick serve","godrick farsan faction"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Godrick Farsan here?",a="You will find Godrick lurking in the shadowy quarters of the Undercity as the devoted assistant to Carendin Halgar. He remains stationed here to oversee trials for aspiring warlocks, helping them bind potent demonic entities such as the succubus.",al={"why is godrick in undercity","godrick farsan purpose undercity","what is godrick farsan doing here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Godrick Farsan want?",a="Godrick seeks to further the dark studies of the Undercity's warlocks. Through grueling trials involving ritual components—such as the hearts of the pure and the innocent—he tests your resolve and ability to command dangerous demons of the Nether.",al={"godrick farsan goal","what does godrick want","godrick farsan motives"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Forsaken warlocks looking to master the art of summoning a succubus must consult Godrick to prepare the necessary lures and understand the devouring nature of demonic servants.",["race:Undead"]="Godrick exemplifies the Forsaken warlock philosophy, embracing physical ruin and blindness while honing dark magical awareness to replace mortal frailties."},kw={"carendin halgar","godrick farsan","hearts of the pure","strahad farsan","succubus","undercity","warlock"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1476","quest:1472","npc:strahad-farsan","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"Godrick Farsan"}}
E["npc:gordon-wendham"] = {t="npc",n="Gordon Wendham",z="undercity",s="Gordon Wendham is a Forsaken weaponsmith and merchant operating out of the bustling Trade Quarter in the Undercity. He equips newly arrived champions and local defenders of the Dark Lady with reliable steel, blades, and bludgeons. Beyond hawking basic armaments, he frequently serves as a local point of contact for couriers arriving from the surface.",h="Gordon Wendham is a Forsaken weaponsmith and merchant operating out of the bustling Trade Quarter in the...",sec={{t="Armaments of the Trade Quarter",b="Situated amidst the damp stonework and chemical canals of the Undercity's Trade Quarter, Gordon Wendham provides essential weaponry to those taking up arms for the Forsaken. From basic daggers and hand axes to sturdy broadswords and maces, his stock caters to fledgling fighters who need dependable iron before venturing out into the contested reaches of Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="A Courier's Destination",b="Beyond his merchant trade, Wendham is integrated into the capital's busy logistics network. Travelers sent on errands from flight masters and couriers—such as those connecting from the bat handlers atop the ruins—are often directed straight to his stall. His central location in the Trade Quarter makes him an accessible and recognizable fixture for coordinating basic supplies and dispatches throughout the underground city.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gordon Wendham?",a="Gordon Wendham is an undead merchant stationed in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity. He sells standard martial weapons and serves as a contact for couriers arriving in the capital.",al={"gordon wendham lore","who is wendham","undercity gordon"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Gordon Wendham located?",a="You can find him tending his weapon stall in the Trade Quarter, the commercial ring situated within the subterranean halls of the Undercity.",al={"gordon wendham location","where is gordon undercity","trade quarter weapon vendor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does he sell?",a="He offers a wide array of basic, standard-grade weapons, including swords, daggers, maces, staves, axes, and various thrown armaments suited for leveling adventurers.",al={"wendham wares","what does gordon sell","gordon wendham weapons"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What quests involve him?",a="He is tied into introductory delivery runs connecting the surface bat roosts to the undercity interior, including deliveries between himself and bat handler Michael Garrett.",al={"gordon wendham quests","ride to the undercity","michael garrett quest"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Gordon Wendham on?",a="Gordon Wendham is loyal to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, standing aligned with the broader Horde. From his shop in the Undercity, he supports his undead kin by outfitting travelers and soldiers defending their reclaimed kingdom beneath the ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"gordon wendham faction","who does gordon wendham serve","is gordon wendham horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Gordon Wendham in the Undercity?",a="Gordon Wendham plies his trade as a weaponsmith in the bustling Trade Quarter of the Undercity. Surrounded by the subterranean halls of the Forsaken capital, he remains on hand to supply blades, axes, and bludgeons to anyone preparing to venture into the hostile lands above.",al={"why is gordon wendham here","gordon wendham purpose undercity","what brings gordon wendham here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For newly liberated Forsaken leaving Deathknell, merchants like Gordon Wendham in the Trade Quarter represent the practical backbone of their nascent nation's war effort.",["class:Warrior"]="Gordon offers dependable basic blades and blunt instruments for frontline fighters looking to practice their weapon proficiencies in the capital."},kw={"forsaken","gordon wendham","michael garrett","trade quarter","undercity","weapon vendor"},rel={"subzone:trade-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:6323","quest:6322","topic:forsaken","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Gordon Wendham"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-norman"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Norman",z="undercity",s="Innkeeper Norman tends the hearth at the primary tavern in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity. A quiet, diligent Forsaken, he offers travelers of the Horde respite, hearthstone bindings, and food suited to the varied tastes of both the living and the dead.",h="Innkeeper Norman tends the hearth at the primary tavern in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity.",sec={{t="Hospitality in the Sewers",b="Located in the bustling Trade Quarter beneath the ruined Capital City of Lordaeron, Innkeeper Norman provides lodging for emissaries, mercenaries, and adventurers passing through the Forsaken stronghold. Despite the damp chill and alchemical stenches of the Undercity, Norman's tavern remains a bustling hub for travelers looking to anchor their hearthstones, share news from across Azeroth, or prepare for expeditions into the Plaguelands.",sp=0},{t="Festive Eccentricities",b="While Norman typically keeps to his duties selling provisions and managing rooms, the seasonal arrival of Hallow's End reveals a more peculiar side. During the holiday, Norman participates in the seasonal revelry, demanding peculiar displays—such as clucking like a chicken—from adventurous patrons eager to earn holiday treats like Undercity mints.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Norman?",a="Innkeeper Norman is found inside the main tavern in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity, situated along the southern curve of the inner ring.",al={"norman location","undercity innkeeper location","where is norman"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does Innkeeper Norman provide?",a="He serves as a primary innkeeper for the Undercity. Players can bind their hearthstones to his tavern, purchase food and drink suited for both the living and the undead, or log out safely to earn rest.",al={"norman services","undercity hearthstone"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does Norman ask patrons to cluck like a chicken?",a="During the Hallow's End festival, Norman participates in traditional holiday trickery. Adventurers seeking special holiday mints must swallow their pride and cluck like a chicken to earn his favor.",al={"chicken clucking mints","norman chicken quest"}},{q="Is Norman related to Innkeeper Bates?",a="While they do not mention each other directly in life or undeath, no kinship between them is known. Their names together are a playful nod from the world's creators to the innkeeper Norman Bates from the film Psycho.",al={"norman bates connection","innkeeper bates norman"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Norman?",a="Innkeeper Norman is a Forsaken barkeep who tends the bustling tavern in the Undercity's Trade Quarter. While many undead have abandoned the comforts of their mortal lives, Norman caters to the weary travelers, soldiers, and emissaries making their way through Lady Sylvanas's subterranean stronghold, offering food, drink, and a place to rest.",al={"who is norman","innkeeper norman lore","norman undercity"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Norman on?",a="Norman is loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, and by extension serves the broader Horde. Located in the heart of the Trade Quarter, he opens his doors to visiting orcs, trolls, and tauren, offering them shelter beneath the ruins of Lordaeron while remaining fiercely devoted to his undead kin.",al={"norman faction","norman allegiance","is norman horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Innkeeper Norman here?",a="Norman manages the primary inn of the Undercity, stationed directly in the Trade Quarter where trade, travel, and politics intersect. Even in undeath, visitors and citizens need a gathering place to exchange rumors, bind hearthstones, and stock up on provisions, and Norman keeps the tavern running smoothly amid the gloom.",al={"why is norman in undercity","norman trade quarter","what is norman doing here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For living Horde allies visiting the Undercity, Norman's tavern is one of the few places offering a secure place to rest and recover amid an otherwise unwelcoming subterranean fortress.",["race:Undead"]="Norman offers fellow Forsaken a central gathering place in the heart of the Trade Quarter to rest their bones between assignments for the Dark Lady."},kw={"bates","hallow's end","hearthstone","innkeeper","norman","trade quarter","undercity"},rel={"subzone:trade-quarter","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","quest:8353","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Innkeeper Norman"}}
E["npc:josef-gregorian"] = {t="npc",n="Josef Gregorian",z="undercity",s="Josef Gregorian is a Forsaken tailoring trainer found working in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. He guides ambitious Horde tailors seeking to weave enchanted fabrics, providing expertise and directing them toward specialized garments.",h="Josef Gregorian is a Forsaken tailoring trainer found working in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",sec={{t="Weaver of the Magic Quarter",b="Amid the dim alchemical lanterns and damp vaults of the Magic Quarter, Josef Gregorian maintains the fine craft of tailoring for the Forsaken and their Horde allies. While life in the subterranean kingdom has turned cold, cloth-working remains vital for warlocks, mages, and priests who channel raw energies through woven fibers. Gregorian serves as a dependable instructor in the capital, ready to teach foundational patterns and direct advanced practitioners toward securing rare materials for enchanted attire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Josef Gregorian?",a="Josef Gregorian is located in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, practicing and teaching the tailoring craft among the city's casters and scholars.",al={"josef gregorian location","where is gregorian","undercity tailor trainer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Josef Gregorian serve in the Undercity?",a="He is a tailoring trainer who teaches sewing recipes and techniques to Horde crafters. He also offers instruction on obtaining rare materials to craft specialized caster vestments like the Robe of the Archmage or other enchanted garments.",al={"what does josef gregorian do","josef gregorian trainer","undercity tailoring"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What quests does Josef Gregorian offer?",a="Gregorian assists tailoring practitioners with quests such as Gathering Materials and fashioning Spellfire Robes, tasking crafters with collecting elusive reagents needed to produce potent cloth garments.",al={"josef gregorian quests","robe quests undercity"},gp=true},{q="Who is Josef Gregorian?",a="Josef Gregorian is an undead artisan who serves as a tailoring trainer within the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Like many Forsaken craftsmen, he has retained the fine skills of his former life, putting his knowledge of thread, cloth, and enchanted garments to work for Queen Sylvanas's people and their Horde allies.",al={"who is josef gregorian","josef gregorian lore","who is the tailor josef gregorian"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Josef Gregorian on?",a="He is loyal to the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed deep within the Undercity, he offers his tailoring knowledge, patterns, and trade wisdom exclusively to those who stand in service to the Dark Lady and the Horde.",al={"josef gregorian faction","is josef gregorian horde","who does josef gregorian serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Josef Gregorian in the Undercity?",a="Josef remains in the Undercity to practice and instruct others in the craft of tailoring. Setting up his workshop among the spellcasters and scholars of the Magic Quarter allows him to weave robes, enchanted garments, and cloth armor for adventurers venturing out into the Plaguelands and beyond.",al={"why is josef gregorian here","what brought josef gregorian to undercity","why is josef in the magic quarter"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="For Horde clothiers, Josef Gregorian is a prime contact in Lordaeron, offering instruction and guiding skilled weavers in gathering materials for powerful woven robes.",["race:Undead"]="Gregorian demonstrates that despite death and undeath, the delicate arts of human tailoring survived the fall of Lordaeron to serve the new Forsaken society."},kw={"gathering materials","josef gregorian","magic quarter","spellfire robes","tailoring trainer","undercity"},rel={"subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:1961","quest:1962","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Josef Gregorian"}}
E["npc:lor-themar-theron"] = {t="npc",n="Lor'themar Theron",z="undercity",s="Lor'themar Theron is the Regent Lord of Quel'Thalas, entrusted with governing the ruined kingdom of the blood elves while Prince Kael'thas is away. A veteran ranger lord and former second-in-command to Ranger-General Sylvanas Windrunner, he bears the heavy burden of keeping his shattered people alive in the wake of the Scourge invasion.",h="Lor'themar Theron is the Regent Lord of Quel'Thalas, entrusted with governing the ruined kingdom of the blood...",sec={{t="From Ranger Lord to Regent",b="Before the Third War, Lor'themar Theron spent centuries serving as a decorated commander of the Farstriders, defending the northern elven borders against the Amani trolls and rising to become second-in-command to Ranger-General Sylvanas Windrunner. When Arthas and the Scourge decimated Quel'Thalas and destroyed the Sunwell, Lor'themar was among the surviving veterans who rallied the living remnants. When Prince Kael'thas Sunstrider departed for the south—and eventually into the unknown seeking a cure for their people's devastating addiction to magic—he named Lor'themar Regent Lord to safeguard the kingdom in his absence.",sp=0},{t="The Weight of the Sunstriders",b="Lor'themar never sought the crown or the political labyrinth of elven nobility. By instinct, he remains a scout and a soldier who prefers a bow and plain orders to courtly diplomacy. Yet with the Sunstrider dynasty abroad and Quel'Thalas surrounded by undead prowling the Ghostlands, Theron oversees the grueling day-to-day survival of the blood elves. His duties frequently bring diplomatic entanglements with the kingdom's former defender, now the Banshee Queen ruling Undercity, whose aid the desperate survivors of Quel'Thalas find difficult to refuse.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lor'themar Theron?",a="He is the Regent Lord of Quel'Thalas and leader of the blood elves remaining in Azeroth. Formerly the second-in-command of the Farstriders under Sylvanas Windrunner, he was granted leadership of the homeland by Prince Kael'thas Sunstrider.",al={"lorthemar lore","who is regent lord","who leads blood elves"},it="identity"},{q="What is his relationship with Sylvanas Windrunner?",a="Lor'themar served as Sylvanas's trusted second-in-command during her life as Ranger-General of Silvermoon. Though they were longtime comrades in the Farstriders, her death, transformation into a banshee, and rule over the Forsaken have made their current relationship far more complicated and guarded.",al={"lorthemar and sylvanas","did lorthemar know sylvanas"},it="ties"},{q="Is Lor'themar the king of the blood elves?",a="No. Lor'themar holds the title of Regent Lord, governing in the name of Prince Kael'thas Sunstrider, who remains the rightful monarch and leader of the sin'dorei while away seeking a remedy for their arcane withdrawal.",al={"is lorthemar king","is he prince kaelthas","who rules quel'thalas"}},{q="What military background does he have?",a="He is a veteran ranger lord who fought in the Second War against the Old Horde and Amani trolls, and served as a warden of the Sunwell. He spent centuries leading Farstrider companies before politics forced him into rulership.",al={"was lorthemar a farstrider","is lorthemar a ranger"},it="fame"},{q="Whose side is Lor'themar Theron on?",a="Lor'themar serves Prince Kael'thas Sunstrider and the surviving blood elves of Quel'Thalas above all else. Though he currently acts as Regent Lord back home and works closely with Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, his ultimate loyalty remains bound entirely to the defense and survival of his devastated elven people.",al={"lorthemar allegiance","who does lorthemar serve","is lorthemar horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Lor'themar Theron want?",a="Lor'themar wants nothing more than to preserve and protect his surviving people following the ruinous Scourge invasion of Quel'Thalas. Entrusted with the regency by Prince Kael'thas, he shoulders the grueling burden of holding the broken elven kingdom together and securing crucial aid while his prince searches abroad for a cure to their magic addiction.",al={"lorthemar goals","what does lorthemar want","lorthemar motives"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken travelers often remember that Sylvanas Windrunner's former comrades still breathe in the ruined north, with Lor'themar serving as the fragile bridge between Silvermoon and the Dark Lady's realm.",["class:Hunter"]="To marksmanship veterans and scouts, Lor'themar represents the pinnacle of the Farstrider tradition—a master marksman thrust from forest patrols into the burden of statecraft."},kw={"blood elf","farstriders","kael'thas","lor'themar","quel'thalas","regent lord","silvermoon","sin'dorei","theron"},rel={"npc:sylvanas-windrunner","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:second-war","topic:third-war","topic:troll","topic:horde"},src={"Lor'themar Theron"}}
E["npc:master-apothecary-faranell"] = {t="npc",n="Master Apothecary Faranell",z="undercity",s="Master Apothecary Faranell is the head of the Royal Apothecary Society, stationed within the depths of the Apothecarium in the Undercity. In life a respected Dalaran scholar, in undeath he directs the Forsaken's search for a devastating New Plague to eradicate both the Scourge and the living.",h="Master Apothecary Faranell is the head of the Royal Apothecary Society, stationed within the depths of the...",sec={{t="A Mind Unhinged by Death",b="Before the Third War, Faranell was an esteemed alchemist who spent decades studying alongside the learned mages of Dalaran. He spent his mortal days seeking cures, remedies, and potions to improve mortal health. When the Scourge plague claimed his life and he arose as a free-willed Forsaken, his former scientific curiosity curdled into cruelty. Retaining his encyclopedic intellect, he traded healing salves for catastrophic reagents, quickly becoming one of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's most valued researchers in the bowels of Lordaeron's fallen capital.",sp=0},{t="The Master of the Apothecarium",b="Operating out of the noxious laboratories of the Apothecarium, Faranell coordinates the far-flung research of the Royal Apothecary Society. He oversees the construction of lumbering abominations and directs subordinate apothecaries stationed throughout Lordaeron and beyond. Every batch of strange venom, tainted blood, and cursed flora gathered by field researchers across the continents eventually passes through his vats for distillation and refinement.",sp=0},{t="Crafting the New Plague",b="Faranell's single driving obsession is fulfilling the Dark Lady's mandate: uncovering the New Plague. To brew a contagion capable of destroying Arthas and his mindless Scourge legions, Faranell coordinates extensive reagent gathering. He dispatches adventurers to recover the research notes of his fallen colleague Apothecary Berard from Pyrewood Village, procures bat guano from the deep dens of Razorfen Kraul, and tests acidic colloids against the organs of zealots from the Scarlet Monastery.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Faranell is the head of the Royal Apothecary Society, the alchemical guild serving Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity. He oversees all research regarding toxins, stitched abominations, and the development of the New Plague.",al={"who is faranell","faranell lore","apothecary leader"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Faranell be found?",a="He resides in the Apothecarium, the alchemical quarter located in the western sector of the Undercity, surrounded by bubbling cauldrons, testing cages, and his apothecary subordinates.",al={"faranell location","where is master apothecary faranell","find faranell"},it="why_here",gp=true},{q="What was Faranell's background before he died?",a="In life, Faranell was an acclaimed alchemist and doctor who studied with the wizards of Dalaran. He spent his living years inventing remedies to heal disease before the plague killed him and twisted his curiosity toward lethal toxins.",al={"faranell history","was faranell in dalaran","faranell mortal life"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society trying to create?",a="Under Queen Sylvanas's directive, the society is manufacturing a New Plague. Their goal is to craft a weapon virulent enough to destroy the Scourge and exact vengeance upon the Lich King, while also defending the Forsaken from mortal enemies.",al={"what is the new plague","what are apothecaries making","apothecary goals"},it="wants"},{q="Why does Faranell send adventurers to Pyrewood Village?",a="He seeks the research journal of his former colleague, Apothecary Berard, who went mad and succumbed to the worgen curse in Pyrewood. Berard's field notes contain critical data on toxic agents needed to refine their plague experiments.",al={"recipe for death quest faranell","why pyrewood village","apothecary berard journal"}},{q="Why does he need reagents from Razorfen Kraul and the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Faranell tests how opposing volatile compounds interact. He uses kraul guano collected from the razorfen quilboar dens alongside the freshly harvested hearts of Scarlet Crusade zealots to test acidic colloids and biological contamination.",al={"kraul guano faranell","hearts of zeal","scarlet monastery hearts"}},{q="Whose side is Master Apothecary Faranell on?",a="Faranell is devoted entirely to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. As Master of the Royal Apothecary Society, he aligns his research directly with the Dark Lady's ambitions, mobilizing his alchemists to eradicate their enemies and secure the undead nation's survival, whatever the moral cost.",al={"faranell allegiance","who does faranell serve","is faranell loyal to sylvanas"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity?",a="Faranell oversees the Apothecarium, the alchemical heart of the Undercity. From this sprawling laboratory of bubbling vats and toxic fumes, he directs the Royal Apothecary Society's research, testing dangerous concoctions and coordinating the synthesis of powerful new blights and abominations for the Forsaken.",al={"why is faranell here","faranell apothecarium","why is faranell in undercity"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell tied to?",a="Faranell directly serves Queen Sylvanas Windrunner and leads the Royal Apothecary Society, directing subordinate researchers like Apothecary Renferrel in Silverpine and Apothecary Lydon in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He also maintains ties to fellow researchers, piecing together work from former colleagues like Apothecary Berard.",al={"faranell connections","who works with faranell","faranell allies"},it="ties",add=true},{q="Why is Master Apothecary Faranell feared?",a="Once a reputable scholar in Dalaran, Faranell's intellectual brilliance turned into depthless sadism after rising in undeath. He is notorious as the dark architect behind the Forsaken's most lethal poisons and plagues, testing horrific new concoctions on living and dead alike without a shred of remorse.",al={"why is faranell famous","faranell reputation","is faranell dangerous"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Faranell represents the vanguard of biological sovereignty, laboring in the dark to ensure their people possess weapons capable of shattering the Lich King.",["faction:Horde"]="Though orc, troll, and tauren allies may be unsettled by the green ooze and caged subjects of the Apothecarium, Faranell's research is tolerated as vital warfare against the common threat of the Scourge.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Faranell's vats consume endless quantities of rare flora, mosses, and fungal extracts, serving as a dark demonstration of botanical study weaponized for destruction."},kw={"abomination","apothecarium","blight","faranell","master apothecary faranell","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","sylvanas","undercity"},rel={"topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","npc:apothecary-renferrel","quest:447","quest:509","topic:forsaken"},src={"Master Apothecary Faranell"}}
E["npc:raleigh-andrean"] = {t="npc",n="Raleigh Andrean",z="undercity",s="Raleigh Andrean is a Forsaken resident found lingering in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity. Once a living citizen of Lordaeron, he exemplifies the cold, twisted detachment common among the undead, caring little for the loss of his wife but fiercely desiring retribution against the friend who murdered her.",h="Raleigh Andrean is a Forsaken resident found lingering in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Bitter Afterlife",b="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, Raleigh Andrean lived an ordinary human life, married to a woman named Deliah and keeping company with his friend Valdred Moray. Like countless others, he fell when the Scourge tore through the kingdom, only to be raised as a mindless thrall in service to the Lich King. He regained his free will following the shattering of the Ner'zhul's grip and Sylvanas Windrunner's uprising, taking his place among the Forsaken in the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance over Grief",b="When presented with his late wife's wedding ring, Raleigh displays the callous emotional decay of undeath. He harbors no sorrow or lingering love for Deliah, coldly dismissing her death. Instead, his focus fixates entirely on spite: he demands the severed hands of Valdred Moray, his former friend who murdered her. Raleigh keeps the gruesome trophies not out of affection for Deliah, but as an eternal memento of betrayal, rewarding whoever aids him with a ring forged of pure scorn.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Raleigh Andrean located?",a="Raleigh Andrean resides within the bustling Trade Quarter of the Undercity, standing among the subterranean city's Forsaken populace.",al={"raleigh andrean location","where is raleigh","find raleigh andrean"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was Raleigh when he was alive?",a="In life, Raleigh was a mortal resident of the kingdom of Lordaeron. He was married to a woman named Deliah and shared a friendship with a man named Valdred Moray before the Scourge swept through the realm.",al={"raleigh backstory","who was raleigh","raleigh andrean lore"},it="history"},{q="Why does Raleigh want revenge on Valdred Moray?",a="Valdred Moray murdered Raleigh's wife, Deliah. While Raleigh no longer feels love or grief for his deceased spouse due to his undead state, he remains driven by bitter fury over his former friend's treacherous betrayal.",al={"why kill valdred","raleigh wife","valdred moray murder"},it="motive"},{q="How did Raleigh become free from the Scourge?",a="Raleigh was slain and raised into servitude by the Scourge during the Third War. When the Lich King's control slipped following attacks on the Frozen Throne, Sylvanas Windrunner led an uprising, freeing Raleigh and many others to form the Forsaken.",al={"how did raleigh become forsaken","raleigh scourge freedom"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Raleigh Andrean?",a="Raleigh Andrean is a Forsaken citizen residing in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity. In life, he was a citizen of Lordaeron who was murdered during the Scourge invasion and raised into undeath. After breaking free from the Lich King's grasp alongside Sylvanas Windrunner, he pledged himself to the Forsaken, lingering in the capital consumed by bitterness and a cold hunger for vengeance against those who betrayed him in his former life.",al={"who is raleigh andrean","who is raleigh","raleigh andrean identity"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Raleigh Andrean on?",a="Raleigh is entirely loyal to Queen Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, and by extension the Horde. Once liberated from the Scourge's control following the Dark Lady's uprising, he found sanctuary beneath the ruins of Lordaeron. Though primarily consumed by personal grudges, he stands firmly among his fellow undead in the Undercity.",al={"raleigh andrean faction","is raleigh horde","whose side is raleigh on"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Raleigh Andrean want?",a="Raleigh seeks retribution against his former friend, Valdred Moray. While he shows callous indifference toward the death of his late wife Deliah, he burns with resentment over Moray's betrayal and murder of her. He wants nothing more than to see Valdred hunted down and slain, desiring Moray's severed hands brought to him as a grim trophy of his vengeance.",al={"what does raleigh want","raleigh andrean goal","raleigh andrean revenge"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Raleigh Andrean in the Undercity?",a="Like many former citizens of Lordaeron who regained their free will, Raleigh took refuge in the Undercity after breaking the Lich King's domination. He now lingers in the Trade Quarter, brooding over past grievances and seeking passing adventurers willing to help him carry out vengeance against his living enemies.",al={"why is raleigh here","why is raleigh in undercity","raleigh andrean trade quarter"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Raleigh Andrean tied to?",a="In life, Raleigh was married to a woman named Deliah and was close companions with Valdred Moray. That bond shattered when Moray betrayed him and murdered Deliah during the kingdom's downfall, turning their former friendship into a bitter, enduring hatred that spans across death itself.",al={"raleigh andrean wife","raleigh andrean connections","raleigh valdred deliah"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Raleigh is a grim reflection of Forsaken reality: undeath strips away warmth and grief, leaving behind only the cold embers of spite, vengeance, and lingering hatred toward those who betrayed them in life."},kw={"a husband's revenge","deliah","forsaken","raleigh andrean","ring of scorn","trade quarter","undercity","valdred moray"},rel={"quest:530","quest:441","zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:lich-king"},src={"Raleigh Andrean"}}
E["npc:sylvanas-windrunner"] = {t="npc",n="Sylvanas Windrunner",z="undercity",s="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner is the Banshee Queen and supreme ruler of the Forsaken, holding court in the Undercity beneath the ruins of Lordaeron. Once the brave Ranger-General of Silvermoon, she was slain and raised into undeath by Arthas Menethil before breaking free from the Lich King's grip. Now allied with Thrall's Horde out of mutual survival, she is fiercely dedicated to securing a future for her free-willed undead and exacting vengeance upon the Scourge.",h="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner is the Banshee Queen and supreme ruler of the Forsaken, holding court in the...",sec={{t="Fall of the Ranger-General",b="In life, Lady Sylvanas was the celebrated Ranger-General of Silvermoon, commanding the defense of Quel'Thalas during the Third War. When Prince Arthas Menethil marched the Scourge into the high elven kingdom to reach the Sunwell, Sylvanas fought fiercely to delay his advance. Frustrated by her resistance, Arthas murdered her, but denied her a clean death. He ripped her soul from her corpse and twisted it into a vengeful banshee, forcing her to serve the Scourge and assist in the slaughter of her own people.",sp=0},{t="Rise of the Forsaken",b="When the Lich King's magical grip fractured after the Third War, Sylvanas broke free of his dominion and repossessed her preserved body. Amassing other undead who had regained their free will, she overthrew the dreadlords occupying the ruins of Lordaeron, dubbed her people the Forsaken, and established the subterranean realm of the Undercity. Recognizing the precarious isolation of her people—threatened by Scourge remnants, zealous Scarlet crusaders, and suspicious human realms—she forged an uneasy alliance of convenience with Warchief Thrall and the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sylvanas Windrunner?",a="She is the sovereign leader of the Forsaken, holding court in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity. In life she was the elven Ranger-General of Quel'Thalas, but after being slain and raised by Arthas Menethil, she broke away from the Scourge to lead the free-willed undead.",al={"banshee queen","who is the dark lady","lady sylvanas","undercity leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Sylvanas align the Forsaken with the Horde?",a="The Forsaken are reviled by the living nations of the Alliance, who see them only as monsters. Surrounded by the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade in Lordaeron, Sylvanas required strong allies to ensure her fledgling nation's survival, prompting her to petition Warchief Thrall for entry into the Horde.",al={"why are undead in horde","forsaken horde alliance","sylvanas thrall pact"},it="side"},{q="How did Sylvanas break free from the Lich King?",a="When the Lich King's psychic power began to bleed away during the aftermath of the Third War, his iron control over the Scourge fractured. Sylvanas was among the first powerful spirits to regain her autonomy, immediately reclaiming her mortal remains and turning her wrath upon Arthas.",al={"how did sylvanas escape arthas","sylvanas free will","lich king control"},it="history"},{q="What is Sylvanas's primary goal?",a="Above all else, Sylvanas seeks total retribution against Arthas Menethil and the Scourge for destroying her homeland and enslaving her soul. Concurrently, she strives to fortify the Undercity and carve out a secure, permanent haven for the Forsaken in Lordaeron.",al={"what does sylvanas want","sylvanas motivation","dark lady goal"},it="wants"},{q="Why is Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity?",a="Sylvanas rules the Forsaken from the Royal Quarter deep within the Undercity, the subterranean labyrinth carved beneath the ruins of the Capital City of Lordaeron. After seizing the capital from the Scourge and Dreadlords, she established it as the stronghold of her free-willed undead. From here, she directs the defense of Tirisfal Glades against the Scarlet Crusade and remnants of the Scourge, while working to forge a secure future for her people in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"why is sylvanas here","why undercity sylvanas","sylvanas location reason"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Sylvanas Windrunner allied with?",a="Sylvanas is supreme ruler of the Forsaken and leads them under an alliance of convenience with Warchief Thrall's Horde. Within her court, she is guarded and advised by figures like the dreadlord Varimathras, who pledged fealty to her after the fall of Lordaeron, and Grand Apothecary Putress of the Royal Apothecary Society. Beyond her undead nation, she maintains fraught geopolitical ties with the orcs and tauren, who granted her people entry into the Horde despite lingering mutual suspicions.",al={"sylvanas allies","who is sylvanas tied to","sylvanas windrunner connections"},it="ties",add=true},{q="Why is Sylvanas Windrunner famous?",a="Before her death, Sylvanas was revered as the Ranger-General of Silvermoon, celebrated for her valiant defense of Quel'Thalas against the Scourge. Today, she is feared across Azeroth as the Banshee Queen. Having endured execution and banshee torment at the hands of Prince Arthas, she reclaimed her mortal vessel and wrested an entire faction of undead from the Lich King's psychic grasp. Her lethal archery, banshee scream, and ruthless cunning make both living and dead tread carefully around her.",al={"why is sylvanas feared","banshee queen fame","why is sylvanas famous"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="To the Forsaken, the Dark Lady is a liberator and protector, the solitary reason they possess free will and a fortified home rather than mindlessly serving the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="Though accepted into the Horde through the advocacy of Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem and Thrall's compassion, many orcs and trolls view Sylvanas and her court with lingering wariness."},kw={"arthas","banshee queen","dark lady","forsaken","lordaeron","ranger-general","sylvanas","undercity","windrunner"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:horde","npc:thrall","zone:tirisfal","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Sylvanas Windrunner"}}
E["npc:varimathras"] = {t="npc",n="Varimathras",z="undercity",s="Varimathras is a dreadlord of the nathrezim race who serves as the chief lieutenant and military advisor to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Forced to pledge loyalty to the Banshee Queen after suffering defeat during the civil war for Lordaeron, he now stands at her right hand in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity.",h="Varimathras is a dreadlord of the nathrezim race who serves as the chief lieutenant and military advisor to...",sec={{t="Jailor of the Lich King",b="Before the Third War, Varimathras and his fellow dreadlords worked directly under Kil'jaeden to break and reshape the spirit of Ner'zhul into the Lich King. Bound alongside his brothers Detheroc and Balnazzar, he oversaw the Scourge in Lordaeron while Archimonde invaded Kalimdor. When the Legion fell at Mount Hyjal, the triumvirate remained entrenched in the ruins of the Capital City, entirely unaware of their master's demise until Prince Arthas returned to drive them into hiding.",sp=0},{t="A Demon's Surrender",b="As the Lich King's hold over his undead forces fractured, Varimathras attempted to coerce the newly freed banshee Sylvanas Windrunner into serving the dreadlords' new regime. Sylvanas refused, rallying liberated undead to crush Varimathras's outpost. Facing execution, the dreadlord fell to his knees and bartered for his life, trading tactical secrets and knowledge of his brothers' fortifications in exchange for survival. Sylvanas accepted, binding him to her service as a living weapon against his kin.",sp=0},{t="Brother Against Brother",b="To secure Sylvanas's trust, Varimathras was made to commit the unthinkable: violating the sacred nathrezim law that forbids a dreadlord from killing another. Under her direct command, he struck down his sibling Balnazzar after the conquest of the Capital City and summarily executed the human warlord Grand Marshal Garithos. Now stationed beside Sylvanas's throne, Varimathras coordinates military excursions across the Plaguelands, though many in the Horde look upon this demonic ally with deep unease.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is a demon serving the Forsaken?",a="When Sylvanas Windrunner gathered her army of newly liberated undead during the Lordaeron civil war, she routed Varimathras's forces. Facing imminent death, the dreadlord pleaded for mercy and offered his cunning, military knowledge, and service in exchange for his life. Sylvanas spared him to use as a tactician and enforcer.",al={"why is varimathras in undercity","why dreadlord with sylvanas","varimathras allegiance"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of creature is Varimathras?",a="Varimathras is a nathrezim, commonly known as a dreadlord. The nathrezim are an intelligent, manipulative race of demons who serve the Burning Legion, specializing in mental domination, shadow magic, and spreading plague and discord.",al={"what race is varimathras","is varimathras a vampire","varimathras species"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Varimathras stand in the Undercity?",a="He can be found standing on the dais in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity, directly beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, surrounded by Forsaken royal guards.",al={"where is varimathras","varimathras location","find varimathras"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Did Varimathras really kill his fellow dreadlord Balnazzar?",a="Dreadlords are strictly forbidden by their own kind from killing another nathrezim. To test his loyalty and secure his place, Sylvanas forced Varimathras to strike down Balnazzar after the reclaiming of Lordaeron's capital city, crossing a line no demon was thought capable of crossing.",al={"did varimathras kill balnazzar","varimathras brother","dreadlord taboo"},it="conflict"},{q="What role did Varimathras play in creating the Scourge?",a="On the orders of Kil'jaeden, Varimathras and his fellow dreadlords tortured the captive spirit of the orc shaman Ner'zhul in the Twisting Nether, breaking his sanity and binding him inside the Frozen Throne to fashion the Lich King before deploying him to Azeroth.",al={"varimathras nerzhul","varimathras lich king origin"},it="history"},{q="Do the other Horde leaders trust Varimathras?",a="Not at all. The orcs, trolls, and tauren carry deep scars from demonic corruption and regard dreadlords as monstrous manipulators. Even among the Forsaken, many view Varimathras as an uneasy weapon held on a very tight leash rather than a true brother-in-arms.",al={"does the horde trust varimathras","thrall varimathras","is varimathras trusted"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Varimathras on?",a="Outwardly, Varimathras serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. When Sylvanas defeated his forces after the Third War, he begged for his life and pledged his loyalty to her, even aiding in the overthrow of his dreadlord brothers. However, he remains a nathrezim of the Burning Legion at heart. While he acts as the Banshee Queen's majordomo, few in the Horde believe a demon's loyalty can ever truly be trusted.",al={"is varimathras loyal","varimathras allegiance","who does varimathras serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Varimathras want?",a="Above all else, Varimathras wants survival and influence. When Sylvanas had him at her mercy, he willingly betrayed his fellow dreadlords to preserve his own skin. By embedding himself as Sylvanas's second-in-command within the Undercity, he maintains a position of tremendous authority in Lordaeron while continuing to advance the ruin of his enemies—namely the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"varimathras goals","what does varimathras want","varimathras motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Varimathras in the Undercity?",a="Varimathras stands beside Lady Sylvanas in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity as her chief lieutenant and master tactician. After helping her conquer Lordaeron's capital and eliminate rivals like Detheroc and Balnazzar, he was bound into her service. He now coordinates military actions, directs spies, and helps oversee the Forsaken kingdom under the Dark Lady's watchful eye.",al={"why is varimathras here","varimathras undercity why","what is varimathras doing here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Why is Varimathras so feared?",a="Varimathras is a dreadlord, one of the cunning nathrezim who helped corrupt Ner'zhul and engineer the Scourge's devastation of Azeroth. Renowned for masterful manipulation, mind control, and ruthless cunning, he and his brothers once commanded the undead legions across Lordaeron. To see such a powerful demon bound into servitude is both a terrifying testament to Sylvanas's power and an unsettling omen to anyone who enters the Undercity.",al={"why is varimathras dangerous","varimathras reputation","is varimathras feared"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Varimathras represents the Forsaken's pragmatic willingness to turn the weapons of their oppressors against them, standing subdued beside the Dark Lady who freed Lordaeron from his grip.",["class:Warlock"]="To practitioners of demonic magic, the sight of a high-ranking nathrezim serving a mortal undead queen is an impressive, if unsettling, display of leveraged will.",["faction:Horde"]="The dreadlord's presence in Undercity is a source of intense friction with Orgrimmar, as the Horde spent decades breaking free from the very demonic masters Varimathras served."},kw={"balnazzar","detheroc","dreadlord","nathrezim","royal quarter","sylvanas","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"npc:sylvanas-windrunner","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron","topic:burning-legion","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","topic:third-war"},src={"Varimathras"}}
E["npc:varok-saurfang"] = {t="npc",n="Varok Saurfang",z="undercity",s="High Overlord Varok Saurfang is a legendary orc warrior of the Blackrock clan and a veteran of the First, Second, and Third Wars. Serving as Warchief Thrall's trusted military commander, he represents the proud martial spine of the modern Horde while privately carrying the heavy remorse of past atrocities.",h="High Overlord Varok Saurfang is a legendary orc warrior of the Blackrock clan and a veteran of the First...",sec={{t="A Living Legend of the Wars",b="Few living warriors possess a martial pedigree to rival Varok Saurfang. A member of the revered Blackrock clan, Saurfang served alongside Eitrigg under Blackhand and later became the trusted second-in-command to Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer himself. Through the savage assaults on Stormwind in the First War and the brutal northern marches across the Hillsbrad Foothills and the Hinterlands in the Second War, Saurfang was considered an unstoppable force on the battlefield. When Thrall rallied the scattered orc clans to cross the Great Sea and establish Durotar, Saurfang took up arms once more, defending Kalimdor through the Third War and standing as a bulwark of the newborn Horde.",sp=0},{t="The Weight of the Blood",b="Though he stands as an unmatched champion of the Horde, Saurfang is not driven by reckless battle-lust. Like many of his generation, he freely partook in the demonic blood of Mannoroth before the opening of the Dark Portal and bears deep sorrow for the cruelties carried out under the Blood Curse. Following the sacrifice of Grommash Hellscream that freed the orcs, Saurfang has dedicated much of his life to counseling fellow veterans through their guilt. While he will relentlessly defend the Horde and enforce Thrall's rule against any threat, Saurfang harbors a profound disdain for warmongering and fights strictly for honor and preservation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Varok Saurfang?",a="Varok Saurfang is a renowned orc warrior of the Blackrock clan, brother of the famous Broxigar, and the primary military commander serving Warchief Thrall in the Horde.",al={"varok saurfang backstory","who is saurfang","high overlord saurfang"},it="identity"},{q="What wars did Saurfang fight in?",a="Saurfang fought in the First, Second, and Third Wars. He led Blackrock forces during the sack of Stormwind, served as Orgrim Doomhammer's second-in-command across Lordaeron, and defended Mount Hyjal alongside Thrall's forces.",al={"saurfang war history","did saurfang fight in the first war","saurfang battles"},it="history"},{q="How does Saurfang view the Horde's past?",a="Saurfang deeply regrets the atrocities committed under the demon blood curse, especially the slaughter of innocent draenei on Draenor. The memory haunts him so thoroughly that he refuses to eat pork because the sound of swine slaughter echoes the screams of dying children.",al={"saurfang blood curse","saurfang draenei guilt","why does saurfang regret the past"},it="motive"},{q="What is Saurfang's role in the current Horde?",a="He serves as High Overlord of Thrall's forces, overseeing military readiness, enforcing the Warchief's commands, and acting as a seasoned mentor to younger warriors within the Horde.",al={"what does saurfang do now","saurfang orgrimmar role"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Varok Saurfang on?",a="Saurfang is fiercely devoted to Thrall's Horde. A veteran of the Blackrock clan, he served the Old Horde under Blackhand and Orgrim Doomhammer, but today he stands unreservedly behind the new Horde. He enforces the Warchief's will and protects the people with absolute dedication.",al={"what faction is saurfang","who does saurfang serve","saurfang loyalty"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Varok Saurfang want?",a="Having lived through the demonic bloodlust that drove the orcs to slaughter innocents on Draenor, Saurfang desires honor, redemption, and stability for his people. He will defend the Horde to his dying breath, but he despises senseless warmongering and strives to keep the orcs from succumbing to their dark past ever again.",al={"what does saurfang want","saurfang goal","saurfang motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Varok Saurfang tied to?",a="He is the younger brother of Broxigar, the famed warrior. In his early years, he was one of Warchief Blackhand's trusted lieutenants alongside Eitrigg and Orgrim Doomhammer, later becoming Doomhammer's second-in-command during the Second War. Today, he is one of Warchief Thrall's most trusted commanders.",al={"saurfang family","saurfang brother","who is saurfang related to"},it="ties",add=true},{q="Why is Varok Saurfang famous?",a="Saurfang is legendary across Azeroth as an unstoppable force on the battlefield. Having fought in the First, Second, and Third Wars—including the sieges of Stormwind and the Battle of Mount Hyjal—his unmatched martial prowess and tactical ferocity have earned him immense renown and fear among enemies and allies alike.",al={"why is saurfang feared","is saurfang famous","saurfang reputation"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="To the orcs, High Overlord Saurfang is both the ultimate paragon of martial strength and a sobering reminder of the spiritual toll exacted by the demonic blood curse.",["class:Warrior"]="Warriors revere Saurfang as a peerless veteran whose axe technique, tactical battlefield brilliance, and enduring resolve define the ideal soldier."},kw={"blackrock","broxigar","doomhammer","korkron","overlord","saurfang","thrall","varok","warrior"},rel={"npc:thrall","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","npc:eitrigg","topic:blackrock-clan","topic:grommash-hellscream","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:third-war"},src={"Varok Saurfang"}}
E["quest:1359"] = {t="quest",n="Zinge's Delivery",z="undercity",s="Zinge's Delivery is a courier task dispatched by Apothecary Renferrel from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. It transports strangely toxic wolf heart tissue back to Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity for formal study by the Royal Apothecary Society.",h="Zinge's Delivery is a courier task dispatched by Apothecary Renferrel from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Toxic Anomaly",b="While examining local wildlife around Silverpine Forest, Apothecary Renferrel observed an unsettling physiological trait within the wolves roaming the ruined woods. Their hearts carried a level of toxicity so profound that, under any ordinary circumstances, it ought to have killed the beasts housing them. Rather than discarding the tissue, Renferrel packaged several samples to share with colleagues at the Apothecarium in the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="The Eyes of the Apothecarium",b="The preserved organs are delivered directly to Apothecary Zinge, a researcher working in the subterranean headquarters of the Royal Apothecary Society. For the society, whose primary ambition is formulating potent plagues and novel alchemical compounds, naturally occurring poisons that sustain rather than slay are of paramount interest. Zinge welcomes the delivery as the foundation for further laboratory trials across the Forsaken alchemical network.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the wolf heart samples?",a="They are preserved biological tissue gathered from wolves in Silverpine Forest. Apothecary Renferrel discovered that the hearts contain natural toxins deadly enough that the animals should not have survived carrying them.",al={"wolf hearts","what are wolf heart samples","renferrel samples"},it="item"},{q="Who is Apothecary Renferrel?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is a member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He oversees field research on regional flora and fauna to harvest ingredients and biological insights for Forsaken alchemy.",al={"who is renferrel","renferrel silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Apothecary Zinge?",a="Apothecary Zinge is an alchemical researcher based within the Apothecarium quarter of the Undercity. She experiments with incoming biological specimens to uncover new toxins and alchemical agents for the Forsaken.",al={"who is zinge","zinge undercity","apothecary zinge lore"},it="target"},{q="Where does this delivery lead next?",a="Once Zinge receives and inspects the strange heart tissue, the research continues as samples are routed to other alchemical outposts, such as Apothecary Helbrim stationed across the sea in the Barrens.",al={"next quest","what happens after zinge's delivery","follow up quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society interested in wolf hearts?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society constantly seeks exotic poisons, diseases, and biological anomalies. A beast that survives lethal self-toxicity presents unique chemical pathways that could aid their development of new plagues and compounds.",al={"why do apothecaries want wolf hearts","ras wolf hearts"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Apothecarium in Undercity?",a="The Apothecarium forms the southwestern wing of the Undercity. It serves as the primary laboratory complex and governing headquarters of the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"undercity apothecary location","where is zinge","apothecarium map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel send you instead of going himself?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is stationed out at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, conducting active fieldwork and ongoing research into the local wildlife. Leaving his outpost to carry samples back to the Capital would pull him away from his experiments, making an able-bodied traveler the ideal courier to transport the fragile specimens directly to Apothecary Zinge in the Apothecarium.",al={"why me renferrel","why does renferrel need a courier","why send an adventurer with the delivery"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Field samples collected in Lordaeron feed directly into the central alchemical laboratories beneath the Capital City ruins, advancing the scientific power of the Forsaken.",["faction:Horde"]="Messengers carrying biological reagents keep remote outposts like the Sepulcher unified with the leadership and research hubs in the Undercity."},kw={"apothecarium","apothecary renferrel","apothecary zinge","sepulcher","silverpine","undercity","wolf heart samples","zinge's delivery"},rel={"npc:apothecary-zinge","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:undercity","quest:1358","quest:3221"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Apothecary Zinge",level="15",faction="Horde",id=1359},src={"Zinge's Delivery"}}
E["quest:1471"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="undercity",s="The Binding is the culminating rite for Forsaken warlocks seeking to command a voidwalker. In the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, Carendin Halgar requires initiates to summon, conquer, and permanently subjugate a creature of the Void.",h="The Binding is the culminating rite for Forsaken warlocks seeking to command a voidwalker.",sec={{t="A Rite of Subjugation",b="Unlike minor imps, which are easily coerced into pacts with dark magic, creatures of the Void despise reality and possess formidable physical might. To earn the right to summon a voidwalker, an aspiring warlock in the Undercity must prove total mastery over it. In the shadowed enclave of the Magic Quarter, the Forsaken mentor Carendin Halgar provides the mystic runes required to tear a voidwalker from the Nether into the physical realm.",sp=0},{t="Within the Circle",b="The ritual takes place within the glowing summoning circle etched beneath the mentor's dais. Once the runes are activated, an unbound voidwalker materializes in fury. Subduing it is not an exercise in diplomacy; the summoner must break the entity through sheer arcane force and raw will. Only when the entity is thoroughly crushed does Carendin reveal the true formula of summoning, binding the creature's essence to the practitioner indefinitely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this ritual?",a="The ritual tests an aspiring warlock's ability to overpower a creature of the Void. By defeating an unbound voidwalker in combat, the summoner proves their will is strong enough to control it, allowing Carendin Halgar to teach them the permanent summoning spell.",al={"why do the binding","what does the binding quest do","binding reward"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the summoning take place?",a="It takes place directly within the purple summoning circle etched into the floor beneath Carendin Halgar's platform in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"where do i summon voidwalker","where is the summoning circle","circle of summoning undercity"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar is the primary warlock trainer residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, overseeing the instruction and dark initiations of newly raised Forsaken practitioners.",al={"who is halgar","carendin halgar lore"},it="identity"},{q="Do warlocks need to defeat every demon they want to summon?",a="Warlocks must establish authority over powerful extradimensional beings before commanding them. While smaller entities like imps are bound by simple contracts and rituals, voidwalkers require physical and magical dominance before they submit to servitude.",al={"do warlocks always fight demons","why fight the voidwalker"}},{q="What happens if a warlock fails to subdue the voidwalker?",a="An unbound voidwalker will relentlessly batter and destroy anyone nearby. As Halgar warns, failing to meet his expectations is nothing compared to the danger of being torn apart by the untamed entity within the circle.",al={"what if i fail the binding","failure lore warlock"},it="danger"},{q="What is a voidwalker?",a="Voidwalkers are shadowy, extradimensional beings originating from the Void. They possess immense physical resilience and an innate desire to extinguish living light and energy, making them ideal protective shields for practitioners of dark magic.",al={"what is a voidwalker","voidwalker lore"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar want this ritual done?",a="Carendin Halgar seeks to cultivate formidable power within the Undercity's warlock ranks. By compelling you to summon and bend an unbound creature of the void entirely to your will, he ensures that Forsaken practitioners master true subjugation rather than fall prey to the otherworldly entities they seek to command.",al={"why carendin halgar binding","carendin halgar motive","why summon voidwalker"},it="motive",rc="Undead",add=true},{q="What is the entity you are sent to summon and defeat?",a="You are drawing forth an unbound voidwalker straight from the Twisting Nether into the summoning circle. Voidwalkers are shadowy demons formed from pure void energy, hostile and resentful of servitude, requiring outright magical and martial defeat before accepting a master's will.",al={"what do you fight in the binding","target of the binding","who am i summoning"},it="target",rc="Undead",add=true},{q="Why must you subdue the voidwalker yourself rather than having Carendin Halgar do it?",a="Demonology demands personal dominance. A summoned demon yields only to the individual who demonstrates the magical authority and physical fortitude to conquer it. If Carendin or the city guards intervened to subdue the creature, the voidwalker would be bound to their will rather than your own.",al={"why do i have to fight it","why doesn't carendin help","why me binding quest"},it="why_me",rc="Undead",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="This rite marks the warlock's transition from petty trickery with imps to genuine domination over entities capable of absorbing immense physical punishment on the battlefield.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, binding a creature of shadow is a natural extension of their resilience and lack of moral restraint regarding forbidden magic."},kw={"carendin halgar","magic quarter","runes of summoning","subjugation","the binding","undercity","voidwalker","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1473","quest:1478","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={start="Carendin Halgar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1471},src={"The Binding (Voidwalker, Undercity)"}}
E["quest:1472"] = {t="quest",n="Devourer of Souls",z="undercity",s="Devourer of Souls is an introductory step in a Forsaken warlock's journey to summon and bind a succubus. Directed by Carendin Halgar in the Undercity's Temple of the Damned, the practitioner must confer with his assistant, Godrick Farsan, to learn how to lure such a creature from the Twisting Nether. The ritual demands an irresistible stimulus: the hearts of pure and loving mortals.",h="Devourer of Souls is an introductory step in a Forsaken warlock's journey to summon and bind a succubus.",sec={{t="Baiting the Nether",b="Carendin Halgar teaches that a succubus cannot simply be pulled across the threshold on command; it must be enticed. Driven by an insatiable hunger to ruin virtue and consume mortal essence, the demon requires a specific lure. The warlock's strategy relies on exploiting this singular desire by offering up the hearts of genuinely virtuous, loving men as bait. Halgar directs his acolytes to Godrick Farsan, who knows where such rare quarry can be harvested.",sp=0},{t="The Blind Assistant",b="Located deeper within the Temple of the Damned, Godrick Farsan assists Carendin with the practical preparations of demonic binding. Though Farsan has lost his physical eyesight, he claims his condition grants him a profound second sight—allowing him to perceive underlying spiritual currents and far-off souls with uncanny clarity. He serves as the guide for locating the pure hearts necessary to draw the demon forth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This quest bridges Carendin Halgar's initial summons with the practical hunting phase required to bind a succubus. It sends the warlock to Godrick Farsan, who details the morbid components needed for the ritual.",al={"why do devourer of souls","succubus quest undercity","warlock quest level 20"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does a succubus need pure hearts to be summoned?",a="A succubus thrives on corrupting goodness, tempting mortal hearts, and devouring virtuous souls. Carendin Halgar explains that the demon cannot easily breach into this world without an irresistible stimulus, making the untainted devotion of good men the ideal bait to lure it across.",al={"why hearts of the pure","succubus bait lore"}},{q="Who is Godrick Farsan?",a="Godrick Farsan is an undead warlock acolyte assisting Carendin Halgar in the Temple of the Damned. Despite being physically blind, he possesses mystical senses that allow him to perceive spiritual truths and locate suitable prey across the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"who is farsan","blind warlock assistant"},it="identity"},{q="Where is this quest completed?",a="The quest is turned in directly within the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity, just a few paces away from Carendin Halgar, where Godrick Farsan stands waiting.",al={"where is godrick farsan","devourer of souls turn in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes after Devourer of Souls?",a="Farsan immediately assigns the quest 'Hearts of the Pure,' tasking the warlock with traveling to the Wetlands and to the Greymane Wall in Silverpine Forest to claim the hearts of two virtuous mortals.",al={"next quest after devourer of souls","hearts of the pure next"},it="next_step"},{q="Can any race undertake this ritual?",a="While it is situated in the Undercity and instructed by Forsaken practitioners, any Horde warlock seeking to bind a succubus through Undercity mentors can perform the ritual steps provided by Halgar and Farsan.",al={"who can do devourer of souls","undead only warlock quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar want to summon a succubus?",a="Carendin Halgar oversees the development of warlocks within the Undercity. A succubus is a creature of deceit, temptation, and malice—a potent tool for bending enemy wills and turning desires into fatal weaknesses. Carendin directs you through the ritual so you can bind the demon directly to your command, expanding the Forsaken's dark arsenal while proving your mastery over the Nether.",al={"carendin halgar motive","why summon succubus carendin","carendin goal devourer of souls"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Carendin send you instead of handling this himself?",a="Demonic enslavement cannot be performed on another caster's behalf. A succubus answers only to the will that directly lures, binds, and dominates her. As a mentor, Carendin Halgar guides your studies and provides the ritual's foundational lore, but you alone must acquire the bait, face the demon, and assert absolute control over its soul.",al={"why does carendin need me","why me devourer of souls","why warlock player succubus"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Binding a succubus is a major milestone in a warlock's training, demonstrating the dark art of leveraging a demon's inherent vices and appetites to enslave it.",["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken warlock trainers in the Temple of the Damned operate without moral restraint, casually treating living purity and devotion as disposable reagents for Nether rituals."},kw={"bait","carendin halgar","godrick farsan","hearts of the pure","succubus","temple of the damned","undercity"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","npc:godrick-farsan","quest:1476"},m={start="Carendin Halgar",["end"]="Godrick Farsan",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1472},src={"Devourer of Souls (Undercity)"}}
E["quest:1473"] = {t="quest",n="Creature of the Void",z="undercity",s="Creature of the Void is a pivotal rite of passage for Forsaken warlocks, tasking them with recovering a lost arcane text from the Scarlet Crusade. To learn how to summon and bind a chaotic voidwalker, an initiate must venture west of Tirisfal Glades and retrieve Egalin's Grimoire from hostile zealots.",h="Creature of the Void is a pivotal rite of passage for Forsaken warlocks, tasking them with recovering a lost...",sec={{t="A Teacher's Legacy",b="Within the dark alcoves of the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity, Carendin Halgar oversees the development of rising Forsaken summoners. When an acolyte proves competent enough to wield power beyond petty imps, Halgar directs them toward binding a creature forged from pure shadow and chaos: the voidwalker. Rather than relying on simple instinct, Forsaken practitioners base their summons on the meticulous research of Egalin, Halgar's own former master, who first penned the rituals necessary to subjugate these monstrous denizens of the void.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Grimoire",b="Mastery of the voidwalker cannot be achieved without Egalin's Grimoire, which contains the precise methods for channeling such volatile magic. However, the precious tome was stolen by an agent of the Scarlet Crusade—a zealot named Perrine stationed in an outpost tower to the west. While Perrine and his crusaders likely viewed the grimoire as mere blasphemous contraband to confiscate and hoard, recovering it is essential if the Forsaken are to secure the ritual secrets before attempting to tear open the veil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Egalin's Grimoire?",a="Egalin's Grimoire is a magical manual authored by the warlock Egalin, who taught Carendin Halgar. It details the intricate channeling techniques and spells required to breach the void and summon a voidwalker under the caster's absolute control.",al={"egalins grimoire","what is the book","who was egalin"},it="item"},{q="Why did the Scarlet Crusade steal the book?",a="The Scarlet Crusade considers all demonic and shadow magic inherently corrupt. An agent named Perrine seized the grimoire during a skirmish or infiltration, stashing it away in a western watchtower in Tirisfal Glades, seemingly unaware of the specific summoning power contained inside.",al={"why did scarlet crusade take it","perrine grimoire","scarlet tower west"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar is a master warlock trainer residing in the Temple of the Damned within the Undercity. He guides novice Forsaken warlocks, teaching them respect for volatile cosmic forces and caution born from his own past summoning mistakes.",al={"carendin halgar","warlock trainer undercity","temple of the damned trainer"},it="identity"},{q="What happens if a warlock loses control of a voidwalker?",a="Voidwalkers are beings of pure chaos and shadow. As Carendin Halgar warns, if an initiate attempts to conjure one without flawless discipline and binding will, the entity will violently tear its summoner apart.",al={"can voidwalker kill you","voidwalker danger","summoning failure"},it="danger"},{q="What comes after recovering the grimoire?",a="Once Halgar has the book, he studies the text to impart the ritual runes to you. This immediately leads into 'The Binding', where the initiate must use the summoning circle to conjure a voidwalker and defeat it in personal combat to establish dominance.",al={"what next after grimoire","next quest","binding ritual"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is the Scarlet Crusade outpost located?",a="The grimoire is hidden inside a Scarlet Crusade watchtower situated to the west across Tirisfal Glades, guarded by crusaders under the command of Perrine.",al={"where is perrine","scarlet tower location","where is the book"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar want this done?",a="Carendin Halgar recognizes your growing strength and considers you ready to bind a voidwalker. That dangerous art requires the precise rituals recorded by his own mentor, Egalin. Beyond training you, Halgar cannot allow such dark, potent knowledge to remain in the hands of the Scarlet Crusade, whose fanatics would gladly use or destroy the stolen text.",al={"halgar motive","why recover the grimoire","why does halgar need the book"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who has Egalin's Grimoire?",a="An agent of the Scarlet Crusade named Perrine stole the grimoire and keeps it stashed inside a Scarlet outpost to the west. While Perrine likely remains ignorant of the true demonological power contained within its musty pages, the zealots maintain a constant presence there to monitor and strike against the Undercity.",al={"who stole the grimoire","who has egalins grimoire","scarlet crusader target"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar send you instead of going himself?",a="Halgar serves as a master summoner within the Temple of the Damned, guiding fledgling warlocks and overseeing the Forsaken's dark craft. More importantly, retrieving the grimoire is a vital test of your resourcefulness and resolve. A warlock who cannot reclaim their own tools from zealous mortal crusaders will surely fail when attempting to dominate a chaotic creature torn from the Nether.",al={"why send me","why cant halgar get the book","why does halgar need me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="This quest marks your transition from dabbling with imps to controlling heavy frontline shadow entities capable of absorbing immense physical punishment.",["race:Undead"]="Striking the Scarlet Crusade to reclaim dark knowledge underscores the bitter struggle between the Forsaken and the living zealots occupying Lordaeron's ruins.",["faction:Horde"]="The dark arts practiced in the Undercity operate on strict scholarly technique, turning dangerous planar forces into reliable assets for the Horde's frontier wars."},kw={"carendin halgar","egalin","egalins grimoire","perrine","scarlet crusade","temple of the damned","tirisfal glades","undercity","voidwalker"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1471","quest:1478","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:undercity"},m={start="Carendin Halgar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1473,ri={"Egalin's Grimoire"}},src={"Creature of the Void (Undercity)"}}
E["quest:1474"] = {t="quest",n="The Binding",z="undercity",s="The Binding is the final initiation in an Undercity warlock's journey to summon and command a succubus. Directed by Carendin Halgar, the practitioner uses pure hearts to draw a demon from the Twisting Nether into a ritual circle, subjugating its will through combat.",h="The Binding is the final initiation in an Undercity warlock's journey to summon and command a succubus.",sec={{t="A Test of Will",b="Within the dark alcoves of the Magic Quarter, Forsaken warlocks refine their command over demonic entities. Summoning a succubus is considered a critical rite of passage. Unlike the brute force of a voidwalker or the minor malice of an imp, a succubus wields seductive and mental enchantments capable of ensnaring the caster. Carendin Halgar requires initiates to prove their mind and magic are ironclad before trusting them with permanent dominion over such an entity.",sp=0},{t="Subjugation in the Circle",b="Drawing upon the harvested Pure Hearts gathered from innocent souls in the Wetlands and Silverpine Forest, the warlock unlocks an aperture into the Twisting Nether. Once summoned into the binding circle, the demon attacks instantly, seeking to overpower or entrance the caster. Only by breaking its physical form and casting its essence back into the void does the warlock assert complete mastery, earning the knowledge needed to call forth the demon at will.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This ritual allows Forsaken warlocks to prove their mastery over higher demons. By summoning and defeating a succubus in the Magic Quarter, the warlock proves they cannot be swayed by its charms, earning the spell to summon and command one in battle.",al={"why do the binding","what does the binding reward","what is this quest for"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar is a warlock trainer located in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. He oversees the training and trials of Forsaken spellcasters, testing their mental endurance and dark arts before granting them more dangerous summoning rituals.",al={"who gives the binding","carendin halgar lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why were pure hearts needed to summon the demon?",a="Demons of the succubus breed feed upon emotion, purity, and corruption. The Pure Hearts acquired in earlier tasks act as an irresistible metaphysical bait, coaxing the demon to manifest directly into the mortal realm through the summoning circle.",al={"why pure hearts","hearts of the pure purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the summoning take place?",a="The summoning takes place directly in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, using the specialized ritual circle near Carendin Halgar and the warlock mentors.",al={"where do i summon the succubus","undercity summoning circle location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the succubus need to be slain?",a="Warlocks do not negotiate with their minions; they subjugate them. By shattering the demon's form in the summoning circle, the warlock bends its spirit to their dominance, ensuring it returns as a subservient thrall rather than a master.",al={"why fight the succubus","why kill summoned succubus"},it="motive"},{q="Are succubi dangerous to Undercity warlocks?",a="Yes. Even though Forsaken possess considerable mental resilience against fear and sleep, Carendin Halgar explicitly warns that a succubus's charms have bound many strong minds. Carelessness during the ritual results in death or enslavement.",al={"can a succubus charm undead","succubus danger"},it="danger"},{q="What is the summoned succubus and why is it here?",a="You are conjuring a succubus across the void directly into the Magic Quarter's summoning circle. Succubi are cunning demons adept at enthralling mortal minds, making them among the most perilous minions for a warlock to bind. This particular fiend does not dwell here naturally; it is drawn into our world solely by the pure hearts you gathered, specifically so you can break its will in combat.",al={"who is the summoned succubus","what am i fighting","succubus target"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why must you summon and defeat the succubus yourself?",a="Demonic subjugation is a personal trial that cannot be delegated. Carendin Halgar serves as a mentor, but the demonic bond requires the summoner's own mind and magic to shatter the creature's defenses. If Halgar or the city guards stepped in to subdue the succubus for you, the demon would never bow to your command, and your authority as a warlock would remain incomplete.",al={"why cant carendin fight the succubus","why does carendin need me","why me succubus"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="This rite represents a crucial step in your dark path, demonstrating your capacity to master seductive mental forces and bind cunning Nether-spawn to your will.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken practitioners view demonic subjugation pragmatically, using whatever dark tools are necessary to secure survival and dominion in Lordaeron."},kw={"binding","carendin halgar","magic quarter","pure hearts","succubus","undercity","warlock"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1476","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={start="Carendin Halgar",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1474},src={"The Binding (Succubus, Undercity)"}}
E["quest:1476"] = {t="quest",n="Hearts of the Pure",z="undercity",s="Hearts of the Pure is a sinister warlock trial assigned in the Undercity by Godrick Farsan on behalf of Carendin Halgar. In order to prepare the ritual bait needed to bind a succubus, an aspiring summoner must hunt down and butcher two uniquely righteous human men. Their pure hearts serve as an irresistible temptation for the demonic temptress awaiting summoning.",h="Hearts of the Pure is a sinister warlock trial assigned in the Undercity by Godrick Farsan on behalf of...",sec={{t="Bait for a Demon",b="Binding a succubus requires an understanding of temptation that cuts both ways. While the Nether's sirens prey upon desire and ruin, nothing draws them out of the Twisting Nether quite like untainted virtue ripe for corruption. Within the Temple of the Damned, master summoner Carendin Halgar delegates the groundwork to Godrick Farsan, who scours human lands for souls whose goodness remains pristine and unbroken.",sp=0},{t="The Quarry",b="Farsan identifies two distinct paragons of virtue. The first is Dalin Forgewright, an honorable man attending to desperate Lordaeron refugees barred from sanctuary outside the sealed Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine. The second is Comar Villard, a faithful husband tirelessly searching the perilous marshlands of the Wetlands for any trace of his lost wife. To a Forsaken warlock, their devotion, empathy, and loyalty make them prime sacrifices.",sp=0},{t="A Forsaken Perspective",b="Carrying out the hunt requires the summoner to traverse dangerous Alliance-held and wild territories, culminating in the butchery of both men. Upon returning the bloody prizes to the Temple of the Damned, Carendin Halgar observes with dark irony that the physical organ of a good man appears no different than any other corpse's remains. Yet in the dark arts of demonology, the spiritual purity clinging to their flesh is potent enough to lure a succubus into captivity.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why do warlocks need pure hearts to summon a succubus?",a="A succubus thrives on corrupting mortal innocence and virtue. To lure one across the Nether and trap her in a binding circle, Carendin Halgar requires bait she cannot resist. The hearts of genuinely pure and selfless men provide that irresistible spiritual temptation.",al={"why pure hearts","succubus bait lore","why kill dalin and comar"},it="item"},{q="Who is Dalin Forgewright?",a="Dalin Forgewright is an honorable human patrolling on horseback along the closed gates of the Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine Forest. He dedicated his life to caring for and protecting the displaced refugees of Lordaeron who were rejected and shut out by the kingdom of Gilneas.",al={"dalin forgewright lore","who is dalin","greymane wall guy"},it="target"},{q="Who is Comar Villard?",a="Comar Villard is a devoted human wanderer found searching the northern road of the Wetlands just south of the Thandol Span. Unlike common travelers, he is driven purely by grief and steadfast love, refusing to abandon his search for his missing wife.",al={"comar villard lore","who is comar","wetlands human heart"},it="target"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead?",a="Delivering the two hearts to Carendin Halgar allows him to prepare the summoning circle in the Temple of the Damned. This immediately leads into 'The Binding', where the warlock summons and subdues a succubus to serve as a permanent minion.",al={"what comes next","after hearts of the pure","succubus quest reward"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Godrick Farsan, an assistant located in the Temple of the Damned within the Undercity's Magic Quarter, gives the assignment. He projects magical illusions of Dalin and Comar to show the warlock exactly whom to hunt.",al={"who starts hearts of the pure","godrick farsan quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar dismiss the appearance of the hearts?",a="Upon completing the quest, Carendin observes with grim detachment that the physical heart of a goodly man looks virtually identical to any other slab of flesh. As an Undead practitioner of the dark arts, physical morality means little to him beyond its utility as a magical reagent.",al={"carendin dialogue","heart appearance"}},{q="Why does Godrick Farsan want these hearts collected?",a="Godrick aids Carendin Halgar in training worthy Forsaken warlocks. To summon and dominate a succubus, Halgar requires rare conduits—specifically the hearts of truly pure, noble men whose virtues can lure a demon of temptation into a binding circle. Godrick tracked down suitable targets so you could harvest their hearts and prove your dark arts.",al={"why does godrick need hearts","godrick farsan motive","why harvest pure hearts"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="This rite of passage teaches that a warlock must learn to weaponize not just misery and fear, but the very nobility of others to bind demons to their will.",["race:Undead"]="The mission illustrates the chilling worldview of the Forsaken, who casually view the remaining survivors of Lordaeron and their enduring virtues as convenient livestock for ritual slaughter.",["faction:Alliance"]="The victims are tragic figures among the Alliance and human remnants—one guarding starving refugees shut out by Gilneas, the other searching in vain for a lost spouse in the marshlands."},kw={"carendin halgar","comar villard","dalin forgewright","godrick farsan","greymane wall","hearts of the pure","succubus","temple of the damned","thandol span","undercity"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","npc:godrick-farsan","subzone:greymane-wall","subzone:thandol-span","zone:silverpine","zone:wetlands","topic:lordaeron","topic:alliance"},m={start="Godrick Farsan",["end"]="Carendin Halgar",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1476,ri={"Comar's Heart","Dalin's Heart"}},src={"Hearts of the Pure"}}
E["quest:1478"] = {t="quest",n="Halgar's Summons",z="undercity",s="Halgar's Summons is a formal directive given to rising Forsaken warlocks who have reached a critical threshold in their dark craft. Master Carendin Halgar requires their presence in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity to begin rigorous advanced training. Answering his call sets the stage for summoning and binding dangerous entities from the Nether.",h="Halgar's Summons is a formal directive given to rising Forsaken warlocks who have reached a critical...",sec={{t="A Master's Notice",b="When a warlock operating around Brill or the Tirisfal wilderness demonstrates adequate control over basic fel energies, word reaches the deeper subterranean halls of the Undercity. Senior practitioners such as Ageron Kargal serve as talent spotters, relaying notices to those who show genuine promise. To be summoned by Carendin Halgar is both a rare privilege and a perilous undertaking, indicating that basic imps and petty curses no longer suffice for the practitioner's education.",sp=0},{t="The Magic Quarter",b="Halgar oversees warlock rites from the shadowed reaches of the Magic Quarter, situated near the sinister altar known as the Temple of the Damned. Forsaken darkcasters operate without the squeamish moral restrictions of the living, yet even they demand rigorous discipline when dabbling in planar summonings. Halgar does not tolerate hesitation or sentimentality; his summons expects immediate deference and complete readiness to confront the hostile horrors of the Twisting Nether.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Carendin Halgar?",a="Carendin Halgar is the primary warlock trainer residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. He oversees the dark development of Forsaken summoners and tests their resolve before teaching them to bind powerful Nether creatures.",al={"carendin halgar","master halgar","who is halgar"},it="identity"},{q="Who directs me to Halgar?",a="Ageron Kargal, an established warlock trainer stationed in Brill, dispatches you after receiving word that Master Halgar has taken a personal interest in your progression.",al={"who gives halgars summons","ageron kargal","who gives quest"}},{q="Where can I find Carendin Halgar in Undercity?",a="Halgar is located within the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, positioned close to the dark dais known as the Temple of the Damned.",al={"halgar location","where is halgar","magic quarter halgar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this summons important?",a="The summons marks your transition from rudimentary spellcasting to high-risk demonic subjugation, specifically initiating the trials required to bind a Voidwalker into your service.",al={"why do i need this quest","quest purpose","what does halgars summons lead to"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Halgar willing to teach anyone?",a="Halgar specifically focuses his attention on promising warlocks. He wastes little time on idle pleasantries and demands that any apprentice brought before him has proven capable of handling volatile fel arts.",al={"can anyone talk to halgar","halgar requirements"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Halgar?",a="Once you report to Halgar, he immediately tests your magical capability by assigning you tasks to acquire the components needed to summon and bind an otherworldly shadow minion.",al={"what comes next","after halgars summons"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Ageron Kargal send you to Carendin Halgar?",a="Ageron Kargal serves as a warlock mentor in Brill, but your growing mastery requires advanced instruction beyond what a village tutor can provide. When word arrives from Master Carendin Halgar himself requesting your presence, Ageron dutifully directs you to the Undercity. For Ageron, guiding promising warlocks upward strengthens the Forsaken's dark arts and honors the hierarchy among the practitioners in the Magic Quarter.",al={"ageron kargal motive","why send me to halgar","why does ageron want this"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Carendin Halgar summon you specifically?",a="Carendin Halgar rarely reaches out to instruct just any novice. Having proven your affinity for the dark arts in Tirisfal Glades, you have reached a critical threshold in your craft where foundational spells no longer suffice. Halgar summons you directly because unlocking deeper and more volatile powers—such as reaching into the Nether to command greater fiends—demands personal oversight from a true master of the craft.",al={"why does halgar need me","why halgars summons me","why am i summoned"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="This rite of passage bridges elementary training with true planar enslavement, bringing you under the scrutiny of Undercity's foremost master of the dark arts.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken warlocks pursue shadow and fel with ruthless, uninhibited ambition, and Halgar's sanctum exemplifies their pragmatic disregard for living caution."},kw={"ageron kargal","carendin halgar","halgar's summons","magic quarter","temple of the damned","undercity","voidwalker","warlock"},rel={"npc:carendin-halgar","quest:1473","quest:1471","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={start="Ageron Kargal",["end"]="Carendin Halgar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1478},src={"Halgar's Summons"}}
E["quest:1803"] = {t="quest",n="Tome of the Cabal",z="undercity",s="This quest tasks Horde warlocks with reuniting the severed halves of the ancient Tome of the Cabal for Jorah Annison in the Undercity. Once kept within the kingdom of Lordaeron, the grimoire was torn apart and scattered across the world before being lost entirely. Tracking down its damp and tattered remnants requires braving hostile waters in the Eastern Kingdoms and deep centaur territory in Kalimdor.",h="This quest tasks Horde warlocks with reuniting the severed halves of the ancient Tome of the Cabal for Jorah...",sec={{t="A Divided Legacy",b="The Tome of the Cabal was once preserved within the library walls of the old kingdom of Lordaeron. At some point prior to the kingdom's downfall, the sinister grimoire was deliberately vandalized, stripped of nearly half its pages, and sundered into two pieces. The remaining formal text was slated for transit south to the dwarven halls of Ironforge, but fate intervened: the transport wrecked along the rocky coastline west of Southshore, leaving the pages to rot in the shallows under the watchful eyes of scavenging murlocs.",sp=0},{t="Scattered across Continents",b="The vandalized half of the tome wandered even farther afield. Snatched away from Lordaeron, it traveled all the way to southern Kalimdor, falling into the rough possession of the Galak centaur deep within Splithoof Hold in Thousand Needles. Recovering the complete text demands that a warlock scour the damp Hillsbrad shoreline for the Moldy Tome and infiltrate the dust and savagery of the centaur canyons for the Tattered Manuscript. Once both remnants are brought together before Jorah Annison, the legendary dark text is restored to a single, readable volume.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Tome of the Cabal?",a="It is an arcane and demonic grimoire once held in the capital of Lordaeron. Containing advanced warlock rituals, it was defaced and split into two portions before being lost across two different continents.",al={"tome of the cabal lore","what is this book","tome of cabal"},it="item"},{q="Why is one part of the book near Southshore?",a="After the book was vandalized, the surviving bound portion was slated for transfer to the scholars of Ironforge. However, the vessel carrying it wrecked on the coast west of Southshore, leaving the grimoire stranded amidst the local murlocs.",al={"why southshore","moldy tome origin","coast west of southshore"},it="history"},{q="How did the pages end up with the centaur in Thousand Needles?",a="Roughly half the pages were torn out of the original tome in Lordaeron and smuggled away. Through trade, plunder, or wandering hands, that tattered manuscript eventually wound up deep inside Splithoof Hold, kept inside a chest by the Galak centaur.",al={"why centaur have it","thousand needles pages","splithoof hold book"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Jorah Annison?",a="Jorah Annison is a Forsaken warlock practitioner based in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. He guides rising Horde warlocks in recovering forgotten, forbidden lore to deepen their mastery over demonic forces.",al={"jorah annison lore","who is jorah"},it="identity"},{q="Who vandalized the tome in the first place?",a="The exact identity of the culprit remains unknown. Jorah Annison himself laments the vandalism, questioning who could commit such a heinous act against a text of such profound occult power.",al={"who tore the book","who stole the pages","tome vandal"}},{q="What does Jorah do with the book once you bring both parts back?",a="Upon receiving both the Moldy Tome and the Tattered Manuscript, Jorah Annison assembles the pieces into a single volume and reads through its pages, preparing you for the next steps in your demonic rites.",al={"what happens after turn in","restored tome"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Jorah Annison want the Tome of the Cabal?",a="Jorah Annison is a Forsaken warlock scholar dedicated to unearthing lost fel lore once housed in Lordaeron. Recovering the fractured Tome of the Cabal allows him to study its occult secrets firsthand while guiding promising warlocks in mastering dangerous, advanced summonings.",al={"why does jorah want this","jorah annison motive","why collect the tome of the cabal"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Moldy Tome?",a="The Moldy Tome contains the salvaged remains of the original text meant for transfer to Ironforge after Lordaeron's fall. Lost in a shipwreck along the coast near Southshore and scavenged by murlocs, it holds one vital half of the Cabal's rituals.",al={"what is moldy tome","moldy tome lore","use of moldy tome"},it="item",add=true},{q="What is the Tattered Manuscript?",a="The Tattered Manuscript is the missing half of the Tome of the Cabal, torn away when the book was vandalized in Lordaeron. Through unknown hands, these stolen pages crossed the sea into Kalimdor, eventually ending up locked in a chest among the Galak centaur of Thousand Needles.",al={"what is tattered manuscript","tattered manuscript lore","use of tattered manuscript"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Reclaiming the Tome of the Cabal is a rite of passage for intermediate practitioners, gathering lost Lordaeron arcana to expand your summoning repertoire.",["race:Undead"]="The tome was preserved in Lordaeron before the kingdom fell, making its recovery a reclamation of occult heritage from the Forsaken's past human lives.",["faction:Horde"]="Tracking down the manuscript sends you through the canyons of Thousand Needles, where Horde forces stationed at Freewind Post wage constant war against the native centaur."},kw={"galak","jorah annison","lordaeron","moldy tome","southshore","splithoof hold","tattered manuscript","thousand needles","tome of the cabal","warlock quest"},rel={"npc:jorah-annison","zone:undercity","subzone:southshore","subzone:splithoof-hold","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","topic:murloc","quest:4841"},m={start="Jorah Annison",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1803,ri={"Moldy Tome","Tattered Manuscript"}},src={"Tome of the Cabal (Horde, 2)"}}
E["quest:1818"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Dillinger",z="undercity",s="Speak with Dillinger is a Horde military directive issued in the Undercity. Austil de Mon dispatches able-bodied fighters to Deathguard Dillinger in Brill to take on a hazardous combat mission in service of Lady Sylvanas.",h="Speak with Dillinger is a Horde military directive issued in the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Front",b="Within the subterranean halls of the Undercity, Austil de Mon keeps a watchful eye out for promising combatants willing to serve the Dark Lady. When the Deathguards stationed on the surface require capable hands, de Mon directs unproven adventurers out of the royal capital and into the field. Deathguard Dillinger, who oversees security on the western edges of Brill, has requested someone with martial competence for an urgent task.",sp=0},{t="Testing the Faithful",b="Brill sits squarely on the front line of Tirisfal Glades, where the Forsaken must constantly prove their martial dominance against hostile threats. Dillinger's post near the village graveyard puts him in prime position to manage local incursions. For the young warrior, reporting to Dillinger is more than a simple errand: it is a formal test of combat prowess and political loyalty to the newly forged Forsaken nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this mission?",a="Austil de Mon, located in the Undercity, identifies potential soldiers and sends them to assist Deathguard Dillinger.",al={"quest giver","austil de mon","who starts speak with dillinger"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Deathguard Dillinger be found?",a="Deathguard Dillinger is stationed on the western edge of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, near the graveyard entrance.",al={"dillinger location","where is dillinger","find dillinger"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of reporting to Dillinger?",a="Dillinger requires an able-bodied champion for a combat mission to defend Brill and prove their allegiance to the Forsaken cause.",al={"why speak with dillinger","dillinger purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What assignment does Dillinger have prepared?",a="Once you report to Deathguard Dillinger, he tasks you with hunting down a dangerous threat known as Ulag the Cleaver.",al={"what does dillinger want","next quest dillinger"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Do other Horde races receive this order?",a="Any Horde warrior who has earned the trust of Undercity officials can take the assignment, though it is primarily designed to assess recruits defending Tirisfal Glades.",al={"is this undead only","can orcs do this"},it="for_you"},{q="Why is this directive given in the Undercity instead of Brill?",a="Austil de Mon serves as an intake scout within the capital, funneling newly capable adventurers outward to frontier commanders who need immediate muscle.",al={"why undercity start","austil de mon role"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Austil de Mon send you to Dillinger?",a="Austil de Mon acts as an intermediary, directing emerging Forsaken who seek greater standing to where their martial talents can serve the realm. By directing capable hands out of the Undercity and into the field under Deathguard Dillinger's command, he ensures that the frontline settlements receive reinforcement while testing whether you possess genuine value and devotion to Lady Sylvanas's cause.",al={"austil de mon motive","why send to dillinger","austil de mon reason"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For newly liberated Forsaken, responding to Dillinger's call is a crucial step in proving your dedication to the Dark Lady and the defense of Tirisfal.",["class:Warrior"]="Deathguard commanders value sheer martial grit above all else, making this dispatch a direct test of your combat capabilities on the front line.",["faction:Horde"]="Answering defense calls for the Undercity cements cross-faction solidarity between Kalimdor's allies and the newly integrated Forsaken."},kw={"austil de mon","brill","deathguard dillinger","speak with dillinger","tirisfal glades","ulag the cleaver","undercity"},rel={"npc:deathguard-dillinger","npc:austil-de-mon","subzone:brill","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Austil de Mon",["end"]="Deathguard Dillinger",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1818},src={"Speak with Dillinger"}}
E["quest:1846"] = {t="quest",n="Dragonmaw Shinbones",z="undercity",s="Dragonmaw Shinbones is a Horde warrior quest directed by the armorer Velora Nitely in the Undercity. To craft the resilient Brutal Legguards, warriors are dispatched into the southern Wetlands to harvest exceptionally thick shinbones from the hostile Dragonmaw orcs.",h="Dragonmaw Shinbones is a Horde warrior quest directed by the armorer Velora Nitely in the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Armature",b="Forging armor fit for a seasoned frontline warrior demands unorthodox materials. When tasked with fashioning Brutal Legguards, the Forsaken armorer Velora Nitely specifies a structural brace constructed from thick, resilient bone. Rather than utilizing common beasts, she directs aspiring warriors toward the Dragonmaw orcs of the Wetlands, whose dense skeletal builds provide the necessary resilience to withstand heavy blows in combat.",sp=0},{t="Testing the Marrow",b="Harvesting bone from the Dragonmaw is only half the ordeal. Velora instructs warriors to manually test every bone taken in the field; any specimen brittle enough to snap in bare hands is utterly useless for the forge. Warriors must scour the renegade encampments along the Wetlands' crags, breaking weak bones until eight genuinely sturdy examples survive the test of strength.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Velora Nitely need orc shinbones specifically?",a="Velora requires dense, thick material to act as a supportive framework for the Brutal Legguards. She considers the Dragonmaw orcs of the Wetlands uniquely suited because their heavy, powerful skeletal frame provides far more structural rigidity than ordinary game or scavenged remains.",al={"why orc shinbones","why dragonmaw bones","velora bone armor"},it="item"},{q="Why are the Dragonmaw orcs fair game for Horde warriors?",a="The Dragonmaw clan remnants entrenched in the Wetlands are hostile renegades clinging to the dark legacy of the Second War. They hold no allegiance to Thrall's modern Horde, making them enemies of the state and fair quarry for Horde adventurers.",al={"are dragonmaw in the horde","why fight dragonmaw","dragonmaw horde standing"},it="target"},{q="Where are the Dragonmaw found for this task?",a="They reside in the Wetlands, south across the Thandol Span from the Arathi Highlands. Warriors typically hunt them around the mountainous bluffs of the Angerfang Encampment, situated southwest of the main northern highway.",al={"dragonmaw location","where to find dragonmaw shinbones","angerfang encampment location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do so many of the bones break during the quest?",a="Velora requires only the densest marrow frames for armor forging. As part of her instructions, warriors test each bone by hand; any bone that snaps under raw physical force is discarded as too fragile to protect a warrior's legs in battle.",al={"broken shinbones","why do shinbones snap","sturdy bone test"},gp=true},{q="Who is Velora Nitely?",a="Velora Nitely is a Forsaken armorer operating within the Undercity. Gruff, morbidly dry, and prone to grim attempts at humor, she assists Horde warriors in fabricating specialized martial gear suited for battle-hardened veterans.",al={"velora nitely lore","who is velora","undercity armorer"},it="identity"},{q="What armor piece is forged from these bones?",a="The collected bones form the internal framing for the Brutal Legguards, a durable set of plate-style greaves created for mid-level Horde warriors.",al={"shinbones reward","what are the shinbones for","brutal legguards craft"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Velora Nitely want this done?",a="Velora Nitely is crafting the legendary Brutal Hauberk armor set for promising Horde warriors. Crafting the Brutal Legguards requires exceptionally dense, resilient bone to form a sturdy reinforcing frame, and she relies on your martial prowess to harvest the raw material while she prepares the forge in the Undercity.",al={"velora nitely motive","why does velora want shinbones","velora nitely why"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="This trial tests both a warrior's physical fortitude in the field and their willingness to harvest morbid materials to craft superior armor.",["faction:Horde"]="Striking down the rogue Dragonmaw clan in Khaz Modan weakens a dangerous Old Horde remnant while empowering the champions of Thrall's new coalition.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs loyal to Orgrimmar, culling the unrepentant Dragonmaw is a stark reminder of their people's fel past and the violent cost of redemption.",["race:Undead"]="Velora Nitely's pragmatic use of humanoid remains exemplifies the Forsaken mentality of weaponizing every available resource, however macabre."},kw={"angerfang encampment","brutal legguards","dragonmaw","shinbones","thandol span","undercity","velora nitely","wetlands"},rel={"npc:velora-nitely","quest:1841","subzone:angerfang-encampment","zone:wetlands","subzone:thandol-span","zone:undercity","zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall"},m={start="Velora Nitely",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1846,ri={"Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbone"}},src={"Dragonmaw Shinbones"}}
E["quest:1881"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Anastasia",z="undercity",s="Speak with Anastasia is an introductory summons directing promising Forsaken mages to Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity. Dispatched by mage trainer Cain Firesong, the young caster is called to the Magic Quarter to undertake critical work for the magi of the Forsaken. This brief summons sets the stage for investigations out into the blighted lands of Tirisfal Glades.",h="Speak with Anastasia is an introductory summons directing promising Forsaken mages to Anastasia Hartwell in...",sec={{t="A Call to the Magic Quarter",b="As nascent spellcasters hone their early talents under the guidance of Cain Firesong, they are soon directed deeper into the capital. The mages of the Forsaken maintain a dedicated enclave within the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, organizing both arcane scholarship and strategic defensive efforts across Lordaeron. Cain Firesong acts as an evaluator, filtering out mere novices and sending those who demonstrate genuine talent directly to senior practitioners who require capable field hands.",sp=0},{t="Anastasia Hartwell's Ambition",b="Anastasia Hartwell stands among the prominent mage instructors within the Undercity. Rather than leaving promising students to study trivial incantations in safety, she wastes little time pressing them into service for the Forsaken's territorial and practical interests. Answering her summons is both a rite of passage for arcane practitioners and an induction into the shadowy, pragmatic magical pursuits that define the post-Scourge undead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Anastasia Hartwell?",a="Cain Firesong, a Forsaken mage trainer, sends you to her after recognizing that your arcane talents are developed enough to assist with more demanding matters within the capital.",al={"who gives speak with anastasia","quest giver speak with anastasia","cain firesong summons"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Anastasia Hartwell be found?",a="Anastasia Hartwell resides in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, where she coordinates and instructs practitioners of the arcane arts for the Forsaken.",al={"where is anastasia hartwell","anastasia hartwell location","find anastasia"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this summons?",a="Anastasia is seeking a capable caster to perform practical tasks outside the city walls, starting with field assignments in Tirisfal Glades such as investigating the Balnir Farmstead.",al={"why does she want me","speak with anastasia purpose","what does anastasia need"},it="purpose"},{q="What quest follows Speak with Anastasia?",a="Reporting to Anastasia directly leads into 'The Balnir Farmstead', sending you out to eastern Tirisfal Glades to gather snapdragons from the farmstead's garden.",al={"what quest comes next","next quest after speak with anastasia","speak with anastasia followup"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest limited to certain classes?",a="Yes, this quest is specifically intended for mages of the Forsaken, serving as a class progression stepping stone as they reach early competence around circle ten.",al={"is this a mage only quest","who can do speak with anastasia","class requirement"},gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken mages maintain their own quarters in Undercity?",a="The Magic Quarter provides a dedicated sanctuary for Forsaken arcanists, warlocks, and researchers to study and cast away from the physical quarters, continuing their pre-Third War traditions within the underbelly of Lordaeron.",al={"why magic quarter","forsaken mages undercity"},it="history"},{q="Why does Cain Firesong send you to Anastasia Hartwell?",a="Cain Firesong serves as an instructor for fledgling Forsaken mages in Brill. Once you demonstrate sufficient skill in the arcane arts, his duty is to direct promising spellcasters to Anastasia Hartwell in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Hartwell coordinates greater undertakings for the Forsaken's magical order, and Cain ensures their ranks are replenished with capable practitioners ready for service.",al={"why does cain send you","cain firesong motive","why visit anastasia hartwell"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="This quest marks your transition from basic arcane training into active service for the mages of the Undercity.",["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken arcanists, answering Hartwell's call represents an opportunity to leverage Lordaeron's intellectual past against its present perils."},kw={"anastasia hartwell","balnir farmstead","cain firesong","mage quest","magic quarter","undercity"},rel={"npc:anastasia-hartwell","npc:cain-firesong","quest:1882","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","npc:talen","subzone:balnir-farmstead","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Cain Firesong",["end"]="Anastasia Hartwell",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1881},src={"Speak with Anastasia"}}
E["quest:1882"] = {t="quest",n="The Balnir Farmstead",z="undercity",s="\"The Balnir Farmstead\" is an early rite of passage for young Forsaken mages, directed by Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity's Mage Quarter. Initiates are sent to eastern Tirisfal Glades to gather snapdragons from an abandoned farmstead sitting dangerously close to the border of the Plaguelands. The floral samples serve as barometers for the encroaching magical corruption spreading from the Scourge-blighted east.",h="\"The Balnir Farmstead\" is an early rite of passage for young Forsaken mages, directed by Anastasia Hartwell...",sec={{t="A Magical Barometer",b="While the Royal Apothecary Society frequently studies the effects of necromancy and decay, the mages of the Forsaken maintain their own watchful eye on the borderlands. Anastasia Hartwell tasks novice spellcasters with travelling to the Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades. Snapdragons native to the farm's gardens are naturally sensitive to shifting magical currents, absorbing ambient energies from the soil and atmosphere. By examining these blooms, arcane scholars in the Undercity can measure whether the corruptive contagion of the Lich King's domain has seeped past the bulwark into Tirisfal proper.",sp=0},{t="The Eastern Border",b="The Balnir Farmstead sits near the fringes of the glades, uncomfortably near the blight-scarred wilderness of the Western Plaguelands. The Forsaken recognize that the Lich King's plague is an unruly and destructive power that actively rots the land itself. Although the Forsaken harness their own dark arts, uncontained Scourge corruption threatens their territorial borders and security. Anastasia intends to pass the gathered snapdragons along to the apothecaries, uniting arcane observation with alchemical investigation to defend Lordaeron's reclaimed heartland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell want snapdragons specifically?",a="Balnir snapdragons possess a distinct natural sensitivity to ambient magical forces. Because they absorb energies directly from the earth and air, studying them allows Forsaken mages to determine whether the arcane and necromantic blight of the nearby Plaguelands is contaminating Tirisfal Glades.",al={"why snapdragons","balnir snapdragons purpose","what are snapdragons for"},it="item"},{q="Where is the Balnir Farmstead located?",a="The farmstead lies in eastern Tirisfal Glades, tucked toward the border where the glades approach the blighted frontier of the Western Plaguelands. The snapdragons grow within the overgrown plots and gardens surrounding the decrepit farm buildings.",al={"balnir farmstead location","where is balnir farm","find balnir farmstead"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Anastasia Hartwell?",a="Anastasia Hartwell is a prominent Forsaken mage and trainer residing in the Mage Quarter of the Undercity. She guides newly emergent undead casters, instructing them on discipline, arcane balance, and the practical defense of their borders against rival powers.",al={"anastasia hartwell lore","who is anastasia"},it="identity"},{q="Why do Forsaken mages care about stopping the plague?",a="Though the Forsaken experiment with their own plagues and blights, the Lich King's infectious scourge magic is considered an uncontrolled aberration. Left unchecked, the Scourge's corruption would swallow Tirisfal Glades whole and undermine the Forsaken's independence.",al={"why stop the plague","do forsaken hate the plague"},it="motive"},{q="What happens to the flowers after you collect them?",a="Upon receiving the snapdragons, Anastasia prepares to hand them over to the Undercity's apothecaries. The alchemists and mages dissect the specimens together to assess how deeply the soil and flora have been tainted by the Scourge.",al={"what does anastasia do with the flowers","who gets the snapdragons"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this quest restricted to mages?",a="Yes. This task serves as a dedicated class quest offered exclusively to young Forsaken mages who have advanced beyond their initial lessons in Deathknell and arrived in the capital to prove their grasp of arcane theory.",al={"is balnir farmstead mage only","mage class quest"},gp=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="This early trial teaches novice mages that their study of the arcane is essential for monitoring and defending against foreign magical corruption.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, safeguarding the borders of Tirisfal Glades against the encroaching Scourge is a matter of immediate survival and sovereignty.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The Balnir snapdragon provides an example of how botanical specimens can serve as direct reservoirs and indicators of magical pollution."},kw={"anastasia","balnir","farmstead","hartwell","mage","plaguelands","snapdragons","tirisfal","undercity"},rel={"npc:anastasia-hartwell","quest:1881","subzone:balnir-farmstead","subzone:mage-quarter","zone:undercity","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:lich-king"},m={start="Anastasia Hartwell",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1882,ri={"Balnir Snapdragons"}},src={"The Balnir Farmstead"}}
E["quest:1885"] = {t="quest",n="Mennet Carkad",z="undercity",s="Mennet Carkad is an introductory rogue quest in the Undercity that brings promising operatives into the fold of the Deathstalkers. Directed by Marion Call, aspiring assassins are summoned to report directly to Mennet Carkad deep within the Rogues' Quarter.",h="Mennet Carkad is an introductory rogue quest in the Undercity that brings promising operatives into the fold...",sec={{t="A Summons from the Shadows",b="Within the dark corridors of the Undercity, word travels quietly among the Forsaken's covert operatives. When a scout or assassin catches the eye of the higher leadership, an invitation is issued. Marion Call passes down word that Mennet Carkad, a prominent figure among the rogue handlers, has taken personal notice. Given the lethal reputation of the Forsaken intelligence apparatus, ignoring such a directive is not considered a viable option.",sp=0},{t="Joining the Deathstalkers",b="Mennet Carkad waits in the shadowy alcoves of the Rogues' Quarter, watching over recruits and evaluating their readiness. Those who heed his call are not simply joining an ordinary guild of thieves; they are being tested for entry into the Deathstalkers, the dreaded espionage and assassination arm of the Forsaken. Swift obedience is merely the first baseline test for anyone seeking to serve the Dark Lady from the shadows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad is a rogue trainer and Deathstalker handler operating within the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity. He oversees promising covert agents and assigns critical missions on behalf of the Forsaken leadership.",al={"mennet carkad lore","who is carkad"},it="target"},{q="What happens if someone ignores Mennet Carkad's summons?",a="Marion Call warns that you would not want to know the fate of those who ignored Carkad's call in the past. In the ruthless hierarchy of the Forsaken, refusing or ignoring orders from intelligence commanders typically results in swift, fatal elimination.",al={"ignoring carkad","what happens if you ignore summons"},it="danger"},{q="Who are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the elite order of rogues, spies, and assassins serving the Forsaken. Operating from the shadows of the Undercity, they eliminate high-value targets, gather intelligence, and secure Lordaeron from enemies like the Scarlet Crusade and the Scourge.",al={"deathstalker lore","what are the deathstalkers"},it="people"},{q="Where can I find Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad is located in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity, typically surrounded by other covert operatives, trainers, and shadowcraft supplies.",al={"carkad location","where is mennet carkad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest to seek out Mennet Carkad?",a="The task is assigned by Marion Call in the Rogues' Quarter, who notices your burgeoning skills and warns you that Carkad expects prompt obedience.",al={"who starts this quest","marion call quest"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What comes after reporting to Mennet Carkad?",a="Reporting to Mennet Carkad immediately leads into direct service for the Deathstalkers, starting with tasks designed to prove your cunning and loyalty to the Forsaken cause.",al={"next quest after carkad","what does carkad want"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Marion Call send you to Mennet Carkad?",a="Marion Call is simply delivering an order from higher up. Mennet Carkad, a master among the Deathstalkers, has taken a personal interest in your potential and formally summoned you to the Rogues' Quarter. Marion knows better than to stand between a powerful Deathstalker and his prospective recruit—those who ignore or obstruct Carkad's summons tend to meet a swift and grim fate.",al={"why does marion call want this done","why go to mennet carkad","marion call motive"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="This summons marks your transition from an unproven cutpurse into a recognized asset of the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken's elite shadow network.",["race:Undead"]="The Deathstalkers are essential to the survival of the Forsaken, hunting Scarlet zealots and Scourge remnants while protecting Queen Sylvanas from hidden threats."},kw={"assassin","deathstalkers","forsaken rogue","marion call","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","undercity"},rel={"quest:1886","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={start="Marion Call",["end"]="Mennet Carkad",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1885},src={"Mennet Carkad (quest)"}}
E["quest:1886"] = {t="quest",n="The Deathstalkers",z="undercity",s="This task marks the trial for initiates seeking entry into the Deathstalkers, the covert and lethal arm answering to Lord Varimathras in the Undercity. Assigned by Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter, the mission demands ruthless initiative to intercept a traveling messenger. Completing it opens the door to deeper clandestine schemes within the Forsaken realm.",h="This task marks the trial for initiates seeking entry into the Deathstalkers, the covert and lethal arm...",sec={{t="A Test in the Shadows",b="The Deathstalkers do not admit just anyone into their ranks. Operating directly under dreadlord Varimathras, this secretive order acts as both the secret police and elite assassination corps of the Forsaken. To earn their notice, a hopeful agent must demonstrate cunning, discretion, and an unhesitating willingness to eliminate targets. In the shadowy corners of the Rogues' Quarter, handler Mennet Carkad sets an initiation trial designed to weed out the weak or overscrupulous.",sp=0},{t="The Interception",b="The initiate's target is Astor Hadren, a courier traveling the road between the Undercity and Silverpine Forest. Carkad offers no tactical advice, leaving the method of securing Hadren's personal introduction entirely up to the operative. The task hinges on intercepting Astor, seizing his credentials, and ensuring the Deathstalkers can masquerade their recruit as the expected envoy to an operative named Andron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the elite stealth and assassination branch of the Forsaken. Headquartered in the Undercity's Rogues' Quarter, they handle espionage, covert executions, and information gathering, reporting directly to Lord Varimathras.",al={"deathstalkers lore","what are deathstalkers","undead rogues"},it="people"},{q="Who is Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad is a Deathstalker handler operating out of the Rogues' Quarter in the Undercity. He oversees early trials and tests recruits hoping to join their covert ranks.",al={"mennet carkad role","who gives quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Mennet need Astor Hadren's letter?",a="Astor Hadren is a courier traveling between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity. Securing his letter of introduction allows the Deathstalkers to substitute their new operative in Hadren's place to deceive an associate named Andron.",al={"astor hadren letter","why intercept messenger","astor letter of introduction"},it="item"},{q="Where does Astor Hadren travel?",a="Astor Hadren journeys along the path connecting the Undercity and Silverpine Forest, carrying correspondence between regions on behalf of his contacts.",al={"astor hadren route","astor hadren location","where is astor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Lord Varimathras?",a="Varimathras is a Nathrezim dreadlord who allied with Queen Sylvanas Windrunner to preserve his own existence. He oversees the Undercity's security, defense, and rogue operations from the Royal Quarter.",al={"varimathras role","dreadlord in undercity"},it="leader"},{q="What happens after this trial?",a="Passing the trial proves an operative's competence, leading into a covert impersonation assignment to deliver Astor's papers and infiltrate Andron's dealings.",al={"what comes next","deathstalkers questline continuation"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want this done?",a="Mennet Carkad is running an infiltration operation that hinges on intercepting communication meant for a contact named Andron. By stealing Astor Hadren's letter, Mennet secures the credentials needed to slip an operative into Andron's confidence unnoticed.",al={"why does mennet need this","mennet carkad motive","why steal the letter"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who is Astor Hadren?",a="Astor Hadren is a courier traveling between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity. He carries an introductory letter intended for a contact named Andron, unaware that the Deathstalkers are targeting his correspondence for their own covert schemes.",al={"who is hadren","astor hadren","target astor hadren"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad send you instead of an established agent?",a="You are seeking to prove yourself worthy of joining the Deathstalkers, the elite rogues serving Lord Varimathras. Mennet deliberately uses aspiring recruits for dangerous, expendable field trials to see if they possess the cunning and lethality needed for the order.",al={"why me deathstalkers","why send me mennet","why not use existing deathstalker"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="For Forsaken rogues, joining the Deathstalkers represents the highest echelon of state service, transitioning streetwise scoundrels into sworn instruments of Varimathras and the Dark Lady.",["race:Undead"]="The Deathstalkers represent the iron grip of internal security in Lordaeron, keeping a watchful, paranoid eye on both external foes and potential traitors within the Forsaken.",["faction:Horde"]="The Deathstalkers operate in deep secrecy, ensuring that the Forsaken maintain vital intelligence networks while keeping the Horde's southern allies largely unaware of their shadier domestic affairs."},kw={"astor hadren","deathstalkers","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","silverpine","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"npc:varimathras","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:1885"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1886,ri={"Astor's Letter of Introduction"}},src={"The Deathstalkers"}}
E["quest:1898"] = {t="quest",n="The Deathstalkers",z="undercity",s="This covert assignment sends an undercover operative into the Undercity's shadowy underbelly to interrogate an unwitting conspirator. Acting under orders handed down from Lord Varimathras, you pose as an expected messenger to uncover treason within the Forsaken's own capital.",h="This covert assignment sends an undercover operative into the Undercity's shadowy underbelly to interrogate...",sec={{t="A Web of Deceit",b="The Deathstalkers do not merely eliminate external threats to the Forsaken; they maintain a ruthless vigil over their own citizens. Acting on suspicions harbored by Lord Varimathras, Deathstalker Mennet Carkad sets an infiltration plan in motion. Armed with a forged or acquired letter of introduction belonging to Astor Hadren, you are tasked with slipping past the suspicions of a local merchant named Andron Gant.",sp=0},{t="The Shop Near the Apothecarium",b="Andron Gant operates out of a shop near the vile fumes and bubbling cauldrons of the Apothecarium. Mennet regards the shopkeeper as foolish and unobservant—lacking the wit to see through an impostor. Presenting the letter establishes your cover as a courier, prompting Gant to eagerly lower his guard and volunteer details about his dealings with an unidentified third party.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Andron Gant?",a="Andron Gant is a shopkeeper in the Undercity situated near the Apothecarium. He has drawn the scrutiny of the Deathstalkers and Lord Varimathras for allegedly funneling intelligence and assistance to an unknown external faction.",al={"andron gant","who is gant","where is andron gant"},it="target"},{q="Why is Lord Varimathras interested in this merchant?",a="Varimathras suspects Gant of collaborating with an organization outside the Forsaken. To safeguard the city and weed out potential subversion, the dreadlord demands concrete proof of Gant's contacts and intentions.",al={"why varimathras cares","varimathras andron gant","why spy on andron"},it="conflict"},{q="How does the player deceive Andron Gant?",a="Mennet Carkad equips you with Astor's Letter of Introduction. Because Gant was expecting a courier and is deemed not particularly sharp by the Deathstalkers, showing him the credentials is all it takes to gain his confidence.",al={"astors letter","how to trick andron gant","messenger disguise"}},{q="What group are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the elite rogue order and secret intelligence agency of the Forsaken. Operating from the shadows under Queen Sylvanas and Lord Varimathras, they root out sedition, sabotage enemies, and eliminate internal threats.",al={"deathstalkers lore","who are deathstalkers","undercity rogues"},it="history"},{q="Where can Andron Gant be found?",a="He resides in his shop close to the entrance of the Apothecarium quarter in the Undercity, conducting business under the watchful eyes of the Royal Apothecary Society and the Deathstalkers.",al={"andron gant location","where is gant shop"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Gant accepts the letter?",a="Gant accepts the letter without suspicion and assumes you are merely an unburdened messenger. He immediately hints at ongoing cooperation with mutual acquaintances, setting the stage for extracting further proof of his betrayal.",al={"what does gant do","gant reaction"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want Andron Gant investigated?",a="Mennet Carkad is acting directly on the orders of Lord Varimathras. The dreadlord suspects that Andron Gant is secretly funneling aid and intelligence to an unknown rival faction from within the Undercity. To protect the Forsaken leadership from internal subversion, Mennet needs definitive proof of Gant's betrayal and the identity of the shadowy organization he serves.",al={"why investigate andron gant","mennet carkad motive","why does mennet send me to gant"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad send you instead of going himself?",a="Mennet Carkad has already met Andron Gant in person, making his own presence an immediate compromise of the mission. Gant would instantly recognize a known Deathstalker operative. Because you possess Astor Hadren's letter of introduction, Gant has no reason to suspect you are anything other than the courier he was scheduled to meet.",al={"why does mennet need me","why cant mennet speak to gant","why use an adventurer"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Infiltrating a spy ring using a dead man's identity to bait a careless conspirator is tradecraft straight from the Deathstalkers' textbook.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, vigilance is survival. Any citizen discovered aiding outside factions risks immediate purging by the dark lady's secret police.",["faction:Horde"]="Beneath the surface of the Undercity lies a nest of political intrigue, proving that even within Horde borders, trust is a rare commodity."},kw={"andron gant","apothecarium","astor hadren","deathstalkers","espionage","forsaken","mennet carkad","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1886","npc:andron-gant","npc:varimathras","quest:1885","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",["end"]="Andron Gant",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1898},src={"The Deathstalkers (2)"}}
E["quest:1899"] = {t="quest",n="The Deathstalkers",z="undercity",s="This errand serves as a vital step in formalizing an arrangement between the informant Andron Gant and the Deathstalkers of the Undercity. After securing his cooperation, an operative delivers Gant's comprehensive ledger directly into the hands of Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter. The exchange marks the transition from simple inquiries to deeper, more covert operations on behalf of the Forsaken state.",h="This errand serves as a vital step in formalizing an arrangement between the informant Andron Gant and the...",sec={{t="A Courier in the Shadows",b="The Deathstalkers do not rely solely on brute force or shadow magic; their operations depend heavily on mundane ledgers, recorded names, and meticulous surveillance. Andron Gant, operating out of the Undercity, agrees to hand over a personal ledger crammed with intelligence that the assassins crave. Rather than dealing directly with the lethal core of the organization, Gant places his faith in an intermediary courier, demonstrating the caution typical of anyone bartering information among the dead.",sp=0},{t="Intelligence in the Rogues' Quarter",b="When delivered to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter, the ledger proves far more revealing than the Deathstalkers anticipated. Instead of cursory notes, Gant's writings yield actionable leads that allow Carkad to widen the scope of their investigations. In an environment as paranoid and fractured as the Forsaken realm, having verified paper trails is essential to ferreting out internal subversion and monitoring external threats before they strike the capital.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is in Andron's Ledger?",a="The ledger contains sensitive information and records gathered by Andron Gant. While the exact contents are not read aloud, Mennet Carkad notes that it contains significantly more detail and valuable intelligence than the Deathstalkers initially expected him to provide.",al={"andron ledger contents","what does the ledger say","deathstalker ledger"},it="item"},{q="Who are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the premier covert organization and assassin guild of the Forsaken. Headquartered in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity, they operate as Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's eyes, ears, and hidden daggers, handling espionage, intelligence, and targeted assassinations across Lordaeron.",al={"deathstalker lore","who are deathstalkers","undercity rogues"},it="people"},{q="Why does Gant want the same courier used in the future?",a="In the murky, distrustful atmosphere of the Undercity, finding an operative who can run sensitive documents without stealing or tampering with them is rare. Gant explicitly requests that future business be handled through the same runner to minimize risks and preserve his established working arrangement.",al={"why does gant like you","andron gant trust","gant courier"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad is a seasoned operative of the Deathstalkers stationed in the Rogues' Quarter. He coordinates local agents, gathers field intelligence from informants like Andron Gant, and directs covert assignments throughout the capital and surrounding territories.",al={"mennet carkad lore","who is carkad"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Rogues' Quarter located?",a="The Rogues' Quarter is the southern district of the Undercity. It serves as the primary base for Forsaken stealth operatives, thieves, and assassins, providing training grounds and dark alcoves far removed from the public plazas of the upper ruins.",al={"rogues quarter location","where is rogues quarter","undercity rogues quarter"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken need an internal intelligence agency?",a="Surrounded on all sides by the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and wary Alliance remnants, the young Forsaken nation faces constant threats of infiltration and rebellion. The Deathstalkers root out subversion within Lordaeron's borders to ensure the fledgling regime survives.",al={"why deathstalkers exist","forsaken spies","undercity intelligence"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Andron Gant want the ledger delivered?",a="Andron Gant operates within the Undercity under the watchful eye of the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken intelligence network. Delivering the requested ledger satisfies their demands and proves his ongoing value to them, keeping their arrangement intact and sparing him unwelcome scrutiny.",al={"why deliver the ledger","andron gant motive","why is andron cooperating"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="For an aspiring rogue in the Undercity, handling sensitive courier runs for Mennet Carkad is a fundamental test of discretion, proving that an operative can manage covert assets without attracting unnecessary attention.",["race:Undead"]="Internal security in the Undercity is absolute survival; assisting the Deathstalkers directly strengthens the Dark Lady's grip over the capital against both living infiltrators and rival undead."},kw={"andron gant","assassins","deathstalkers","espionage","ledger","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","undercity"},rel={"npc:andron-gant","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:undercity"},m={start="Andron Gant",["end"]="Mennet Carkad",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1899,ri={"Andron's Ledger"}},src={"The Deathstalkers (3)"}}
E["quest:1960"] = {t="quest",n="Investigate the Alchemist Shop",z="undercity",s="Investigate the Alchemist Shop is an Undercity quest for Horde mages tasked with resolving an arcane anomaly in the Apothecarium. Guided by Anastasia Hartwell, practitioners track and capture invisible creatures made of pure magical energy running loose inside Algernon's shop.",h="Investigate the Alchemist Shop is an Undercity quest for Horde mages tasked with resolving an arcane anomaly...",sec={{t="A Disturbance in the Apothecarium",b="The Undercity is no stranger to unnatural phenomena, but the Apothecarium recently developed a problem of purely arcane origin. Unseen magical entities were detected wandering Algernon's alchemy shop, passing silently among bubbling cauldrons and toxic reagents. Recognizing an unnatural breach in the flow of magic, the Undercity's mage instructor, Anastasia Hartwell, directs promising arcane initiates to investigate and contain the entities before catastrophic damage occurs.",sp=0},{t="Manifestation and Containment",b="Because the entities are invisible and composed entirely of raw arcane force, ordinary tracking methods are useless. Anastasia equips her students with a specialized Cantation of Manifestation to strip away the entities' invisibility, alongside sturdy containment coffers. Once revealed, the volatile rift spawns must be battered down and sealed safely inside the coffers before they can unravel further or harm the alchemists at work.",sp=0},{t="Accident or Arcane Assault?",b="Upon securing the specimens, Anastasia's concern shifts to their origin. A spontaneous rift in the ambient flow of magic is troubling enough, but an intentional breach would imply an active, coordinated magical assault against the Forsaken capital. The captured creatures are turned over for study to determine whether the Apothecarium merely suffered an arcane accident or sits on the frontline of a targeted threat.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest and where do I find them?",a="The quest is offered by Anastasia Hartwell, the mage trainer stationed in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"quest giver","where to start","anastasia location"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Where is the disturbance located?",a="The disturbance is centered around Algernon's alchemy shop, located down within the Apothecarium district of the Undercity.",al={"where do i go","alchemist shop location","where is algernon"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are the creatures wandering the shop?",a="They are rift spawns, invisible beings made entirely of concentrated magical energy that appeared through an anomaly in the local flow of magic.",al={"what are the monsters","invisible creatures","rift spawns"},it="target"},{q="How do you capture the creatures?",a="You must recite the Cantation of Manifestation in the shop to reveal the rift spawns, weaken them with spells, and then deploy a containment coffer to trap them inside.",al={"how to catch them","using the coffer","how to complete"},gp=true},{q="Why does Anastasia want these creatures captured alive?",a="Anastasia and the Undercity's scholars need live specimens to determine whether the tear in magic was a natural, random rift or an intentional attack against the city by an outside magical force.",al={"why capture them","containment coffers purpose","why study them"},it="motive"},{q="Can classes other than mages do this quest?",a="No, this quest is specifically part of the early training lineage restricted entirely to Horde mages.",al={"mage only","who can take this quest"},gp=true},{q="What is the Cantation of Manifestation for?",a="The Cantation of Manifestation is an incantation inscribed upon a scroll, provided by Anastasia Hartwell to reveal the unseen. The entities haunting Algernon's shop are pure magical energy and naturally invisible to the naked eye. Reading the cantation within the shop tears away their veil of concealment, forcing them into physical manifestation so you can battle and subdue them.",al={"cantation of manifestation purpose","why use cantation of manifestation","what does the cantation do"},it="item",add=true},{q="What is the Chest of Containment Coffers for?",a="The Chest of Containment Coffers holds specially warded vessels crafted to bind raw magical entities. Because the rift spawns in the Apothecarium cannot simply be carried by hand, you must deploy these arcane coffers once the creatures are weakened in combat, securely trapping them inside so they can be transported without dissipating.",al={"chest of containment coffers","what are containment coffers","purpose of containment coffers"},it="item",add=true},{q="What is the Filled Containment Coffer for?",a="Each Filled Containment Coffer holds a living rift spawn captured from Algernon's shop. Anastasia Hartwell requires three of these trapped entities brought back intact so the Undercity's greatest arcane scholars can examine them, unraveling whether their sudden manifestation was an accidental tear in the weave of magic or a deliberate assault.",al={"filled containment coffer use","why bring filled coffers","filled containment coffer purpose"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="This task tests an apprentice's mastery over pure arcane forces, demanding the use of specialized manifestation cantations and containment vessels rather than mere destructive force.",["race:Undead"]="While Forsaken apothecaries focus heavily on alchemy and plaguecraft, this mission highlights the vigilance of the Undercity's arcane scholars in guarding their city from magical infiltration."},kw={"algernon","anastasia hartwell","apothecarium","cantation of manifestation","containment coffer","magic quarter","rift spawn","undercity"},rel={"npc:anastasia-hartwell","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","quest:1959"},m={start="Anastasia Hartwell",["end"]="Anastasia Hartwell",level="16",faction="Horde",id=1960,ri={"Cantation of Manifestation","Chest of Containment Coffers","Filled Containment Coffer"}},src={"Investigate the Alchemist Shop"}}
E["quest:1961"] = {t="quest",n="Gathering Materials",z="undercity",s="Gathering Materials is a rite of passage for aspiring Horde mages training in the Undercity. Assigned by Anastasia Hartwell, the task sends apprentices into Silverpine Forest to claim arcane gems from the wizards of Dalaran, assembling the components needed to weave their first true mage's robes.",h="Gathering Materials is a rite of passage for aspiring Horde mages training in the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Rite of Arcane Standing",b="Within the arcane cloisters of the Magic Quarter, novice mages must prove their mastery over more than just raw incantations. To earn their first true robes—a formal mantle marking their station and personal worth—initiates are directed by Anastasia Hartwell to harvest the raw components required for enchanted weave: a bolt of simple linen and a set of potent Dalaran mana gems.",sp=0},{t="Pragmatism of the Forsaken",b="The mana gems cannot simply be purchased or manifested; they must be torn from Dalaran mages stationed across Silverpine Forest, particularly near Ambermill. Anastasia Hartwell remarks with cold detachment that while Dalaran's arcane philosophies mirror their own, sentimental hesitation has no place in the Undercity. In the eyes of the Forsaken, if those living wizards lack the strength to defend their relics, they forfeit both their treasures and their lives.",sp=0},{t="The Tailor of the Magic Quarter",b="Once gathered, the cloth and gems are delivered to Josef Gregorian, a tailor residing in the Magic Quarter. While Gregorian readily admits he lacks the magical talent to gauge the pristine quality of Dalaran's enchanted stones, he possesses the rare artisan skill needed to weave their raw power directly into the fabric of the robes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Gathering Materials?",a="The quest serves as an initiation for Horde mages. Completing it provides the tailor Josef Gregorian with the necessary components—linen and mana gems—to craft the initiate's first formal enchanted robes.",al={"why do gathering materials","gathering materials quest purpose","mage robe quest undercity"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell send you after Dalaran mages?",a="Dalaran wizards stationed in Silverpine Forest carry refined mana gems capable of channeling strong magical currents. Hartwell views these living mages pragmatically: despite shared intellectual roots, weakness in the field means their lives and resources are forfeit to the Forsaken.",al={"why kill dalaran mages","dalaran mana gems lore","why silverpine mages"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Dalaran wizards located?",a="They can be encountered in Silverpine Forest, occupying outposts and grounds southeast of the Sepulcher, centered around the settlement of Ambermill.",al={"where to find dalaran mana gems","silverpine mages location","ambermill mages"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Josef Gregorian?",a="Josef Gregorian is an Undead tailor working out of the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Though he is an artisan rather than an arcane spellcaster, he specializes in stitching enchanted garments like spellfire robes.",al={"josef gregorian undercity","who is the tailor in magic quarter","gregorian tailor"},it="identity"},{q="What robes are crafted from these materials?",a="Josef Gregorian uses the linen and Dalaran mana gems to stitch Spellfire Robes, a classic garment marking an apprentice's transition into an established mage.",al={"what robe do you get","spellfire robes reward","gathering materials reward robe"},it="item"},{q="Why does Anastasia find killing Dalaran mages somewhat distasteful?",a="Many Forsaken spellcasters, including Hartwell herself, were trained in Dalaran's traditions in life and share similar intellectual and magical philosophies. Despite this kinship, survival and necessity override sentiment.",al={"hartwell dalaran feelings","forsaken mages vs dalaran","anastasia hartwell lore"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Linen Cloth for?",a="The linen cloth serves as the mundane foundation for your Spellfire Robes. Josef Gregorian, the tailor in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, weaves the fabric into fine garments before weaving magical reagents into the threads to empower them.",al={"linen cloth use","why linen cloth","what is linen for"},it="item",add=true},{q="What is the Dalaran Mana Gem for?",a="Dalaran mana gems hold raw arcane energy channeled by the Kirin Tor mages. Josef Gregorian stitches them directly into your robes to infuse the fabric with the magical power required to forge true spellfire garments.",al={"dalaran mana gem use","why dalaran mana gems","what are the mana gems for"},it="item",add=true},{q="Who are the Dalaran mages in Silverpine Forest?",a="They are human sorcerers loyal to Dalaran, stationed around Ambermill in eastern Silverpine Forest. Though their arcane discipline mirrors that of the Forsaken mages, their presence directly threatens Undercity's dominion over the region, making them prime targets for ambitious apprentices.",al={"dalaran wizards silverpine","who are the dalaran mages","dalaran humans silverpine"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Anastasia Hartwell send an apprentice instead of handling it herself?",a="Earning your first mage's robes is a rite of passage. Anastasia Hartwell expects you to prove your worth and arcane station by taking reagents from rival spellcasters through force of will and personal power.",al={"why me gathering materials","why send apprentice","why doesn't anastasia get the gems"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="This quest represents a pivotal milestone for Horde mages, marking their graduation from simple apprentice attire into tailored robes woven with captured arcane power.",["race:Undead"]="The mission illustrates the Forsaken's ruthless worldview: former kinship with Dalaran's sorcerers yields no mercy if those living wizards prove too weak to hold Silverpine.",["profession:Tailoring"]="The process highlights how mundane linen cloth can be bound with potent mana gems to create enduring enchanted garments."},kw={"ambermill","anastasia hartwell","dalaran mana gem","gathering materials","josef gregorian","linen cloth","magic quarter","spellfire robes","undercity"},rel={"quest:1962","npc:anastasia-hartwell","npc:josef-gregorian","subzone:magic-quarter","subzone:ambermill","subzone:dalaran","subzone:sepulcher","quest:1960"},m={start="Anastasia Hartwell",["end"]="Josef Gregorian",level="15",faction="Horde",id=1961,ri={"Dalaran Mana Gem","Linen Cloth"}},src={"Gathering Materials (Horde)"}}
E["quest:1962"] = {t="quest",n="Spellfire Robes",z="undercity",s="Spellfire Robes is the culminating rite in the training of young Horde mages in the Undercity, completed by the tailor Josef Gregorian. After gathering rare components from across the realm, the apprentice is rewarded with custom enchanted vestments that signify their growing mastery over the arcane.",h="Spellfire Robes is the culminating rite in the training of young Horde mages in the Undercity, completed by...",sec={{t="A Mage's Vestment",b="For apprentices mastering the arcane arts in Lordaeron, standard cloaks and common garments do little to channel or insulate against raw eldritch forces. Josef Gregorian, a tailor working in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, weaves genuine magical garb from the specialized materials promising Horde spellcasters gather. The final stitching of the Spellfire Robes represents an apprentice's transition beyond basic incantations into an established practitioner of arcane and fire arts.",sp=0},{t="Woven Power",b="Crafting garments capable of safely focusing high-intensity magic is an exacting task. Rather than mere tailoring, the creation of robes such as these requires specific alchemical and arcane components secured through dangerous trials. Once these supplies are gathered and presented in Gregorian's sanctum, the tailor weaves them together on the spot, bestowing a tangible mark of status and protection upon the aspiring mage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Spellfire Robes quest?",a="It serves as the final step in an early class rite for Horde mages, rewarding them with specially enchanted robes after they have gathered tailoring components for the tailor Josef Gregorian.",al={"spellfire robes purpose","what do spellfire robes do","why do this quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Josef Gregorian?",a="Josef Gregorian is a Forsaken tailor working in the Magic Quarter's tailor shop in the Undercity. He stitches the first proper class garments for newly minted mages sent to him by Anastasia Hartwell.",al={"who is josef","who makes the robe","josef gregorian undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The entire interaction takes place within the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, directly at Josef Gregorian's tailor shop.",al={"spellfire robes location","where to turn in spellfire robes"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why don't you have to leave to do another task for this quest?",a="All the labor was completed in the preceding assignment, Gathering Materials. Once you hand those reagents to Josef, he simply takes a moment to weave the garment and immediately hands over the finished robes.",al={"why is it instant","how to complete spellfire robes","auto complete robe"},gp=true},{q="Can classes other than Mages obtain these robes?",a="No. The entire quest chain and the resulting enchanted vestments are exclusive to mages allied with the Horde.",al={"is this mage only","can warlock get this","who can do spellfire robes"},gp=true},{q="What materials were required to make these robes?",a="The robe is constructed from the rare supplies collected during the previous task, which include linen cloth and Dalaran mana gems taken from the Kirin Tor mages of Silverpine Forest.",al={"what goes into the robe","robe ingredients","gathering materials turn in"},it="item"},{q="Why does Josef Gregorian tailor the Spellfire Robes for you?",a="Josef Gregorian serves as a mentor to rising Forsaken and Horde mages within the Magic Quarter. By weaving the gathered reagents into suitable enchanted vestments, he ensures you are properly outfitted to channel and endure the arcane forces demanded of your growing craft.",al={"why does josef make the robes","josef gregorian motive","why does josef help you"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Obtaining these robes is an early rite of passage for Horde practitioners, providing tailored attire capable of handling volatile fire and arcane energies.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken spellcasters in the Undercity preserve Dalaran-style arcane discipline, combining old magical traditions with their new existence in Lordaeron's ruins.",["profession:Tailoring"]="The quest demonstrates how mundane cloth is augmented with exotic reagents to withstand and enhance powerful magical currents."},kw={"arcane robes","gathering materials","josef gregorian","mage quest","magic quarter","spellfire robes","undercity"},rel={"quest:1961","npc:josef-gregorian"},m={start="Josef Gregorian",level="15",faction="Horde",id=1962},src={"Spellfire Robes"}}
E["quest:1978"] = {t="quest",n="The Deathstalkers",z="undercity",s="This errand marks the formal induction of a capable operative into the ranks of the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken order of assassins and spies. Tasked with delivering Andron's Ledger directly to the dreadlord Varimathras, the courier brings proof of the Syndicate's covert activities to the highest tier of Undercity leadership.",h="This errand marks the formal induction of a capable operative into the ranks of the Deathstalkers, the...",sec={{t="Induction into the Shadows",b="After unearthing incriminating records from Andron Gant, Mennet Carkad officially welcomes the operative into the Deathstalkers. The organization serves as Lady Sylvanas's eyes, ears, and daggers throughout Lordaeron, relying on intelligence networks, ruthless efficiency, and stealth to eliminate threats before they surface. Gaining formal recognition within the order is a major milestone for any aspiring rogue or scout in the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="The Syndicate Connection",b="The prize of this covert investigation is Andron's Ledger, which exposes illicit ties between local agents and the Syndicate. Once the noble aristocracy of the fallen human kingdom of Alterac, the Syndicate turned to banditry and subversion after their realm collapsed in the Second War. Carkad expresses surprise and disdain at how far the fallen lords of Alterac have descended, stooping to petty conspiracies to claw back power.",sp=1},{t="Audience with the Dreadlord",b="Because of the sensitive nature of the intelligence, the ledger is delivered directly to Varimathras in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity. The nathrezim commander oversees Forsaken tactical intelligence under Sylvanas Windrunner. Pleased with the Deathstalkers' initiative, Varimathras welcomes the operative's demonstrated capability, noting that his intelligence division can always make use of someone who delivers results.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the premier espionage, scouting, and assassination order of the Forsaken. Headquartered in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity, they operate across Lordaeron to neutralize political rivals, infiltrate hostile factions, and protect the Forsaken realm from external and internal subversion.",al={"who are the deathstalkers","deathstalker lore","forsaken assassins"},it="people"},{q="Why is the Syndicate involved?",a="The captured ledger reveals secret connections to the Syndicate, the displaced aristocracy of Alterac who turned to organized banditry. The Forsaken keep careful watch over Alterac remnants operating in their territory, as Syndicate agents continuously seek opportunities to reclaim lost land and plunder resources across northern Lordaeron.",al={"why syndicate","alterac connection","syndicate ledger"},it="conflict"},{q="Why report directly to Varimathras?",a="Varimathras serves as Queen Sylvanas's tactical advisor and oversees Undercity security and intelligence operations. Significant discoveries concerning foreign conspiracies—such as the Syndicate's covert operations—require review at the highest executive level to coordinate broader military and diplomatic countermeasures.",al={"why varimathras","who is varimathras","dreadlord role"},it="purpose"},{q="Who was Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad is a senior handler and contact for the Deathstalkers operating in the Undercity. He oversees field agents, evaluates new recruits, and sifts through gathered intelligence before routing critical findings up the chain of command.",al={"mennet carkad role","quest giver carkad"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this audience take place?",a="The audience takes place in the Hall of the Dark Lady, located in the Royal Quarter deep within the Undercity. Varimathras stands beside Queen Sylvanas Windrunner at the heart of the Forsaken seat of power.",al={"where is varimathras","hall of the dark lady location"},it="place"},{q="What happens after joining the Deathstalkers?",a="With your credentials established and your reliability proven to both Mennet Carkad and Varimathras, you are recognized as a trusted field operative for the Forsaken, setting the stage for future reconnaissance and elimination contracts across the contested lands of Lordaeron.",al={"deathstalker questline continuation","what next"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want Andron's Ledger delivered to Varimathras?",a="The ledger exposes that the Syndicate—the fallen nobles of Alterac—is conspiring against the Forsaken. Uncovering their treachery is a vital intelligence victory for the Deathstalkers, and Mennet knows such urgent news concerning Lordaeron's security must be placed directly into the hands of Lord Varimathras, who oversees the order's operations.",al={"why deliver the ledger","mennet carkad motive","why report the syndicate to varimathras"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Mennet send you instead of reporting to Varimathras himself?",a="You were the one who tracked down the conspirators and secured Andron's ledger in the field. Mennet believes it is only fitting that you present the intelligence yourself, allowing you to claim credit before Lord Varimathras and mark your formal induction into the ranks of the Deathstalkers.",al={"why me deathstalkers","why does mennet send me","why deliver ledger yourself"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, induction into the Deathstalkers is a direct pledge to safeguard the fragile sovereignty of Lordaeron from human survivors and lurking traitors.",["class:Rogue"]="This induction represents official entry into the Forsaken's dedicated rogue cadre, elevating simple cutpurses into state-sponsored intelligence operatives.",["faction:Horde"]="While internal to Forsaken security, monitoring the human remnants of Alterac protects the northern Horde territories from subversive sabotage."},kw={"alterac","andron's ledger","deathstalkers","hall of the dark lady","mennet carkad","syndicate","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1886","quest:1885","npc:varimathras","zone:undercity","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",["end"]="Varimathras",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1978},src={"The Deathstalkers (4)"}}
E["quest:1998"] = {t="quest",n="Fenwick Thatros",z="undercity",s="Mennet Carkad assigns promising rogues in the Undercity to hunt down Fenwick Thatros on orders directly from Lord Varimathras. Thatros is suspected of organizing independent undead forces along the shores of Silverpine Forest. Eliminating him proves an operative's mettle to the Deathstalkers, opening the way for more sophisticated trade training.",h="Mennet Carkad assigns promising rogues in the Undercity to hunt down Fenwick Thatros on orders directly from...",sec={{t="A Command from the Dreadlord",b="Within the dark corridors of the Rogues' Quarter, Mennet Carkad handles internal contracts and training for the Deathstalkers—the Forsaken's secretive intelligence wing. When Lord Varimathras sends down a priority target, it is not an assignment handed to novice recruits lightly. Fenwick Thatros has drawn the dreadlord's attention by establishing a foothold among the rogue undead in Silverpine Forest. Left unchecked, independent undead leadership could jeopardize Forsaken consolidation across Lordaeron's old holdings.",sp=0},{t="The Decrepit Dock on Lordamere",b="According to Deathstalker reconnaissance, Thatros does not hide in deep fortresses or crypts. Instead, scouts placed him near a decrepit dock along the waters of Lake Lordamere in Silverpine Forest. Striking him down there requires traversing contested wilderness dominated by feral beasts, the Rot Hide gnolls, and remnants of the Scourge. Bringing back his severed head provides the tangible proof Varimathras demands before inducting an operative into deeper covert operations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fenwick Thatros?",a="Fenwick Thatros is an undead leader operating along the edges of Lake Lordamere in Silverpine Forest. Unlike the Forsaken who serve Lady Sylvanas, Thatros commands pockets of undead that remain unaligned or hostile to the Undercity, leading Lord Varimathras to single him out for execution.",al={"fenwick lore","who is thatros","fenwick thatros background"},it="target"},{q="Why does Varimathras want Fenwick Thatros dead?",a="Varimathras views Thatros as a rising threat who could rally stray undead in Silverpine against the Forsaken. To secure the borders around the Undercity, any rival leaders who threaten Sylvanas's absolute control over the region must be swiftly eliminated.",al={"varimathras thatros","why kill fenwick"},it="motive"},{q="Who are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the premier espionage, assassination, and reconnaissance agency of the Forsaken. Based out of the Rogues' Quarter in the Undercity, they operate across Lordaeron to eliminate internal threats, spy on rival factions, and secure territories for the Dark Lady.",al={"deathstalkers lore","what are deathstalkers","undead rogues faction"},it="people"},{q="Where is Fenwick Thatros located?",a="Deathstalker reports place Thatros near a ruined, decrepit dock on the shore of Lake Lordamere in northeastern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is fenwick","fenwick dock location","thatros lake lordamere"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does completing this mission earn with the Deathstalkers?",a="Executing Thatros proves an operative's capability and loyalty to Mennet Carkad and the Deathstalkers. With your reliability demonstrated, Carkad offers to advance your training in the shadow arts through specialized trade instructions.",al={"fenwick reward lore","what comes after fenwick"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Mennet Carkad?",a="Mennet Carkad is a rogue trainer and Deathstalker handler situated in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity. He oversees field agents and assigns missions directly tied to the security of the Forsaken realm.",al={"mennet carkad","who gives fenwick quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad need Fenwick's Head?",a="Fenwick Thatros represents an organized threat lurking right along the borders of Silverpine Forest. Mennet Carkad demands his severed head as undeniable proof that the rogue undead commander has been eliminated. In the clandestine operations of the Deathstalkers and Lord Varimathras, an assassin's word is never enough without physical trophy to confirm the kill.",al={"what is fenwick's head for","why take fenwick's head","fenwicks head purpose"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad choose you for this mission?",a="Mennet Carkad operates as a handler and trainer for Deathstalkers in the Rogues' Quarter. When Lord Varimathras orders a surgical assassination, ordinary city guards are ill-suited for stealthy outdoor reconnaissance. Mennet specifically selects you because you have shown promise in the shadow arts, using this critical contract to evaluate whether you are ready for advanced training among the Forsaken's elite operatives.",al={"why send me","why does mennet pick me","why not send deathstalker guards"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="This contract serves as a proving ground for Forsaken rogues, confirming their stealth and lethality before they are trusted with the deeper tools of the Deathstalker trade.",["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken cannot tolerate rival undead factions claiming sovereignty so close to the Capital City, making Thatros's head a political necessity."},kw={"deathstalkers","fenwick thatros","lake lordamere","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","silverpine forest","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1999","npc:varimathras","quest:1886","quest:1885","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:undercity","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",level="16",faction="Horde",id=1998,ri={"Fenwick's Head"}},src={"Fenwick Thatros (quest)"}}
E["quest:1999"] = {t="quest",n="Tools of the Trade",z="undercity",s="Tools of the Trade is an initiation mission for Horde rogues given by Mennet Carkad in the Undercity. Ordered by Lord Varimathras, agents must obtain lockpicking gear and infiltrate Ambermill to recover sensitive Kirin Tor reports detailing Dalaran's current state.",h="Tools of the Trade is an initiation mission for Horde rogues given by Mennet Carkad in the Undercity.",sec={{t="Eyes on Ambermill",b="Following the interrogation of a Kirin Tor captive, the Deathstalkers learned that vital intelligence concerning the ruins of Dalaran lies hidden in Ambermill. Silverpine Forest remains a precarious front line, and the human mages guarding the village guard their communications fiercely. Under the orders of Lord Varimathras, Deathstalker handler Mennet Carkad directs promising operatives to bypass Kirin Tor sentries and secure the Dalaran Status Report.",sp=0},{t="The Art of the Breach",b="Unlike straightforward assassinations, this mission serves as a practical proving ground in infiltration and lockpicking. Operatives are outfitted with specialized thieves' tools from Estelle Gendry before marching into hostile Kirin Tor territory. Cracking the secured chest in Ambermill demonstrates that an operative has progressed beyond raw street brutality into an indispensable espionage asset for the Forsaken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders this mission?",a="Mennet Carkad, a master rogue of the Deathstalkers stationed in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity, assigns the task. The overarching mandate comes directly from Lord Varimathras, who oversees intelligence gathering for the Forsaken.",al={"who gives tools of the trade","quest giver","mennet carkad quest"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Dalaran Status Report?",a="It is a sealed Kirin Tor dispatch detailing conditions within Dalaran. Deathstalker interrogators extracted its location from an imprisoned human mage, alerting the Undercity that crucial information about their southern neighbors was vulnerable.",al={"what are the documents","kirin tor papers","status report"},it="item"},{q="Where is the report kept?",a="The report is secured inside a locked chest within the Kirin Tor outpost of Ambermill, located in southern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where do i find the documents","ambermill chest location","where is the status report"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who provides the lockpicking tools?",a="Estelle Gendry, an outfitter in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity, provides the necessary thieves' tools to open the Kirin Tor's locked chest.",al={"where do i get tools","estelle gendry role","outfitter tools"},gp=true},{q="Why is Dalaran important to the Forsaken right now?",a="Dalaran's surviving wizards maintain a fortified pocket behind an arcane dome right on the southern border of Silverpine Forest. The Forsaken keep careful tabs on their movements, strength, and defensive readiness to protect their own holdings in Lordaeron.",al={"why care about dalaran","forsaken vs dalaran","kirin tor threat"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before taking this mission?",a="Operatives must first complete the assassination contract Fenwick Thatros, hunting down a target in Silverpine Forest before Mennet Carkad trusts them with delicate infiltration work.",al={"prereq","what quest comes before","fenwick thatros quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad want this done?",a="Lord Varimathras tasked the Deathstalkers with retrieving the report after extracting its whereabouts from a prisoner. As an operative within the Rogues' Quarter, Mennet Carkad carries out the dreadlord's directives while simultaneously testing your burgeoning skills in infiltration and espionage.",al={"why does mennet carkad want this","mennet carkad motive","why recover dalaran status report"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you sent against at Ambermill?",a="Your target is the Kirin Tor stationed at Ambermill in Silverpine Forest. These human wizards maintain an enclave near Dalaran's magical dome, guarding confidential intelligence about the broken city's current condition from the Forsaken.",al={"who holds the report","tools of the trade target","who are you targeting"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Mennet Carkad need you for this mission?",a="The mission serves as a rite of passage. After demonstrating basic aptitude by eliminating Fenwick Thatros, Mennet selected you to prove you can handle the Deathstalkers' more delicate tradecraft—relying on stealth, lockpicking, and infiltration rather than brute force.",al={"why send me","why me mennet carkad","why cant deathstalkers get the report"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="This mission marks a rite of passage for Horde rogues, requiring you to procure formal lockpicking tools and apply stealth and finesse rather than brute force.",["race:Undead"]="Infiltrating Ambermill allows the Forsaken to outwit the very Kirin Tor mages who seek to reclaim Lordaeron from the grave.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing human intelligence in Silverpine solidifies the Horde's foothold across northern Lordaeron against remnants of the Alliance."},kw={"ambermill","dalaran","deathstalkers","estelle gendry","kirin tor","lockpicking","mennet carkad","rogues' quarter","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"quest:1998","quest:1886","subzone:rogues-quarter","zone:undercity","subzone:ambermill","npc:varimathras","subzone:dalaran"},m={start="Mennet Carkad",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1999,ri={"Dalaran Status Report"}},src={"Tools of the Trade (Classic)"}}
E["quest:357"] = {t="quest",n="The Lich's Identity",z="undercity",s="The Lich's Identity is an Undercity quest given by Bethor Iceshard in the Magic Quarter. Seeking to uncover the identity of a reclusive lich living on Brightwater Lake, Bethor sends an emissary to steal the figure's spellbook to gauge his power and allegiance.",h="The Lich's Identity is an Undercity quest given by Bethor Iceshard in the Magic Quarter.",sec={{t="A Recluse on the Lake",b="North of the Undercity, in the misty waters of Brightwater Lake, a lone lich dwells in self-imposed exile on a small island. Unlike the mindless pawns of the Lich King, this necromancer possesses his own free will, yet he lives in deep paranoia. Convinced that any undead who approach him are Scourge thralls sent to drag him back into servitude, he unleashes his summoned minions on anyone setting foot on his shores.",sp=0},{t="A Valuable Asset",b="Word of the rogue lich eventually reached Bethor Iceshard, the archmage overseeing the mages in the Undercity. Bethor recognized the strategic importance of such an entity: Lady Sylvanas Windrunner seeks every scrap of magical mastery and every capable will to bolster the Forsaken against their many foes. To assess whether the hermit could be recruited, Bethor requires proof of his identity and necromantic expertise.",sp=0},{t="An Old Friend Found",b="After the stolen spellbook is delivered to the Magic Quarter, Bethor examines its arcane script and discovers the lich's true identity: Gunther Arcanus. In life, Gunther had been a talented necromancer and a close comrade of Bethor before the plague ravaged Lordaeron. The realization confirms that Gunther is not only an independent soul, but an old ally whose expanded necromantic powers could greatly benefit the Dark Lady's realm.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this mission?",a="Bethor Iceshard, a prominent undead mage trainer stationed in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, assigns the task.",al={"quest giver","bethor iceshard location","who gives the lichs identity"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the lich attack anyone who approaches him?",a="The lich broke free of the Lich King's control by his own will, but he mistakenly believes that all other undead in Lordaeron remain mind-controlled Scourge thralls. As a result, he orders his minions to attack any who approach his island to defend his freedom.",al={"why is gunther hostile","why does the lich attack","brightwater lich hostile"},it="hostile"},{q="Where is the lich's camp located?",a="He lives on an island in the middle of Brightwater Lake, located in Tirisfal Glades directly north of the Ruins of Lordaeron and Undercity.",al={"where is the lich","brightwater lake island","gunther arcanus location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Lady Sylvanas want him brought into the Forsaken?",a="Independent undead of high magical talent are exceptionally rare. A free-willed necromancer capable of wielding potent death magic would provide the Forsaken with crucial power against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"why recruit the lich","forsaken interest in gunther","sylvanas lich"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who does the lich turn out to be?",a="Bethor reveals the lich to be Gunther Arcanus, a former Dalaran mage and skilled necromancer who was a close comrade-in-arms of Bethor before the Third War.",al={"lich identity","who is the lich","identity of the lich"},sp=1,it="origin"},{q="What happens after you deliver the spellbook?",a="Once Bethor confirms Gunther's identity, he sends you back to Brightwater Lake with the spellbook to convince Gunther that the Forsaken are truly free and wish to welcome him.",al={"what next","return the book quest","after the lichs identity"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want the lich's spellbook?",a="Bethor Iceshard seeks to bring the reclusive undead mage into the Forsaken fold on behalf of the Dark Lady. Because the lich violently drives off anyone who approaches, Bethor cannot simply talk to him. He needs to inspect the spellbook to uncover the caster's true identity, gauge the extent of his necromantic power, and determine whether his talents can truly serve the Forsaken cause.",al={"bethor motive","why does bethor want the book","why steal the lich spellbook"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Lich's Spellbook for?",a="The spellbook belongs to the reclusive lich living on Brightwater Lake. It contains his necromantic arcana and personal magical signatures. Bethor Iceshard uses it to identify the hermit and assess his necromantic prowess without needing to engage him in direct conversation.",al={"lich's spellbook","lich spellbook purpose","what is the spellbook for"},it="item",add=true},{q="Who is the lich on Brightwater Lake?",a="The target is a powerful, free-willed undead mage dwelling on an island in Brightwater Lake to the north. Mistrustful of everyone, he believes all other undead are still mindless slaves of the Scourge. Consequently, he has surrounded himself with summoned minions and violently repels any who draw near.",al={"who is the lich","brightwater lake lich","who do i steal the book from"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming independent undead proves that breaking free from the Lich King was not an isolated miracle, while securing vital necromantic power for Sylvanas's court.",["class:Mage"]="Mages visiting Bethor Iceshard in the Magic Quarter see the surviving remnants of Lordaeron's and Dalaran's magical traditions transformed into instruments of Forsaken survival.",["faction:Horde"]="Recruiting powerful necromancers strengthens the northern frontier of the Horde against relentless attacks by the Scarlet Crusade and Scourge."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brightwater lake","forsaken","magic quarter","necromancer","sylvanas","the lich's spellbook","undercity"},rel={"npc:bethor-iceshard","npc:gunther-arcanus","quest:405","quest:366","subzone:brightwater-lake","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},m={start="Bethor Iceshard",level="8",faction="Horde",id=357,ri={"The Lich's Spellbook"}},src={"The Lich's Identity"}}
E["quest:405"] = {t="quest",n="The Prodigal Lich",z="undercity",s="Following your service in Brill against Scourge remnants and rot hide gnolls, Magistrate Sevren directs you south to the Undercity. Bethor Iceshard, a prominent archmage in the Magic Quarter, requires a capable operative for a sensitive mission regarding a wayward lich.",h="Following your service in Brill against Scourge remnants and rot hide gnolls, Magistrate Sevren directs you...",sec={{t="Summons to the Capital",b="Having proven your capability in the ruined town of Brill, Magistrate Sevren deems you worthy of higher-level Forsaken endeavors. Bethor Iceshard, a formidable mage dwelling in the Undercity's Magic Quarter, has demanded an agent tested in combat against the Scourge. Sevren hands over official orders, dispatching you beneath the ruins of Lordaeron into the subterranean corridors of the Forsaken capital.",sp=0},{t="A Wayward Lich",b="While Sevren admits ignorance of the exact specifics, he reveals that the task revolves around finding and recruiting a rogue lich. Liches are among the most lethal spellcasters raised by the Scourge, making any interaction fraught with peril. When you deliver the orders to Bethor atop his arcane sanctum, the icy mage cuts straight to business, eager to assess whether Brill's magistrate has sent someone strong enough to handle such dangerous quarry.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this task?",a="Magistrate Sevren, the Forsaken official administering the town of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, sends you with written orders directly to Bethor Iceshard.",al={"who gives the prodigal lich","quest giver prodigal lich","sevren orders"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Bethor Iceshard?",a="Bethor Iceshard resides in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, typically found atop the central elevated structure surrounded by arcane energies.",al={"where is bethor","bethor iceshard location","how to find bethor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the mission mentioned in the orders?",a="Bethor intends to enlist a wandering, rogue lich into service, but he first needs an agent capable of tracking down clues to the lich's identity and whereabouts.",al={"what is the lich mission","who is the wayward lich","prodigal lich purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Bethor require an agent tested against the Scourge?",a="Liches are masters of necromantic frost and death magic bound originally to the Lich King. Handling a free-willed or isolated lich requires someone who has already proven capable of surviving against undead Scourge threats.",al={"why scourge testing","why does bethor need me"},it="motive"},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before receiving this quest?",a="You must complete Magistrate Sevren's previous assignment, 'Graverobbers', clearing out the Rot Hide gnolls and grave thieves in Garren's Haunt.",al={"prodigal lich prequest","how to unlock prodigal lich"},gp=true},{q="What comes after reporting to Bethor?",a="Upon turning in Sevren's orders, Bethor offers the quest 'The Lich's Identity', directing you to investigate artifacts and clues to uncover who this mysterious entity was in life.",al={"what is next after prodigal lich","prodigal lich follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Magistrate Sevren want this done?",a="Magistrate Sevren is acting on direct orders from Bethor Iceshard, a formidable mage dwelling in the Undercity. Bethor specifically requested a capable operative with proven experience fighting the Scourge to handle a delicate and perilous matter regarding a wayward lich. As the civic authority in Brill, Sevren ensures Undercity's commands are fulfilled promptly by sending his most capable champion.",al={"why sevren orders","sevren motive","why send me to bethor"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Magistrate Sevren choose you for this mission?",a="Bethor Iceshard explicitly demanded an agent who has already proven their worth and mettle against the Scourge. Rather than dispatching standard town guards or untested recruits, Sevren selected you because your recent actions around Brill demonstrated that you have both the resilience and the capability to survive whatever dangerous assignment Bethor has planned.",al={"why me prodigal lich","why sevren picks me","why not royal guard"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Taking your first direct orders from the capital marks your transition from local militia work in Brill to executing the greater geopolitical will of the Undercity.",["class:Mage"]="Reporting to Bethor Iceshard offers an audience with one of the most powerful arcane and frost masters among the Forsaken.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing unaligned or powerful necromantic assets strengthens the Forsaken's precarious hold on the ruins of Lordaeron against common enemies."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brill","magic quarter","magistrate sevren","prodigal lich","sevren's orders","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"npc:bethor-iceshard","npc:magistrate-sevren","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:357","quest:358","topic:scourge"},m={start="Magistrate Sevren",["end"]="Bethor Iceshard",level="8",faction="Horde",id=405},src={"The Prodigal Lich"}}
E["quest:411"] = {t="quest",n="The Prodigal Lich Returns",z="undercity",s="The Prodigal Lich Returns marks the conclusion of the effort to recruit Gunther Arcanus into the Forsaken. Having proven your intentions and restored his grimoire, you carry an arcane communion gem back to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.",h="The Prodigal Lich Returns marks the conclusion of the effort to recruit Gunther Arcanus into the Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Rare Reconciliation",b="Gunther Arcanus spent years isolated on an island in Brightwater Lake, having broken free from the Lich King's grip through sheer force of will, completely unaware that Sylvanas Windrunner had liberated Lordaeron. Bitter and suspicious of outsiders, Gunther distrusted the emissaries of the Undercity until an adventurer returned his spellbook and proved their hostility toward the Scourge. Satisfied that his visitor was not an enemy, Gunther entrusted them with a Nether Gem to establish contact with his former colleague.",sp=0},{t="Communion in the Magic Quarter",b="Returning to the Mage Quarter of the Undercity, the bearer delivers the Nether Gem to Bethor Iceshard. Bethor channels the gem's power to conjure Gunther's ethereal visage right within the sanctuary. Through this magical communion, the self-made lich formally agrees to ally with the Forsaken cause. Securing a necromancer of Gunther's independent mastery is a tremendous coup for the Dark Lady's nascent kingdom, bolstering their magical defenses against both the Scourge and the living.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gunther Arcanus?",a="Gunther Arcanus is an exceptionally powerful necromancer who broke free from the Lich King's mental domination on his own. He lived in reclusive exile on an island in Brightwater Lake, assuming all other undead were mindless thralls until adventurers proved otherwise.",al={"gunther arcanus lore","who is the prodigal lich","gunther undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Bethor Iceshard?",a="Bethor Iceshard is a senior mage and scholar residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. He is an old colleague of Gunther Arcanus and coordinated the efforts to find and recruit him into the Forsaken.",al={"bethor lore","who is bethor","iceshard undercity"},it="identity"},{q="What does the Nether Gem do?",a="The Nether Gem is an enchanted artifact provided by Gunther Arcanus. When Bethor Iceshard channels arcane power into it, it manifests a spectral projection of Gunther, allowing the two spellcasters to converse across great distances.",al={"what is the nether gem","gunther gem"},it="item"},{q="Why does Gunther agree to join the Forsaken?",a="Gunther spent years fearing he was the only free-willed undead in Lordaeron. Once convinced that Sylvanas's Forsaken are genuinely free of the Scourge and actively fighting the Lich King, he willingly pledges his allegiance and re-establishes ties with his former peers.",al={"why join forsaken","gunther allegiance"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Why does the quest call Gunther a 'Lich'?",a="While Gunther uses the standard skeletal and decayed form of a Forsaken rather than the floating, frost-wreathed silhouette of a Scourge lich, he attained lichdom independently through his advanced mastery of necromancy and sustained will.",al={"is gunther a real lich","gunther lich form"},it="name"},{q="What happens when you turn in the Nether Gem?",a="Upon completing the delivery, Bethor activates the gem, conjuring Gunther's Visage in the Magic Quarter. The projection moves toward Bethor to initiate their long-overdue reunion before fading.",al={"nether gem turn in event","what happens at bethor"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gunther Arcanus need you to deliver the Nether Gem?",a="Gunther Arcanus remains isolated on his island in Brightwater Lake, maintaining his cautious seclusion while he re-establishes contact with the world beyond. As an emissary who proved your loyalty by recovering his spellbook and destroying his necromantic enemies, you have earned his trust. Handing you the Nether Gem allows him to reach out to his old comrade Bethor Iceshard and negotiate his allegiance without having to abandon his sanctuary or march straight into the Undercity.",al={"why send player nether gem","why does gunther need me","why deliver the gem"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Gunther's liberation without the Banshee Queen's intervention serves as living proof of the sheer willpower Lordaeron's fallen can muster.",["class:Mage"]="Watching Bethor commune with Gunther demonstrates the seamless fusion of traditional Dalaran spellcraft and dark necromancy practiced in the Undercity's Magic Quarter.",["faction:Horde"]="Recruiting an independent, master-level necromancer like Gunther significantly fortifies the Horde's magical standing in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"arcanus","bethor","brightwater lake","gunther","iceshard","lich","nether gem","prodigal","undercity"},rel={"npc:gunther-arcanus","npc:bethor-iceshard","quest:409","zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Gunther Arcanus",["end"]="Bethor Iceshard",level="12",faction="Horde",id=411},src={"The Prodigal Lich Returns"}}
E["quest:441"] = {t="quest",n="Raleigh and the Undercity",z="undercity",s="This quest bridges an investigation from Brill to the Undercity, tasking an adventurer with delivering a recovered heirloom ring to a widower named Raleigh. Found on a woman's stolen corpse bound for Fenris Isle, the jewelry points to a tragedy among Lordaeron's former inhabitants. Delivering it sets into motion a dark pursuit of vengeance.",h="This quest bridges an investigation from Brill to the Undercity, tasking an adventurer with delivering a...",sec={{t="A Tragic Heirloom",b="In Brill, Magistrate Sevren pieced together clues surrounding a stolen corpse and an engraved ring that once belonged to a woman named Deliah. Hoping to confirm its origin and see it returned to her family, Sevren directed the finder deep into the subterranean halls of the Undercity to seek Deliah's surviving husband, Raleigh.",sp=0},{t="Cold Hearts, Bitter Vengeance",b="Located in the bustling Trade Quarter of the Undercity, Raleigh Andrean recognizes his former wife's ring without hesitation. Like many of the Forsaken, undeath has withered his capacity for sorrow, grief, or remorse over Deliah's passing and desecration. However, where tender emotions have died away, an unyielding thirst for retribution remains, prompting Raleigh to plot revenge against those who violated her final rest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Magistrate Sevren starts this quest in the town of Brill within Tirisfal Glades, immediately after you return Deliah's Ring to him.",al={"where do i get raleigh and the undercity","quest giver","magistrate sevren quest"},gp=true},{q="Where is Raleigh Andrean located?",a="Raleigh Andrean is located in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity, standing among the subterranean city's merchants and craftsmen.",al={"raleigh location","where is raleigh","trade quarter raleigh"},gp=true},{q="Whose ring is being delivered?",a="The ring belonged to Deliah, a woman from Brill who was Raleigh Andrean's wife prior to the fall of Lordaeron.",al={"deliah ring","who was deliah","whose ring is this"},it="item"},{q="Why doesn't Raleigh mourn his dead wife?",a="As one of the Forsaken, Raleigh admits that tender emotions like grief and love have grown cold within his undead heart. Instead, his lingering passions have curdled into a cold desire for vengeance.",al={"raleigh reaction","does raleigh care","why is raleigh cold"}},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="Handing in the ring leads directly into the quest 'A Husband's Revenge', where Raleigh sends you to avenge his wife's desecration.",al={"next quest","follow up to raleigh","what comes after"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="How was Deliah's ring found initially?",a="The ring was recovered during the quest 'Rot Hide Clues', taken from Deliah's hand among the wrapped corpses on a boat at the Decrepit Ferry in Silverpine Forest.",al={"ring origin","where did the ring come from"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Magistrate Sevren want Deliah's ring brought to Raleigh?",a="When the engraved ring was recovered, Magistrate Sevren recalled that a woman named Deliah once lived in Brill with her husband, Raleigh. Raleigh now resides among the Forsaken in the Undercity. Sevren sends you to deliver the keepsake so Raleigh can confirm whether the heirloom truly belonged to his former wife, bringing closure or clarity to the fate of his lost family.",al={"why send ring to raleigh","magistrate sevren motive","why deliver deliah ring"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Raleigh's cold reaction to his wife's tragic demise reflects the widespread psychological trauma shared by the Forsaken, whose mortal attachments have decayed into bitter wrath.",["faction:Horde"]="Carrying tokens of old Lordaeron through the gates of the Undercity illustrates the somber realities of life among your Forsaken allies."},kw={"a husband's revenge","brill","deliah","deliah's ring","raleigh","sevren","trade quarter","undercity"},rel={"quest:440","quest:530","npc:raleigh-andrean","npc:magistrate-sevren","zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","subzone:brill"},m={start="Magistrate Sevren",["end"]="Raleigh Andrean",level="16",faction="Horde",id=441},src={"Raleigh and the Undercity"}}
E["quest:444"] = {t="quest",n="Rot Hide Origins",z="undercity",s="\"Rot Hide Origins\" is a Forsaken quest bridging the research of the Royal Apothecary Society in the Silverpine forest with the sorcerous expertise of the Undercity. After analyzing putrid fluids taken from gnolls, Apothecary Renferrel sends an adventurer to consult Bethor Iceshard to uncover the magical lineage behind these rotting beasts.",h="\"Rot Hide Origins\" is a Forsaken quest bridging the research of the Royal Apothecary Society in the...",sec={{t="A Concoction of Death and Fel",b="While examining the fluid harvested from the rot hide gnolls infesting Silverpine Forest, Apothecary Renferrel manages to reduce the foul substance into its basic elements. His preliminary chemical distillation reveals something far stranger than ordinary gnoll disease: the ichor carries the unmistakable dual signature of necromancy and warlock arts. Realizing pure alchemy cannot unravel the full scope of the sorcery at play, Renferrel tasks an agent with taking a prepared sample directly to the capital for esoteric scrutiny.",sp=0},{t="Audience with the Mage",b="The sample is carried to Bethor Iceshard, an accomplished Forsaken mage stationed high within the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Bethor does not belong to the Royal Apothecary Society, but his deep familiarity with arcane and dark disciplines makes him an invaluable resource for decoding unusual weaves of power. Upon receiving the vile vial, Bethor detects old, potent enchantments that he has not observed in years, immediately preparing a divination spell to identify who wove the foul magic.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends the player on this quest?",a="Apothecary Renferrel, an alchemist of the Royal Apothecary Society based in Silverpine Forest at the Sepulcher, assigns this task after examining the ichor recovered from nearby rot hide gnolls.",al={"who starts rot hide origins","where do i get rot hide origins"},gp=true},{q="Why does Renferrel send the sample to Bethor Iceshard?",a="Renferrel discovers that the rot hide ichor is steeped in necromantic and warlock magic. Since alchemy alone cannot fully explain the enchantments at work, he seeks the arcane expertise of Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity to divine its magical origins.",al={"why bethor iceshard","why give sample to mage"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Bethor Iceshard located?",a="Bethor Iceshard resides in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, surrounded by arcane researchers and trainers.",al={"bethor location","where is bethor iceshard"},gp=true},{q="What are the Rot Hides?",a="Rot hides are undead gnolls prowling Silverpine Forest. Unlike ordinary mindless beasts, their rotting condition is artificially induced by foul magical experiments.",al={"what are rot hides","rot hide gnolls silverpine"}},{q="What happens when you deliver the sample to Bethor?",a="Bethor recognizes ancient and potent magic laced throughout the fluid, noting that he has not encountered these particular spells in a very long time. He immediately begins casting a divination spell to track the source of the magic.",al={"what does bethor do","bethor iceshard reaction"}},{q="What quest comes next?",a="Following this delivery and Bethor's divination, he sends the adventurer on the quest 'Thule Ravenclaw' to investigate the renegade mage responsible for corrupting the gnolls.",al={"next quest after rot hide origins","follow up to rot hide origins"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="This task demonstrates the cooperation between the Royal Apothecary Society and the arcane masters of the Undercity, coordinating science and sorcery to safeguard Lordaeron.",["class:Mage"]="Bethor Iceshard's role underscores how arcane divination and scholarly spellcraft remain vital tools for solving dark mysteries that confound ordinary alchemy.",["class:Warlock"]="The discovery of fel and warlock magics intermingled with necromancy in the rot hide ichor points toward deliberate, taboo spellcraft at work in the Silverpine wilderness."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","bethor iceshard","magic quarter","rot hide ichor","rot hide origins","sample ichor","silverpine forest","undercity"},rel={"npc:bethor-iceshard","npc:apothecary-renferrel","zone:undercity","subzone:magic-quarter"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Bethor Iceshard",level="17",faction="Horde",id=444},src={"Rot Hide Origins"}}
E["quest:447"] = {t="quest",n="A Recipe For Death",z="undercity",s="A Recipe For Death is an alchemical errand commissioned by Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Tasked with gathering grizzly bear hearts and arachnid blood, adventurers transport the volatile biological reagents to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity to aid in formulating the Forsaken's lethal New Plague.",h="A Recipe For Death is an alchemical errand commissioned by Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher in...",sec={{t="A Weapon Against Two Foes",b="Positioned on the front lines in Silverpine Forest, Apothecary Renferrel recognizes the grim arithmetic facing Sylvanas's people. Surrounded by the relentless legions of Arthas and enduring remnants of humanity, conventional warfare offers little hope. The Forsaken's grand ambition lies in developing a New Plague—an engineered contagion potent enough to rot both living humans and undead Scourge alike. Renferrel's field research determined that combining arachnid venom from the Skittering Dark with toxins concentrated in the hearts of native bears yields a virulent foundation.",sp=0},{t="Dispatch to the Apothecarium",b="Once the harvested organs and blood are collected from the wilderness of Silverpine, they must be delivered beneath the ruins of Lordaeron into the heart of the Apothecarium. There, Master Apothecary Faranell oversees the grand design of the Royal Apothecary Society. Faranell immediately takes custody of Renferrel's samples, testing their contaminable properties to refine formulas that might one day secure Forsaken supremacy across the continent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of collecting bear hearts and spider blood?",a="Apothecary Renferrel's research showed that spider blood from the Skittering Dark reacts lethally when combined with toxins found in grizzled bear hearts. Together, these reagents provide vital raw materials for testing and developing the Royal Apothecary Society's New Plague.",al={"why bear hearts","why spider blood","what is this recipe for"},it="item"},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell is the head of the Royal Apothecary Society, stationed in the Apothecarium quarter of the Undercity. He oversees all research into concocting the New Plague on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"faranell lore","who is faranell","master apothecary"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want to create a New Plague?",a="Outnumbered by the Scourge and despised by living humans, the Forsaken lack the sheer military manpower to win an extended conventional war. A bespoke New Plague is engineered to eliminate both living adversaries and undead Scourge, securing their survival and autonomy.",al={"why make new plague","forsaken plague motivation","new plague lore"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Apothecary Renferrel located?",a="Apothecary Renferrel conducts his research out of the Sepulcher, the primary Forsaken settlement nestled within Silverpine Forest.",al={"renferrel location","where is renferrel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where is the Skittering Dark?",a="The Skittering Dark is an arachnid-infested wilderness located northwest of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, filled with giant spiders whose blood Renferrel requires.",al={"skittering dark location","where to find spiders silverpine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does this quest continue further?",a="Yes. Master Apothecary Faranell uses the delivered reagents to continue his experiments, leading directly into subsequent tasks within the Apothecarium to refine and test the lethal mixture.",al={"recipe for death follow up","is there a part 2"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want you to gather these reagents?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is dedicated to the Royal Apothecary Society's grand goal of crafting a New Plague. Facing the overwhelming armies of the Scourge and lingering human enclaves, Renferrel believes conventional warfare cannot secure the Forsaken's survival. He seeks to provide Master Apothecary Faranell with viable biological ingredients to brew a blight capable of obliterating both undead and living enemies alike.",al={"why does renferrel need this","renferrel motive","why help apothecary renferrel"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you sent against to collect the ingredients?",a="You are sent into the wilds of Silverpine Forest to hunt grizzled bears and the venomous arachnids infesting the Skittering Dark. These untamed beasts roam the ancient pine woods, thriving amid the creeping blighted decay, and their venom and resilient organs provide the potent natural toxins the Royal Apothecary Society requires.",al={"recipe for death targets","what do i kill recipe for death","who do i fight recipe for death"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Contributing to the Apothecary Society's plague research is among the highest duties an aspiring Forsaken can undertake to safeguard their fragile realm against the Scourge and humanity.",["faction:Horde"]="While Forsaken apothecaries pursue victory through virulent biological concoctions, such horrific methods are kept under tight wraps from the honor-bound leadership in Kalimdor."},kw={"faranell","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","silverpine","skittering dark","undercity"},rel={"npc:apothecary-renferrel","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","topic:royal-apothecary-society","quest:367","subzone:skittering-dark","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity","topic:scourge"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Master Apothecary Faranell",level="12",faction="Horde",id=447,ri={"Grizzled Bear Heart","Skittering Blood"}},src={"A Recipe For Death"}}
E["quest:450"] = {t="quest",n="A Recipe For Death",z="undercity",s="Master Apothecary Faranell tasks Horde adventurers with recovering the lost research of Apothecary Berard from Pyrewood Village. Berard fell victim to Archmage Arugal's shadow magic, leaving behind critical notes on an ancient blight that wiped out Lake Lordamere's aquatic life.",h="Master Apothecary Faranell tasks Horde adventurers with recovering the lost research of Apothecary Berard...",sec={{t="A Mind Lost to Shadow",b="Before his downfall, Apothecary Berard was considered one of the Royal Apothecary Society's most promising researchers. Stationed in Pyrewood Village, he investigated past ecological disasters to aid the Forsaken's alchemical pursuits. However, when Archmage Arugal unleashed his dark sorcery over Silverpine Forest, Berard succumbed to the curse, degrading into a mindless servant under the mage's thrall.",sp=0},{t="The Secrets of Lake Lordamere",b="Though Berard is considered a lost cause by Master Apothecary Faranell, his research remains immensely valuable to the Society. Berard had been cataloging the characteristics of a forgotten plague that eradicated all aquatic life in Lake Lordamere long ago. Recovering his journal from the Pyrewood Village Inn and delivering it to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher ensures the Royal Apothecary Society can adapt those deadly properties for the Dark Lady's arsenal.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Berard?",a="Apothecary Berard was once a brilliant researcher for the Royal Apothecary Society based in Silverpine Forest. His promising career ended when Archmage Arugal cast a dark curse across the region, shattering Berard's mind and binding him as a thrall in Pyrewood Village.",al={"berard lore","who was berard","apothecary berard pyrewood"},it="people"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want Berard's journal?",a="Prior to his mental degradation, Berard was documenting an ancient plague that killed off all aquatic life in Lake Lordamere ages ago. The Society seeks these records to understand the virulent agent and incorporate its lethal mechanisms into their ongoing research.",al={"why get the journal","berards journal purpose","lake lordamere plague notes"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Berard's journal located?",a="The journal is kept in Berard's study on an upper floor of the Pyrewood Village Inn, located toward the rear of the village. The afflicted apothecary still guards his former quarters.",al={"where is the journal","find berard journal","pyrewood inn journal"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who receives the recovered journal?",a="The journal must be delivered to Apothecary Renferrel, who oversees the Royal Apothecary Society's field operations from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"who turns in berard journal","who do i bring the journal to","where take journal"},it="next_step"},{q="What happened to Pyrewood Village?",a="Pyrewood Village fell under the corrupting influence of Archmage Arugal, who unleashed shadow magic from nearby Shadowfang Keep. The curse warp the minds and bodies of the villagers, subjecting them to Arugal's dark will.",al={"pyrewood curse","what is wrong with pyrewood","arugal curse pyrewood"},it="history"},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell is the head of the Royal Apothecary Society, conducting operations from the Apothecarium in the Undercity. He directly oversees the creation of new blights and venoms to defend the Forsaken and eradicate their enemies.",al={"faranell","who gives recipe for death","apothecary leader undercity"},it="leader"},{q="What is Berard's Journal?",a="Berard's Journal contains the research notes of Apothecary Berard before Archmage Arugal's curse stripped him of his mind. In it, Berard documented an ancient plague that eradicated aquatic life across Lake Lordamere ages ago. The Royal Apothecary Society hopes to study his findings to develop new plagues for the Forsaken.",al={"berards journal","what is in berards journal","berard journal purpose"},it="item",add=true},{q="Who is guarding Berard's journal in Pyrewood?",a="The journal remains in the Pyrewood Village inn, guarded by Berard himself alongside the cursed villagers. Once a promising alchemist for the Royal Apothecary Society, Berard succumbed to Arugal's shadow magic and now serves the mad mage mindlessly as a feral creature, hostile to any who intrude upon his former study.",al={"who guards berards journal","who is guarding the journal","who do i fight for the journal"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Royal Apothecary Society shows cold pragmatism: when a promising peer like Berard is lost to madness, his personal tragedy is disregarded in favor of salvaging his lethal research.",["faction:Horde"]="Assisting the Royal Apothecary Society in Silverpine helps secure the Forsaken's borders against the wild terrors unleashed by Arugal."},kw={"arugal","berard","faranell","journal","lordamere","pyrewood","renferrel","sepulcher"},rel={"quest:447","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:pyrewood-village","subzone:sepulcher","npc:arugal","topic:royal-apothecary-society"},m={start="Master Apothecary Faranell",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="15",faction="Horde",id=450,ri={"Berard's Journal"}},src={"A Recipe For Death (2)"}}
E["quest:451"] = {t="quest",n="A Recipe For Death",z="undercity",s="A Recipe For Death concludes an investigation into the findings of a fallen researcher, directing adventurers to gather rare biological reagents across Lake Lordamere. By recovering harvested mosses and a strange tumor, the Forsaken bring essential components to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity. This work directly supports the Royal Apothecary Society's overarching goal to develop a New Plague.",h="A Recipe For Death concludes an investigation into the findings of a fallen researcher, directing adventurers...",sec={{t="A Legacy of Research",b="The loss of Apothecary Berard to Arugal's curse struck a blow against the Royal Apothecary Society, but his field journal left behind crucial insights into the blighted biology of Silverpine Forest and Lake Lordamere. Stationed at the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel parsed through Berard's recovered notes and discovered that Berard had documented promising properties in local freshwater organisms. Rather than let Berard's sacrifice go to waste, Renferrel tasks champions of the Horde with fulfilling his lost colleague's vision.",sp=0},{t="The Hazards of Lake Lordamere",b="Gathering Berard's specified reagents requires venturing onto the Dawning Isles, the mist-shrouded islands situated along the eastern waters of Lake Lordamere. The lake skulkers and lake creepers inhabiting these isles gather peculiar strains of moss that survive in tainted waters. More elusive is the hardened tumor, a bizarre growth noted by Berard among the vicious Vile Fin murloc tribes that nest along the islets and southern lake shoreline near Ambermill.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the Apothecarium",b="Once collected, the specimens bypass the Sepulcher entirely and are delivered straight to the Apothecarium in the Undercity, into the waiting hands of Master Apothecary Faranell. Faranell views these strange mutations as indispensable steps toward crafting a New Plague capable of eradicating both Scourge and living foes. Berard's research is swiftly integrated into the Society's ongoing cauldron vats, bringing the Forsaken one step closer to their ultimate weapon.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society need moss and a tumor?",a="Apothecary Berard's field journal noted that the aquatic mosses found on lake beasts and the bizarre hardened tumors developing on local Vile Fin murlocs possess unique biological properties. Master Apothecary Faranell utilizes these rare mutated reagents to brew and refine the Royal Apothecary Society's New Plague.",al={"why moss and tumor","apothecary recipe ingredients","what is the tumor for"},it="item"},{q="Who was Berard?",a="Apothecary Berard was a researcher for the Royal Apothecary Society operating in Silverpine Forest. After Arugal's curse left him a mindless servant, his recovered field journal provided Apothecary Renferrel and Master Apothecary Faranell with the vital reagent specifications needed to continue his work.",al={"apothecary berard","who is berard","berard journal"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Dawning Isles located?",a="The Dawning Isles are a cluster of small islands situated in eastern Lake Lordamere, just east of Silverpine Forest. They are heavily infested with lake skulkers, lake creepers, and tribes of hostile Vile Fin murlocs.",al={"where are dawning isles","dawning isles location","lake skulker location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell is the leader of the Royal Apothecary Society, stationed deep within the Apothecarium of the Undercity. He oversees all research and development concerning chemical warfare, biological concoctions, and the creation of the New Plague on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"faranell","who is faranell","master apothecary faranell"},it="leader"},{q="Why are Vile Fin murlocs growing hardened tumors?",a="The waters and shores around Lake Lordamere have been heavily warped by blighted decay and nearby arcane conflicts. The hardened tumors found on the Vile Fin are rare, abnormal growths resulting from this contaminated environment, making them of immense scientific interest to the Forsaken.",al={"why murloc tumor","vile fin tumor lore","hardened tumor murlocs"},it="origin"},{q="How does this quest connect to the New Plague?",a="The entire Recipe for Death chain is an ingredient-gathering endeavor directly tied to the development of the New Plague. While junior apothecaries like Renferrel decipher and collect regional materials, everything is funneled directly to Faranell's central plague-brewing operations in the Undercity.",al={"new plague connection","a new plague questline","is this the plague"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want this done?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is dedicated to advancing the Royal Apothecary Society's research into the New Plague. Following the loss of his colleague Berard, Renferrel deciphered Berard's field journal and discovered promising leads on unique biological reagents. By sending you to collect these specimens and deliver them directly to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity, Renferrel ensures that Berard's sacrifice is not wasted and that their work for the Dark Lady continues without delay.",al={"why does renferrel want this","renferrel motive","why does apothecary renferrel send you"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are you hunting on the Dawning Isles?",a="You are dispatched to eastern Lake Lordamere to hunt the lake beasts and local murlocs dwelling around the Dawning Isles. Lake Skulkers and Lake Creepers yield the vital mosses identified in Berard's journal, while the aggressive Vile Fin murloc tribes inhabiting the shores occasionally develop the strange, hardened growths Master Apothecary Faranell needs to experiment on.",al={"who are you sent against","what do you kill in a recipe for death","lake lordamere targets"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Fulfilling Berard's unfinished experiments directly empowers the Dark Lady's vision, proving that every Forsaken mind contributes to the nation's survival even in death.",["faction:Horde"]="While Forsaken apothecaries welcome help from allied Horde combatants, they keep the finer chemical secrets and ultimate destructive potential of their New Plague carefully guarded."},kw={"a recipe for death","apothecarium","berard","dawning isles","faranell","hardened tumor","lake creeper","lake lordamere","lake skulker","new plague","renferrel","vile fin"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:apothecary-renferrel","quest:447","quest:367","topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:dawning-isles","zone:undercity","topic:murloc"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Master Apothecary Faranell",level="18",faction="Horde",id=451,ri={"Hardened Tumor","Lake Creeper Moss","Lake Skulker Moss"}},src={"A Recipe For Death (3)"}}
E["quest:491"] = {t="quest",n="Wand to Bethor",z="undercity",s="This quest concludes the Fenris Keep confrontation by delivering a long-lost relic, the Woven Wand, back to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity. Crafted years ago by three apprentice mages as a symbol of fellowship, the wand was hidden away when Thule Ravenclaw chose the Scourge. Returning it closes a bitter chapter in Bethor's past.",h="This quest concludes the Fenris Keep confrontation by delivering a long-lost relic, the Woven Wand, back to...",sec={{t="A Token of Fractured Fellowship",b="Long before Lordaeron fell into ruin, three young mages bound their training wands together into a single instrument known as the Woven Wand. It was meant to symbolize their shared bond and ambition within the magical arts. However, when Thule Ravenclaw turned his loyalty toward the Lich King and embraced the Scourge, that fellowship broke irrevocably. Though Thule came to despise the friendship they once shared, he could not bear to destroy the wand, nor could he stomach leaving it in his former comrades' hands.",sp=0},{t="Hidden in the Keep",b="Rather than part with the wand or destroy it, Thule carried it to Fenris Isle and concealed it in a dusty hidden shelf inside Fenris Keep. Untouched for years, its enchantment remained dormant; Thule never invoked its magic, an act Bethor noted would have immediately betrayed its whereabouts. Bringing it back to the Magic Quarter of the Undercity returns a rare keepsake of Bethor's mortal youth, recovered from the lair of a traitor who could neither love his friends nor let them go.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Woven Wand?",a="The Woven Wand is a unique magical tool fashioned long ago by Thule Ravenclaw and two fellow mage apprentices, one of whom was Bethor Iceshard. Each contributed their early apprentice wand, weaving them together as a physical emblem of their mutual friendship and shared arcane studies.",al={"woven wand","what is the wand","thule wand lore"},it="item"},{q="Why did Thule Ravenclaw steal the wand?",a="When Thule defected to the Lich King, the bond between the colleagues disintegrated. Even though Thule came to hate the friendship it represented, he was too possessive to part with the relic or allow Bethor and his other companion to keep it. Instead, he stole the wand and hid it on Fenris Isle.",al={"why did thule take it","why steal the wand","thule stolen wand"},it="history"},{q="Who is Bethor Iceshard?",a="Bethor Iceshard is a Forsaken mage trainer residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. In life, he was a peer and friend to Thule Ravenclaw before the kingdom collapsed and Thule surrendered his will to the Scourge.",al={"who is bethor","bethor iceshard lore","bethor undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Why didn't Thule use the Woven Wand's magic?",a="Had Thule ever invoked the wand's latent enchantments, Bethor would have sensed the resonance across the arcane weave. Thule kept it tucked away on a forgotten shelf in Fenris Keep solely out of spite and possessiveness, leaving its power untouched.",al={"did thule use wand","wand power","why not use it"},it="power"},{q="Who was the third apprentice who helped make the wand?",a="The third apprentice was Gunther Arcanus, who wove the wand together with Bethor and Thule long before Thule's betrayal.",al={"third apprentice","three mages wand","third mage"},it="people"},{q="Where did the wand end up before being found?",a="The wand was stashed away in a dusty shelf within a hidden niche inside Fenris Keep, the stronghold on Fenris Isle where Thule Ravenclaw established his Scourge operations.",al={"where was wand","hidden niche wand","fenris keep wand"},it="place"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The Woven Wand represents a classic arcane tradition: apprentice mages binding their foci together in fellowship, an innocence shattered when the Scourge tore Dalaran and Lordaeron apart.",["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken mages like Bethor, recovering pre-plague artifacts is a bittersweet reminder of mortal ambition and the former friends who chose the Lich King's tyranny over free will."},kw={"bethor iceshard","fenris isle","fenris keep","magic quarter","silverpine","thule ravenclaw","undercity","woven wand"},rel={"quest:461","quest:460","quest:446","npc:bethor-iceshard","subzone:magic-quarter","subzone:fenris-keep","zone:undercity","topic:lich-king"},m={start="Dusty Shelf",["end"]="Bethor Iceshard",level="18",faction="Horde",id=491},src={"Wand to Bethor"}}
E["quest:513"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Agony",z="undercity",s="This errand carries Apothecary Lydon's freshly mashed Mudsnout Composite from Tarren Mill straight to the heart of the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity. Master Apothecary Faranell requires the plant mash to treat it with a colloid of decay, furthering the Forsaken's development of a new plague.",h="This errand carries Apothecary Lydon's freshly mashed Mudsnout Composite from Tarren Mill straight to the...",sec={{t="A Courier to the Capital",b="In the ongoing efforts of the Royal Apothecary Society, regional researchers frequently send their raw discoveries back to Undercity for specialized refinement. Apothecary Lydon has mashed down local Mudsnout Blossoms into a composite, but bringing it to lethal fruition requires the advanced reagents kept only in the capital's laboratory.",sp=0},{t="The Master's Urgency",b="Master Apothecary Faranell works under tremendous pressure within the Apothecarium. Caught between the ever-present shadow of the Scourge in the north and aggressive human populations to the south, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner has demanded a potent new plague to defend their people. Receiving Lydon's composite provides Faranell with exactly the kind of toxic breakthrough the Dark Lady expects.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do I need to take the Mudsnout Composite to the Undercity?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill lacks the specific reagents required to finish this stage of his experiment. Master Apothecary Faranell holds a colloid of decay in the Apothecarium that must be applied to the Mudsnout Composite before the mixture can progress.",al={"why go to undercity","mudsnout composite destination","why bring to faranell"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society from his laboratory deep in the Undercity. He oversees all major chemical and alchemical research for the Forsaken, answering directly to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who is faranell","master apothecary faranell lore","apothecarium leader"},it="identity"},{q="What is the new plague the apothecaries keep mentioning?",a="The new plague is an ongoing Forsaken project commanded by Lady Sylvanas. It is engineered to annihilate both the living and the undead Scourge, providing the Forsaken with an absolute weapon against their enemies.",al={"what is the new plague","forsaken plague project","why make a new plague"},it="threat"},{q="Where can I find Master Apothecary Faranell?",a="Faranell resides within the Apothecarium, the southwestern quarter of the Undercity dedicated entirely to alchemy, poison brewing, and surgical experimentation.",al={"where is faranell","faranell location","apothecarium location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Apothecary Lydon trying to create?",a="Lydon is concocting the Elixir of Agony, an intensely virulent toxin brewed from Hillsbrad flora and decay agents, designed to prove the effectiveness of new strains in the field.",al={"what is lydon making","elixir of agony purpose","lydon experiment"},it="motive"},{q="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society so rushed?",a="The Forsaken perceive threats on every side. Northrend's Scourge threatens to overrun them, while remnants of human resistance apply relentless pressure from the south, making the completion of a decisive biological weapon urgently necessary.",al={"why rush","faranell busy","undercity threat"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon send you instead of going himself?",a="Apothecary Lydon is stationed in the Hillsbrad Foothills running critical field research for the Royal Apothecary Society. Preparing toxic compounds and monitoring local developments requires his constant attention at Tarren Mill, so trusted couriers must carry his raw mixtures to the Undercity for specialized refinement.",al={"why send me","why doesn't Lydon go to Undercity","why can't Lydon deliver it"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every batch of raw plant matter delivered to Faranell contributes to the ultimate survival and sovereign defense of the Forsaken against both the living and the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on Forsaken territory to hold northern Lordaeron, and the Royal Apothecary Society's research forms a vital part of holding those vulnerable borders."},kw={"apothecarium","apothecary lydon","colloid of decay","elixir of agony","master apothecary faranell","mudsnout composite","new plague","undercity"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","quest:509","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","quest:367","zone:hillsbrad","topic:scourge","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Master Apothecary Faranell",level="28",faction="Horde",id=513},src={"Elixir of Agony (2)"}}
E["quest:515"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Agony",z="undercity",s="This errand continues the development of the Royal Apothecary Society's new plague, dispatching a courier from Undercity back to Tarren Mill. Master Apothecary Faranell enriches Lydon's Mudsnout mixture with his own decaying compounds, demanding coastal reagents and alchemical draughts to catalyze the lethal brew.",h="This errand continues the development of the Royal Apothecary Society's new plague, dispatching a courier...",sec={{t="A Colloid of Decay",b="When Apothecary Lydon's field work produced a potent composite from Mudsnout Blossoms gathered at gnoll-held Nethander Stead, he sent it straight to the Apothecarium in the Undercity. Master Apothecary Faranell, head of the Royal Apothecary Society, immediately recognized the concoction's grim potential. Delighted by its toxic properties, Faranell added his own specialized colloid of decay to the mixture before outlining the catalysts required to weaponize it fully.",sp=0},{t="Catalysts from the Coast",b="Activating the volatile contaminating agents requires precise reagents that Lydon must assemble in Tarren Mill. In addition to a restorative draught of Strong Troll's Blood to feed and stabilize the chemical reaction, Faranell requires organic components harvested from the southern shoreline of Hillsbrad: scales stripped from the serpentine Daggerspine naga and eyes carved from the coastal Torn Fin murlocs.",sp=0},{t="Cruelty in Tarren Mill",b="Back in Tarren Mill, Lydon passes the waiting hours in morbid amusement, routinely poisoning, infecting, and reanimating his unfortunate undead test subject, Umpi. The delivery of Faranell's enriched mixture and coastal catalysts brings the apothecary closer to his ultimate goal: perfecting a new strain of agonizing blight to unleash against the living settlements of Hillsbrad.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does the plague require a restorative troll's blood elixir?",a="Apothecary concoctions frequently use regenerative substances to sustain, fuel, and rapidly mutate aggressive biological agents. The restorative properties of Strong Troll's Blood keep the toxic cultures thriving long enough to catalyze against the other reactive tissues.",al={"why troll blood","strong trolls blood purpose","trolls blood elixir plague"},it="item"},{q="Where are the Daggerspine scales found?",a="Daggerspine scales are harvested from the hostile Daggerspine naga inhabiting the eastern beaches of the Hillsbrad Foothills, situated along the shoreline east of the Alliance town of Southshore.",al={"daggerspine scales location","where are naga scales","where to get scales"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where are the Torn Fin eyes obtained?",a="Torn Fin eyes are gathered from the Torn Fin murlocs dwelling in tribes along the western coastline of the Hillsbrad Foothills, just west of Southshore.",al={"torn fin eye location","where are torn fin murlocs","murloc eyes hillsbrad"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is the frog Apothecary Lydon keeps as his 'assistant' in Tarren Mill. Lydon spends his idle hours using her as a disposable test subject, repeatedly inflicting lethal toxins and diseases upon her only to reanimate her once more.",al={"who is umpi","umpi hillsbrad","lydon assistant umpi"},it="people"},{q="Why is Master Apothecary Faranell involved in this local project?",a="As the leader of the Royal Apothecary Society, Faranell oversees all research into new biological agents and plagues. Field apothecaries like Lydon send promising wild discoveries directly to Faranell in the Undercity for refinement and authorization.",al={"why faranell","master apothecary faranell role","royal apothecary society leader"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Mudsnout Mixture?",a="It is an unrefined toxic composite Lydon mashed from Mudsnout Blossoms, foul mushrooms gathered at gnoll-infested Nethander Stead in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Recognizing its unusual virulence, Lydon sent it to Undercity, where Faranell blended it with decayed colloids to build a deadlier contagion.",al={"mudsnout mixture","gnoll poison","mudsnout composite"},it="item"},{q="What are the Daggerspine Scales and Torn Fin Eyes for?",a="Master Apothecary Faranell specifies that both the reptilian scales of the Daggerspine naga and the eyes of the Torn Fin murlocs are necessary reagents to activate the contaminating agents dormant within the Mudsnout Mixture. Combined with his own colloid of decay and restorative troll blood, these coastal aquatic harvests provide the reactive catalyst Apothecary Lydon requires to bring his lethal compound to life.",al={"daggerspine scale use","torn fin eye why needed","why daggerspine scales"},it="item",add=true},{q="Who are the Daggerspine and Torn Fin along the coast?",a="The southern shoreline of Hillsbrad Foothills has been overrun by hostile aquatic tribes flanking Southshore. To the east, the Daggerspine naga have encroached onto the beaches from the Great Sea, claiming territory with serpentine ferocity. To the west dwell the Torn Fin murlocs, scavengers clinging to the shallows. Their biology makes them unwitting sources of reagents for Forsaken alchemical warfare.",al={"hillsbrad naga murlocs","who are daggerspine","who are torn fin"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every refined reagent in this quest line brings the Royal Apothecary Society one step closer to fulfilling Lady Sylvanas's desire for an ultimate weapon against the living.",["faction:Horde"]="Tarren Mill stands on the brink of constant border skirmishes with the Alliance of Southshore; Lydon's toxic experiments are meant to tip the regional balance of power."},kw={"daggerspine","elixir of agony","faranell","lydon","mudsnout","tarren mill","torn fin","umpi","undercity"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:royal-apothecary-society","npc:umpi","quest:509","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","subzone:southshore"},m={start="Master Apothecary Faranell",["end"]="Apothecary Lydon",level="30",faction="Horde",id=515,ri={"Daggerspine Scale","Strong Troll's Blood Elixir","Torn Fin Eye"}},src={"Elixir of Agony (3)"}}
E["quest:530"] = {t="quest",n="A Husband's Revenge",z="undercity",s="A Husband's Revenge is the conclusion to a tragic tale of past betrayal carried into undeath. Raleigh Andrean, a Forsaken residing in the Undercity, charges travelers with tracking down his former friend Valdred Moray, who murdered his wife in life.",h="A Husband's Revenge is the conclusion to a tragic tale of past betrayal carried into undeath.",sec={{t="A Bitter Memory",b="When Raleigh Andrean received the engraved ring carried from Silverpine Forest, it rekindled memories of his mortal life that undeath had mostly withered away. Among those memories was a profound betrayal: his close friend, Valdred Moray, had murdered Raleigh's wife, Deliah. While the chill of the Scourge and subsequent Forsaken existence dulled Raleigh's capacity for grief and love, his thirst for retribution remained entirely intact.",sp=0},{t="Justice at the Wall",b="Fleeing the consequences of his past actions and the horrors of Lordaeron, Valdred Moray fled southward through Silverpine Forest, desperate to escape into the isolationist human kingdom behind the Greymane Wall. Yet the colossal gates remained sealed against refugees and outcasts alike. Trapped against the stonework, Valdred met his end at the behest of the friend he betrayed, his severed hands severed and carried back to the Undercity.",sp=1},{t="Cold Keepsakes",b="Upon receiving the hands of his former friend, Raleigh feels no rush of warmth or redemption—only cold finality. Having settled the score, he surrenders Deliah's wedding band without sentiment, declaring it a useless bauble. In its place, the severed hands of Valdred Moray remain in the Undercity as Raleigh's grim, permanent reminder of mortal betrayal.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Raleigh want Valdred's hands specifically?",a="Raleigh demands Valdred's hands because they are the physical instruments that ended his wife's life. He intends to keep them in the Undercity as a permanent trophy and reminder of his friend's betrayal.",al={"why hands","valdred hands","raleigh wants hands"},it="item"},{q="Where is Valdred Moray hiding?",a="Valdred Moray is located in far southern Silverpine Forest, camped against the colossal Greymane Wall, having failed to gain entry into the closed kingdom of Gilneas.",al={"where is valdred","valdred location","valdred moray spot"},gp=true},{q="Why does Raleigh give back the wedding ring?",a="In undeath, Raleigh's emotional attachment to Deliah has withered away to nothing. Without the capacity for grief or affection, her ring is an empty trinket to him; only the malice of revenge held any real value.",al={"why give ring away","ring of scorn lore","why discard ring"},sp=1},{q="Can Valdred Moray enter Gilneas?",a="No. King Genn Greymane ordered the wall sealed during the Third War to shut out the rest of the world and the Scourge. Valdred, like many desperate refugees, found himself stranded at the locked gates.",al={"greymane wall closed","why is valdred outside wall"}},{q="What quests lead up to this task?",a="The chain begins with 'The Engraved Ring' in Silverpine Forest, which directs you to the Undercity in 'Raleigh and the Undercity', unlocking 'A Husband's Revenge'.",al={"husband revenge chain","prerequisite quest","previous quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Raleigh Andrean want revenge?",a="Valdred Moray was once Raleigh's close friend, but he murdered Raleigh's wife, Deliah. While the cold grasp of undeath has stripped Raleigh of his ability to mourn or grieve his lost love, the burning urge for retribution remains. Avenging her death and punishing his former friend's betrayal is the only desire he has left in his unlife.",al={"why does raleigh want valdred dead","raleigh andrean motive","why kill valdred moray"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who is Valdred Moray and why is he at the Greymane Wall?",a="Valdred Moray is Raleigh Andrean's former friend who murdered Raleigh's wife, Deliah. Having committed the crime, he fled south into Silverpine Forest and holed up by the sealed gates of the Greymane Wall, desperate to escape into the closed kingdom of Gilneas before his past catches up with him.",al={"who is valdred moray","why is valdred moray in silverpine","valdred moray greymane wall"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Raleigh's cold detachment from his dead wife, paired with his lingering obsession with hatred and vengeance, is a stark portrait of how undeath warps mortal psychology.",["faction:Horde"]="Carrying out justice across Silverpine Forest helps secure the borders around the Undercity against lingering human outlaws."},kw={"deliah","engraved ring","greymane wall","raleigh andrean","ring of scorn","silverpine forest","undercity","valdred moray"},rel={"npc:raleigh-andrean","quest:441","quest:440","subzone:greymane-wall","zone:undercity"},m={start="Raleigh Andrean",level="20",faction="Horde",id=530,ri={"Valdred's Hands"}},src={"A Husband's Revenge"}}
E["quest:550"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="undercity",s="This mission marks the conclusion of the Forsaken campaign against the human township of Hillsbrad. Having shattered the local Alliance forces, you are sent by High Executor Darthalia to present an official commendation to Varimathras in the Undercity.",h="This mission marks the conclusion of the Forsaken campaign against the human township of Hillsbrad.",sec={{t="A Decisive Campaign",b="The campaign in the Hillsbrad Foothills represents a brutal struggle for southern Lordaeron. Across a protracted series of strikes coordinated from Tarren Mill, Horde champions dismantled the human township's farmers, militia, blacksmiths, and civic leaders. With the Alliance presence crippled and the territory secured for the Forsaken, High Executor Darthalia drafts an official commendation to ensure the executor's exploits reach the highest ranks of command.",sp=0},{t="Audience with the Dreadlord",b="Carrying Darthalia's sealed commendation leads directly to the Royal Quarter of the Undercity, into the presence of Varimathras. Standing alongside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the dreadlord oversees military operations across Lordaeron. While the Scourge descending from the northern Plaguelands remains the Dark Lady's paramount existential threat, securing the southern borders against surviving human enclaves is vital for the nascent Forsaken nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is this quest?",a="It is the final turn-in for the extensive Battle of Hillsbrad quest chain. After completing your tasks for High Executor Darthalia at Tarren Mill, she gives you a sealed letter of commendation to deliver personally to Varimathras in the Undercity.",al={"battle of hillsbrad finale","hillsbrad final quest","quest 550"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do I turn in Darthalia's Sealed Commendation?",a="You turn it in to Varimathras, who stands beside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"where is varimathras","turn in commendation","darthalia letter turn in"},gp=true},{q="Why does Varimathras care about Hillsbrad?",a="As the Dark Lady's chief military lieutenant, Varimathras oversees strategic defense and expansion. Although the Scourge in the north is the Undercity's greatest threat, human settlements to the south constantly harass Forsaken lines. Eliminating the threat in Hillsbrad protects their southern frontier.",al={"why varimathras","varimathras role in hillsbrad"},it="ties"},{q="Who is High Executor Darthalia?",a="High Executor Darthalia is the senior Forsaken commander stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, directing the offensive operations against the nearby human settlement.",al={"darthalia","who gave the quest"},it="identity"},{q="Does this quest lead to further missions in Hillsbrad?",a="No. Delivering the commendation to Varimathras is the official conclusion of the Battle of Hillsbrad storyline, rewarding you for breaking the town's defenses.",al={"next quest after battle of hillsbrad","what comes after quest 550"},it="next_step"},{q="Why were the Forsaken attacking Hillsbrad in the first place?",a="The town of Hillsbrad represents one of the last organized human footholds in Lordaeron. Aligned with the Alliance, its militia and proximity pose an immediate military threat to Tarren Mill and the southern approaches to the Undercity.",al={"why attack hillsbrad","hillsbrad lore"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia want this commendation delivered?",a="You have fought with valor and perseverance throughout the brutal campaign across the Hillsbrad Foothills. High Executor Darthalia wants your battlefield heroics formally recognized by the Forsaken high command in the Undercity. By sending you directly to Varimathras with her sealed commendation, she ensures that the leadership acknowledges a capable champion whose decisive strikes broke human resistance on the southern front.",al={"why send commendation","darthalia motive","why send to varimathras"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Reporting your victory over the living of Hillsbrad earns direct praise from the Royal Quarter, affirming your place within the Dark Lady's rising empire.",["faction:Horde"]="By driving back Alliance forces in Lordaeron, you secure vital ground for the Horde in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","hillsbrad foothills","royal quarter","sealed commendation","tarren mill","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"npc:varimathras","npc:high-executor-darthalia","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:lich-king"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",["end"]="Varimathras",level="32",faction="Horde",id=550},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (7) (Classic)"}}
E["quest:5679"] = {t="quest",n="Devouring Plague",z="undercity",s="Devouring Plague is a rite of instruction offered to Forsaken priests who have proven their dedication to shadow magic. Granted by Priestess Aelthalyste in the Undercity, the teaching marks an acolyte's initiation into one of the most dreaded curses woven by the undead priesthood.",h="Devouring Plague is a rite of instruction offered to Forsaken priests who have proven their dedication to...",sec={{t="A Curse of the Shadow",b="In the murky cloisters of the War Quarter, Priestess Aelthalyste guides Forsaken practitioners through the grim arts of the Shadow. While living priests of other races appeal to the Holy Light or ancestral spirits for their power, the Forsaken have forged their own spiritual doctrines. Devouring Plague represents the crystallization of their philosophy: inflicting suffering upon their foes while leeching the stolen vitality back into their own decaying bodies.",sp=0},{t="A Test of Mastery",b="Aelthalyste does not offer the knowledge of the plague lightly. The spell is considered a weapon of potent malice, intended to turn the tide against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade. When imparting the spell, Aelthalyste warns her disciples to hone their command over it through relentless practice, cautioning that far greater trials lie ahead for those who seek to master the dark arts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The quest serves as a formal lesson for Forsaken priests reaching seasoned standing. By speaking with Priestess Aelthalyste, the priest is taught how to cast Devouring Plague, a signature shadow affliction unique to undead practitioners.",al={"why do devouring plague","what does devouring plague quest do","devouring plague purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Priestess Aelthalyste?",a="Priestess Aelthalyste is a Forsaken priest trainer residing in the War Quarter of the Undercity. She oversees the development of emerging shadow casters and ensures they wield their destructive blessings effectively for the Forsaken.",al={"who is aelthalyste","aelthalyste lore","aelthalyste undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Can priests of other races learn Devouring Plague from Aelthalyste?",a="No. Devouring Plague is an esoteric spell exclusive to Forsaken priests. Trolls, humans, night elves, and dwarves commune with different spiritual forces and possess their own distinct racial teachings instead.",al={"can trolls learn devouring plague","is devouring plague undead only","other races devouring plague"},gp=true},{q="Where do I turn in this quest?",a="Priestess Aelthalyste can be found in the War Quarter of the Undercity, lingering among the Forsaken's priest instructors and practitioners.",al={"aelthalyste location","where is devouring plague quest","undercity priest trainer location"},gp=true},{q="Why do Forsaken priests specialize in plague and shadow magic?",a="Forsaken priests endure intense physical pain whenever they channel the Holy Light due to their undead state. As a result, many turn toward the teachings of the Shadow, using afflictions, curses, and stolen life-force to survive and wage war.",al={"why forsaken shadow priests","lore behind undead priests","forsaken priest magic"},it="origin"},{q="What tests is Aelthalyste referring to?",a="Aelthalyste warns that as a priest grows in power, the trials faced across Lordaeron will intensify. Wielding dark magic invites dangerous scrutiny and deadly foes, demanding absolute command over every curse in an acolyte's repertoire.",al={"tests later meaning","future tests aelthalyste","what tests"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Priestess Aelthalyste want you to learn Devouring Plague?",a="Priestess Aelthalyste sees Devouring Plague as a vital, potent weapon for the Forsaken's survival. She instructs Forsaken priests in this dark art so that you will be properly equipped to defend the Undercity and prevail in the relentless trials and conflicts awaiting the Forsaken across Lordaeron.",al={"aelthalyste motive","why teach devouring plague","why does aelthalyste want this done"},it="motive",rc="Undead",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This rite provides Forsaken priests with one of their most iconic racial spells, binding their survival directly to the affliction they inflict on enemies.",["race:Undead"]="Embracing plague-like shadowcraft reflects the Forsaken's divergence from traditional Lordaeron worship following the Third War.",["faction:Horde"]="While other Horde allies rely on ancestral spirits or elemental balance, the Forsaken bring ruthless, disease-like curses into the faction's collective arsenal."},kw={"aelthalyste","devouring plague","forsaken","lordaeron","priest","shadow","undercity","war quarter"},rel={"npc:aelthalyste","quest:5644"},m={start="Aelthalyste",level="20",faction="Horde",id=5679},src={"Devouring Plague (Undercity)"}}
E["quest:6322"] = {t="quest",n="Michael Garrett",z="undercity",s="Michael Garrett is a simple courier task linking trade in the Undercity with the Forsaken's flight network. After collecting supplies packed by Gordon Wendham in the Trade Quarter, you are directed to deliver the crate to the bat handler Michael Garrett to arrange aerial transport out toward the Sepulcher. It highlights how the Forsaken utilize trained vampire bats to connect their capital with outposts across Lordaeron.",h="Michael Garrett is a simple courier task linking trade in the Undercity with the Forsaken's flight network.",sec={{t="Supplying the Outposts",b="Running a fledgeling kingdom carved out of the ruins of Lordaeron requires constant logistics. Outposts like the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest rely heavily on goods, munitions, and provisions moving out from the Undercity. Gordon Wendham packs the necessary field supplies into a single crate in the city's Trade Quarter, but carting freight by ground through blighted forests is both slow and vulnerable to ambush by Scourge remnants or wild beasts.",sp=0},{t="Wings of the Forsaken",b="To bypass the dangers on the roads, the Forsaken rely on captive vampire bats bred and maintained by skilled handlers. Michael Garrett oversees these winged beasts from his roost in the Undercity's Trade Quarter. Delivering the cargo to him ensures the supplies can be strapped to a bat and flown directly over the hills to Silverpine, teaching new couriers how the capital coordinates with remote settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Michael Garrett?",a="Michael Garrett is the Undercity's bat handler, stationed in the Trade Quarter. He manages the flight network's vampire bats, arranging travel and air delivery between the Forsaken capital and allied flight masters throughout Lordaeron.",al={"michael garrett","undercity bat master","who is garrett"},it="identity"},{q="What is in Gordon's Crate?",a="The crate contains vital provisions and field supplies gathered by Gordon Wendham in the Trade Quarter, earmarked specifically for the Forsaken forces stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"gordon's crate","what supplies","sepulcher crate"},it="item"},{q="Why use bats instead of carts or horses?",a="The overland roads winding out of Tirisfal Glades into Silverpine Forest are fraught with hazards, including roaming Scourge beasts, hostile humans, and treacherous terrain. Flying routes overhead via trained giant bats are drastically faster and completely bypass ground ambushes.",al={"why bat flight","why use bats","flying supplies"}},{q="Where does the delivery go after Michael Garrett?",a="Once Michael Garrett receives Gordon's Crate, the cargo is prepped to fly by bat directly to the bat master stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, completing the logistics chain.",al={"next step","after michael garrett","where do bats fly"},it="next_step"},{q="Where can Michael Garrett be found in Undercity?",a="He is located in the southwestern part of the Trade Quarter, the same quarter where bats arriving from the Sepulcher land.",al={"where is garrett","find bat handler","undercity flight master location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Do you need to have visited the Sepulcher before doing this?",a="To ride a bat yourself alongside the delivery, you must have previously spoken with the flight handler at the Sepulcher to unlock the aerial route; otherwise, you will have to travel there by foot.",al={"sepulcher flight path required","can i fly immediately"},gp=true},{q="Why does Gordon Wendham want this done?",a="Gordon Wendham is tasked with coordinating vital logistical supplies destined for the Sepulcher, the Forsaken outpost in Silverpine Forest. Since he must remain at his trade post in the Undercity to manage goods, he needs you to transfer the packed crate to Michael Garrett so it can be dispatched swiftly along their aerial courier route.",al={"why send gordon's crate","gordon wendham motive","why bring crate to michael garrett"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Understanding the aerial supply line run by handlers like Michael Garrett is essential for maintaining Sylvanas's presence beyond Tirisfal Glades.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers arriving from Kalimdor, the Forsaken bat network serves as the primary mode of rapid transit across the northern Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"bat master","flight master","gordon wendham","gordon's crate","michael garrett","sepulcher","silverpine","undercity"},rel={"npc:gordon-wendham","zone:undercity","subzone:sepulcher","quest:6324"},m={start="Gordon Wendham",["end"]="Michael Garrett",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6322},src={"Michael Garrett (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6323"] = {t="quest",n="Ride to the Undercity",z="undercity",s="Ride to the Undercity introduces fledgling Forsaken adventurers to the Horde's aerial flight network across Lordaeron. Carrying weapon requisitions from the embattled outpost of the Sepulcher, couriers take a dread bat directly into the Undercity's Trade Quarter to resupply regional defenders.",h="Ride to the Undercity introduces fledgling Forsaken adventurers to the Horde's aerial flight network across...",sec={{t="Wings Over Silverpine",b="Maintaining lines of communication between the Forsaken capital and its frontline outposts requires swift, reliable transit. Karos Razok, the bat handler stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, manages the trained dread bats that ferry messengers and supplies across the plagued landscape. With roads crawling with hostile beasts, Moonrage worgen, and remnants of the Scourge, taking to the skies is the safest and fastest way to ensure urgent military requests reach the capital.",sp=0},{t="Arming the Front",b="Upon touching down in the Undercity's bustling Trade Quarter, the courier delivers Podrig's equipment requisition directly to Gordon Wendham. As an Undercity weaponsmith dedicated to the Dark Lady's cause, Wendham ensures that regional outposts like the Sepulcher remain outfitted with clean, battle-ready armaments. Sustaining these defensive hubs is vital for the fledgling Forsaken nation as it secures its borders against surrounding enemies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this flight to the Undercity?",a="The mission serves to deliver an official weapons requisition from Deathguard Podrig at the Sepulcher directly to Gordon Wendham, a weapon dealer working in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity, while teaching new champions how to use the Forsaken flight network.",al={"why ride to undercity","ride to the undercity objective","podrig's order use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Karos Razok?",a="Karos Razok is the bat master stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He oversees the roost of dread bats used by the Forsaken to maintain rapid travel and communication with the Undercity.",al={"karos razok role","who is the sepulcher bat master"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Gordon Wendham?",a="Gordon Wendham is a Forsaken weapon crafter located in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity, right near the bat handler's landing platform. He takes pride in keeping weapons cleaned, sharpened, and ready for Lady Sylvanas's frontline forces.",al={"gordon wendham","where is gordon wendham"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the Forsaken use bats for transit?",a="Dread bats are native nocturnal predators well-suited to Lordaeron's blighted skies. They provide swift passage above treacherous ground hazards such as feral worgen, hostile rot hides, and the Scourge.",al={"why bats","forsaken flight mounts"}},{q="What happens after completing the delivery?",a="After receiving the order, Gordon Wendham directs couriers to Michael Garrett, the Undercity bat handler, establishing a return flight path back toward the Sepulcher.",al={"what comes next","follow up to ride to the undercity"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does the dread bat land in the Undercity?",a="The dread bat lands on the raised bat roost perched directly in the center of the Undercity's Trade Quarter, providing immediate access to the city's craftsmen and supply merchants.",al={"undercity bat landing","where does bat land"},it="place"},{q="Why does Karos Razok want this done?",a="As the flight master stationed at the Sepulcher, Karos Razok oversees the aerial courier network binding Silverpine Forest to the capital. Outposts like the Sepulcher depend entirely on steady supply lines and rapid correspondence to survive against surrounding threats. By carrying Deathguard Podrig's equipment requisition directly to the weapon suppliers in the Undercity, you ensure the front-line sentries defending the realm receive the arms and armor they desperately need.",al={"why send podrig order","karos razok motive","why ride to undercity"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Taking wing from Silverpine to the capital highlights the reach and organization of the Dark Lady's network, ensuring isolated garrisons are never cut off from Undercity's industry.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Delivering orders to Gordon Wendham offers smiths a look at the logistical spine of Lordaeron, where every piece of iron is kept sharp and ready for war.",["faction:Horde"]="Flight masters form the essential connective tissue of the Horde's territorial expansion, turning arduous wilderness treks into rapid tactical deployments."},kw={"dread bat","flight master","gordon wendham","karos razok","podrig's order","ride to the undercity","sepulcher","trade quarter"},rel={"npc:karos-razok","npc:gordon-wendham","zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","subzone:sepulcher","quest:6321"},m={start="Karos Razok",["end"]="Gordon Wendham",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6323},src={"Ride to the Undercity (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6324"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Podrig",z="undercity",s="Return to Podrig is a logistics quest concluding a courier run between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity. After delivering a dispatch to the capital, the courier is entrusted with a crate of weapons to ferry back to Deathguard Podrig at the Sepulcher using the Forsaken bat handler network.",h="Return to Podrig is a logistics quest concluding a courier run between Silverpine Forest and the Undercity.",sec={{t="The Undercity Supply Line",b="Outposts throughout Lordaeron depend heavily on regular shipments from the Undercity to remain operational. At the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, Deathguard sentries face pressure from local worgen, Dalaran remnants, and Scourge stragglers. Supplying remote garrisons with freshly forged armaments is vital to holding the region under Forsaken control.",sp=0},{t="Wings of the Forsaken",b="Bat Master Michael Garrett operates the central roost in the Undercity courtyard, serving as the hub for Forsaken aerial travel. While bats naturally return to the capital, riders must first coordinate with local handlers like Karos Razok before flights to distant outposts can be charted. Flying Gordon's Crate across Lordaeron's skies teaches couriers how the Forsaken bind their scattered strongholds together.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is in Gordon's Crate?",a="The crate contains fresh weapons produced in the Undercity to keep the Deathguards stationed at the Sepulcher properly equipped against surrounding threats.",al={"gordons crate contents","what am i delivering to podrig"},it="item"},{q="Who is Deathguard Podrig?",a="Deathguard Podrig is a Forsaken soldier stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest who oversees logistical and defense duties for the local garrison.",al={"podrig","who is podrig"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Michael Garrett?",a="Michael Garrett is the Forsaken bat master stationed in the upper courtyard of the Undercity, responsible for coordinating flight paths across Lordaeron.",al={"michael garrett","undercity bat master"},it="identity"},{q="Why do you have to speak to a bat master before flying somewhere?",a="Forsaken bats naturally know the way back to the central roost in the Undercity, but outward flights require establishing a route with a regional handler first to ensure safe arrival.",al={"flight path rules","how do bat handlers work"}},{q="Why is the Sepulcher so important to supply?",a="The Sepulcher is the Forsaken's main forward base in Silverpine Forest. It anchors their military presence against worgen packs, Moonrage threats, and Dalaran forces in the area.",al={"why sepulcher matters","sepulcher importance"},it="place"},{q="Who is Karos Razok?",a="Karos Razok is the bat master stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, managing roosted bats that connect the outpost to the Undercity.",al={"karos razok","sepulcher bat master"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Michael Garrett want this done?",a="As the Undercity's bat master, Michael Garrett oversees aerial transit and courier routes across Forsaken lands. Deathguard Podrig and the soldiers holding the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest desperately require fresh armaments from the capital. Garrett ensures these vital weapons are dispatched efficiently using the bat network, strengthening the Dark Lady's frontier outposts against nearby threats.",al={"why michael garrett crate","garrett motive return to podrig","why send crate to sepulcher"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Michael Garrett send you instead of going himself?",a="Garrett must remain stationed at the Undercity's bat roost to tend to the beasts and coordinate flights in and out of the capital. Since you are an able courier already journeying back toward Silverpine Forest, entrusting you with the crate ensures the delivery is made without pulling valuable flight masters or guards away from their essential posts.",al={"why send me","why doesn't garrett deliver it","why me return to podrig"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Keeping forward garrisons armed is essential to defending Lordaeron and securing Queen Sylvanas's fledgling realm.",["faction:Horde"]="This task demonstrates the logistical framework connecting the Undercity to remote outposts across the northern continent."},kw={"bat master","gordons crate","karos razok","michael garrett","podrig","sepulcher","silverpine","undercity"},rel={"quest:6322","zone:undercity","subzone:sepulcher","npc:karos-razok"},m={start="Michael Garrett",["end"]="Deathguard Podrig",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6324},src={"Return to Podrig"}}
E["quest:8354"] = {t="quest",n="Chicken Clucking for a Mint",z="undercity",s="During the festive season of Hallow's End, Innkeeper Norman of the Undercity offers a piece of candy to travelers helping an ailing child. To earn the Undercity Mint, adventurers must cast aside their dignity and flap about like a chicken.",h="During the festive season of Hallow's End, Innkeeper Norman of the Undercity offers a piece of candy to...",sec={{t="A Rare Bit of Mirth",b="The Undercity is rarely known for laughter or warmth, built as it is beneath the ruins of Lordaeron by the liberated Forsaken. Yet when Hallow's End arrives, even the grim denizens of the Trade Quarter join in seasonal revelry. Innkeeper Norman holds onto a stash of Undercity Mints, designated for those collecting treats on behalf of young Spoops, a sick orphan in need of holiday cheer.",sp=0},{t="Earning the Treat",b="Rather than surrendering the treat outright to seasoned adventurers, Norman demands a bit of humiliating spectacle. Believing that grown warriors and spellcasters ought to earn their confections, he refuses to part with the mint until the petitioner mimics a barnyard chicken right before his counter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Innkeeper Norman want me to cluck like a chicken?",a="Innkeeper Norman believes grown champions are too old to go around trick-or-treating without putting on a show. To lighten the mood during Hallow's End, he demands a ridiculous performance—flapping and clucking like a chicken—before he will hand over his holiday treat.",al={"why chicken emote","why cluck norman","norman chicken dance"},it="motive"},{q="Who is the treat intended for?",a="The Undercity Mint is collected on behalf of Spoops, a sick orphan resting in Orgrimmar who is unable to go trick-or-treating himself during the Hallow's End festival.",al={"who gets the mint","what is the mint for","why get undercity mint"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Innkeeper Norman located?",a="Innkeeper Norman operates the central tavern within the Trade Quarter of the Undercity, serving Forsaken patrons and visiting Horde travelers.",al={"norman location","where is undercity innkeeper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is this a seasonal festival quest?",a="Yes. This quest is part of the annual Hallow's End holiday celebrations celebrated across Azeroth by both Horde and Alliance.",al={"is this hallows end","when is this quest available"},gp=true},{q="Do Forsaken normally celebrate Hallow's End?",a="The Forsaken celebrate Hallow's End with great enthusiasm, burning a massive wicker man outside the ruins of Lordaeron to commemorate their liberation and break with their former mortal lives.",al={"forsaken hallows end","undead holiday"},it="history"},{q="What happens after getting the Undercity Mint?",a="The mint is combined with other signature treats gathered from the various Horde racial capitals to assemble a full holiday gift for young Spoops.",al={"next quest","what do i do with the mint"},it="next_step",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Finding silly humor among the rotting halls of the Undercity is rare, making Norman's seasonal demand a bizarre break from daily necromantic pragmatism.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers travel between every capital city during Hallow's End, braving foolish indignities in each to bring joy to an orphaned child."},kw={"chicken","cluck","hallow's end","innkeeper norman","spoops","trade quarter","undercity","undercity mint"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-norman","zone:undercity"},m={start="Innkeeper Norman",faction="Horde",id=8354},src={"Chicken Clucking for a Mint (Horde)"}}
E["quest:8648"] = {t="quest",n="Darkcore the Elder",z="undercity",s="Darkcore the Elder is a seasonal quest encountered during the Lunar Festival within the Undercity. By seeking out Elder Darkcore, travelers pay homage to the ancient spirits honored across Azeroth and receive a Coin of Ancestry in return.",h="Darkcore the Elder is a seasonal quest encountered during the Lunar Festival within the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Spirit in the Undercity",b="During the Lunar Festival, spirits of ancient night elven and earthen ancestors appear throughout the continents to share their wisdom and blessings. Elder Darkcore resides in the shadowed halls of the Undercity, bearing witness to the modern realm while offering remembrance to those who seek out the roots of the world.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Ancestors",b="Approaching Elder Darkcore satisfies an ancient custom of showing respect to the venerable dead and the timeless wardens of Azeroth. In recognition of this pilgrimage, the spirit gifts travelers a Coin of Ancestry as a token of goodwill and enduring memory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of visiting Elder Darkcore?",a="Visiting Elder Darkcore during the Lunar Festival allows adventurers to pay homage to the ancient peoples of Azeroth. Speaking with him completes the quest and earns a Coin of Ancestry.",al={"elder darkcore goal","why visit darkcore","darkcore quest purpose"}},{q="Where can Elder Darkcore be found?",a="Elder Darkcore manifests inside the Undercity, standing among the somber subterranean avenues of the Forsaken capital.",al={"elder darkcore location","where is elder darkcore","darkcore undercity spot"}},{q="What is the Lunar Festival?",a="The Lunar Festival is an annual season of remembrance and renewal observed across Azeroth, celebrating the triumph over the Burning Legion and paying reverence to ancient elders who guided mortal races.",al={"lunar festival lore","why are elders appearing","what are the elders"}},{q="What do the elders represent?",a="Elders are ancient spirits, typically linked to the night elves or early earthen cultures, who emerge during the Lunar Festival to bless those who remember their deeds and carry forward the lessons of antiquity.",al={"who are the elders","lunar festival elders lore","ancestor spirits"}},{q="Can Alliance adventurers speak to Elder Darkcore?",a="Elder Darkcore will greet any traveler who manages to reach him, though Alliance players must brave the heavily defended Forsaken capital to do so.",al={"alliance darkcore","can alliance get darkcore","elder darkcore alliance"}},{q="What is a Coin of Ancestry?",a="A Coin of Ancestry is a festive token bestowed by elders during the Lunar Festival, symbolizing reverence for antiquity and tradable for festive garb and seasonal keepsakes.",al={"what are coins of ancestry","coin of ancestry use","lunar festival coin"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken walking through the ruins of their former kingdom, Elder Darkcore offers an eerie reminder of older times before the Scourge and the fall of Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Elder Darkcore allows members of the Horde to partake in the continent-wide rites of the Lunar Festival directly within the safety of an allied capital."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","darkcore the elder","elder darkcore","elders","lunar festival","undercity"},rel={"npc:elder-darkcore"},m={start="Elder Darkcore",id=8648},src={"Darkcore the Elder"}}
E["quest:9265"] = {t="quest",n="Investigate the Scourge of the Undercity",z="undercity",s="Lieutenant Rukag dispatches Horde defenders to combat the Scourge forces that have dared to encamp outside the Undercity. Agents are tasked with investigating ominous, glowing runic circles linked to the dread necropolis overhead and retrieving Dim Necrotic Stones as proof of their destruction.",h="Lieutenant Rukag dispatches Horde defenders to combat the Scourge forces that have dared to encamp outside...",sec={{t="On the Doorstep",b="The Scourge invasion pushes right to the gates of Lordaeron's fallen capital. Rather than hiding behind the fortified gates of the Undercity, Horde commanders like Lieutenant Rukag organize an immediate counter-offensive to eradicate the encroaching dead before they can mount an assault.",sp=0},{t="Necrotic Relics",b="Outside the citadel, the Scourge have erected glowing runic circles pulsing with foul necromantic energies that resonate with the floating necropolises darkening the skies. Defeating these Scourge trespassers yields Dim Necrotic Stones, dark focuses used to fuel their terrifying rituals and sustain their unnatural march.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders the investigation outside the Undercity?",a="Lieutenant Rukag, a Horde officer stationed to defend the Undercity, commands warriors to investigate the growing Scourge presence outside the gates and cut down their forces.",al={"who gives investigate the scourge","lieutenant rukag","rukag undercity"},it="identity"},{q="What are Dim Necrotic Stones?",a="Dim Necrotic Stones are shadowy magical artifacts carried by the invading Scourge. They hum with foul necromancy and serve as proof of their demise when returned to Horde officers.",al={"what are necrotic stones","dim necrotic stone","scourge stones"},it="item"},{q="What are the glowing runic circles?",a="They are ritualistic circles scribed upon the ground by the Scourge encampments, radiating the same dark magic that shields and sustains the necropolis looming overhead.",al={"runic circles outside undercity","glowing circle scourge","scourge runes"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the Scourge attacking outside the Undercity?",a="The Lich King seeks to eradicate the renegade Forsaken and conquer the ruins of Lordaeron, deploying necropolises and ground troops to besiege the capital directly.",al={"why is scourge at undercity","scourge invasion undercity","undercity under attack"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does this matter to the Forsaken?",a="The Forsaken fought tirelessly to break free of the Lich King's iron will. The Scourge landing at their very threshold threatens the freedom and sovereignty of their fledgling nation.",al={"forsaken scourge threat","undead defending undercity"},it="conflict"},{q="Can non-Forsaken Horde members take this mission?",a="Yes. All members of the Horde are summoned to aid in Lordaeron's defense, as a threat to the Undercity threatens the security of the entire coalition.",al={"can orcs do this quest","horde defense undercity"},gp=true},{q="Why does Lieutenant Rukag want this done?",a="Lieutenant Rukag sees the Scourge brazenly encamped right outside the gates of the Undercity as an intolerable insult and an immediate peril. Leaving mindless thralls and dark necropolises sitting upon the threshold risks a full breach into the Forsaken capital. He wants their ranks culled swiftly and their strange ritual runes unraveled before they can launch a coordinated assault.",al={"rukag motive","why does rukag care","rukag scourge quest why"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you being sent against outside the Undercity?",a="You are sent to confront the encroaching Scourge invaders gathering on the surface ruins of Lordaeron above the Undercity. Beneath floating necropolises, these mindless undead aberrations and necromantic agents are setting up camps and glowing runic circles, probing the Forsaken defenses and threatening to overrun the entryway to the catacombs below.",al={"what scourge are outside undercity","target of investigate the scourge","what are we fighting"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Scourge represents your former master and perpetual enslaver; repelling them from Lordaeron's soil is a matter of pure survival and vengeance.",["faction:Horde"]="Honor demands coming to the defense of the Forsaken, securing the Horde's vital foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms against the Scourge."},kw={"dim necrotic stone","lordaeron","necropolis","rukag","runic circle","scourge","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:scourge"},m={start="Lieutenant Rukag",level="8",faction="Horde",id=9265,ri={"Dim Necrotic Stone"}},src={"Investigate the Scourge of the Undercity"}}
E["subzone:apothecarium"] = {t="subzone",n="Apothecarium",z="undercity",s="The Apothecarium is the southwestern quarter of the Undercity and the headquarters of the Royal Apothecary Society. Within these noxious laboratories, Forsaken alchemists labor tirelessly under Master Apothecary Faranell to concoct virulent plagues, toxins, and engineered horrors. It stands as the grim heart of Undercity's biological research, vital to Lady Sylvanas's campaign against the living and the Scourge.",h="The Apothecarium is the southwestern quarter of the Undercity and the headquarters of the Royal Apothecary...",sec={{t="Chamber of Horrors",b="Occupying the southwestern terrace of the subterranean capital, the Apothecarium is a labyrinth of bubbling vats, dissection tables, and pungent chemical fumes. Led by Master Apothecary Faranell, the Royal Apothecary Society utilizes this district to advance their understanding of mortality and rot. Here, alchemists and surgeons experiment on tissue grafts, vivisection, and the assembly of mighty abominations. Their overriding purpose, mandated by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, is the formulation of a new plague capable of eradicating both the Scourge and the lingering human presence across Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Center of Forsaken Alchemy",b="Beyond grand military ambitions, the quarter serves as the premier center of practical alchemy and herbalism for the Horde in the Eastern Kingdoms. Initiates and masters alike gather beside toxic canals to distill concoctions, study botanical blights, and consult master practitioners.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Apothecarium used for?",a="The Apothecarium serves as the research and manufacturing wing for the Royal Apothecary Society. It is where Forsaken alchemists brew experimental poisons, refine the New Plague, construct abominations, and instruct practitioners in alchemy and herbalism.",al={"apothecarium purpose","what happens here","why does the apothecarium exist"},it="purpose"},{q="Who leads the Apothecarium?",a="The district and its researchers are led by Master Apothecary Faranell, the chief scientist of the Royal Apothecary Society, operating with the full authority and patronage of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"apothecarium leader","who runs the apothecarium","faranell undercity"},it="leader"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society trying to create?",a="Their primary endeavor is cultivating a lethal New Plague engineered to annihilate both the Scourge forces of the Lich King and any living human resistance contesting Forsaken territory in Lordaeron.",al={"forsaken plague research","new plague undercity","what are they brewing"},it="wants"},{q="Can players learn professions here?",a="Yes. The district is the capital's main hub for alchemists and herbalists, hosting advanced profession trainers along its walkways and chambers.",al={"apothecarium trainers","alchemy in undercity","undercity herbalism trainer"},gp=true},{q="What is the Apothecarium?",a="The Apothecarium is the southwestern quarter of the Undercity, serving as the grim headquarters and laboratory complex of the Royal Apothecary Society. Deep within its cavernous chambers, Forsaken alchemists and researchers brew noxious concoctions, engineer powerful abominations, and conduct grisly experiments to advance the Forsaken cause.",al={"what is the apothecarium","apothecarium undercity","undercity apothecarium"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Apothecarium dangerous?",a="It is safe enough for Horde travelers, but outsiders find it a chamber of horrors. The air is foul with toxic vapors, open vats churn with corrosive chemicals and blighted reagents, and shambling abominations roam its halls. Any living trespasser foolish enough to wander in risks ending up strapped to an apothecary's dissecting table.",al={"is apothecarium safe","apothecarium hazards","danger in apothecarium"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Apothecarium is the forge of their survival, producing the chemical and stitched weapons essential to holding Lordaeron against overwhelming enemies.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Botanists supply the foul distillers of the Royal Apothecary Society with rare, blighted flora gathered from the ruins of the northern kingdoms."},kw={"abominations","alchemy","apothecarium","faranell","new plague","royal apothecary society","sylvanas","undercity"},rel={"topic:royal-apothecary-society","npc:master-apothecary-faranell","zone:undercity","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","quest:447","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron","quest:445"},src={"Apothecarium"}}
E["subzone:canals-undercity"] = {t="subzone",n="Canals (Undercity)",z="undercity",s="The Canals form a murky, circular moat winding between the distinct quarters of the Undercity. Filled with an unnatural, noxious green slime rather than fresh water, they serve as both a sewage system and a grim symbol of the Forsaken's subterranean stronghold.",h="The Canals form a murky, circular moat winding between the distinct quarters of the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Toxic Moat",b="Carved into the subterranean depths beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, the Canals encircle the heart of the Undercity, dividing its quarters with wide channels of sluggish green sludge. While mortal cities channel flowing river water to clean their avenues, the Forsaken have filled these stone conduits with industrial refuse, chemical runoff, and alchemical waste. The liquid emits a faint, sickly glow and foul vapors, making it impossible to traverse by ordinary magical means like water walking. Despite the lethality of the slurry, desperate anglers occasionally haul bizarre, tainted curiosities from the muck.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the green liquid in the canals?",a="It is an alchemical sludge composed of toxic runoff, plague byproducts, and industrial waste that collects within the Undercity's drainage system. Unlike clean water, it is visibly tainted and noxious.",al={"undercity green water","what is the slime in undercity","green slime river"}},{q="Can you fish in the Undercity canals?",a="Yes, patient anglers can cast a line into the sludge. Along with sickly, contaminated fish, people occasionally haul up discarded junk, including old human skulls from Lordaeron's fallen past.",al={"fishing undercity","can you fish here","fishing in green slime"},gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Water Walking work on the canals?",a="The thick, chemical slurry does not behave like natural water. Its foul viscosity and unnatural composition prevent shamans and other spellcasters from holding surface tension through conventional water-walking magic.",al={"water walking undercity","shaman water walking bug","why cant i walk on water undercity"},gp=true},{q="What are the Canals in the Undercity?",a="The Canals are the sunken waterways that wind between the Undercity's distinct quarters. Flowing in a broad circular loop throughout the subterranean city, these deep stone channels carry a sluggish river of foul green sludge, dividing the districts while tying the cavernous lower city together.",al={"undercity canals","what are the canals","undercity canal system"},it="place",add=true},{q="Are the Canals dangerous?",a="While the canals pose little immediate physical threat from lurking predators, their murky green depths are far from pristine. The viscous sludge is foul enough to harbor discarded bones, human skulls, and sickly, mutated aquatic life, making an accidental plunge thoroughly unpleasant.",al={"canals danger","is it safe to swim in undercity canals","are undercity canals safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the foul canals are entirely harmless to their unliving physiology, serving as a functional moat and chemical runoff channel suited to their subterranean realm.",["class:Shaman"]="The elements hold little sway over the polluted muck filling the Undercity's waterways, causing conventional spells like Water Walking to fail entirely."},kw={"canals","fishing","forsaken","green slime","lordaeron","sludge","toxic","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken","subzone:canals-stormwind-city"},src={"Canals (Undercity)"}}
E["subzone:magic-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="Magic Quarter",z="undercity",s="The Magic Quarter is the northeastern district of the Undercity, serving as the center for Forsaken arcane study and dark spellcraft. Dominated by an ominous Temple of the Damned, the quarter houses practitioners of both the arcane and fel arts.",h="The Magic Quarter is the northeastern district of the Undercity, serving as the center for Forsaken arcane...",sec={{t="A Conclave of Dark Arts",b="Occupying the northeastern quadrant of the subterranean city, the Magic Quarter is where the Forsaken preserve their arcane heritage and delve into darker methodologies. The centerpiece of the district is a looming Temple of the Damned, an architectural relic of Scourge design that has been repurposed by the free-willed undead. Beneath its vaulted, shadowy ceilings, mages practice subtle manipulations of magical energies alongside warlocks communing with demonic entities, making the quarter the nexus of intellectual power and occult research in Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Scholars, Weavers, and Summoners",b="Beyond the study of raw evocation and summoning, the Magic Quarter functions as an essential civic hub for spellcasters. Portal trainers maintain transport links across Horde territories, while master tailors work with magically infused fabrics to craft robes, shrouds, and spellthread. Unlike Dalaran's strict segregation between academic wizardry and forbidden magic, the Forsaken blend arcane curiosity and fel power openly within these halls to secure their place against their many enemies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Magic Quarter?",a="The Magic Quarter serves as the center of arcane and demonic studies for the Forsaken. It houses class trainers for mages and warlocks, portal masters connecting to other cities, and tailoring professionals who weave enchanted cloth.",al={"what is magic quarter","magic quarter purpose","undercity magic district"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is there a Temple of the Damned in the Undercity?",a="When the Undercity was carved out beneath the ruins of Capital City by the Scourge, they erected structures like the Temple of the Damned. When Sylvanas and her free-willed Forsaken seized the subterranean complex, they claimed these existing facilities and repurposed them for their own spellcasters.",al={"temple of the damned undercity","why temple of the damned here","scourge building undercity"}},{q="Who can be trained in the Magic Quarter?",a="Mages, warlocks, and demon trainers instruct practitioners within the quarter, while portal specialists and tailoring artisans offer training in transport and craft.",al={"trainers in magic quarter","who trains here","magic quarter classes"},gp=true},{q="Where is the Magic Quarter located?",a="It is situated in the northeastern quadrant of the Undercity, directly across the central ring from the Rogue and Apothecary quarters.",al={"where is magic quarter","magic quarter location","find magic quarter"},gp=true},{q="What is the Magic Quarter?",a="The Magic Quarter is the northeastern district of the Undercity, serving as the heart of the Forsaken's arcane and occult research. Towering over the quadrant sits an ominous Temple of the Damned, repurposed from Scourge architecture to serve the dark spellcasters, scholars, and weavers who pledge their craft to the Banshee Queen.",al={"what is magic quarter","magic quarter undercity","undercity magic quarter"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Magic Quarter?",a="The district takes its name directly from its primary function within the Undercity: it is the realm of Forsaken spellcraft. Here, practitioners of the arcane, summoners of demonic power, and weavers of enchanted cloth gather to hone their dark arts and conduct arcane experiments in service of Lady Sylvanas.",al={"why is it called magic quarter","magic quarter name origin","magic quarter name meaning"},it="name",add=true},{q="Is the Magic Quarter dangerous?",a="For loyal subjects of the Forsaken and their Horde allies, the Magic Quarter is secure. However, it is thick with volatile arcane energies, summoned fel entities, and grim rituals. Reckless outsiders or enemies of the Dark Lady who trespass beneath the Temple of the Damned will quickly find themselves overwhelmed by its resident warlocks and mages.",al={"is magic quarter dangerous","magic quarter danger","is undercity magic quarter safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The Magic Quarter is the heart of Forsaken wizardry, offering training in arcane arts and teleportation networks that link the Undercity with the wider Horde.",["class:Warlock"]="Within the dark alcoves of the Temple of the Damned, warlocks summon demonic minions and hone shadow magic far from the judgmental eyes of the Alliance."},kw={"forsaken","mage","magic quarter","portal trainer","tailoring","temple of the damned","undercity","warlock"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"Magic Quarter"}}
E["subzone:rogues-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="Rogues' Quarter",z="undercity",s="The Rogues' Quarter is a dimly lit district in the southeastern wing of the Undercity. It serves as the staging ground for the Forsaken's scouts, assassins, and underworld operatives, along with the craftsmen who support them.",h="The Rogues' Quarter is a dimly lit district in the southeastern wing of the Undercity.",sec={{t="Shadows of the Undercity",b="Tucked away in the southeastern quadrant of the subterranean city, the Rogues' Quarter gathers the Forsaken's most cunning and lethal survivors. In life, many were thieves, cutpurses, or silent blades for the Kingdom of Lordaeron; in death, their expertise in stealth, poisons, and misdirection has been repurposed to protect the fledgling nation from the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade. The district hums with quiet activity, offering a covert haven where operatives sharpen their daggers, brew deadly toxins, and hone clandestine skills.",sp=0},{t="Tools of the Trade",b="Beyond stealth and assassination, the Rogues' Quarter is home to the specialized trades that enable undercover survival. Artisans gather here to instruct travelers in leatherworking and skinning, turning raw hides into light, silent armor. The clatter of engineering benches echoes through the stone halls as tinkers assemble gadgets, while field medics and apothecaries provide instruction in first aid and vend lethal poisons essential for covert work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Rogues' Quarter located?",a="The Rogues' Quarter is situated in the southeastern section of the Undercity's outer ring, past the Trade Quarter.",al={"rogues quarter location","where is rogues quarter","undercity rogues quarter map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What trainers can be found here?",a="The quarter houses trainers for rogues, as well as instructors for leatherworking, skinning, engineering, and first aid. Poison vendors are also stationed nearby to supply reagents.",al={"rogues quarter trainers","undercity rogue trainer","who trains in rogues quarter"},it="residents",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken maintain a dedicated district for rogues?",a="Surrounded by hostile forces like the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade, the Forsaken rely heavily on espionage, assassination, and hit-and-run tactics to defend their territory, making covert operatives vital to their survival.",al={"why do forsaken need rogues","forsaken assassins","undercity rogue lore"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Rogues' Quarter?",a="The Rogues' Quarter is the southeastern district of the Undercity, carved into the subterranean ruins beneath Lordaeron. It serves as the domain for the Forsaken's rogues' guild and their network of shadowy operatives. Beyond espionage and stealth, the quarter hosts specialized craftsmen, poisoners, leatherworkers, skinners, and engineers who support the clandestine efforts of the Forsaken.",al={"what is rogues quarter","rogues quarter undercity","about rogues quarter"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Rogues' Quarter dangerous?",a="If you walk here as an ally of the Forsaken and the Horde, the Rogues' Quarter poses no outward physical threat. However, it is populated by assassins, thieves, and covert agents who thrive on deception and secrecy. Lingering too long or prying into the business of the guild's poisoners and spies is never wise, as the district's residents are trained to eliminate threats without leaving a trace.",al={"is rogues quarter safe","danger rogues quarter","rogues quarter hostiles"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Rogues' Quarter?",a="The district takes its name from the rogues' guild that established its base within these dim halls. It gathers the Forsaken's scouts, infiltrators, and cutthroats under one roof, housing the instructors, poison vendors, and craftsmen who supply their lethal craft.",al={"why is it called rogues quarter","rogues quarter name origin","name rogues quarter"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="For Forsaken and Horde assassins, this quarter is the premier hub for mastering stealth, learning combat techniques, and stocking up on lethal poison reagents.",["profession:Engineering"]="Tinkers visit the Rogues' Quarter to learn schematics and craft bombs, gadgets, and mechanical tools favored by undercover agents."},kw={"engineering","forsaken","leatherworking","poison vendor","rogue trainer","rogues quarter","rogues' quarter","skinning","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"Rogues' Quarter"}}
E["subzone:royal-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="Royal Quarter",z="undercity",s="The Royal Quarter is the secluded seat of power within the Undercity, serving as the throne room for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Here, the Banshee Queen directs the Forsaken alongside her dreadlord enforcer, Varimathras, guarded by an elite cohort of Royal Dreadguards.",h="The Royal Quarter is the secluded seat of power within the Undercity, serving as the throne room for Lady...",sec={{t="The Seat of the Dark Lady",b="Tucked away behind towering archways and shadowed corridors, the Royal Quarter—also known as the Hall of the Dark Lady—is the political and military nerve center of the Forsaken. Sylvanas Windrunner holds court in this cavernous subterranean chamber, plotting the survival of her free-willed undead and the destruction of the Scourge. Heavily armored Royal Dreadguards stand vigil along the dais, ensuring that uninvited guests and would-be assassins never reach their queen.",sp=0},{t="A Dangerous Alliance",b="Standing beside the Dark Lady is the nathrezim Varimathras, an unexpected and uneasy fixture in the heart of the Undercity. After siding with Sylvanas during the civil war in the ruins of Lordaeron to save his own life, the dreadlord pledged loyalty to her cause. From the Royal Quarter, he commands deathstalkers and coordinates defensive operations across the realm. While his tactical cunning serves the Forsaken well, his demonic nature leaves many Horde allies wary of his true allegiances.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules from the Royal Quarter?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen, rules the Forsaken from the throne within the Royal Quarter. She is flanked by the nathrezim Varimathras, who pledged allegiance to her after the liberation of Lordaeron.",al={"who is in the royal quarter","undercity throne room leader","who leads undercity"},it="residents"},{q="Why is there a dreadlord standing in the throne room?",a="Varimathras surrendered to Sylvanas Windrunner during the reconquest of Capital City after betraying his brothers Detheroc and Balnazzar. He spared his own life by swearing loyalty to Sylvanas, and now acts as her enforcer and master of scouts.",al={"why is varimathras here","dreadlord in undercity","why is demon in royal quarter"}},{q="What are the Royal Dreadguards?",a="The Royal Dreadguards are elite Forsaken protectors chosen specifically to guard Lady Sylvanas and the Royal Quarter. They are among the most disciplined and lethal defenders in the Undercity.",al={"dreadguards","undercity throne room guards","royal quarter guards"}},{q="What other function does this chamber serve?",a="Beyond serving as the primary audience chamber for the Dark Lady and Varimathras, the Royal Quarter houses battlemasters who coordinate Horde combatants for foreign campaigns and strategic skirmishes across Azeroth.",al={"what else is in royal quarter","royal quarter purpose","battlemasters royal quarter"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Royal Quarter?",a="The Royal Quarter, also known as the Hall of the Dark Lady, is the grand seat of power within the Undercity. Found deep beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, this cavernous throne room serves as the command center where Lady Sylvanas Windrunner guides the Forsaken, surrounded by her most trusted protectors and advisors.",al={"what is royal quarter","royal quarter undercity","hall of the dark lady"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Royal Quarter dangerous?",a="For champions of the Horde, the chamber is a secure sanctuary, heavily defended by towering Royal Dreadguards. However, any trespassing Alliance intruders will find it exceptionally deadly, as both the Banshee Queen herself and the Nathrezim Varimathras stand ready to obliterate any who dare threaten the heart of the Forsaken realm.",al={"is royal quarter safe","danger in royal quarter","royal quarter hostile"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Royal Quarter?",a="The district takes its name from its role as the seat of royalty and supreme command in the subterranean capital. Here, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner rules her kingdom as the sovereign of the free undead, styling the chamber as her personal royal court.",al={"why is it called royal quarter","royal quarter name meaning","why royal quarter"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Royal Quarter represents the heart of Forsaken independence, where Sylvanas Windrunner and her dreadlord lieutenant chart the future of their liberated people.",["faction:Horde"]="Visiting Horde envoys to the Royal Quarter often view the Dark Lady's nathrezim councilor with intense suspicion, questioning the wisdom of trusting a demon in the heart of a Horde capital."},kw={"banshee queen","hall of the dark lady","royal dreadguard","royal quarter","sylvanas windrunner","throne room","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"zone:undercity","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","npc:varimathras","quest:1886","topic:horde","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Royal Quarter"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-lordaeron"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Lordaeron",z="undercity",s="The Ruins of Lordaeron are the hollowed-out surface remnants of Capital City, the once-glorious heart of humanity's northern empire. Destroyed when Prince Arthas murdered his father and unleashed the Scourge, the blasted courtyards and throne room now serve as the fortified gateway to the Undercity below.",h="The Ruins of Lordaeron are the hollowed-out surface remnants of Capital City, the once-glorious heart of...",sec={{t="A Fallen Empire's Gateway",b="Capital City was once the radiant summit of human civilization, uniting the northern realms under King Terenas Menethil II. When Prince Arthas returned from Northrend carrying the cursed runeblade Frostmourne, the celebrations turned into a slaughterhouse. Arthas slew his father on the throne, leaving the metropolis to rot under Scourge rule. Following the civil war that tore the Scourge apart, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner claimed the devastated palace, securing the surface while expanding the crypts and dungeons beneath into the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of Betrayal",b="The palace ruins remain psychically scarred by their violent fall. Travelers walking through the entryway and courtyards often hear the ghostly chime of celebration bells, hushed murmurs of adoring crowds, and the chilling dialogue between Arthas and his father just before the regicide. Blood still stains the floor of the grand throne room, and those possessing magical detection can glimpse spectral citizens eternally reliving the afternoon their prince doomed them all.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do I hear bells and whispers when walking through the entrance?",a="The sudden slaughter of King Terenas and his city left a psychic imprint on the stone. Anyone passing through the outer gate and the shattered throne room can hear phantom bells, spectral cheers, and the final conversation between Terenas and Arthas echoed across time.",al={"creepy sounds lordaeron","throne room whispers","haunted castle sounds"}},{q="Who rules the ruins today?",a="The surface ruins are held and patrolled by the Forsaken under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. While Sylvanas and her court reside directly below in the Undercity, the ruins above serve as the grand fortified entrance to her subterranean realm.",al={"who owns lordaeron ruins","who controls ruins of lordaeron"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happened to the people who used to live here?",a="Most of the inhabitants were slaughtered when Arthas unleashed the Scourge upon the city. Many were raised into mindless undead and later broke free to join Sylvanas as the Forsaken, while the unseen spirits of others still drift through the palace courtyards.",al={"where did lordaeron people go","what happened to capital city humans"},it="people"},{q="What is the dark stain in the throne room?",a="The dark, dried residue marking the royal dais is the blood of King Terenas Menethil II, spilled by his own son Arthas when the prince drove Frostmourne through his heart.",al={"blood on throne room floor","stain in lordaeron throne room"},it="history"},{q="What is the Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="These shattered ramparts and grand halls are all that remain of Capital City, the magnificent seat of the fallen human kingdom of Lordaeron. Once the heart of the Alliance during the Second War, the city collapsed when Prince Arthas Menethil betrayed his realm and unleashed the Scourge. Today, the surface palace sits crumbling and haunted, serving as the gateway to the sprawling Forsaken subterranean metropolis known as the Undercity.",al={"what are the ruins of lordaeron","ruins of lordaeron overview","capital city ruins lore"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is Lordaeron in ruins?",a="Lordaeron fell to treachery from within. Crown Prince Arthas Menethil, corrupted by the cursed blade Frostmourne, returned from Northrend under the banner of the Lich King. After slaying his father, King Terenas, Arthas and his undead Scourge slaughtered the populace and shattered the city's defenses. Subsequent clashes involving dreadlords, surviving Alliance resistance forces, and Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken completed the ruin of the surface city.",al={"why is lordaeron destroyed","how was lordaeron destroyed","why is lordaeron ruined"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is the Ruins of Lordaeron dangerous?",a="For champions of the Horde, the surface ruins are secure, as Forsaken guards patrol the courtyards and passages leading into the Undercity. However, Alliance travelers will find it fiercely hostile territory crawling with Forsaken sentries. The area is also spiritually unsettled, echoing with tragic phantom whispers and invisible ghosts of slaughtered citizens, while vile Scourge and beasts prowl the surrounding Tirisfal countryside.",al={"ruins of lordaeron danger","is ruins of lordaeron safe","are ruins of lordaeron hostile"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="The site was originally Capital City, the majestic center of the Kingdom of Lordaeron. Following the utter annihilation of the realm and the slaughter of its people by the Scourge, only the cracked marble walls, shattered throne room, and crumbling courtyards remain. It is named to mark the fallen majesty and tragic devastation of humanity's greatest northern kingdom.",al={"ruins of lordaeron name origin","why ruins of lordaeron","where does ruins of lordaeron get its name"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="These ruined ramparts are your ancestral home. What was once the seat of the living kingdom that birthed you is now the hallowed doorway guarding the Undercity and the Banshee Queen.",["race:Human"]="Standing within these halls is a bitter reminder of the greatest betrayal in human history, where Prince Arthas shattered the Alliance of Lordaeron and left humanity's jewel in the hands of the dead."},kw={"arthas","capital city","haunted","lordaeron","palace","scourge","sylvanas","terenas","throne room","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:lordaeron","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:forsaken","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand"},src={"Ruins of Lordaeron"}}
E["subzone:sewers"] = {t="subzone",n="Sewers",z="undercity",s="The Sewers are a sprawling subterranean drainage network that provides a secondary, unguarded entrance directly into the Undercity. Cutting beneath the hills west of the ruined palace of Lordaeron, this conduit allows bat handlers and stealthy travelers to bypass the precarious elevators leading down from the throne room.",h="The Sewers are a sprawling subterranean drainage network that provides a secondary, unguarded entrance...",sec={{t="A Backdoor into the Catacombs",b="Before the plague wiped out Lordaeron, these stone culverts served as the mundane sewer lines draining the royal capital. In the hands of Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken, however, the runoff tunnels have been integrated into the Undercity's outer defenses. Emerging west of the surface ruins near a contested Scarlet Watchtower in Tirisfal Glades, the passage provides a level, direct slope inside. Forsaken bat handlers use this cavernous conduit to fly riders swiftly into the subterranean rings, avoiding the sluggish cage lifts entirely. Because it circumvents the heavily fortified surface courtyards, it remains a dangerous vulnerability that hostile infiltrators constantly seek to exploit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the sewer tunnel lead outside?",a="The conduit empties onto the rolling hills of Tirisfal Glades, just west of the main gates of the Ruins of Lordaeron. It is situated not far from the Scarlet Watchtower overlooking the lake.",al={"undercity sewer exit","where do sewers go","sewer back entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why would anyone use the sewers instead of the main entrance?",a="The primary way into the Undercity requires riding iron cage elevators down from the palace ruins, which can be slow and dangerous during an attack. The sewer is a direct, ramped route that handles the Forsaken bat transit and permits quick egress without waiting on lifts.",al={"why use sewers","sewers vs elevators","undercity backdoor"},it="purpose"},{q="Is the sewer safe from Alliance raiders?",a="Hardly. Because it bypasses the fortified gatehouse and throne room of Lordaeron, the sewer is the preferred breach point for daring Alliance scouts and strike teams attempting to sneak directly into the Forsaken capital.",al={"alliance attack sewers","is sewer guarded","undercity sewer defense"},it="danger"},{q="What are the Sewers of the Undercity?",a="The Sewers serve as a sprawling drainage system beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron that empties out into Tirisfal Glades, just west of the palace gates. Rather than relying on the precarious palace elevators, many Forsaken travelers and bat handlers utilize these foul tunnels as an alternate conduit directly into the subterranean heart of the Undercity.",al={"what are the sewers","undercity sewers","sewers undercity"},it="place",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the sewers are an essential lifeline and flight corridor that keeps the Undercity connected to the rest of Lordaeron without bottling up traffic in the courtyard elevators.",["faction:Alliance"]="Anyone foolish or brave enough to assault the Forsaken capital knows the sewers provide the only covert path past the heavily defended surface ruins."},kw={"backdoor","bat handler","drainage","flight path","lordaeron","sewers","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","zone:tirisfal","subzone:scarlet-watchtower","topic:lordaeron","topic:alliance"},src={"Sewers"}}
E["subzone:trade-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="Trade Quarter",z="undercity",s="The Trade Quarter forms the central core of the Undercity, resting directly beneath the lifts from the Ruins of Lordaeron. It functions as the beating economic heart of the Forsaken, housing their primary bank vaults, auction market, and essential civic services. From this concentric hub, vaulted corridors branch outward into the surrounding districts.",h="The Trade Quarter forms the central core of the Undercity, resting directly beneath the lifts from the Ruins...",sec={{t="Heart of the Crypts",b="Descending from the shattered surface of Lordaeron, travelers step off the lifts into the echoing stone expanse of the Trade Quarter. Designed around a tiered, circular layout, its central platform holds the city coffers and central bank, framed by bridges spanning noxious runoff canals. Surrounding terraces buzz with vendors, guild registries, and auctioneers bargaining amidst the eerie gloom. Even basic accommodations reflect Forsaken pragmatism: the local inn offers unlined wooden caskets rather than soft beds. From this central nexus, stone archways lead outward into the city's specialized quarters, making it the unavoidable crossroads for any business conducted within the capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Trade Quarter located?",a="The Trade Quarter occupies the dead center of the Undercity. When entering the capital via the surface elevators beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron, you step out immediately onto the upper ring of the district.",al={"trade quarter location","how to find trade quarter","where is trade quarter"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services are found in the Trade Quarter?",a="The district hosts the central Undercity bank, an auction house along the outer ring, the primary inn, a bat handler for air travel, guild registrars, and various trade trainers including the city's cooking mentor.",al={"trade quarter services","what is in trade quarter","undercity bank location"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why are there coffins in the inn?",a="Forsaken physiology requires no true sleep, and many retain habits suited to their undead condition. The inn provides plain, unlined wooden caskets rather than traditional bedding—a matter of routine comfort for the dead, though deeply unsettling for living visitors.",al={"undercity inn coffins","why caskets in inn","undercity beds"}},{q="Who is the vendor lurking beneath the bridges?",a="Jeremiah Payson makes his living under one of the central bridges crossing into the bank. While standard merchants peddle weaponry and trade goods up above, Payson sells live pet cockroaches to curious passersby.",al={"jeremiah payson","cockroach guy undercity","who sells cockroaches"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Trade Quarter?",a="The Trade Quarter serves as the central hub and beating heart of the Undercity. Positioned immediately beyond the elevators descending from the ruins of Capital City above, this tiered circular chamber connects directly to all other quarters via winding canals. It functions as the realm's bustling center of commerce, housing the grand bank vault, general vendors, guild services, and the city's primary gathering spaces.",al={"what is the trade quarter","trade quarter undercity","undercity center"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to create the Trade Quarter?",a="Originally carved beneath the royal palace and capital of Lordaeron, these subterranean halls once held dungeons, crypts, and sewers. Following the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge and Prince Arthas, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner led the Forsaken in reclaiming the territory. They expanded and refashioned the central subterranean chambers into a fortified city center to conduct trade and govern their new sovereign realm.",al={"trade quarter history","how was trade quarter made","history of trade quarter"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is the Trade Quarter dangerous?",a="For members of the Horde and allies of the Dark Lady, the Trade Quarter is one of the safest places in the realm, heavily guarded by towering Abominations and royal sentries. However, it is utterly lethal to members of the Alliance or uninvited trespassers, who will be slain on sight the moment they descend from the ruins above.",al={"is trade quarter safe","is trade quarter dangerous","threats trade quarter"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Trade Quarter?",a="It earns its name as the foremost commercial district of the Forsaken capital. The central vault houses the city coffer and bank, while surrounding rings and tiers host merchant stalls, auctioneers, craft suppliers, and guild liaisons, facilitating all major business transactions throughout the kingdom.",al={"why is it called trade quarter","trade quarter name","why trade quarter"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Trade Quarter represents the swift reclamation of civilized order by the Forsaken, turning subterranean dungeons into a thriving market dedicated to funding their survival.",["faction:Horde"]="For Orc, Tauren, or Troll emissaries arriving in Tirisfal Glades, the Trade Quarter serves as the foreign, shadowy market center of their northern allies."},kw={"auction house","bank","bat handler","caskets","inn","jeremiah payson","trade quarter","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron","topic:horde"},src={"Trade Quarter"}}
E["subzone:war-quarter"] = {t="subzone",n="War Quarter",z="undercity",s="The War Quarter is the northwestern district of the Undercity, serving as the command post and martial training ground for the Forsaken. Within its echoing stone chambers, the soldiers, priests, and crafters of Lordaeron hone their weapons and shadow magic in defense of their fledgling kingdom. It houses training halls for warriors and priests alongside weapon masters and heavy industry.",h="The War Quarter is the northwestern district of the Undercity, serving as the command post and martial...",sec={{t="The Forsaken Garrison",b="Occupying the northwest sector of the subterranean metropolis, the War Quarter stands as the bastion of martial strength for the Forsaken. Beneath its gloomy stone arches, rank-and-file guards and elite champions assemble to drill in armed combat. Unlike traditional barracks of living kingdoms, this military center combines ruthless iron warfare with the chilling rites of shadow, housing an ominous Altar of Darkness where spiritual discipline merges with military ambition.",sp=0},{t="Forge and Steel",b="Beyond housing warrior and priest guilds, the quarter functions as the heart of Undercity's wartime production. The clatter of blades and armor echoes continually against the stone, supported by the district's blacksmiths, smelters, and weapon masters. Here, iron forged deep in the earth is shaped to outfit the forces defending the ruins of Lordaeron from the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the War Quarter?",a="The War Quarter serves as the military headquarters of the Undercity. It hosts martial training grounds for warriors and priests, along with vital crafting centers for blacksmithing and mining to keep the Forsaken army armed and armored.",al={"what is war quarter","war quarter purpose","why visit war quarter"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are priests located in the War Quarter?",a="Forsaken priests largely focus on the discipline of the Shadow, using it as a potent weapon alongside their warriors rather than maintaining pastoral sanctuaries. Their presence near the martial forces and the Altar of Darkness reflects how deeply intertwined faith and warfare are in the defense of the Forsaken.",al={"undead priest location","why are priests in war quarter","priest trainers undercity"},it="people"},{q="What is the Altar of Darkness?",a="The Altar of Darkness is a focal point of dark spiritual power located within the War Quarter. It is tied to the Forsaken's dark rites and training, anchoring the shadowy magic wielded by their priests and champions.",al={"altar of darkness undercity","altar in war quarter"},it="place"},{q="Where is the War Quarter located in the Undercity?",a="The War Quarter occupies the northwest quadrant of the Undercity's circular layout, situated between the Rogues' Quarter to the west and the Trade Quarter towards the center.",al={"where is war quarter","war quarter location","war quarter directions"},gp=true},{q="What is the War Quarter?",a="The War Quarter is the northwestern district of the Undercity, serving as the primary bastion and training ground for the Forsaken military. Deep beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, its cavernous halls ring with the clash of steel and dark chants, housing warrior barracks, martial instructors, hunter lodges, and the practitioners of the Cult of Forgotten Shadow.",al={"what is war quarter","war quarter undercity","undercity war quarter"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called the War Quarter?",a="It earned its name by serving as the martial heart of Lady Sylvanas's domain. Here, the Forsaken organize their standing army, drill soldiers, sharpen blades, and prepare the tactics necessary to wage war against the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and any other threats to their sovereignty.",al={"why called war quarter","war quarter name","why war quarter"},it="name",add=true},{q="Is the War Quarter dangerous?",a="For champions of the Horde, the district is safe and heavily guarded by elite Forsaken forces and Deathguard sentries. To outsiders, the Alliance, or agents of the Scourge, however, stepping into the War Quarter means facing an armed garrison ready to strike down intruders without hesitation.",al={"is war quarter dangerous","danger war quarter","is the war quarter safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="The War Quarter is your primary haven in the Undercity, offering weapon masters, advanced combat instructors, and heavy armories to prepare you for the brutal frontline battles of Lordaeron.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Housing both training masters and high-heat anvils, the War Quarter is the central hub for smiths hammering out munitions and plate for the Forsaken war effort."},kw={"altar of darkness","barracks","blacksmithing","forsaken","priest trainer","undercity","war quarter","warrior trainer"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:forsaken"},src={"War Quarter"}}
E["zone:undercity"] = {t="city",n="Undercity",z="undercity",s="Deep beneath the shattered ruins of Lordaeron's Capital City lies the Undercity, the dark stronghold of the Forsaken. Originally carved out of ancient royal crypts and dungeons by the Scourge, it was seized by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and remade into an impenetrable subterranean sanctuary. Today it serves as the seat of Forsaken power and the Horde's vital bastion in the northern Eastern Kingdoms.",h="Deep beneath the shattered ruins of Lordaeron's Capital City lies the Undercity, the dark stronghold of the...",sec={{t="From Royal Crypts to Scourge Redoubt",b="Long before the plague swept Lordaeron, the catacombs, dungeons, and sewers beneath the palace were collectively known as the Undercity. It held the tombs of nobility, the kingdom's deepest prisons—where the former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer was once held before his escape—and the poorest denizens of the realm. When Arthas Menethil murdered King Terenas and laid waste to the capital in 20 ADP, the prince ordered his undead servants to excavate and expand the subterranean passages into a fortified seat of Scourge rule.",sp=0},{t="Rise of the Forsaken",b="The Scourge never saw their dark capital completed. When the Lich King's powers waned following the battle of Mount Hyjal, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner broke free from the hive mind, taking thousands of undead with her. She lured Arthas into an ambush and drove him back to Northrend. After a vicious three-way civil war against Scourge remnants, dreadlords, and human resistance, Sylvanas claimed the half-finished catacombs. Naming her people the Forsaken, she oversaw years of labor completing the sprawling subterranean city.",sp=0},{t="Architecture of the Damned",b="The Undercity is laid out in concentric rings divided into functional quarters. At its heart lies the Trade Quarter, connected by great lifts to the palace ruins above. Surrounding it are the War Quarter, Rogues' Quarter, Magic Quarter, and the toxic Apothecarium, where the Royal Apothecary Society brews virulent plagues in green slime-filled canals. Deeper still lies the Royal Quarter, where the Banshee Queen holds court alongside her dreadlord commander, Varimathras, guarded by legions of towering abominations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Undercity before the undead took it over?",a="Beneath the palace of Lordaeron lay the ancient crypts of human royalty, along with the city's dungeon complex and vast sewer network. It housed prisoners of war, including Orgrim Doomhammer, as well as destitute citizens living in the subterranean shadows. After sacking the capital, Prince Arthas began turning these catacombs into a Scourge fortress before Sylvanas captured them.",al={"undercity origins","what was undercity originally","lordaeron sewers history"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the city built underground instead of on the surface?",a="The surface city of Lordaeron was utterly ruined during the Third War, making it difficult to defend against the Scarlet Crusade, Scourge forces, and Alliance survivors. The subterranean tunnels offered natural fortification, choke points, and secrecy, allowing the Forsaken to complete the Scourge's initial construction and thrive unseen.",al={"why live underground","why not rebuild lordaeron","why undercity beneath ruins"},it="why_here"},{q="Who rules the Undercity?",a="The city is ruled by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen and Queen of the Forsaken. She governs from the Royal Quarter, guarded by Forsaken royal sentries and her subjugated dreadlord lieutenant, Varimathras.",al={"who is leader of undercity","undercity ruler","who runs undercity"},it="leader"},{q="What is King Terenas's memorial in the ruins above?",a="Above the city's main lifts sits a stone memorial for the slain King Terenas Menethil II. It does not contain his body, as his corpse was cremated and his ashes discarded during Kel'Thuzad's resurrection. Surviving Alliance humans bravely carved the monument amidst the ruins so the memory of Lordaeron's last true king would endure.",al={"king terenas tomb","lordaeron throne room grave","who built the tomb above undercity"}},{q="What are the strange noises in the Lordaeron throne room?",a="In the ruined throne room above the Undercity lifts, spectral echoes of the past still linger. Visitors standing in the center can hear faint phantom sounds: the celebratory bells and rose petals of Arthas's return, the warning words of the prophet Medivh, and the final conversation between King Terenas and his patricidal son.",al={"ghost sounds throne room","throne room whispering","voices in lordaeron throne room"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken allow other Horde members here?",a="The Forsaken formed an alliance of convenience with Warchief Thrall's Horde for survival, surrounded as they are by hostile Scarlet zealots and Scourge legions. While living Horde races find the toxic fumes and alchemical rivers stifling, emissaries and travelers are allowed access to foster diplomatic and military ties.",al={"why are orcs in undercity","horde in undercity","why is undercity part of horde"},it="allies"},{q="What is the Undercity?",a="The Undercity is the subterranean capital of the Forsaken, built directly beneath the shattered ruins of Capital City in Tirisfal Glades. Carved out of ancient royal crypts, sewers, and catacombs, it was expanded by Prince Arthas as a Scourge stronghold before Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her renegade undead seized it during the civil war. Today, it stands as a fortified sanctuary for free-willed undead, crisscrossed by toxic sludge and guarded vigilantly against all living intruders.",al={"what is undercity","tell me about undercity","undercity lore"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to the old king of Lordaeron?",a="King Terenas Menethil II was murdered in the throne room directly above this city by his own son, Prince Arthas. After returning from Northrend corrupted by the runeblade Frostmourne, Arthas struck down his father and unleashed the Scourge upon the kingdom. Terenas's ashes were later stolen by the death knight to resurrect Kel'Thuzad, leaving behind only the memorial stone and the dried trail of blood you can still see near the ruined throne.",al={"king terenas fate","what happened to king terenas","who killed king terenas"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who was Arthas?",a="Arthas Menethil was the Crown Prince of Lordaeron and a celebrated paladin of the Silver Hand. Desperate to stop the Plague of Undeath sweeping his homeland, his crusade turned ruthless and fanatical. In Northrend, he claimed the cursed runeblade Frostmourne, which devoured his soul and made him the dread champion of the Lich King. He returned home only to butcher his father, raze Lordaeron, and eventually travel back north to merge with the Frozen Throne.",al={"who is arthas","prince arthas lore","arthas menethil"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who is Sylvanas Windrunner?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner was once the valiant Ranger-General of Silvermoon, defending Quel'Thalas against the Scourge during the Third War. When she fell, Arthas tore her soul from her corpse and twisted her into a banshee to torment her. When the Lich King's grip weakened, she broke free, reclaimed her physical form, and rallied other independent undead into the Forsaken. Now she reigns as their Banshee Queen from the Royal Quarter.",al={"who is the banshee queen","sylvanas lore","who is sylvanas"},it="leader",add=true,nx={11}},{q="Why is Sylvanas called the Dark Lady?",a="The Forsaken honor Sylvanas as the Dark Lady because she liberated them from the mindless thrall of the Lich King and gave them shelter when the rest of Azeroth sought their total extermination. Revered alongside her title as the Banshee Queen, the moniker reflects both her shadowy mastery over death and the fierce, unyielding devotion of her undead subjects.",al={"why dark lady","dark lady title sylvanas","dark lady meaning"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken part of the Horde?",a="Surrounded by hostile Scarlet Crusaders, relentless Scourge, and vengeful Alliance remnants, the Forsaken could not survive alone in Lordaeron. Lady Sylvanas reached out across the sea to Warchief Thrall, forging a pragmatic alliance of convenience. The Horde gained a crucial military foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms, while the Forsaken secured essential reinforcements and political legitimacy in their war for survival.",al={"why forsaken horde","undead join horde","forsaken horde alliance"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What is the Scourge and are they still nearby?",a="The Scourge is the vast, ravenous army of mindless undead created by the Burning Legion and ruled by the Lich King from Northrend. Though the Forsaken wrested the Undercity and Tirisfal from their grasp, the Scourge remains an immediate, lethal danger. Their legions still choke the nearby Plaguelands under Kel'Thuzad's command and infest abandoned farmsteads and crypts across the glades.",al={"is the scourge nearby","what is the scourge","scourge in lordaeron"},it="threat",add=true,nx={14,15}},{q="Where is the Lich King now?",a="The Lich King resides atop the Frozen Throne in the distant, icy wastes of Northrend. Following the civil war in the Plaguelands, Prince Arthas fled Lordaeron to protect his weakening master, ascending the glacier and merging their essences into a single terrifying entity. From that arctic bastion, his chilling gaze still watches over Azeroth.",al={"where is lich king","lich king location","where is arthas now"},it="threat",add=true},{q="Who are the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is a fanatical order of human zealots born from the ruins of Lordaeron's defense. Blinded by their righteous hatred of the undead, they make no distinction between mindless Scourge and free-willed Forsaken, viewing anyone tainted by undeath—and any living outsider who tolerates them—as vile abominations fit only for the pyre. Their primary bastion in Tirisfal is the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"who is scarlet crusade","scarlet crusaders","scarlet crusade lore"},it="threat",add=true},{q="Is the Undercity dangerous?",a="It is extraordinarily dangerous, especially for the living. Channels of raw alchemical waste and poisonous sludge run through the city streets, filling the cavernous halls with toxic fumes that make breathing hazardous for flesh-and-blood visitors. Beneath the paved quarters lie infested sewers, and deeper still are secretive experiments where dark alchemy and ruthless assassinations are plotted daily.",al={"is undercity safe","danger in undercity","undercity dangers"},it="danger",add=true},{q="How did I end up in Undercity?",a="As a Forsaken, your path naturally led here after awakening from death in Deathknell and proving your loyalty through Tirisfal Glades, following the roads past Brill to descend beneath the shattered ruins of Capital City. If you hail from Kalimdor or distant lands, you likely arrived aboard a Horde zeppelin docking at the towers just outside the capital, or trekked across the blighted countryside. The Undercity stands as the Horde's primary stronghold in northern Lordaeron, offering shelter and purpose beneath the ancient palace catacombs.",al={"how did i get here","how did i reach undercity","how do you get to undercity"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Undercity?",a="You are here to aid the Forsaken and muster the strength of the Horde against the perils surrounding Lordaeron. Within the city's concentric quarters, you can consult class trainers, acquire supplies, and consult the dark researchers of the Royal Apothecary Society. Beyond tending to your trade, your duty is to take up assignments for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her lieutenants. The Forsaken fight a war on multiple fronts: scouring the remnants of the mindless Scourge, driving back the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, and securing safe ground for the free-willed undead to endure.",al={"what am i doing here","what should i do in undercity","why am i here"},it="purpose",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Undercity is your sovereign sanctuary and homeland, carved out by your own hands after breaking the Lich King's iron grip on your mind.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde's primary foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms, the Undercity secures zeppelin links directly back to Durotar and Grom'gol Base Camp.",["race:Human"]="Beneath the soil of your fallen ancestral kingdom lies a grim perversion of Lordaeron's royal crypts, occupied by the walking corpses of your former brethren.",["race:Orc"]="Deep within these very dungeons, the legendary Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer was once imprisoned by the Alliance of Lordaeron before making his historic escape."},kw={"apothecarium","arthas","forsaken","lordaeron","scourge","sylvanas","terenas","tirisfal","undercity","varimathras"},rel={"npc:sylvanas-windrunner","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","topic:arthas-menethil","subzone:apothecarium"},src={"Undercity"}}
